{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought","id":1200127,"title":"Isator Levi reads Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-27T10:43:39-07:00","id":1200127,"title":"Isator Levi reads Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought","content":"All right, so it\u2019s once again time to react to an Exalted book as I read it. Starting off with a chapter fiction about the Wyld Hunt, for once.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s off to a good start with the image of somebody retreating alongside a reclaimed heirloom weapon, on which higher priority was placed than even the body. That\u2019s the kind of introduction that conveys some culture and character all on its own. It also looks like we\u2019re being acquainted with members of our signature Kinship. I\u2019m guessing that they\u2019re fighting\u2026 actually, I don\u2019t want to assume. Still, I like the image that most of the bodies can\u2019t be given proper due; it strikes a personal note with something that horrifies me.<br /> <br /> Ooh, one of them is dismissing the camp servants because of the danger, that\u2019s neat.<br /> <br /> Oh great, is it going to be using the Immaculate names? I can never keep those straight\u2026 I think the Wretched are the Dawn/Dusk Caste?<br /> <br /> Anyway, it\u2019s a nice cross-section of Exalted they\u2019ve got here in the signatures. And it\u2019s a good conceit to present this Wyld Hunt in terms of a battle of attrition, of sorts.<br /> Oh, and they\u2019re being joined by Exalted from Lookshy, for extra representation.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an interesting choice to present this Wyld Hunt in a heroic, underdog kind of role, while still referencing their possible ruthlessness. It captures the contrasts inherent to the Dragon Blooded position in the world.<br /> <br /> Ooooh, seeing a Sworn Kinship/Brotherhood being formed in narrative. I\u2026 don\u2019t think that\u2019s <i>ever</i> been shown before, which now seems like a remarkable oversight. It\u2019s short, but an effective little scene.<br /> <br /> Oh no, they <i>are</i> Lunars. Should have run with the first instinct. Let\u2019s see, fight scene, fight scene\u2026 yeah, it\u2019s okay to keep it minimalist at this stage, since it\u2019s not really the point; it\u2019s more about the emotions, and the <i>sense</i> of coordination. But the notion of taking one of them captive is intriguing.<br /> <br /> Annnd final note is on how they\u2019re sticking together regardless.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good opening fiction. It sets the stage of the Dragon Blooded, their place and power and diversity, and gives them an effective triumph. I think that it\u2019s good to introduce them with something like this, more at the ground level, which I think might be more accessible in what they\u2019re about than the typical representations of Realm intrigue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T10:56:51-07:00","id":1200132,"title":"","content":"Link to where you're reading?<br /> <br /> I've kicked, but haven't gotten any updates beyond the kick confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:01:16-07:00","id":1200136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200132#post1200132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Link to where you're reading?<br /> <br /> I've kicked, but haven't gotten any updates beyond the kick confirmation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its on the front page of the kickstarter right under <u> About</u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:01:55-07:00","id":1200137,"title":"","content":"It's a backer update. So on the main page you should see a little 1 next to the Updates, right next to Comments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:03:38-07:00","id":1200139,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> (10)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:03:54-07:00","id":1200140,"title":"","content":"Dawns are called Forsaken. The Wretched are Night Castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:07:26-07:00","id":1200141,"title":"","content":"Now, the introduction chapter\u2026<br /> <br /> The summary is familiar, but it\u2019s got emphasis on key points such as them being the only Exalted that civilized Creation have ever known. I also like some of the terminology that is employed, such as referring to the Empress as their God-Matriarch.<br /> <br /> Hmm, what chapters are we getting\u2026 an overview of the Dragon Blooded in general, and all of the Great Houses. Shouldn\u2019t be too dense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I knew that there was going to be sorcery, but wasn\u2019t expecting it to be a dedicated part of a chapter, so I\u2019ll be interested in seeing what kinds of spells are there.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, anything new in the Lexicon\u2026 a specific term for a school\u2019s headmaster portends an interesting new take on Realm education. Oh, there are <i>three</i> Dominions now.<br /> <br /> And the inspirations list is about what one would expect, although it\u2019s stoked my interest in Basilisk, and I\u2019m excited to see what the Charms might have gotten from Legend of Korra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:07:57-07:00","id":1200142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200140#post1200140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Dawns are called Forsaken. The Wretched are Night Castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo then a Solar-Lunar pairing, it would seem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:10:19-07:00","id":1200173,"title":"","content":"Now, Chapter One\u2026<br /> <br /> Interesting choice to tell a chapter fiction from the perspective of the Empress\u2026. where she isn\u2019t being horribly tortured. I suppose this book shall be full of firsts. I wonder if there\u2019s anything substantial to not wanting to sleep in sunlight, or if it\u2019s just a bit of superstition. I would wonder if it\u2019s leaning too hard on her possession of the hearthstone for the Imperial Manse, but it at least adds to her iconography.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on to the meat:<br /> <br /> It\u2019s nice that the origin story of the Terrestrials is appropriately brief, and lacking in any\u2026 unsuitable details. Much more interesting is the wording of the Celestial Exalted having needed to <i>court</i> their service, rather than being entitled to it, as well as the idea that many of them had independent dominion. <br /> <br /> Hmm, has the order of the Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusade been\u2026 switched?<br /> <br /> This chapter probably has a lot to get into, so I can see why they\u2019d want to abridge the history of the Empress and the Realm. Here\u2019s hoping that it gets a somewhat longer form in the Realm\u2019s own book.<br /> <br /> A sidebar to establish the rough numbers should help keep a number of things straight.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, a section dedicated to describing their Exaltation\u2026 yes, given how there are several cultures built around it, some focus and clarity there is a good call. It\u2019s also a succinct place to introduce new concepts, such as procreative Essence.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad that it takes time to state that having a leisurely life does not outright prevent the Exaltation.<br /> I\u2019m guessing that the presentation of the little Exaltation snippets (which, don\u2019t get me wrong, are nice) will work better in the finished book.<br /> <br /> And now there\u2019s some stronger emphasis on Aspects, so let\u2019s see what we\u2019ve got\u2026 clarification on where the line is looks like a good start, and the elements themselves are familiar. Their own version of Essence Fever\u2026 well, the image of their blood rate actually being higher is unusual, but it does seem like a good small detail to make their power feel more grounded and physical.<br /> <br /> Ahh, the idea that it\u2019s also something that impels them to kinship, and they build upon this to make the Hearth oath, that\u2019s a very nice bit of mysticism.<br /> <br /> Oh I see; they\u2019re framing the societies of the Dragon Blooded in the same terms as the different Exalted in the core book. I like that, that\u2019s clever.<br /> <br /> Ohh, it\u2019s cute that Lookshy frames the Shogunate\u2019s constant warfare as something character building. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, Prasad, something new\u2026 but personally familiar from the preview of The Realm. I do like the idea of them having cultural interchanges with the Scarlet Dynasty, though. Particularly with the focus on them as a newer and more dynamic empire; the Realm is good, but I\u2019d warrant that them being on top for centuries prevented certain kinds of stories in the past, so Prasad makes a good alternative, actively expanding and making war on equal terms, while retaining the characteristic Dragon Blooded authority.<br /> <br /> Heh, it\u2019s a bit ambitious to introduce the Forest Witches this early, but if it captures somebody\u2019s attention\u2026 at the very least, the shorter format might make them more readily comprehensible to newcomers.<br /> <br /> And with a summary of outcastes, that\u2019s the end of this chapter. It was a bit less detailed than I might have expected, but that\u2019s probably for the best; trim a lot of fat, stay on message (and leave enough space for all of the magic later on). It\u2019s a solid introduction to these Exalted.<br /> <br /> The Great Houses is liable to be a long and intricate chapter, so I\u2019m going to save that for tomorrow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:17:46-07:00","id":1200178,"title":"","content":"Yeah you might want to go one house at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:26:49-07:00","id":1200179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200173#post1200173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This chapter probably has a lot to get into, so I can see why they\u2019d want to abridge the history of the Empress and the Realm. Here\u2019s hoping that it gets a somewhat longer form in the Realm\u2019s own book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T17:08:42-07:00","id":1200265,"title":"","content":"Before I get on, a small detail that I like more on reflection:<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, here we've got a chapter fiction in which we see a group's signature circle actually come together. I... don't think that's ever happened before; the closest we've gotten is a few references to why the circle of new Solars is together strewn throughout some of their fiction pieces, but even then we've not actually gotten a story of them coming together; what drove it, their perspectives on one another, the shared turmoil that forged a bond. <br /> <br /> \u200bIt... actually highlights weaknesses in the previous ones to me. For the old Solars, what exactly brought any of them besides Swan and Arianna together, and what did they get out of that relationship? Neither the Lunars nor the Dragon Blooded ever had a signature group before (especially weird for the latter, considering how important kinship was supposed to be for them, and unlike the Lunars, that group of characters who, but for two, could conceivably have never spoken to one another before in the game's fiction kept showing up in other art pieces), and for the rest, they only ever seem to be together because they have the same boss, and never seem to like each other.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm sorry, this isn't what I wanted to talk about, it's just that the line of thought streamed off when I came to it... what were they thinking?! Why have circles and Brotherhoods by a conceit of the game world's culture, and feature <i>no</i> prominent examples of them that seem positive or make sense?<br /> <br /> \u200bLeaving that aside, being the game's signature Hearth suggests to me that they have to still exist in Year Zero, so any time that a date of earlier in the century is provided, that establishes how they're not only together, but have been so for decades. That's an enjoyable idea to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T17:43:12-07:00","id":1200283,"title":"","content":"We know why Jade and Dace are together from A Day As Dark As Night.<br /> <br /> It's almost a classic superhero meet up. Both investigating same atrocity, someone gets confused and thinks the other did it, and then punch out leads to team up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T18:05:13-07:00","id":1200291,"title":"","content":"Okay, something to keep on track of me reading the book...<br /> <br /> Additional perspectives on the Scarlet Empress fiction:<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually like the way it's about her morning routine, for a combination of how those can often be one of the more unusual and intriguing aspects of a monarch's life, and how there are few things I find more humanising for a powerful figure than the basic idea that they go to sleep at night and have to sort themselves out in the morning. When I was young, a basic common detail in my imaginings of villainous figures would be the idea that they never actually slept, and in retrospect I think that was from a combination of making them more alien and an association between sleep and vulnerability.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yeah, it works for me to have a simple vignette of the Empress waking up in the morning and going over to get dressed. It's not quite Catherine the Great's daily kickstart of coffee, but it works on its own merits.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do like some of the ritual elements that Neall came up with for it as well, such as how the servants have to avert their eyes while she crowns herself, or how to get to her dressing room she walks past expensive murals depicting her own public persona.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T01:49:59-07:00","id":1200376,"title":"","content":"All right, Chapter Two:<br /> <br /> I wonder if Sesus Daral\u2019s derision represents a cultural bias, or a personal one. I\u2019ve often thought that the Realm wouldn\u2019t have something like the Imperial Chinese Confucian disdain for merchants, if a number of Dynasts are involved in commercial activity, but perhaps they draw exacting distinctions in a manner that would leave the kind of business the Nellens are involved in looked down upon. In any case, I like introducing the Dynasty with a tense social scene.<br /> <br /> Aww darn it; this is going to have artwork when published, possibly ruining my mental image of Daral as Jasper from Steven Universe.<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, Daral is a man; nevermind.<br /> <br /> Heh, the only thing that could have improved my liking of such an argument is it fluidly turning into a duel.<br /> <br /> (What does he mean by insult to Sesus\u2019 father?)<br /> <br /> And it ends nicely. I enjoy these characters.<br /> <br /> So, let\u2019s have a look at this general introduction\u2026<br /> <br /> Yes, that\u2019s a good basic introduction to what Houses are and how they do; I think the comparison to nations in particular casts a certain light on their operations. Prominent bloodlines are about the same\u2026 but here\u2019s an addition that I\u2019d caught before, how the House leadership is now specifically referred to as the matriarch. That seems like quite a bit of power conferred in an individual, and it looks like a much more official position than it used to be. I wonder at the implications that has for how the Realm in general is organised.<br /> <br /> Huh, I wasn\u2019t expecting a guideline on naming conventions\u2026 if Dynastic names are mostly chosen for euphony, does that mean that they\u2019re generally ad hoc? Or at least were when they originated?<br /> <br /> Aaaand important House properties, such as land and magical prodigies, are held in a corporate manner, which should add an interesting dimension to internal House politics.<br /> <br /> Oooof, I\u2019m taken aback by that use of the word \u201csymbology\u201d; even leaving aside whether it\u2019s a real word or not, it would refer to the <i>study</i> of symbols, not the application of them. That really should be symbol<i>ism</i>. As to the substance of their symbolism\u2026 the idea that House colours are out of fashion, and thus carry a particular statement, is an interesting dimension to add to House culture.<br /> <br /> Okay, the Houses themselves; taking two at a time. And to start, we have Cathak, so let\u2019s see what they did to finally make them interesting.<br /> <br /> Still a military focus (nothing wrong with that), but with a general predilection for adventure\u2026 they get standing from the assumption that their military service or similar leaves them well-travelled (possibly in contrast with the more austere Tepets)\u2026 and a certain competitive streak. I think it\u2019s a good idea to add a subtle recent trend to a House; gives them a sense of organic history, as well as framing the power of a House matriarch.<br /> <br /> The idea that they have a military approach to politics is curious, and I wonder what it might consist of in practice.<br /> <br /> Ahh, now <i>there</i> is something interesting; that their priorities in marriage negotiations can favour Dynasts of lower status, giving them a romantic image in the Dynasty as a whole. There\u2019s a<br /> lot that can be built on that foundation. Plus the idea of military husbands being put through the wringer, an amusing reversal of certain literary conventions.<br /> <br /> Hmm, here\u2019s a rather significant change to the conventions of the Realm; limiting House legions to only three of them. Even apart from what it\u2019s saying here, about the business and social dynamics behind that, it probably eliminates the idea that House legions were generally inferior. It also casts the Houses appropriating the Imperial military in a very different light. I can\u2019t quite remember the dynamic that was given to the Tepet military, but the Cathaks strike me as a more military adventurer type, with the stated emphasis on acquiring territories, with the interesting twist of it including some financial chicanery and flipping businesses; between that and the marriage section, I can already imagine some strong partnerships that can be made in the setting.<br /> <br /> The relationship with their satrapies is about the same, buuut\u2026 ah, here\u2019s something that I was particularly hoping for; distinct House strategies for the Realm\u2019s future. I\u2019ve always said that I\u2019ve liked the sidebar in the Second Edition core, and this idea that Cathak\u2019s strategy is to state that it will support whomever acquires the Throne as a means of courting favour and wealth from the<br /> other Houses definitely feels like it is in the spirit of that sidebar. I approve of it.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, their military philosophy\u2026 the idea of Cainan\u2019s influence leading to the practice of attaching spiritual advisors is nice, but I particularly like the notion that they apply the principle of the Thousand Correct Actions in terms of how <i>units</i> need to be heroes, rather than individuals.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s interesting that Cathak doesn\u2019t really seem to have any distinct allies, which casts its strategy in the succession crisis in a particular light. Plus how even its antagonistic relationships are more\u2026 subtle, it makes Cathak seem like a good choice for playing a Dynast who can move in a lot of circles.<br /> <br /> So, Cathak has a headquarters now, in the form of a spiritually provocative fortress, aaaand they\u2019re the ones attached to the old standby of Harborhead <i>and</i> the new hotness of Fa\u2026 ah, I initially misread that as being Faxai (as in the Caul), but no, it\u2019s \u201cjust\u201d a new Western satrapy.<br /> <br /> As for the personages, it\u2019s an interesting idea to detail the House founder and a line of continuity to the current matriarch like this, in a bit of House mythmaking. Cainan\u2019s position in particular has a strong change to it, that plays more off of the matriarchal bent of the Realm as a whole, with his leadership being something unusual that he strives to live up to, while still retaining (in a somewhat lower key form) the element of him being a viable candidate for the throne but for his age.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I find the idea that even a leading man gets called \u201cmatriarch\u201d to validate my long-held notion that most people expect to call the new monarch \u201cEmpress\u201d regardless of gender. \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> Garel\u2019s not bad, although I don\u2019t find anything to particularly stand out about her. Nothing wrong with that, just that it leaves her a bit utilitarian. Whereas Elanda\u2026 well, it\u2019s a distinct idea to have somebody with a form of disability (at least prior to Exaltation) exist to provide a kind of internal outsider\u2019s perspective on the Realm and Dynasty.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm going to leave it at that for the moment, since half of this post consists of the general House assessment, I'll be skipping Tepet anyway, and I have a pressing engagement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T02:49:47-07:00","id":1200380,"title":"","content":"The mention of how apparently it's a long-held romantic fantasy for a charming Cathak soldier to come in and sweep a guy off his feet made me realize that I would love to see some more examples of Realm Romantic Literature Tropes, just to see how they differ from what I'm used to.<br /> <br /> Edit: Thinking on it... If Minton put out an actual in-universe Realm Romance Novel I'd buy it. That's not a joke or hyperbole. I would buy it and probably make my own Read Thread on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-28-2018, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T04:42:31-07:00","id":1200387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200376#post1200376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (What does he mean by insult to Sesus\u2019 father?)<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The mortal Nellens was consort to the Empress and father to Sesus. House Sesus finds the elevation of House Nellens distasteful because the latter is formed from a bunch of blood relations to their father with poor Dragon-Blooded lineage. The preview covers it in the section on Nellens enemies, it was a nifty bit of lore even back in 1E,<br /> <br /> Overall I liked the Cathak description, most of the changes are subtle and consist of taking snippets of lore tucked into the old Aspect Books and contextualizing them. Probably my favorite line relates to how the younger Cathaks have started emulating Cainan's piety to the point they think their House has always been devotedly Immaculate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T05:43:20-07:00","id":1200398,"title":"","content":"Heyeyey, the detail of Nellens being father of Sesus was in previous Editions, so that's fine, but don't go trying to tell me things from later in the book than I have read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T10:56:15-07:00","id":1200485,"title":"","content":"Now, I\u2019ve been waiting to see what would be done with Cynis.<br /> <br /> Right off the bat, there\u2019s the good strong focus on them less as debauched, and more as masters of high society, and I can see interesting possibilities in the idea that they trade in specific and desirable slaves. Agriculture is a bit of a new focus for them (at least apart from drugs), but hardly out of place, and I was already on board with the idea that they have strong international trade links. In fact\u2026 yes, Cynis has always been Wood, but playing up the aspect of Wood as having a strong tendency to relationships even by the standards of Dragon Blooded melds nicely with the House.<br /> <br /> Still, they wouldn\u2019t be Cynis if there wasn\u2019t a <i>bit</i> of debauchery, although here I find the framing to focus less on that as something to judge, and more as an expression of a kind of libertarianism (which is rather ironic for the House tasked with trading in slaves), even before it gets into the idea that at least part of the reputation is an act to leave them underestimated and lax with their secrets.<br /> <br /> The House economics are about what one would expect, but for the very good addition of them as the foremost medical practitioners in the Dynasty. You know, between that and the stated proclivity for experimentation\u2026 okay, I\u2019ve skipped ahead a bit to confirm that Bhagwai has not been reassigned to his mother\u2019s House, and considering that he doesn\u2019t seem to have been mentioned yet, he really ought to be. He fits with it a lot more closely, especially now, and considering the matrilineality, he really should have always been. My God, even the stated reason of \u201ca child of two House founders would be too politically contentious\u201d\u2026 that\u2019s <i>easier</i> to do if you leave him with the mother. \u201cHey Cynis, who\u2019s the father of that child you\u2019re pregnant with?\u201d \u201cSome guy.\u201d Anyway, rant over\u2026<br /> <br /> Good contrast between their weaker overt military and their more subtle methods of infiltration and sabotage. I particularly like the idea of them being a kind of chemical weapons dealer, playing both sides of any covert conflict as suits them, to their compounding profit. Particularly with the idea that part of their capacity to engage in such is the nigh-unparalleled trade network.<br /> It's interesting that, as their enemies and allies go, the House has a stronger antagonism with Mnemon herself than her family, and that otherwise their most antagonistic relationship is with a House that they owe a lot of money to. I can see an interesting plot hook in which Cynis is forced to go a lot more open to protect itself, with the potential military support of Sesus (although I could personally see somebody championing courting more of Tepet).<br /> <br /> So I take it that all of the Houses are getting fancy headquarters now. Greyfalls looks to be more interesting, with the trade connections to some nifty new Eastern locales. I\u2019m also guessing that part of the Realm\u2019s motivation for empire now might be the need to control the manses to power the Defence Grid.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, I wonder if it might be a bit on the nose for Cynis to have died from a drug overdose, although I do like the idea that she was a great explorer and merchant, plus the notion that her crypt is an object of the family\u2019s veneration. I can\u2019t quite remember what the personalities of the Cynis triumvirate was before, but if it was different, then this distribution of skills and personality traits makes them feel like a good showing of the House capabilities and keeping them in the black.<br /> <br /> Ooohh, we\u2019ve got a new candidate for the position of Empress, and one who plays into the possibility of the House developing its military fortunes if it needs to. I also like the idea of Laseral having the public persona of being a ruthless battle commander contrasted against a concealed genuine love with her husband.<br /> <br /> Hmm, was Cynis Umara in Masters of Jade? No, probably not, and even if she was this would be a significant revision; she probably just happens to be a very similar character. Aaaaand between Cynis Cerise and Cathak Elanda, I can only assume that the provision against the Dragon Blooded ever being born with birth defects or physiological disorders has just been dropped entirely. I approve.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T13:15:30-07:00","id":1200537,"title":"","content":"Now, House Ledaal, one that was always more interesting in concept than execution. It\u2019s starting off strong with language that conveys a sense of spiritual motive in their imperial mission\u2026. contrasted by being the first seen that is divided against itself. The rise of Ledaal herself represents a fun, weird take on dynastic policies, as well as the mythmaking that inspires the House.<br /> <br /> Ahh, and here\u2019s the context behind the division in its leadership; the need to balance pushing for (and independently pursuing) responses to growing supernatural threats, and participation in the political game to actually maintain their constitution.<br /> <br /> So, Ledaal still has Arjuf Dominion; I wonder if it\u2019s still run by somebody who is in a relationship with her father. Hmm, didn\u2019t Greyfalls used to belong to Ledaal? It would certainly fit in with the idea that they take a more direct hand in governing their satrapies.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a nice middle ground between preceding depictions of military prowess; they\u2019re not half bad, but they\u2019ve got too many possible targets to focus military ventures on, and the heart of their power lacks security.<br /> <br /> Jeez, Ragara sure has some problems making friends, eh? Whereas it\u2019s nice to see a faction that actually does think that Mnemon is right for the job.<br /> Oh wow; I wonder how many people are going to pursue that plot hook about Essence amplification. And it\u2019s neat to use Ledaal\u2019s particular hang-up to give it a unique relationship with an odd satrapy (or at least the shadowland that it borders and maintains contact with).<br /> <br /> I think the scions of Ledaal are some particular standouts, with the slightly hypocritical matriarch and Rae\u2019s particularly strong vendetta against Thorns, on top of the old favourite of Kebok Coren and her storm-demon lineage.<br /> <br /> \u200bOh, that was a lot shorter than it took to read and write. Perhaps I'll take a look at Mnemon a bit later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T04:09:35-07:00","id":1200754,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Now, moving on to Mnemon, which is interesting for already having had a few references to at least its leading personage in the run up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I had already suspected that there was going to be a stronger emphasis on piety in the House (not least since the Cynis write-up attributed it to Mnemon herself). An emphasis on architecture is interesting to me, because for the longest time, I was sure that Mnemon had been referenced somewhere as a literal architect by profession, and was very attached to the image, and yet it seemed to turn out to alternately be a misreading of her Nature or a complete fabrication on my part. Either way, it\u2019s a role for them that satisfies me.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">If I\u2019m guessing right, then it would seem that the House\u2019s perceived legitimacy for the succession, and power with which it backs it up, is coming from association with the Immaculate Order more than Mnemon having a sense of entitlement.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hmm, I had always assumed that Cynis would be the one associated more with scandalous exoticism, so the idea that it\u2019s a strong focus in Mnemon is both an interesting subversion of my expectations, and an amusing contrast considering the antipathy between those Houses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">And if I\u2019m reading that line about snubbing other Houses correctly, they\u2019ve got a curious predilection for insularity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I see, if Mnemon\u2019s backstory includes learning her skills while in hiding from Ragara, I\u2019m guessing that whole line about the Empress promising to kill him if anything happened to his sister has been removed. Heh, I feel a surprising degree of sympathy for the idea of Mnemon falling into deeper debt to that brother\u2019s scions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">And this is a very interesting change to Mnemon\u2019s military predilictions, with the shift from \u201csure they could take on many other Houses alone\u201d to \u201conly recently acquired a large military, and has committed most to war with Perfect Soul\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I was always fond of the more unpleasant Mnemon of Editions past, but I\u2019m sold on this more measured revision of her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">My, but does Mnemon have by far the most elaborate inter-House relations thus far. I suppose that\u2019s what comes from being run by one of the stronger candidates for the Throne. It\u2019s also another strong extrapolation from the revision from them being a militarily strong House independently.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Whatever is changed in her, I do like that Mnemon retains a general dislike of V\u2019Neef, even if the reasons have changed. In particular, for what they say about Mnemon; I\u2019m liking this feel I\u2019m getting of her as a powerful, respected, and intelligent figure but who lacks for social adeptness in a manner that makes it hard for her to be widely liked, and is a shortcoming in comparisons to the Empress. I\u2019m getting this image of her as a kind of stern, slightly self-righteous nerd.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I kind of adore the idea of Mnemon renaming a city that she restored after herself, and the notion of her leaving dues to lost siblings\u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Yeah, I\u2019m, I\u2019m completely sold. Mnemon is dead, long live Mnemon!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">(Seriously, I am really surprised by just how much I like this shift)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Aaand we finally get Paragon in this Edition. I\u2019m guessing that a more thorough exploration of its relationship with the Realm will be explored in the other book.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I like the idea of the inner circle; it represents that old idea of Mnemon exercising particular power over her House within this new context, with the added sense that the poor woman has some severe trust issues. Hmm, Caras Farim, I\u2019m sure that person was in prior Editions\u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ohoho I\u2019m looking forward to seeing Mnemon\u2019s dedicated profile. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ah well, I guess it makes sense that most of what there is has already been said. I suppose that\u2019s what you get when the founder is the still-living matriarch. Still, as a final cherry on the Sundae, I do like the idea that she has a tendency to austerity and a dislike of sycophants.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Ohoho, I just had a thought: previous Editions Mnemon was the Cersei Lannister of the books, while Third Edition Mnemon is the Cersei of the tv show. </span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\ud83d\ude09</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">And we\u2019re continuing with fun altered family conventions and endearing Mnemon characteristics with her having brought in a sister as an adopted daughter, who\u2019s a cool freaky occultist to boot!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I think Pallan may be the first strong example of the place of sons in the matrilineal system of the Dynasty; his values as a member of Mnemon give him traits that are attractive to be drawn into another House, while also constituting a form of soft power that can be projected into them. That would have been good even without crossing his stars with a Ragara. I believe that I had anticipated the notion that a man impregnating another woman would have controversy if his procreative Essence is considered to be his wife\u2019s property.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">And it\u2019s all topped off nicely with somebody who takes the House\u2019s tendency towards spirituality in a very different direction.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">So yeah, House Mnemon: A+ right there.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-29-2018, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T04:36:03-07:00","id":1200759,"title":"","content":"Compering Mnemon to Cersei seems mean. Whatever problems the narrative and characters had with Mnemon they always acknowledged that she was competant in her chosen fields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T04:37:51-07:00","id":1200760,"title":"","content":"Huh.<br /> <br /> \u200bThinking more about it, I recalled how the Dragon Blooded are supposed to have a natural predilection for forming communities now, and how in the leadership of other Houses, even when the groups are a bit contentious, they still seem to be on board with one another.<br /> <br /> So the idea that Mnemon's youth was marked by murdered siblings (but for the at least one that she managed to save) and risks to her own life from Ragara's ambitions being so traumatic that she can't work with an inner circle that doesn't contain people she's sure she can cow or take in a fight or whatever... that is <i>profoundly</i> sad.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would have never expected to feel such sympathies for Mnemon, and I regard that I do so as a triumph of writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T04:39:31-07:00","id":1200761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200759#post1200759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compering Mnemon to Cersei seems mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more about the contrast between media.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:39:48-07:00","id":1200817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200761#post1200761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more about the contrast between media.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a stern hater of the tv series (lack of narrative logic and being as subtle as an avalanche), I object to you being so mean to poor Mnemon! <br /> <br /> ...Actually, let me rephrase that: I object to you being so mean to stinking-rich Mnemon! For one thing, Mnemon seems to be one of the few to take Anathema seriously whereas Show!Cersei is sort of like a volatile mix of negative stereotypes.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note. Ya, Mnemon is much better in this edition. Read through the thing a few times and have yet to find a 'bad' house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-29-2018, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:44:46-07:00","id":1200819,"title":"","content":"The daughter Ragara was told &quot;Protect her or I'll fucking kill you you brat&quot; by the Empress was Sesus, not Mnemon. Though that makes the timeline a touch strange as Mnemon is a hundred years younger than Sesus was, unless Ragara was basically &quot;Okay, this kid is alive, but I'll still kill all the rest of you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:47:54-07:00","id":1200822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200819#post1200819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The daughter Ragara was told &quot;Protect her or I'll fucking kill you you brat&quot; by the Empress was Sesus, not Mnemon. Though that makes the timeline a touch strange as Mnemon is a hundred years younger than Sesus was, unless Ragara was basically &quot;Okay, this kid is alive, but I'll still kill all the rest of you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAre you talking about in the previous Editions, or is yet <i>another</i> person coming into my first response thread, and telling me about stuff that I haven't read yet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bIf the former, then they both got the same deal with regards to Ragara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:59:56-07:00","id":1200830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200819#post1200819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The daughter Ragara was told &quot;Protect her or I'll fucking kill you you brat&quot; by the Empress was Sesus, not Mnemon. Though that makes the timeline a touch strange as Mnemon is a hundred years younger than Sesus was, unless Ragara was basically &quot;Okay, this kid is alive, but I'll still kill all the rest of you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We've done our best to clear up the inconsistencies in the Realm's timeline. In this case, it meant making Sesus younger than Mnemon. (There's a timeline of major events in <i>The Realm</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T09:09:37-07:00","id":1200832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200822#post1200822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAre you talking about in the previous Editions, or is yet <i>another</i> person coming into my first response thread, and telling me about stuff that I haven't read yet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bIf the former, then they both got the same deal with regards to Ragara.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from the 1e DB book, actually. There's an entire sectioned headered &quot;Ragara&quot; where it talks about his killing all his siblings with a goal of making sure he's the only legitimate heir to the THrone and then the Empress stepping in to put a stop to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"ty