,"edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:21:36-07:00","id":1200926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200920#post1200920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> No worries! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My thanks! Do you want me to post the comment there or will you just elaborate on its own? I ask since I am having a bit of difficulty converting it into a concise question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:51:48-07:00","id":1200941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200847#post1200847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the Empress' disappearance, the Wyld Hunt was usually victorious over young Solars. The setting would look very different otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that in addition to Realm disorganization now as the looming civil war distracts them, and the fact that more Solars means more division of Wyld Hunt resources, another factor in this trend would have been that with less Solars, most Wyld Hunts for Solars were for young lone Solars, while now Circles are more common?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T13:58:30-07:00","id":1200970,"title":"","content":"To be honest, the fact that the Dragonblood beat the Solar and Lunar at the beginning of the book was a great start. Dragonblood virtually never won in 2nd ed comics and fiction. They should at least get to kick Solar ass in their own book (and no doubt lose heavily to Lunars in the Lunar book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:03:08-07:00","id":1201008,"title":"","content":"Now to see Nellens get its due.<br /> <br /> Given what I\u2019m presuming of their status, it\u2019s fun to see what I suppose is a combination of edifying family legend, and piece of popular narrative to cement their place.<br /> <br /> With the changes to Mnemon, the idea of her having been made an advocate for unExalted Dynasts\u2026 it doesn\u2019t make <i>less</i> sense, but it would stand out less and is less necessary. So if House Nellens is going to be expanded, he fits nicely with that position.<br /> <br /> Good to see that they\u2019re still run by that group of seven, plus that dynamic of outsiders assuming that the Dragon Blooded are in charge. I do wonder how Nellens Odem\u2019s mortality is squared with membership in the Greater Deliberative.<br /> <br /> Oh good, they did end up implementing that idea that it\u2019s possible for mortals to have superior breeding to Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> So it seems to me that, unlike the other Houses, Nellens doesn\u2019t really have a designated position, so they capitalise in areas vital to the Realm\u2019s function that the other Houses largely neglect. The different dynamic that gives to their Dragon Blooded is also fascinating, that distinct pressure that is put upon them.<br /> <br /> I know there\u2019s always been the idea that Nellens spreads through the various minor industries and businesses of the Realm, but I think the take of that making them immensely wealthy is new. It\u2019s a strong advantage to be sure, although I have to imagine that it being spread over so many ventures can make it hard to bring to bear on any singular instance (even if their methods probably rely on diffuse action anyway).<br /> <br /> I can see some interesting story possibilities in the idea of the House being in the early process of building up its military. In particular, something like a party of Nellens travelling Threshold warzones in search of experience and instructors. Maybe even some overtures to somebody in the margins of Lookshy.<br /> <br /> I enjoy the notion that Nellens responds to being widely despised with a kind of duplicitous turning of the other cheek, or otherwise taking it in stride while making their plans. So yeah, as was said to me before, House Sesus has issues with Nellens due to being named for their ancestor (which seems to come with the revision of the House not really even being descended from him\u2026 and also how he\u2019s no longer the father of Ledaal, who isn\u2019t even a biological daughter anymore), so that probably makes for a good history of almost open feuding that many of the others didn\u2019t have. It\u2019s also nice to have a prospective conflict based on something as simple as geographic proximity, combined with the issues that Ledaal is having in its own right, and thinking that Nellens would make for an easy win.<br /> <br /> And after everything built up with Ragara, it does warm my heart to see them being so heavily frustrated by a House consisting largely of mortals. They really need to find a way to make friends with Mnemon.<br /> <br /> Ah come now, what did Nellens do to deserve having assets reassigned to V\u2019Neef? While Nellens and Tepet offer a nice example of a conflict between fresh new money and old money on hard times. And of course, the untapped resource that is the general mortal society of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Juche\u2026 didn\u2019t that used to be the centre of Realm manufacturing and mining? Eh, hardly anything was ever done with that, so might as well revise it as the Nellens headquarters. It\u2019s also interesting for there to be a heavily fortified prefecture even before the Isle is in open war. Probably keeps things interesting for the Sesus who try infiltrating. It might also give them a leg up if it actually comes to war; between that and their weaker military, it gives the idea that they might at least spend the initial stage adopting a siege mentality, and letting the others fight it out for a while\u2026 although Ledaal might be equipped to break through such fortification anyway. Still, the possible strategic pictures it paints are compelling.<br /> <br /> Heh, what kinds of bookkeeping chicanery do they need to engage in to conceal their financial assistance to other satrapies? They\u2019re probably too practically minded to do anything as silly as ensure that a House is repaid with its own money just because.<br /> <br /> Ahh, I love the contrast between Nellens\u2019 advocacy for mortals, and undermining abolition of slavery. Sabine paints a fine picture of a powerful mortal situated among the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Oh God, the idea of taking the Righteous and Accountable Ministry of Weights and Measures, always held up as an overwrought and insignificant office, and making a bigger deal out of it\u2026 a hair in either direction, and it would be a very silly idea, but matched with Nellens and with this execution, it does its job. Here\u2019s hoping that <i>somebody</i> will be able to take inspiration from it to get some actions out of the Bureaucracy Ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T17:50:49-07:00","id":1201084,"title":"","content":"Juche was always the homebase of House Nellens, even as far back as 1E. But it was a throwaway factoid in the actual Nellens write-up back then. Part of 3E's writing that I like is that the author of the Great House section makes sure that each family is easily associated with their home prefecture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T18:36:42-07:00","id":1201107,"title":"","content":"Now, House Peleps. I've already gotten an impression from previews in how it's discussed in other House write-ups that it's currently a bit different from my preconception of a bit of a villainous House. It still has the nautical focus, but at the core of a general image of travel and adventure, plus an edge of righteous judgement, that apparently lends them a lot of domestic popularity. I\u2019m inferring that, as one of the older and more prominent faces of the Realm abroad, the need to hold themselves to a higher standard of behaviour and accomplishment was at least partially driven by a sense of wanting to present a good face for the world at large.<br /> <br /> Ahh, and it\u2019s counterbalanced by a particularly strict, meritocratic outlook. I\u2019m already seeing some things that can be done with that, particularly for stories in which one might want to play a Dynast who is still a bit fringe.<br /> <br /> Exactly what the basis of Peleps in the Imperial Navy was is something that was always vague (and probably a bit inconsistent) in the past, so I appreciate the definition of it here, and think it\u2019s a good choice to just commit to the connection. Even with that, I never would have expected the governing body of the navy and the ruling council of the House to be one and the same, nor for it to be elected. As something to make this House stand out, it feels a bit reminiscent to the nation of Sova to me. It\u2019s a curious, although not altogether unfitting, notion that the navy of the Realm is basically a law unto itself, at least as administration goes. I\u2019ll be interested to see if Peleps\u2019 write-up casts any light on the history of that.<br /> <br /> And going along with the trend of Houses having interesting policies for the future is the prospect of Peleps taking its toys and establishing a new dominion elsewhere.<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s see\u2026 that the Merchant Fleet had recently been reassigned from Peleps to V\u2019Neef has always been in the game, and a sticking point between Houses, but key details have been changed. The Merchant Fleet has gone from the coastal defence of the Blessed Isle to the ships that escort tribute back to the homeland, and take a cut. That certainly makes more sense as to how it would materially benefit the new House, and given the changed setup of Peleps, how it was old and respected and financially secure, it makes the conflict have somewhat more substantive stakes.<br /> <br /> Hmm, they <i>are</i> still a bit villainous, but it\u2019s certainly rooted in a clear context and purpose. Heh, it\u2019s a kind of ironic twist on my initial read; they start off as projecting the positive public face of the Realm in the Threshold, and now they\u2019re transitioning to being the early portent of renewed conquest and war. It feels a bit reminiscent of Tolkien\u2019s Numenor.<br /> <br /> And it finally comes down to the plan that the Empress was always said to fear; just seceding altogether and establishing an independent power base in the West. I can imagine that the possibility of hundred or thousands of warships, decked out with innumerable Exalted, coming out of the east to seize control might be the kind of thing that would give even the Silver Prince pause.<br /> <br /> So Peleps got as large a share of the legions as Cathak did (although without the pre-existing ones to makes its land army truly massive), placed at the side of the Imperial Navy. I like that idea that they find the notion of directly appointing their members to officer positions within those legions distasteful, but necessary for rapidly securing control. The Navy is certainly massive, but the limited deployment and nature of the Realm\u2019s land probably places the advantage with the rest of the Dynasty, if they should set differences aside.<br /> <br /> Ohh, now <i>there\u2019s</i> a fascinating idea; that the image of the House, and its reputation with the Dynasty as a whole, might protect it from direct assault by enemies within, a protection that exists in tension with the ultimate treachery that secession would entail.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a very evocative idea, that Peleps, of all Houses, would have this stature and history among the Realm, and exist in a state of crisis very different from that of Tepet; that idea that it\u2019s become too big to sustain itself in the long term, without drastic action.<br /> <br /> Jeez, everybody dislikes House Ragara, don\u2019t they? With all of this build-up, I\u2019ll be very interested to see it next, particularly since I was only recently struck by the point that Ragara may be the only son of the Empress to ever be granted a House, and what he needed to do to earn that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I like the way it suggests that Cathak and Peleps together could be an unstoppable military force, and wonder at the meaning behind Peleps savouring the possibility of the Dynasty united against them.<br /> <br /> To go along with V\u2019Neef representing a much deeper blow to the House, I like the way that the rival is elevated in stature and agency here to make for a more active and even feud.<br /> It\u2019s funny, I always looked at the broken west of the Blessed Isle and saw it as the least desirable collection of prefectures, but with this revised status and format for Peleps, I can see new value in it (making a nice home for some evocative landscapes).<br /> <br /> And hey, they actually did include a form of the Realm stripping satrapies bare and leaving them to rot after all. I wonder if they were deliberately misdirecting me when I asked about that before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The relationship between the Realm and Wavecrest is already vastly more interesting.<br /> <br /> Wow, Peleps was the second daughter? That must make the House very old indeed. To just imagine how widely travelled she was\u2026 and at that age, she may very well have been part of the inception of those Imperial values that her descendants are considered exemplary of.<br /> <br /> By the by, I\u2019ve noticed how many House founders get more elaborate interment than the prior Editions stating that Dynasts went for simple cremation. I wonder if this is a general change, or a privilege of founders.<br /> <br /> Peleps Lai must also be pretty damn old, and I enjoy the way that this makes her conservative in a manner that she actually believes that the Empress might come back. The notion that she dearly wants to directly conquer the West and then present it to the Scarlet Empress is positively cute, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think we\u2019ve yet seen many characters who entertain ambitions for the throne themselves, rather than being presented as supporters for other claims, and Peleps stature does make it seem like the type where at least one of the admirals would have such a vision; in a way, they feel like they\u2019ve got a stronger claim than even Mnemon (which has to really complicate Mnemon\u2019s desire for their support). I\u2019ve got to admire her faith in Tepet, when there are possibly more immediately valuable prospective supporters.<br /> <br /> Heh, considering the Peleps disgust for Nellens, which may represent one of the best hopes for Tepet\u2019s recovery, the idea of an alliance between the three Houses through Aramida\u2019s pursuit of the position is rather inviting.<br /> <br /> God, the game has been missing the groundwork for such complex politics and strategies.<br /> <br /> And to top it off, an Immaculate missionary who intends to try and convert the Mask of Winters to the faith. Good luck to him.<br /> <br /> Peleps has risen dramatically in my estimations. It may be my second favourite House so far, and is vastly more vivid and alive and complex than ever it was in the past. This\u2026 this is a House of Water. I\u2019m really amazed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T18:51:40-07:00","id":1201112,"title":"","content":"I've been using the term &quot;Omnicorp&quot; for House Nellens after reading their current write-up. I've also seen at least two comparisons to Aztecnologies from Shadowrun due to their pretty broad portfolio.<br /> <br /> My personal favorite part of them helping the satrapies of other houses is a little bit like with Ledaal. &quot;If we take Juche, what the hell are you gonna do about it?&quot; To which I can imagine at least one or two Nellens saying &quot;Watch.&quot; and pulling some plugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T05:57:49-07:00","id":1201220,"title":"","content":"All right Ragara, you\u2019ve gotten a lot of build-up; dazzle me.<br /> <br /> A comparison to the Imperial Mountain seems like a suitably ominous introduction, given the note of how there are freaky horrors beneath it.<br /> <br /> Being the Imperial Bank is an old mainstay, but the emphasis has been a bit adjusted what with how this is giving them tremendous capital over the other Houses. Nice to see that Banoba is still the boss, particularly if Ragara himself is going to be developed more. Aaaand even more ominousness with the idea that the House wants everything.<br /> <br /> Ah, so that\u2019s rooted a bit more specifically in the idea of them being particular ardent in the seeking out of powers and Artifacts. I\u2019ve often had a thought of Realm military forces going on expeditions in the Threshold to pick that stuff up, so it\u2019s good to see that given more roots in the agenda and remit of a specific House.<br /> <br /> Oh, but they\u2019re plumbing some greater depths than even that. Diabolism, the Underworld, association with the Anathema\u2026 I had an impression that Ragara was going to be the more villainous House, but this is going further than even my expectations. Mind, it creates an intriguing avenue to undermine their otherwise seemingly implacable power\u2026 or confirm it.<br /> <br /> Hmm, so like Mnemon, Banoba also has an Inner Circle to go along with his singular authority, but the relationship is more\u2026 let\u2019s say reciprocal, and they\u2019re less about administering the House, and more about managing the research into forbidden arts. And they\u2019re studying Exaltation itself, jeez, I\u2019m getting some real \u201cModern Age take on Infernals\u201d vibes from them.<br /> <br /> What the devil is the Final Realm-Controlling Utterance? Is that a specific thing, or is it a term for a hypothetical pursuit?<br /> <br /> Heh, it\u2019s funny that the description of their social standing is comparatively straightforward. Guess that\u2019s the benefit of being old and reliably powerful, while most of their issues are kept in the dark.<br /> So, it would seem as though Ragara\u2019s technically official remit is in locating and mining valuable minerals, which provides the security behind the immense wealth that they leverage into financial chicanery such as Threshold land-sharking in the interests of imperialism. Heh, I\u2019m suddenly reminded of how Akira Toriyama said that one of his seminal villains was based on Japanese land sharks of the 80s. And it\u2019s not just about money, but funding their pursuits and research.<br /> <br /> Hmm, it\u2019s interesting how their philosophy and practices informed their approach to acquiring a military, basically flipping it. Also interesting how, for all of their power, this is presented as a less than successful strategy. It\u2019s another interesting possible weak spot.<br /> <br /> I like how it starts off saying that the House has no real friends among the others, but as well as their relations being complex and detailed, they do see a practical need to make overtures to at least a few other Houses. I also like that final note on how one of Banoba\u2019s plans is something that might leave them in a vulnerable position if it actually <i>succeeds</i>.<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s just my bias arising from Masters of Jade, but I\u2019m getting real Masters of Jade vibes from the Stepped Palace particularly; like a kind of combination of the headquarters of the Timeless Order and Coindelving. The typical Ragara policy towards satrapies represents an interesting contrast to their domestic activities.<br /> <br /> Jau Dei is a neat location with its unique qualities and manner of living, the complications this creates for the House, and the stakes it represents for them.<br /> <br /> So, Ragara: generally familiar with his whole thing of enormous ambition and hating his family, and the policy of his kill switch being tied only to one sister. Under other circumstances, I might be critical of the idea of giving an explanation for his longevity, but it <i>has</i> always been an elephant in the room, and if it\u2019s in the form of a neat and ominous Artifact\u2026 yeah, I\u2019m good with it. Mind, given some of the other references, I\u2019m surprised that Blood Zenith turned out to \u201cjust\u201d be a daiklave. I was always fine with the idea that Ragara was at peace with his retirement, but if the implication here is that he\u2019s clinging to life in hopes of the House\u2019s experiments bearing some fruits, I\u2019m okay with it. It would still technically leave him a bit on the sidelines.<br /> <br /> No word on how he founded the House, that will probably come up in The Realm.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Banoba\u2019s write-up here is short, but he <i>has</i> already gotten a lot of details, so this seems to serve as mostly wrapping things up with his private life. I note that some of Banoba\u2019s details have been changed, such as no longer having a public persona of being dull (which probably wouldn\u2019t fit with the new context of the House), and his relationship with Heral seems a lot more open and committed, so\u2026 good for him.<br /> <br /> Ahh, nice to finally see Szaya get her due. She\u2019s got a strong basis in the current construction of the House, which contrasts interestingly with her having a more national loyalty.<br /> <br /> And finally, Iuna strikes me as a Ragara who has a more altruistic take on their mission, if she\u2019s focused primarily on preserving culture, while still possibly being involved in something a bit sinister. That actually puts me in mind of another possible vulnerability of the House; that they might bite off more than they can chew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T06:36:15-07:00","id":1201231,"title":"","content":"Ragara is very neat now, went from a dull sort of mafia to something reminiscent of an occult cabal under the front of a legitimate corporation. Really liked it as well.<br /> <br /> You are definitely right that Blood Zenith is not so much introducing a new detail as filling a fairly gaping plothole. It also makes Ragara seem more personally threatening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T06:36:49-07:00","id":1201232,"title":"","content":"Oh, incidentally, I can't be the only one who envisions Mnemon and Ragara having a whole Gustavo Fring and Hector Salamanca thing going on, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T06:39:34-07:00","id":1201234,"title":"","content":"You are indeed not alone, they are almost radiating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T06:40:07-07:00","id":1201235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201231#post1201231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are definitely right that Blood Zenith is not so much introducing a new detail as filling a fairly gaping plothole.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's not what a plot hole is. A plot hole is a gap in the logical sequence of a story that makes the resolution of the narrative lazy or incomplete. The basis of Ragara's longevity was just an undisclosed detail.<br /> <br /> And hardly a completely inexplicable one, considering that even back then the setting contained a whole range of means for extension of life span.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:01:53-07:00","id":1201239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201235#post1201235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat's not what a plot hole is. A plot hole is a gap in the logical sequence of a story that makes the resolution of the narrative lazy or incomplete. The basis of Ragara's longevity was just an undisclosed detail.<br /> <br /> And hardly a completely inexplicable one, considering that even back then the setting contained a whole range of means for extension of life span.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty, well it was an absence that had bothered me and I was happy to see it filled with an interesting artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:39:11-07:00","id":1201251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200376#post1200376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooof, I\u2019m taken aback by that use of the word \u201csymbology\u201d; even leaving aside whether it\u2019s a real word or not, it would refer to the <i>study</i> of symbols, not the application of them. That really should be symbol<i>ism</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote the OED on &quot;symbology&quot;: &quot;The science or study of symbols; <i>loosely</i>, the use of symbols, or symbols collectively; symbolism.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:45:26-07:00","id":1201253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201251#post1201251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>loosely</i>, the use of symbols</div> </div> </div> </div>Loose lips sink ships.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T10:20:48-07:00","id":1201312,"title":"","content":"Am I missing something? What's all this talk about Blood Zenith? Is there a preview I didn't see?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T10:50:25-07:00","id":1201323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201312#post1201312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something? What's all this talk about Blood Zenith? Is there a preview I didn't see?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check the first update of the Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T11:27:26-07:00","id":1201333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201323#post1201323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check the first update of the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writeup of the Great Houses? I read that, was it in that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T11:36:52-07:00","id":1201341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201333#post1201333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writeup of the Great Houses? I read that, was it in that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Ragara writeup, where it's profiling Ragara himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T11:54:21-07:00","id":1201346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201341#post1201341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Ragara writeup, where it's profiling Ragara himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, now I feel like a dumbass. Read the writeup, didn't take note of the name. Carry on!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T12:16:23-07:00","id":1201356,"title":"","content":"You know, I've never really been a fan of the notion of Ragara as secretly badass, but damn it if I can't see something to work with in the idea of him drawing longevity from a daiklave. If nothing else, it could be an idea that getting it to up the juice to him so that he can fight at a higher level is something he would only do under the most desperate circumstances because it would rapidly eat away at the life he has left.<br /> <br /> \u200bI developed this image: Ragara sitting in a wheelchair, alone for the fact that his orderly has already gone out and fallen in his defence. He's sitting there, in a white robe yellowed with age, shrivelled and with lank, brittle hair hanging down from his pate, lifting himself slightly to look at the people confronting him. One ultimately moves forward to finally put him out of everybody's misery... and then a needle of blackened blood shoots from his left wrist, piercing the attacker in a vulnerable spot just enough to make them stagger back. <br /> <br /> \u200bRagara grasps the needle and drags it across the length of his body, pulling away lines of blood that follow the traces of his veins and arteries, shredding through his robe as they go, before congealing into the shape of a black and gold daiklave, with red accents. His left hand drops to the ornate ceramic head of his arm rest, crushing it to reveal a hearthstone, that he places into the daiklave.<br /> <br /> \u200bRagara stands, the remains of his robe dropping away to reveal a thin, wiry body covered in scar tissue, that rapidly blackens as though blood was congealing throughout his skin. He falls into a feral stance and lifts his weapon to rest upon his shoulder, while what hair he has straightens out and darkens a bit, and he raises his glance to look at those confronting him from beneath his brow.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, it's good enough for me.<br /> <br /> \u200b(For a less overwrought version, and what originally came to my mind, there's something as simple as him keeping the sword concealed within his wheelchair, and if he draws it to fight, it confers enough vitality to effectively swing it around, but not quite sufficient to fully restore mobility)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:15:06-07:00","id":1201379,"title":"","content":"The one thing that really kind of bugs me about the Ragara write up- they *really* need a plan for &quot;what happens when a bunch of Houses just default on their debts&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like- financial power is *great* in a stable system that helps enforce contracts and property rights. It's... less useful when your debtors could credibly just walk away. And it's not hard to imagine a bunch of defaults once the Civil War proper starts- hell, that's the sort of thing that could reasonably precipitate it.<br /> <br /> Pelleps Bob says &quot;Fuck you&quot; to the Ragara Alice who comes to repossess his ship.<br /> And then, Ragara Alice leaves and comes back with a brute squad to forcibly claim their lawful property.<br /> And then, Pelleps Bob and his Hearth say 'You and what army'<br /> And then...<br /> <br /> (Also, man, House Ragara must be salty as hell over not having Harborhead)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:39:33-07:00","id":1201392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201379#post1201379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing that really kind of bugs me about the Ragara write up- they *really* need a plan for &quot;what happens when a bunch of Houses just default on their debts&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like- financial power is *great* in a stable system that helps enforce contracts and property rights. It's... less useful when your debtors could credibly just walk away. And it's not hard to imagine a bunch of defaults once the Civil War proper starts- hell, that's the sort of thing that could reasonably precipitate it.<br /> <br /> Pelleps Bob says &quot;Fuck you&quot; to the Ragara Alice who comes to repossess his ship.<br /> And then, Ragara Alice leaves and comes back with a brute squad to forcibly claim their lawful property.<br /> And then, Pelleps Bob and his Hearth say 'You and what army'<br /> And then...</div> </div> </div> </div>... somewhere down the line \u2014 and probably not far down the line, since Peleps Bob is going to need money to pay his troops and maintain his ships now that there's a war on \u2014 Peleps Bob needs another loan and goes to a non-Ragara lender, only to find that the terms are harsher than even the most cutthroat Ragara loan. This is because defaults aren't unilateral. &quot;If you won't pay Ragara back,&quot; lenders think, &quot;how can I be sure you'll pay <i>me</i> back?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Ragara's fiscal vulnerabilities are discussed in the economics section of <i>The Realm</i>.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Certainly, a situation like you propose can happen anyway. But it's risky. Those who agree to default with you might back out, leaving you stranded and financially floundering. Or if Ragara ends the war in a stable position vis-a-vis the new regime, the defaults will cripple you (or, if you didn't survive, your next of kin) and your allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":1120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","user":"Eric Minton","date":". 03-30-2018, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:54:49-07:00","id":1201401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201392#post1201392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... somewhere down the line \u2014 and probably not far down the line, since Peleps Bob is going to need money to pay his troops and maintain his ships now that there's a war on \u2014 Peleps Bob needs another loan and goes to a non-Ragara lender, only to find that the terms are harsher than even the most cutthroat Ragara loan. This is because defaults aren't unilateral. &quot;If you won't pay Ragara back,&quot; lenders think, &quot;how can I be sure you'll pay <i>me</i> back?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Ragara's fiscal vulnerabilities are discussed in the economics section of <i>The Realm</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is sort of darkly hilarious that the Water-Aspect House cant keep themselves fiscally afloat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:54:49-07:00","id":1201402,"title":"","content":"So, Sesus. This is another one that, off the bat, makes a reversal of my previous perceptions of a House. I always saw Sesus as the crude, brutal military one (which\u2026 may or may not have actually been how they were written), and here they are now as the ones focused on information gathering and subtle warfare.<br /> <br /> Sooo, basically the whole House is being run with the principles of Sesus Rafara\u2019s childhood? Makes me wonder if she\u2019ll really be part of the setting anymore. Still, it\u2019s not a bad foundation to build on, and it gives them a neat shadowy cabal.<br /> <br /> Ahhh, my previous perception of Sesus is now their <i>public</i> image. Clever. It\u2019s also interesting to see them having a role for socialites that might give Nagezzar more context.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I suppose if they want to maintain such a spy network, it makes sense for even members of the House to not know who their leadership is\u2026 presumably beyond the matriarch. I presume that there\u2019s basic and reliable magic to mask their voices as well.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, the House economics seem a bit more nebulous than many of the others, let me see if I can parse it\u2026 so they\u2019ve got a combination of general financial opportunities in newly conquered territories, the benefit of commercial contacts and expertise brought in by close ties to Cynis, aaand subversion and sabotage of the conflicting activities of foreign powers, especially the Guild. Plus the basic idea of mercenary contracts.<br /> <br /> So their current army is the second largest, but they\u2019re not well-suited to direct confrontation. Seems to me that their best tactics are to use their agents to break down opposing forces beforehand, and then using their troops to mop up what\u2019s left. It\u2019s interesting that they\u2019re so close to Cynis that they\u2019re hoping for them to provide improved military expertise as well. Given the other House\u2019s description, I can imagine their respective policies have a kind of co-terminous evolution.<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s see, Sesus is generally disliked, but has strong blood that keeps a stream of marriages. Cynis is closely aligned because they compound that blood strength, and the methods and proclivities of the respective Houses complement each other well. The Mnemons are similarly connected by blood and their romantic streak, but it\u2019s counterbalanced by their piety and the matriarch\u2019s personal concern that they would oppose her royal ambitions. They had a rivalry with Tepet and took measures to help in their downfall, and has shifted that attention to Cathak. And they have the general hatred of Nellens due to the historical element.<br /> <br /> I wonder what it would take to get them to be more open about the existence of Iselsi. I\u2019ll be interested to see all of the details of that House\u2019s deal.<br /> <br /> Heh, I like to imagine in-character that the Empress or Sesus would have deliberately chosen some harsher territories to be their homeland, just for the ambience and character-building. It also wouldn\u2019t be a spy drama if it didn\u2019t have a fancy and ornate mountainside spa.<br /> <br /> Nothing to say about the satrapy besides it being an example of them undercutting Tepet in action, and what some of the long term political implications of their action.<br /> <br /> Nothing much in Sesus, besides another interesting example of what the Houses do with their founders\u2019 bodies. It\u2019s interesting that the matriarch exists separately from the Masked Council, and is overall somebody who lives at odds with their methods. It is kind of weird that she\u2019s married to her uncle, though.<br /> <br /> I suppose that it makes sense with all of that super-powered espionage, there would be at least one person who was so secretive that even the other spies hardly know anything about them. I suppose that, with her having an actual name, it makes sense that there was a point at which she lived publically, and then just\u2026 vanished. I wonder if it would be too passe to ever have a scenario where it turned out that the actual Sesus Agelin was killed by an outcaste early on, who managed to assume her identity.<br /> <br /> Ah, so Rafara <i>is</i>, and the childhood is standard but for the whole traumatic event of her mother brutally (and idiosyncratically) murdering everybody that she loved. So now her gimmick is focused primarily on being the spy who works for her own agenda and the benefit of the Realm as a whole.<br /> <br /> And it finishes off with somebody in the vein of the familiar old jerks, even if he\u2019s still got that side of spying and social popularity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:02:38-07:00","id":1201405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201392#post1201392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Ragara's fiscal vulnerabilities are discussed in the economics section of <i>The Realm</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201392#post1201392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Certainly, a situation like you propose can happen anyway. But it's risky. Those who agree to default with you might back out, leaving you stranded and financially floundering. Or if Ragara ends the war in a stable position vis-a-vis the new regime, the defaults will cripple you (or, if you didn't survive, your next of kin) and your allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm thinking of something more like a cascade of Houses defaulting- probably starting with an inciting incident like Peleps Bob. It's always good to remember, when you owe the bank $100, you have a problem, but when you owe the bank $1,000,000 the bank has a problem. Having basically everyone in their debt is nominally advantageous, but also means House Ragara very badly needs for no Civil War to actually break out, or else those investments will be up in smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:03:30-07:00","id":1201406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201401#post1201401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is sort of darkly hilarious that the Water-Aspect House cant keep themselves fiscally afloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wrote a blog post about that a couple years back, intending to publish it when <i>Dragon-Blooded</i> was finally in print. I'll see about digging it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:30:07-07:00","id":1201416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201405#post1201405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yay!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I guess I'm thinking of something more like a cascade of Houses defaulting- probably starting with an inciting incident like Peleps Bob. It's always good to remember, when you owe the bank $100, you have a problem, but when you owe the bank $1,000,000 the bank has a problem. Having basically everyone in their debt is nominally advantageous, but also means House Ragara very badly needs for no Civil War to actually break out, or else those investments will be up in smoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I imagine Ragara would want to avoid all out civil war just on the simple basis that almost everyone seems to have a reason to end them. Afterall if there isn't a House Ragara then House Ragara can't really call in their debts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:33:03-07:00","id":1201439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201405#post1201405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's always good to remember, when you owe the bank $100, you have a problem, but when you owe the bank $1,000,000 the bank has a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDoes it? I mean, that money is mostly imaginary anyway, and debt is the kind of thing that can make you money even beyond the debtor periodically repaying it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T16:50:12-07:00","id":1201466,"title":"","content":"Wait...<br /> <br /> \u200bShit, did I never actually say anything about the <i>details</i> of the Tepet preview, just praising its broad outline of the new principles in writing Great Houses?<br /> <br /> \u200bJesus, I know I read about them months back, but it would feel like giving that write-up short shrift if I didn't say anything about the neat specifics...<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll come back in a moment, and it will be shorter than the other responses are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T18:26:43-07:00","id":1201495,"title":"","content":"Okay, cliff notes version of reacting to Tepet:<br /> <br /> Considering how much people have always disliked the Shogunate feeling like a non-entity, it's a good choice to give one of the extant Houses a foundation in Shogunate culture. Likewise further distinguishing Tepet from Cathak with the greater emphasis on personal heroism than on unit tactics, as well as how that informs their cultural regard for non-martial pursuits.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that one of the military Houses based its wealth not on military adventures or mercenary work, but acting as consultants and instructors, especially with the novel manner in which this served the imperial agenda by creating stronger buffer states. It also creates a stronger basis for why the loss of the legions has damaged them so, and a particular irony for how a disproportionate number of survivors come from the mildly diversified House businesses.<br /> <br /> The warrior code as rite of adulthood really helps to add to the House's mystique, and as demonstrated by Niruz, represents a unique avenue for characters to express and legitimize their identity. I've already said how I appreciate some clarity on what the Vermilion Legion is and how it relates to Tepet.<br /> <br /> With most of the other Houses already seen, their relationships to Tepet have more significance to me, especially the rival military Houses. It's an interesting idea that Sesus saw their difficulties as an opportunity to expand their own prestige, while Cathak views its attempt to secure the House's final demise as a show of respect. There's also an interesting sense of contrast in how Tepet relates to more outlying Houses; to have assisted V'Neef in their early days, only to be snubbed when in need, and to have wealthy Nellens waiting in the wings to offer new opportunities. Same goes for how Iselsi sees Tepet as a possible avenue for their own vengeance.<br /> <br /> Not much is really said about Lord's Crossing itself, since it's mostly a basis for talking about how the House is led in the absence of a matriarch. While it's not stated, I suppose that the relationship with the spirits of the Vale of Reverie is another instance of something from their Shogunate roots. Medo as the remaining secure satrapy presents a few plot hooks for Tepet's possible resurgence; I'd say secession, but think that departing from the Realm altogether wouldn't be their style, even if Peleps can manage it.<br /> <br /> Can't think of much to say about the scions; Arada is about the same as he ever was, and Niruz has the benefit of being somebody who demonstrates the significance of warrior oaths. I feel as though Corino matters primarily because she's in a position where just about any story of rebuilding the legions would include her. Gadurin is probably the most interesting of the bunch, with that idea that applying Tepet ideals to his art has made him very popular, and he's now trying to capitalise on that by crafting narratives to draw more support to his House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T06:05:48-07:00","id":1201594,"title":"","content":"Okay, two Houses left.<br /> <br /> It was already the kind of thing stated before the book was even written much, but it\u2019s a great idea for the first thing to be said about House V\u2019neef is that it consists of a large number of adopted Exalted (although even I wasn\u2019t expecting them to number in the hundreds). It never really helped the House before to be super unclear on how large it actually was, especially when there were writers who seemed to run with the idea that it literally consisted solely of V\u2019neef\u2019s nuclear family, which was just\u2026 completely unbelievable as something that could make an impact in the Dynasty. I also think the notion that much of the family consists of rags to riches stories lends a strong sense of character to them, a basis why it would have a driving ideal even while very new, and more to set it apart from the other Houses. Plus a bit more significance to the much vaunted charisma of V\u2019neef herself. And it\u2019s fun to picture a bunch of elder Dragon Blooded regarding the youthful leader as their mother.<br /> <br /> Plus how it has them on their own imperialist drive, and frequently thumbing their nose at Peleps.<br /> <br /> I also like the tension between having militarily experienced daughters to give the House more power, and the matriarch being very cautious about actually sending them out.<br /> <br /> So their economics are about what they always were, wine, horse-breeding and the Merchant Fleet (even if the significance of the Fleet has been altered). Ahh, but the Merchant Fleet is now tied to the reduced tribute, which is the background for why they\u2019re focusing so much in the West (which is compounding their rivalry with Peleps). It\u2019s all a rich tapestry.<br /> <br /> So they\u2019ve got a small number of legions, their sole military forces owing to their youth, rendered disproportionately strong by the number of experienced outcastes in their ranks. And they\u2019ve retrofitted the Merchant Fleet into a naval force to compete with the Peleps Water Fleet. It\u2019s interesting, the sense of maximizing limited resources.<br /> <br /> So, V\u2019neef\u2019s ties to Tepet from their perspective: before the loss of the legions, they were seen as a firm ally and somebody to back for the throne, but since became a liability that they still can\u2019t afford to cut loose entirely, for political and personal reasons. Hmm, suddenly I\u2019m seeing a \u201cbreakup of the First Triumvirate\u201d situation, where V\u2019neef\u2019s husband dying creates an impetus to fully sever ties.<br /> <br /> Ragara doesn\u2019t like their financial security, so there are a few paths of conflict there.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve never really seen V\u2019neef\u2019s perspective on Mnemon, and it seems eminently practical to be deeply threatened by her. It\u2019s an interesting loop there; part of why Mnemon hates V\u2019neef is that others would see her on the Throne, creating a threat to V\u2019neef (and those she\u2019s taken responsibility for) that she feels she can only avert by taking the Throne.<br /> <br /> Heh, I\u2019m amused by the manner in which rivalry of Peleps can be a source of strength, by making them a draw for support from other Houses. Nellens is a rival on a different front, but could be a viable ally if it wasn\u2019t for their reputation, and Cynis is only good for continuing to buy stuff.<br /> <br /> Ahh, it\u2019s very clever of V\u2019neef to set up a haven for the magistracy. That\u2019s the kind of move that, properly capitalised on, could have a grand payoff.<br /> <br /> Hmm, considering how broken up the western quadrant of the Isle is, I wonder where exactly there is coast for Eagle\u2019s Launch to go; it sounds like it\u2019s taking up a position as a kind of Realm Casablanca.<br /> <br /> Oh wait, I initially misread Nansha as being part of Wavecrest, but I see now that it\u2019s just nearby. I like the way that it\u2019s dealing with the social turmoil of being a relatively new satrapy, particularly the distinctly imperialist issue of messing around with the local power dynamics so that they turn on one another.<br /> <br /> And finally some mention of Faxai, which should be expanded on interestingly in the Caul\u2019s chapter in The Realm. That\u2019s a nice mix of mystical and pragmatic needs for maintaining a presence in the city.<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s see, the partnership of V\u2019neef and Tepet Igan is at the heart of the house\u2026 I wonder how S\u2019thera became blind. I\u2019d usually have concerns over the notion of a Dynast woman being under a pressure of having children rather than following her own aspirations, but it\u2019s a singular instance, and the circumstances work.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think we\u2019ve ever seen a reformed, pacifist type among the Dragon Blooded, and I wonder if a story in which Dancing Boar becomes obligated by V\u2019neef to lead the troops that he\u2019s trained into battle would be too cruel.<br /> <br /> Oh Agayo, don\u2019t compromise your House\u2019s security from Ragara just for fancy demon ships.<br /> <br /> So yeah, they\u2019ve done a very good job of building upon the basic premise of V\u2019neef, which was always one of the stronger and more distinct in the Dynasty, and giving it a lot more heft and some interesting nuances. The explicit note on the size of the House in particular is liable to give it a lot more attention; I can\u2019t help but assume that, in the past, the implication that it was very small made it feel too proprietary to have any players come from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T12:36:30-07:00","id":1201681,"title":"","content":"And finally, there\u2019s the mysterious Iselsi.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s another one where the game used to be a bit unclear and even occasionally contradictory on the details of its status; was it dead, was it dying, was it on the ropes? If it\u2019s going to be anything, it might as well be a House that has truly fallen, to help distinguish it from the likes of Tepet.<br /> <br /> \u2026 Oh, the plot point of them being a shadow army remains, but\u2026 altered a bit. Like the Empress had a master plan, but the House still suffered indignities in the course of it being carried out\u2026<br /> Ah, I remember now; it <i>used</i> to be that the Empress was keeping them in secret, with the promise that in the future she would stage a big revival for them that would allow them to re-enter society in prestige, and her disappearance meant that the House was adrift with nobody to bring them in from the cold. Now it\u2019s a case of the loss of the Empress taking the leash off of them, that they\u2019re ready to capitalise on to take vengeance. Okay, I get it. Cool.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that\u2019s some neat imagery for initiation into the Vendetta. Real Masonic kind of deal there. I suppose that the pride of a Great House is not the kind of thing that can sit easily when it\u2019s driven underground.<br /> <br /> The details of them being given new identities around the Threshold and entering the Order en masse are familiar (although the former has the new twist of being granted training in techniques unfamiliar to the Dynasty), but I think the notion of them being widely attached around the other Houses waiting for a day of reckoning is new. That\u2019s a fun take on that kind of long-haul conspiracy, deep cover agent story, where there are not only Iselsi who might be emotionally compromised, but those who fear that it will happen to them.<br /> <br /> Heh, I love the idea that the House has built up a Keyser Soze kind of figure in its ranks as a false target for enemies to pursue, while actually being highly decentralized. It provides a lot of verisimilitude for them being able to sustain their organization. That and how they\u2019ve only been doing it a relatively short while.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the distribution of Iselsi\u2019s resources, and the legal and administrative avenues for permits to it, is another kind of thing that Bureaucracy could work with, a game of obscuring and uncovering all of the details.<br /> <br /> Well, coming at the end as it does, most of Iselsi\u2019s relationships have already been expounded upon, but it does have the new detail of how any possible alliance with Tepet would be seen as a temporary measure before finishing the final House off. The last new thing is this idea that the infiltration of the Immaculate Order is used heavily as a basis for cultivating possible alliances with gods.<br /> <br /> I wonder what it\u2019s like to be an Iselsi living on the mattresses. The Last Little Sapling is a nice addition, as I do often like a good set of code exchanges in plain sight.<br /> <br /> Now, what it is about the inhabitants of Ditola Village that makes them amenable to being trained like that, and taking part in that attack when it comes. Is it just hatred of House Mnemon?<br /> <br /> So, if Iselsi was an economic expert, I wonder if that meant that the House was initially more deeply connected to the Thousand Scales, and drifted to intelligence and espionage after she died.<br /> Awww, poor Dileko, going to have to eventually kill all of his friends. And jeez Ragara, how much of a dick do you have to be that even as an old man dining with a devout Immaculate, she thinks it would improve the Realm to murder you? Probably comes to the same result for the House anyway.<br /> <br /> Oh dear, they\u2019ve got an agent who went off training in the Southeast. That can\u2019t end well, all the weird shit that they\u2019ve got down there.<br /> <br /> Ohh, and finally a mysterious old man of uncertain loyalties, who took part in distributing the military in the absence of the Scarlet Empress. That sounds like the kind of fellow that one would want to meet in a game.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand it turns out that this isn\u2019t quite the end; one last, short entry on Cadet Houses. I\u2019ll get on to that promptly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T13:08:21-07:00","id":1201685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200376#post1200376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooof, I\u2019m taken aback by that use of the word \u201csymbology\u201d; even leaving aside whether it\u2019s a real word or not, it would refer to the <i>study</i> of symbols, not the application of them. That really should be symbol<i>ism</i>. As to the substance of their symbolism\u2026 the idea that House colours are out of fashion, and thus carry a particular statement, is an interesting dimension to add to House culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a real word, it refers to the study or use of symbols.<br /> <br /> Symbolism refers to the meaning of those symbols. They're discussing the symbols themselves and what they <i>look like</i>, symbology is the correct term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T14:13:03-07:00","id":1201698,"title":"","content":"Oh I know, good point. That's wonderful news! You and me both pal.<br /> <br /> \u200bGod, the acoustics in here are <i>fantastic</i>. <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266aTomorrow, tomorrow, I love you tomorrow, you're only a day-\u266a</span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T15:43:49-07:00","id":1201724,"title":"","content":"To finish off, the Cadet Houses: provincial Dragon Blooded families that didn\u2019t see an advantage in relocating to the Blessed Isle, who were still seen as valuable to tie to the Dynasty with marriage, and occasional fruitful unions between Dynasts and mortal royalty.<br /> <br /> Oh, a historical event relating to the subject of remaining Shogunate gentes. That\u2019s a good call right there. The question of lingering remnants of the Shogunate on the Blessed Isle, now <i>that</i> was a bit of a plot hole, so it\u2019s useful to address it in its own right at the same time as it adds another layer to Cadet Houses.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ve got the privileges of Dynasts individually, but lack the benefits of the large, corporate structure that the Great Houses have through their hundreds of Exalted, vast numbers of mortal scions, and probably things like imperial territories and remits; I imagine that it\u2019s hard to make the kind of money that a Great House has when you aren\u2019t given a monopoly (or close) on a lucrative industry, or a portion of imperial tribute.<br /> <br /> Or at least not directly; it seems that the Empress would subtly send them opportunities to keep them afloat, as part of a whole system of keeping a semi-independent and rival power to counterbalance Great Houses in the Threshold. At times like this, it\u2019s worth me remembering that the Blessed Isle is large, developed and lucrative enough that a large amount of their business could take place exclusively there.<br /> <br /> House Ferem is back, the previously existing cadet. Not much change there, except for having been affected by Bagrash Kol\u2019s empire, and having cousin house\u2019s in neighbouring regions. House Desai lives in proximity to Jiara, having lived under the government of others so that they could focus on art and luxury, and feeling the pressure of expectation that they join the Wyld Hunt. Burano and Ophris of Prasad are technically counter as cadet houses, but having been actual Great Houses that seceded from the Dynasty and established their own dominion, their status and relationship stands as its own, distinct thing. Finally there\u2019s Yueh, far down the Southern coast, with some rather unfortunate ties to Houses such as Tepet and V\u2019neef; also, if I\u2019m reading this correctly, have an interesting position in which their monarchy was overthrown, but they\u2019re still strong participants in the successor government.<br /> <br /> The cadet houses are obviously a bit of a footnote, but they get the point across, and add some diverse personalities to the margins of the Scarlet Dynasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T16:10:40-07:00","id":1201736,"title":"","content":"All right, so since there's an interim before we get the next couple of chapters, my final assessment of Chapter Two:<br /> <br /> \u200bI've often found one of the interesting things given about the Great Houses to be in the Second Edition corebook, that little sidebar describing them and their different objectives and priorities in the Realm's future, that nothing else ever seemed to pick up upon. If a revised write-up of the Scarlet Dynasty had taken the principle of that to heart, that alone would have been enough to satisfy me.<br /> <br /> \u200bThese write-ups do that, but they have so much more. The Houses feel like something much bigger than they ever used to be, expanding from extended aristocratic families to sprawling, corporate tribal bodies, with everything that implies. Unique cultures and lifestyles, traditional territories in which they have left their mark and industries that they have made their own, a deep sense of history. They feel alive and breathing in a way that they never have before, that very few other things in the game ever have. The sheer detail of them, from their spirituality and high ideals, to their pragmatic material concerns, and the manner in which they intersect and clash from one another gives so many possibilities for character and storyline.<br /> <br /> \u200bMore than ever before, they feel as though they have achievements in the past, and a place in the setting's future, which really firms up the significance and credibility of the Dragon Blooded. And those aspects are guided so much by how they want concrete <i>things</i>, that provide context and direction to their actions, and that arise logically from the backgrounds they've been given. Not meaning it as a criticism, but in the past, I would have generally viewed the Houses as slight variations on a general desire for maintaining their luxurious lifestyles; any notion of them valuing power over money stymied by the question of what they would even use power for. This Edition gives multiple answers to that question, and it makes the motivation of their characters, and the bodies as a whole, much richer.<br /> <br /> \u200bSprinkle all of that with many of the Houses being faced with complex situations, numerous priorities and objectives and limited resources, without easy answers to trouble their characters with, and meaningfully guide their politics.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand effectively redeeming the weaker, less interesting Houses of yesteryear.<br /> <br /> \u200bAll with only about five pages each, no particular area of focus ever needing to outstay its welcome with unnecessary detail.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's an excellent job. That this is only a quarter of a way through the book... heh, it's more than I deserve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T07:06:35-07:00","id":1201906,"title":"","content":"I, too, have enjoyed the first preview. I really got a much better sense of the Great Houses and how to utilise them in the 2e book.<br /> <br /> However, one thing that struck me is, what about the Roseblack? She was mentioned in the Tepet section (though not as a Scion of Note?), and while the bit about her made her out as a competent general, it didn\u2019t mention her shot at the Scarlet Throne. In 2e, it was essentially her or Mnemon that the race came down to. Is she no longer a serious competitor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-01-2018, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T07:38:05-07:00","id":1201913,"title":"","content":"I was kind of glad for that, tbh. If the Roseblack's supposed to be the outside bet, coming in when no one expects her, a charismatic young officer... they really went on about her too much in 2e.<br /> Also, she kind of fits a role that can easily be one of PCs, whereas Mnemon does not.<br /> As the assumed competitors for PCs, I think the more institutional characters like the Empress's own daughters make more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-01-2018, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T07:57:21-07:00","id":1201917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201439#post1201439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bDoes it? I mean, that money is mostly imaginary anyway, and debt is the kind of thing that can make you money even beyond the debtor periodically repaying it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's an expression, capturing the real idea that if you hold a sufficient amount of debt then your creditors cannot risk you defaulting lest you bring ruin upon them as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T08:20:43-07:00","id":1201923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201917#post1201917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's an expression, capturing the real idea that if you hold a sufficient amount of debt then your creditors cannot risk you defaulting lest you bring ruin upon them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think my point addresses some of the manners in which that risk can be mitigated, whether it be trading with the debt as a financial instrument or collateral, or futures based on basically getting people to gamble on whether or not the debt will be repaid, not to mention forms of insurance that can compensate you in the event of a debtor folding.<br /> <br /> Also the possibility of still being able to sell a defaulted debt on to somebody else, to at least recoup some of your losses.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot to mention how things like interest rates can be calibrated in such a manner that, after a long enough amount of time (which can be shorter than one might think), the debtor defaulting doesn't really matter, because they've already paid back the actual value of their loan several times over, even if they haven't yet failed to repay their debt.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, I wouldn't think it's unlikely that House Ragara doesn't frequently engage in deals where they'll ultimately need to eat a loss; what business doesn't? I would suspect that they've got enough going on all over to prevent any reasonably small number of losses from being a disaster, that even if the House as a whole ends a year with the accounts in the red that they'll have enough assets and plans for the future, and that it helps that a lot of it is technically taking a back seat to their occult research anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T09:01:48-07:00","id":1201930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201917#post1201917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's an expression, capturing the real idea that if you hold a sufficient amount of debt then your creditors cannot risk you defaulting lest you bring ruin upon them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this quote is how it applies in practice. The reason for it in the real world is because banks typically ride the line between solvency/not being solvent as a matter of course. However i am not sure how true that was in the historical context. That is, how accurate was that statement in less risk-accepting systems? For example even in relatively modern times, when several Latin American countries defaulted in their debt to the IMF etc, they did not bring about the financial ruin of their creditor nations/institutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T10:29:00-07:00","id":1201961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201906#post1201906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is she no longer a serious competitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I feel as though she has a lot less need to be, and makes more sense as somebody focused on the more sophisticated milieu of the current House Tepet.<br /> <br /> \u200bI have a sense that Ejava as she was back then was a contender primarily as a kind of expy for Julius Caesar, which was all well and good at the time, but the setting and the Scarlet Dynasty has kind of moved beyond that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T13:59:22-07:00","id":1202013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201906#post1201906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, too, have enjoyed the first preview. I really got a much better sense of the Great Houses and how to utilise them in the 2e book.<br /> <br /> However, one thing that struck me is, what about the Roseblack? She was mentioned in the Tepet section (though not as a Scion of Note?), and while the bit about her made her out as a competent general, it didn\u2019t mention her shot at the Scarlet Throne. In 2e, it was essentially her or Mnemon that the race came down to. Is she no longer a serious competitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Mnemon's ambitions in that direction only get one line in her entry.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, I beleive it was mentioned, back when House Tepet was previewed, that T.Ejava doesn't get a Scion's entry because she has a character write up elsewhere.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd expect the whole &quot;race for the thrown&quot; who's who, to be detailed more in The Realm than in the Dragon-blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-01-2018, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:04:06-07:00","id":1202014,"title":"","content":"Tepet Ejava makes a great deal of sense as a candidate for the throne in a situation where there's been open war for a couple of years, and the economy has been fucked, and a lot of the clever plans and lofty ambitions of the houses going <i>into</i> the war have just shattered against the reality of the situation, and a few matriarchs have fallen to assassination, and hey, look, here's this competent, charismatic general who's endured and prospered and proven herself valuable in a bunch of situations and whose apparent personal integrity has impressed a lot of folks who want, more than anything, for the war to end, and she's starting to look like the one who can do that.<br /> <br /> She makes very little sense as a candidate before the war's started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:05:33-07:00","id":1202015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202013#post1202013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Mnemon's ambitions in that direction only get one line.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, I beleive it was mentioned, back when House Tepet was previewed, that T.Ejava doesn't get a Scion's entry because she has a character write up elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It's just that the House articles had been pretty good at pointing out and making a very practical reference sheet over both old and new pretenders to the throne, and I was really expecting, y'know, the second most likely candidate in 2e to have it at least mentioned. I'm fine with her character changing between editions, as I agree with The Wizard of Oz that she's sort of filling a PC role, but it just sort of confused me. Like, was I missing something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:28:54-07:00","id":1202021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202015#post1202015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, was I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like it? Look at Lea's post before yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:55:14-07:00","id":1202026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201392#post1201392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... somewhere down the line \u2014 and probably not far down the line, since Peleps Bob is going to need money to pay his troops and maintain his ships now that there's a war on \u2014 Peleps Bob needs another loan and goes to a non-Ragara lender, only to find that the terms are harsher than even the most cutthroat Ragara loan. This is because defaults aren't unilateral. &quot;If you won't pay Ragara back,&quot; lenders think, &quot;how can I be sure you'll pay <i>me</i> back?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, &quot;I'm not paying Ragara, oh Guildsman, because their House legions are fighting my House's legions&quot; is something any businessman with the sense to stay out of the warlord game can understand.<br /> <br /> So the Scylla of the civil war is that Ragara gets involved in the fighting, sees a whole bunch of Houses array against it in part because arraying against it gives them a good excuse to repudiate their debts, and the House winds up (in the worst case) destroyed. The Charybdis is that Ragara stays out of the fighting, the victorious side owes House Ragara a lot of money while resenting them for sitting out of the bleeding, and (in the worst case) the firmly-established new Empress liquidates the debts of her supporters by liquidating House Ragara.<br /> <br /> And, of course, whatever Ragara is doing with the occult would seem to be the insurance policy in case their navigation falters and their course slips too close to either side in the passage through the Realm civil war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:17:26-07:00","id":1202080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201356#post1201356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've never really been a fan of the notion of Ragara as secretly badass, but damn it if I can't see something to work with in the idea of him drawing longevity from a daiklave. If nothing else, it could be an idea that getting it to up the juice to him so that he can fight at a higher level is something he would only do under the most desperate circumstances because it would rapidly eat away at the life he has left.<br /> <br /> \u200bI developed this image: Ragara sitting in a wheelchair, alone for the fact that his orderly has already gone out and fallen in his defence. He's sitting there, in a white robe yellowed with age, shrivelled and with lank, brittle hair hanging down from his pate, lifting himself slightly to look at the people confronting him. One ultimately moves forward to finally put him out of everybody's misery... and then a needle of blackened blood shoots from his left wrist, piercing the attacker in a vulnerable spot just enough to make them stagger back. <br /> <br /> \u200bRagara grasps the needle and drags it across the length of his body, pulling away lines of blood that follow the traces of his veins and arteries, shredding through his robe as they go, before congealing into the shape of a black and gold daiklave, with red accents. His left hand drops to the ornate ceramic head of his arm rest, crushing it to reveal a hearthstone, that he places into the daiklave.<br /> <br /> \u200bRagara stands, the remains of his robe dropping away to reveal a thin, wiry body covered in scar tissue, that rapidly blackens as though blood was congealing throughout his skin. He falls into a feral stance and lifts his weapon to rest upon his shoulder, while what hair he has straightens out and darkens a bit, and he raises his glance to look at those confronting him from beneath his brow.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, it's good enough for me.<br /> <br /> \u200b(For a less overwrought version, and what originally came to my mind, there's something as simple as him keeping the sword concealed within his wheelchair, and if he draws it to fight, it confers enough vitality to effectively swing it around, but not quite sufficient to fully restore mobility)</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:26:21-07:00","id":1202085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202080#post1202080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Posts like that one drive me to check out his recent posts, just to make sure I didn't miss anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:59:47-07:00","id":1202098,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As a visual reference, my image of Ragara is King Bumi crossed with David Lo Pan crossed with the Old Monk from Demon's Souls when he's in the chair, and when he pulls Blood Zenith from out of himself he goes to Bumi crossed with Mishima Heihachi crossed with Slave Knight Gael (except very thin, as opposed to those rather bulky characters).</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:26:15-07:00","id":1202205,"title":"","content":"Something that I only just considered about the Houses having descriptions of their military forces:<br /> <br /> \u200bQuite apart from how it's very beneficial to lay that kind of thing out in reasonable detail if a war is supposed to be in their future, it's a very solid change for them to actually have the number of legions divided differently in accordance with need and political bargaining, as opposed to the old system of everybody getting exactly two each (with... probably some adjustment for Nellens, Tepet and Iselsi, that I can't quite remember because it was probably vague). I'll admit, the notion that they divided the legions evenly always struck me as rather odd, as well as leaving them with forces that seemed a bit flimsy for what they intended to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T08:47:29-07:00","id":1202231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202205#post1202205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, the notion that they divided the legions evenly always struck me as rather odd</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T08:51:26-07:00","id":1202234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202231#post1202231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you did there.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bEntirely coincidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T13:08:48-07:00","id":1202297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202205#post1202205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that I only just considered about the Houses having descriptions of their military forces:<br /> <br /> \u200bQuite apart from how it's very beneficial to lay that kind of thing out in reasonable detail if a war is supposed to be in their future, it's a very solid change for them to actually have the number of legions divided differently in accordance with need and political bargaining, as opposed to the old system of everybody getting exactly two each (with... probably some adjustment for Nellens, Tepet and Iselsi, that I can't quite remember because it was probably vague). I'll admit, the notion that they divided the legions evenly always struck me as rather odd, as well as leaving them with forces that seemed a bit flimsy for what they intended to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The legions were not divided evenly two to each House in previous editions, though you get a different distribution depending on which pieces of contradictory information you choose for interpretation (whether the total count is 30 or 31 is contested between editions!). I found <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/archive/index.php/t-254942.html\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a> compiling info from late 1E and early 2E that gives a fairly wide spread between the Houses even back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T13:47:57-07:00","id":1202302,"title":"","content":"What was said in the First Edition core, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T14:01:28-07:00","id":1202303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202302#post1202302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was said in the First Edition core, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Houses Cathak and Sesus each maintain five legions, with the other nine houses funding the other 20 legions.&quot; page 46 of Exalted First Edition, &quot;The Legions&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:01:43-07:00","id":1202588,"title":"","content":"All right, time to cover chapter three, Life in the Scarlet Dynasty.<br /> <br /> Our opening fiction features Sesus Eshevur (obviously our only signature who is actually <i>part</i> of the Scarlet Dynasty proper), visiting his lover as he contemplates his tumultuous marriage to an unExalted Dynast. What\u2019s interesting here is that even though she\u2019s the mortal, and the idea that such marriage (and the implication of having borne Exalted children) is a necessary elevation of her status, that some of the gender stereotypes still seem to hold true; his philandering seen as an insult to her, as he plays into the image of being a disobedient playboy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, he\u2019s recounting a bit of the values that his mother taught him, contemplating whether or not his life should be elevated above those of mortals, and recounting his relationship to his Hearth (which he seems to feel unworthy of). Ah, that\u2019s interesting, a sense of anxiety over his gender. I presume that by \u201cmother\u2019s only son\u201d he means that he has sisters.<br /> <br /> Aaaand that\u2019s about it, before he\u2019s off for a tryst.<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s an interesting fiction to introduce the Dynasty; it doesn\u2019t shy away from the privileges, and the values and skills that they would be raised with, while also giving insight into some unique aspects of their culture and the issues that might produce in somebody.<br /> <br /> Now, let\u2019s see how the other half lives.<br /> <br /> You know, I\u2019m kind of glad that there\u2019s no preamble giving an overview of them. We\u2019ve really already gotten that anyway in the first couple of chapters, so I approve of diving straight into each phase of their life. So, what is the childhood of a Dynast like?<br /> <br /> It opens up with the familiar nigh-Victorian attitude to child-rearing, albeit with a more direct focus on it being the responsibility of the mother, and not entirely against the idea of loving one\u2019s child; it just shouldn\u2019t get in the way of raising them to be Princes of the Earth. Specifically also how they\u2019re not against being barely involved, so much as one carefully manages their rearing and education.<br /> <br /> Now that\u2019s an interesting take on the idea that early life is spent primarily in the presence of servants; one is being conditioned from a very early age to command, and see oneself as higher in status. I\u2019m guessing that primary school is the first time one starts to be acclimatised to an environment of peers. Also works well with the idea that one is still subject to corrections if one\u2019s childhood authority should be misused.<br /> <br /> Ahh, I like the idea of breaking down and detailing the specific roles of one\u2019s childhood servants. So they\u2019ve got the nanny, the initial provider and possible first source of affection, protected against the possibility of a cruel charge by how this would damage the family\u2019s reputation. The tutors, who oversee their early play activities and introduce them to the first stage of education, with a focus on the physical and probably basic ideas of history, culture and the layout of the Dynasty (with an erroneously repeated line). And the slaves, who provide early playmates and a class environment for their initial instruction (Dragons help the Dynastic child who is initially outperformed by the slaves, although their prospects can\u2019t be good either), who can grow up alongside them and sometimes be valued servants. With a final note on the exceptional circumstances in which one has a sibling of the same age, as well as how children from family friends are also gradually introduced (so the peer environment comes shortly before attending school), and regular encounters with actual Exalted, to help instil their sense of awe.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an interesting picture of the Dynast childhood, with a bit more texture than it used to have. It\u2019s not just a harsh educational regimen, there\u2019s also the earliest stage of instilling their values and laying the groundwork to define their place in the world.<br /> <br /> Huh, a sidebar on the subject of Dynast orphans; I don\u2019t think I\u2019d ever really considered those to be a thing before. So in their value system, it\u2019s generally viewed that one needs a mother to oversee their early life, even if the father is still alive, so one without a mother will generally be taken in by somebody else in the House. There\u2019s a value there for couples that can\u2019t have children of their own for any reason, which I suspect can resolve the complication of dissolved marriages (if those are still around). In any case, so long as one has parents to arrange the nannies, tutors and slaves, their childhood is about the same.<br /> <br /> We get an overview of education, how it\u2019s funded by the Empress and donations from applying parents, and what its aims are, and a summary of the four secondary schools. Tutors are given a more detailed explanation; it starts within the first couple of years, and they\u2019re selected by the House matriarch, with the child\u2019s own mother in consultation. Generally patricians, although it\u2019s sometimes how newly graduated Exalted spend their sabbaticals. As well as the basics, different Houses have their own priorities, such as appreciation for fine art and music and recognising good lackeys in Cynis, or more specific fields such as mathematics and history for Mnemon (particularly being taught about the life <i>of</i> Mnemon). Oh, I like this particular detail of them all being taught basic medicine and how to recognize poisons; I wonder if that\u2019s a case of a later life skill that can\u2019t be taught early enough, being better safe and sorry, or if enemies of a House actually do regularly attempt to poison the children. Actually, with the two details together, I\u2019m given to wonder how many Dynastic children have been required to give life-saving first aid to any of their school mates or friends.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad for this section; a lot of these things were still <i>present</i> in the prior books, but in a more vague and generic manner, that meant that they evidently stuck less. A firm focus, with examples, this is a case in which clarity and detail is to the benefit of the material.<br /> <br /> The motivation of their tutoring is laid out, with a final note of how it\u2019s regularly tested in public, as well as a sidebar about occasionally, a child with a special future in mind (or possibly more personal motives) is kept home for specialized education throughout the primary, or even secondary level.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s primary school, with the notion of class environment being not just about competing against peers, but for the actual attention of teachers, which can be a stress to new students. The staff of schools will be used to dealing with even young Dragon Blooded, and function to ensure that they won\u2019t be cowed (probably because it would interfere in their education; it\u2019s probably doing no nine-year old any favours if they go around threatening their teachers with elemental bolts, and I imagine that their mothers make that very clear to them). Childhood friendships (or other relationships; I imagine that there are more than a few cases of somebody lower on the totem pole suddenly rising above with Exaltation) have a hard time surviving the pressure of their environment, not just to excel, but as every year brings them closer to the deadline for being Chosen, with the higher years of high school in particular starting to fixate on superstitions and rituals in the hopes of becoming Exalted. The methods are technically futile, but have credibility from being stressful and dangerous enough to occasionally trigger the power in those who already had the potential, which is a fun idea about how such things continue and compound. To actually be Exalted is to have a pall of separation fall between oneself and the mortal student body.<br /> <br /> On the note describing the quality of the schools themselves, I like the note on how for some schools and some families, it actually represents a step down in one\u2019s familiar standard of living, while still being viewed as necessary as a means of seeing life outside of the manse one was born in. It\u2019s also got to be a singularly stressful experience to be part of the staff of an underfunded school, when one of the patrician children Exalts; possibly, the Great House that will adopt them make a point of paying for the repair of any damages.<br /> <br /> The curriculum is government mandated, with an eye to ensuring uniformity and conformity, and has a requirement for an advanced political or religious course. Makes sense; either one probably is probably intrinsic to the Dynastic place in the world, so they\u2019d want to ensure that everybody comes through with related skills and indoctrination. And there are the specialty schools, with additional advanced courses to make them more attractive to a particular kind of parent. I wonder about how possible patronage for that interacts with Dynastic policies; would Mnemon fund an architectural school for the sake of giving her own scions an early start in the family business, or be against it as a system that might educate competitors? I also like the idea of field trips to the Threshold by schools specializing in the government of satrapies; that must be a stressful time for parents, and a golden opportunity for the likes of the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s a breakdown of the typical school day, with the classics after breakfast, specialty practical subjects in the afternoon, and metaphyics and the world in the evening. The merits of study past lights out varies depending on how it affects performance. There\u2019s also a sidebar on what to do with students who show themselves incapable of aligning with the disciplined school life, sent off to the industrial schools of the House of Ancient Stone and Palace of the Tamed Storm. I like the comment on how the child being killed by the schools harsh discipline is an undesirable outcome, but a risk worth taking if one has demonstrated themselves to be uncontrollable by the other schools (which may still include the odd individual with a learning disability or tendency to question imperial dogma, unfortunately).<br /> <br /> Secondary school is definitely going to be a lengthy section, what with each institution being detailed, so I\u2019ll return to that in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:17:18-07:00","id":1202619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202588#post1202588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AHuh, a sidebar on the subject of Dynast orphans; I don\u2019t think I\u2019d ever really considered those to be a thing before. So in their value system, it\u2019s generally viewed that one needs a mother to oversee their early life, even if the father is still alive, so one without a mother will generally be taken in by somebody else in the House.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about needing a mother, but about the mother's house retaining control of the children. (Where the mother was a patrician or a member of the father's house, the children could be expected to stay with the father; unfortunately, I didn't think to specify that during development.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:18:52-07:00","id":1202701,"title":"","content":"All right, secondary schools. They\u2019re elective, but the students themselves don\u2019t really get a say in it, instead being another area managed by their mother and matriarch, based on extensive reports on the entirety of the child\u2019s life and the needs for the House and the Dynasty (and maybe the child, if it comes to that). Admission is not automatic, but influenced by making sure that the prospective stands out, and offering generous donations.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a clarification on how each of the schools has a comprehensive curriculum to ensure that the graduates are well-rounded in the pursuit of the careers associated with the more specialized program of each school, so that\u2019s good to diversify characters and ensure that nobody needs to have major shortcomings.<br /> <br /> Secondary school also contrasts with primary on account of how everybody is going to be on a more even footing, so it\u2019s where they\u2019ll form their peer groups and reciprocal friendships, creating the skeleton of Dynastic decision-making.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, anything interesting in the sidebar on mortal attendees\u2026 requires them to excel and have access to wealth and influence even before admittance, at which point they face the new pressure of needing to keep up with the Exalted. Oy, the idea that washing out leaves one being labelled as arrogant for ever having thought they could try, that\u2019s rough. But the rewards for making it through seem as though they would be great.<br /> <br /> So, if it takes particular benefits to be admitted, what becomes from those who can\u2019t (or don\u2019t wish to) get in? There\u2019s a number of lesser secondary schools now, mostly for instructing people directly towards various branches of Realm service, several of which operate around the Spiral Academy (I like that \u201cOuter Coil\u201d name). This answers the question of what kind of higher education the mortals from primary school generally go on to; Exalted who attend get to be big fish in small ponds for a little while, but will be disadvantaged afterwards by lesser qualifications and lack of networking. Oh, but they\u2019ll have the benefit of connections among patricians and the like, which certainly have their place in Dynast business.<br /> <br /> Finally, some satrapies (particularly home to cadet houses) have a few secondary schools of their own, and there\u2019s the brutal regime of Pasiap\u2019s Stair for those outcastes who take the coin. Pasiap\u2019s Stair seems a bit more standardised now, if Dragon Blooded will generally Exalt around their teens, even when more thin-blooded. It says that Dynasts might enrol if they want to test their stamina, but I wonder if doing so represents a certain break from your mother and matriarch.<br /> <br /> Now, the schools themselves. First, the Cloister of Wisdom. Let\u2019s see, the centre of their curriculum has been made meditation and mastery of their own Essence, surrounded by subjects that I would deem a general education rooted in Immaculate ethics. I think the layout of the school is about the same as it ever was, monastic structure, ascetic lifestyle for the students (including many outcastes preparing for life in the Order), instruction by the monks. I like the lengthy description of how the faculty break in new students and deal with them if they get unruly. It says that exposure to the prowess of instructors is desirable for the martial arts that it yields, but I can also readily image a matriarch looking at somebody who is a bit too heady from a recent Exaltation and thinks that they need the monks to offer some discipline.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s a note on the graduates, with the intriguing notion that one of the benefits of the mindset cultivated by the time spent there gives them serenity and unobtrusiveness, being another reason to send students to that school specifically. Conversely, the Order benefits from running such a school by putting out sympathetic Dynasts who can be relied on to keep them informed.<br /> Next is the Heptagram, something that I\u2019ve been wondering about with the changes to how sorcery works. The introduction notes familiar points such as the school being based on the Isle of Voices and the complicated attitude that the Dynasty has towards sorcery. There\u2019s an emphasis on how small the school is by how it only has a single lecture hall, and the idea of designated seating gives me a sense of there being a certain hierarchy to how they\u2019re arranged (although I might not be thinking that through). Oh, the description of the more autodidactic instruction here reminds me of how the Cloister seems to have been changed up a bit, but I\u2019ll come back to that. The important thing is that this seems to be where alternate initiations come in; they\u2019re taught the basic principles, and then determine their personal path to true sorcery, under advisement from the teachers. They have big lectures for the entire student body to attend, and specific courses come up at the leisure of the master sorcerer. They otherwise have large amounts of material and infrastructure with which to study and experiment in their own right.<br /> <br /> It may just be me, but several details of this are putting me in mind of the college of Byrgenwerth from Bloodborne. \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> It\u2019s still a difficult course on account of how hard it can be to master sorcery and the limited attention of the instructors, and there\u2019s a reference to how not everybody who attends can even cut it for initiation. Between that and how there\u2019s always liable to be a few who die, well, it\u2019s definitely still far from the Hogwarts that many people would want it to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here\u2019s the sidebar laying out the Realm perspective on sorcery; generally off-putting due to its mysteries, the powers that it affords, and association with demons. Conversely, they\u2019re still useful and can demand high prices for their services. The net result is lonely spellbinders who get visited only for as long as it takes to secure the use of their powers.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, I\u2019ve got another perspective on Mnemon; where whatever went on behind her own initiation in the adverse environment of her youth, the manner in which she was regarded afterwards contributed to her social coldness and made it that much harder to establish herself. With that perspective, I could see her capacity to build such a powerful House as even more of an achievement.<br /> <br /> Err, the House of Bells, the Realm\u2019s premier military academy (something that stands out more now that there are definitively other secondary schools for officer training). Historically more comprehensible but less interesting than the prior two, so let\u2019s see what it\u2019s got now. For one thing, it\u2019s <i>big</i>, to accommodate the resources for military exercises (including a bay for naval training), as well as its own villages for accommodation and recreation, in addition to urban combat training. Now, it\u2019s interesting that in comparison to the usual fantasy take on military training from hell, the House of Bells has an emphasis on safety (such as a preference for students to wash out over staying and being killed), and especially on the idea that camaraderie should help somebody who isn\u2019t entirely up for it on their own to make it through the program. It makes sense, really, considering the communal nature of the Dragon Blooded, and how they might fight together. I suspect that more than a few training fangs become Sworn Kinships in the course of time. There are probably some interesting story hooks in the idea of a new tension between veteran House of Bells graduates and dropouts that the new policy in the legions makes room for.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ve got their intense early-morning physical training, a variety of military academic disciplines (interestingly including ethics), and specialized training under veteran Exalted (one of which gives the impression that the Realm approach to cavalry has been adjusted significantly; I\u2019ve actually been wondering myself if their approach to archery is also different, if they\u2019re engaged in more active warfare). Aaand they only get a few hours a day of sleep. Field exercises still include that unfortunate practice of hunting condemned criminals. And they\u2019ll often name their Hearths for the squads that they trained in.<br /> <br /> The House of Bells still isn\u2019t quite as colourful as the others, but it\u2019s a solid write-up.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s the Spiral Academy*. Now, here\u2019s an interesting idea with them being focused on extensive study of the Imperial Service not because they\u2019ll actually take part on it, but because understanding the system is necessary to use it to their ends. They\u2019ve got the comprehensive curriculum for study of rulership, and that old nugget of them being used for raw paperwork processing for the government and local businesses, for which they make bank. Despite the paper pushing, graduation means being qualified for high ranking administrative positions in the Imperial government and House businesses, and occasionally even fast track into the ranks of the ministers.<br /> It also doubles up to teach the Dynasts general espionage skills in their diplomatic functions and to serve the purposes of the Houses, with a secret advanced course only for those who discover it. That seems like it might be a circuitous method of training All-Seeing Eye candidates, but considering the kinds of powers that they might be up against, I suppose that filtering them for the highest qualified has its merits.<br /> <br /> And a note on secret societies that pervade the Academy, and provide a grounding and extension of the intrigues and scheming of the Dynasty at large. I\u2019d say that for those who are put off by that, it\u2019s offset a bit by at least one of them being focused on uncovering judicial corruption.<br /> <br /> Yes, short write-up for the Spiral Academy, but it was always the workhorse school; the place where you got taught the general skills of being a Dynast, as opposed to the fraught military, the rare and esoteric sorcery, and the\u2026 necessary discipline of the Order\u2019s school.<br /> <br /> Need a moment, and then I\u2019ll get into\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, right, they\u2019re talking about Pasiap\u2019s Stair here as well. Okay, work through it\u2026<br /> <br /> Ahh right, <i>this</i> is the one with the more hellish training environment, owing to how most attending outcastes will not have powerful people to advocate for them. They\u2019ve got to live in rough hewn cells and classrooms, and climb up and down a steep mountain just to get their field training. They\u2019ve got some training to round out the lack of being brought up as Dynasts, and have the elder students help out and look out for the younger as part of that and building up their own form of camaraderie. Apart from what that does for the legions, I\u2019ve got to imagine that House V\u2019neef has a lot of vigour and closeness built into it from even before it was legally incorporated as a family. On the other hand, the group punishments lead to that occasional bit of murder of somebody holding the group back, and the associated official story with its colourful euphemism.<br /> <br /> Outcaste sorcerers cut the teeth there rather than the Heptagram, and they end terms with big mock battles before graduates are sent to join the legions. Or were; with the legions made into arms of the power of the Great Houses, outcaste graduates of the last few years have had difficulty finding a position to reflect their qualifications. One has to wonder if any Dynasts have given serious consideration as to what happens to that backlog of highly trained outcastes that they\u2019re refusing to give a job, or plans for the academy\u2019s future.<br /> <br /> And one last sidebar, concerning the subject of those who can\u2019t cut it. They can get education elsewhere, although it reduces their prestige, and they can also make their own way with pursuits related to travel and society (I would guess that this can include the more artistic and adventurous types), who can make their own reputations. This is also where it details the postgraduate sabbatical, in which new Dynasts take some time off to cut loose and travel on their own terms after a life of highly regimented education. Many are expected to return within only a couple of years, but the Dynasty accommodates those who go much further and might take years or decades to come back and contribute to society.<br /> <br /> Hmm, if sabbatical is in the sidebar, I suppose that the next section will be what happens when one actually returns to take on their first job. But I\u2019ll come back to that later. <br /> <br /> * I just want to say that I <i>have</i> noted that they all start off with a three word motto summarising their school\u2019s focus and philosophy, I just can\u2019t think of much to say about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:44:12-07:00","id":1202770,"title":"","content":"Okay, I\u2019ve covered the entirety of childhood, and am close to halfway through the chapter, so I\u2019m going to see how far I can get into their early adulthood, and then call it a day.<br /> It had already come up a couple of times in the secondary school section, but the education period at that stage has definitely been extended. I\u2019m guessing that it goes as far as the age of 21 so that it covers the real life stages of both later secondary school (or high school) and college years. More comprehensively getting them into adulthood before they join society, with the associated privileges and duties.<br /> <br /> The celebratory gala sounds like a fun affair, the kind of thing that you could open a chronicle with, and a particularly like the ritual of amending the rolls of the House to include the new Dynast. Likewise, the idea that it would be the first time you start to get sized up as a possible marriage partner plays into my image of an opener, where there\u2019s somebody to introduce the players to all of the big names in the local circles. I think it\u2019s good to lay out how, even at minimum, marriage negotiations can go on for a decade, to alleviate a sense that it\u2019s something that is foisted upon the young.<br /> <br /> So even apart from the sabbatical, the period after graduation is a time for relaxation, and taking consultation with House elders about one\u2019s future. The idea that this is generally done without the input of the new addition reinforces the emphasis on conformity, the sense that, even if they don\u2019t control the whole of your life, they ensure that you\u2019re drawn into the fold in a function that benefits the House as a whole.<br /> <br /> So, for House of Bells graduates, it used to be that the family would secure the highest ranked position possible for them, and if that wasn\u2019t to taste they\u2019d be liable to go off on sabbatical and await an opening or impressing an officer. I wonder if it was considered gauche to take sabbatical in proximity to a legion stationed in a satrapy or on campaign. Whereas since the Empress disappeared, they get drawn more or less immediately into the House legions, and are horded jealously while awaiting war.<br /> <br /> Administrative training gets you assigned to one of the House\u2019s businesses, unless one\u2019s particular skills and inclinations show potential in administration of the Realm. Between the reference to being guided towards the Deliberative here, and a few comments about satraps, I\u2019m guessing that the exact standards of those positions have been changed a bit this Edition; less of a thing proscribed for people with a lot of experience in service to the state.<br /> <br /> And the sorcerers will be provided with the resources they need to utilize and pursue their power, and otherwise largely left alone ala the prior sidebar. That\u2019s got to really reinforce the image of the Dynastic sorcerer, if they pigeonhole you a bit like that.<br /> <br /> A sidebar on the Grand Tour that sabbatical tends to take the form of, going to visit the satrapies so that one can see the world from the perspective of a Dynast; what one rules, and the luxuries that it affords. I like the specificity and sense of the wider world given by the idea that the South is favoured for that vacation, on account of the wealthy and exotic city-states down there.<br /> Some sections on everyday life are a good way to give perspective on Dynastic characters, particularly since they\u2019re likely to be rather unfamiliar to most players. Let me see\u2026 reiterating the time spent assessing marriage possibilities, moving on into that note I always liked on how young Dynasts would spend time living with an older relative. I would like if this part covered a bit more detail on what both parties get out of the arrangement, but it at least gets the point of what they do in that place.<br /> <br /> The matter of duelling has always been vague verging on neglected to my mind, so good for there to be a sidebar on that. Informally accepted, but to the death was strictly forbidden by the Empress, harshly (but not mortally) punished, but picking up in her absence.<br /> <br /> Last for the moment is the subject of their money. The core of Dynastic wealth is still the house stipend, although it strikes me as a bit higher than it used to be if it can purchase such lofty accommodations. Something that is definitely new is the idea that the increase in stipend is specified for daughters, and the notion that they need to support husbands, which I\u2019m going to chalk up as an extension of their authority rather than a perception that men can\u2019t support themselves. With the conditions of the stipend, income (which is now specific to working in your own right, rather than in a position provided by your elders, or for the state) is primarily about being able to afford greater luxuries or being less under the family\u2019s thumb. Actual purchases are still a matter of taking what you please, and allowing your retainers to handle the particulars.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s another useful bit of detailing by going into exactly what kinds of luxuries they\u2019ll actually spend money on. The cloth, drugs and mechanical toys I would expect, but if there are food stalls that can offer imported luxury foods, I would have to imagine that in the major cities, Dynasts going shopping is either an extremely regular occurrence (that they do for hours at a time), or they\u2019re <i>just</i> within the price range of patricians.<br /> <br /> Speaking of patricians, you wouldn\u2019t be a villainous ruler of the world if you couldn\u2019t expect to have hordes of minions. Come to think of it, I could see that as the basis of covering luxury street foods; how any given Dynast on the go is going to be surrounded by hangers-on that they\u2019ll be expected to buy treats for. Yes, that could make it work. The image of them typically having combat training is also neat; get the occasional elaborate street brawl going.<br /> <br /> Okay, Dynasts who are travelling can be expected to perform respectable services in the lands that they\u2019re in as a means of supplementing their stipend so that they can continue living in the manner to which they\u2019re accustomed\u2026 Ah debt, really glad to say a point concerning that in a discussion of money. I\u2019m guessing that personal debt isn\u2019t the province of House Ragara so much as the debt of House businesses, which would be the basis of having a rather disparaging attitude towards one getting into debt. I wonder what the circumstances of the courts assigning services to debtors is; does that happen because one\u2019s debt is to the Treasury or the Empress, or was that a matter of people who were forced to default on debts? Either way, it\u2019s another useful plot hook; that and the idea that really bad debts get you sent to take a walk in the Threshold while the family sorts things out.<br /> <br /> And finally a sidebar reminding us of the subject of Imperial and House patents, basically a form of advertising by letting a business display a brand showing that they provide services to respective powerful entities of the Realm. Sure, that\u2019s likely to cover a lot of luxury goods, but one should not forget how many basic resources even a Dynastic household would require; you keep a stable of horses, you need to buy their fodder, and the merchants who sell that get to display the mon, which draws the attention of patricians, and even citizens. I mean, it\u2019s probably the kind of thing that would only work if it\u2019s a business that has an arrangement with the House as a whole, rather than just a single family (probably a bulk discount deal, to be made up by the added business brought in by the advertising), but it gives a sense of the depth of the endeavours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T20:41:44-07:00","id":1202857,"title":"","content":"Ah screw it, a little bit more this evening.<br /> <br /> Next along is the high society of the Realm, an important (but possibly a bit underappreciated) detail, so elaborate that it requires a varied terminology. And I see that Lea finally got that line about the difference between proscription and description into a book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There may be a party going on in any city, but surely the majority of them would be held by patricians?<br /> <br /> So, we\u2019ve got the salon: the informal party of the small, intimate group, dedicated to more relaxed activity and a bit of backroom dealing. The kind of party where, even if they\u2019re trying to impress and outdo each other, they can try and let their hair down for a bit. There\u2019s the gala, the highly expensive and elaborate party in which everybody will dress their best (or provocatively not), the entertainments are lavish, and everyone who\u2019s anyone needs to be invited (such that you need to plan around them being away if you don\u2019t want them to show up), the exception being personal events like one\u2019s birthday. Patricians occasionally get invited, which represents a golden opportunity to advance a career. They\u2019re also not places for conducting business, but are for celebrating business that has already taken place (meaning that I\u2019m now picturing something like a Mnemon gala to celebrate having received a rather lucrative construction contract, featuring things like ice sculptures of the planned building, or a chocolate fountain emulating the one to be built). This is also where we get the description of the Dynast wedding ceremony, which is directly incorporated into the gala, and still a largely secular affair.<br /> <br /> Next is the celebration, the public festival in which peasants can attend. The lesser status means that the Exalted put less into them (leaving organisation to associated mortals), and dress less elaborately, while also conducting themselves in an austere fashion. The very idea represents a very intriguing new take on Realm society; the occasional event in which Exalt and mortal\u2026 not mingle, as such, but are in proximity for a shared cultural event. I\u2019ve got a picture of the Disney Notre Dame film, where Frollo comments on how he\u2019s obligated to be present at a peasant festival, but has no personal enjoyment of it. I guess the idea there is to not so much endear themselves to the commoners as provide a visible reminder that they exist, as well as cultivate that sense of cultural commonality.<br /> <br /> Visits are less formal even then salons, just covering any time one hosts another Dynast in their home, either to arrange personal business between them, or to provide hospitality while one is travelling. There\u2019s still a particular etiquette to be rigidly observed, concerning the order of events and how one is to conduct oneself in the stages. It also refers to the times when friends or family are simply getting together to enjoy each other\u2019s company, with no particular obligations. There\u2019s the return of that format of hospitality that I always liked, where there\u2019s a set maximum of how much time must pass before one is overstaying their welcome, and the notion that when you leave, you\u2019re supposed to make a big show of giving your host an unsolicited gift to compensate them for the expense of keeping you.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s finally a sidebar to go into Gateway. It\u2019s still not very detailed, beyond the addition of extra possible players and a change from several variations to the board being applied to play alternate games. It\u2019s mostly just about the social context in which it is played, rather than the game itself. I think that\u2019s definitely the better call; modelling a board game within a role-playing game would be weird, but pointing to the idea that it\u2019s mostly a prop in social interactions gives it a more concrete place, as well as adding detail to Dynastic society.<br /> It\u2019s a good section; not very long, but it gets the point across about what the importance of these events to the Dynasts is, and the manner in which they\u2019re conducted, with some intriguing new points.<br /> <br /> Next is marriage and children, and it is far too late to cover that complex subject, so that will be where I start next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T02:57:04-07:00","id":1202925,"title":"","content":"Actually coming up with rules for gateway sounds like a fun fan-project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T04:57:25-07:00","id":1202950,"title":"","content":"Now, to break down what is sure to be one of the more dense subjects of the book.<br /> <br /> We get the Dynasty\u2019s perspective on the bloodline that begats their Exaltation, a sacred trust that is valued more than anything, and for which they feel a deep obligation to pass it along. More pragmatic is how it forms the basis of connections between Exalted families, binding the Realm together. I think placing marriage up there with the Wyld Hunt really emphasizes and contextualizes the significance of it in this culture.<br /> <br /> Reiteration of the typical time between graduation and marriage, along with the priorities in negotiation; partners of a similar age if it can be managed, elevated station for one\u2019s sons, a source of good blood for daughters. Good, keep reinforcing the matriarchal elements. That element of women getting the higher stipend is put into context now; it\u2019s not about a sense that men can\u2019t support themselves, it\u2019s about how once your son is married, somebody else is paying for his stipend, and they\u2019re doing it to compensate you for how all of his children belong to their House rather than yours. That\u2019s a more interesting element of the matriarchy, and adds a fun additional layer of complication to their relationships and negotiations, particularly the element of wanting husbands of lesser status whose stipends will cost less. Really, that whole idea of how you\u2019ll need to pay for everybody married into the House for the rest of their lives; among other things, there\u2019s a shiny new motive for assassinations. To finish off, there\u2019s the humorous image of a man pricing himself out of the marriage market, at which point they need to marry lower status women, who need to make a big one off payment to compensate.<br /> <br /> Suddenly I\u2019m thinking that the reason that Sesus Eshuvar is married to a mortal is because having taken part in a successful Wyld Hunt (that followed up on a disastrous one, no less) when he was still very young greatly increased his stipend, making him more expensive than many Houses were willing to pay for. I\u2019ve actually got a general image of there being a delicate balancing act in one\u2019s stipend and how that relates to marriage; a prominent early achievement elevates it above one\u2019s peers, but leaves potential spouses\u2019 families asking \u201cokay, but what else have you got that would justify us paying so much?\u201d<br /> <br /> I like the image of how being able to choose your own spouse is either something that comes from some very canny interactions with your own House, and either the House of the one you want or the one you\u2019re refusing (possibly both)\u2026 or just being low enough on the totem pole that your marriage wasn\u2019t going to make much anyway, so you\u2019re not worth the effort of bringing into line.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s the note on the difficulty of getting a judge to officiate an unsanctioned marriage, including that tidbit I had hoped for about the necessities of marrying a peasant (with the implication that it\u2019s actually a thing that happens sometimes). Aand I think the details of how marriages can end has been adjusted somewhat; as I recall, it used to be that if the union went without children after fifty years, it was <i>automatically</i> dissolved, in contrast to now when it is twenty years (a more readily achieved timeline), and with the agreement of both matriarchs or a judge. That implies to me that there can be infertile unions (including same sex ones) that get to continue existing indefinitely, if nobody in authority should object. Other than that and one of the partners being convicted of a major crime, there is no divorce.<br /> <br /> And here\u2019s laying out the details of the newly added same-sex marriage; it faces stigma over the possibility of lacking children (that it possesses several means of getting around) and lacking House approval that any other marriage might, but they\u2019re unconcerned with homosexuality itself. The difficulties are still sufficient that there are many gay Dynasts who\u2019ll just accept an arranged marriage, and they\u2019ve got a system worked out for which House gets the children. It\u2019s not stated here, but I imagine that\u2019s got to add another layer to possible objections; I imagine it can be a bit of a blow to have a daughter who falls in love with an older women, meaning that your grandchildren through her won\u2019t belong to your House as you would have expected them to. Overall, I\u2019d say this is an effective way of getting this into the setting.<br /> <br /> Now, getting into the details of the matrilineality: children belonging to the mother\u2019s House and status, husbands being expected to show the same deference to their wives\u2019 mothers as their own, uh-huh. It doesn\u2019t specify a gender subject to the matter of peasants and outcastes who lack names of their own marrying a Dynast (or patrician), so I presume that applies to men and women. I guess it can still maintain a certain matrilineal element in the case of the latter, if a peasant woman is automatically considered a member of the House (even if the earlier sidebar stated that mortals assume the masculine role as a rule). One thing that\u2019s different than what I would have expected is the social acceptability; I always imagined that marrying a peasant was the kind of thing that necessitated becoming a virtual pariah from Dynast society, but here\u2019s the idea that it officially elevates their status in a manner that allows one to keep showing their face in respectable company. That really carries a whole range of unique scenarios into the game.<br /> <br /> Husbands who outlive their wives return to their own families (unless they should get permission to stay with the new House, which typically angers one\u2019s birth House), and I\u2019ve already seen how the children remain under the control of their mother\u2019s family and get adopted in elsewhere. They occasionally game the system by marrying a useful Dragon Blood to a mortal so that they can come back within a few decades (which probably synergizes nicely with that element of higher ranking ones being above what Exalted wives will pay), or even just within the House (which is surely big enough to have many distant cousins) or people that are closely associated with the House.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m curious about precisely what has been changed with pregnancy\u2026 not much, other than it\u2019s no longer a year. It still has the elements of how long it takes to show prominently, and how little it debilitates even then. The biggest element to the childbirth itself is stating that it\u2019s possible (even if still rare) for stillbirths and miscarriages to happen (with some prior characters having already demonstrated a capacity for defects). The main improvements on the process seem to favour the Exalt, while the still mortal foetus retains a few risks.<br /> <br /> I believe that this section on the transferred loyalty of husbands answers my question concerning whether husbands are ever trusted with a House\u2019s secrets; if they\u2019re raised with the idea that their loyalty goes to their wives House, then once they demonstrate necessary competence, I\u2019d say they can probably be drawn in. It likely represents a complication if the wife should die, though; I can picture another scenario for assassinations coming from the occasion in which a freed husband might compromise a House\u2019s secrets, and they can\u2019t effectively get another marriage to bind him back in. I can also see that as a particular scenario in which a freed husband requests to stay with his wife\u2019s family; it\u2019s probably better to have your birth House angry with you then to have the likes of Ragara kill you to ensure your silence.<br /> <br /> In any case, it\u2019s being complicated as hostility between the Houses rises. It\u2019s interesting to me that the typical scenario still consists of a man trying to show loyalty to his wife\u2019s House, or evade the matter altogether, rather than there being a huge prospect of men siding with their birth families\u2026 beyond the matter of how many Houses are starting to stonewall them out of fear. I also enjoy the note on how even if a man should serve with his family, there\u2019s the risk that he\u2019d need to fight his wife. There\u2019s a whole minefield in there.<br /> <br /> And there\u2019s a sidebar concerning the subject of marriage in play. I\u2019ll admit, when I saw that heading, I expected something commenting on the subject of how a Dynast player might relate to a spouse that isn\u2019t an active part of the story or play group, but this is mostly about reiterating the significance of not using in-character conceits to force marriages on players who don\u2019t want them (as opposed to players who want to play characters who don\u2019t want the marriage). I\u2019ve certainly seen enough concerns about the subject to think it\u2019s a valid and necessary piece of Storyteller advice, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T05:47:05-07:00","id":1202956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202950#post1202950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;on not marrying pcs whose players don't want to&gt;I\u2019ve certainly seen enough concerns about the subject to think it\u2019s a valid and necessary piece of Storyteller advice, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a reminder of the red rule, I suppose.<br /> I'd try to persuade the player to accept it because, well, unwanted marriages are a major point of the dragon-blooded socialite narrative, which can lead to fun stories. Whatever making the player uncomfortable is likely easy to dodge while still having the marriage there. (it compares neatly with L5R in this aspect)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T06:35:32-07:00","id":1202968,"title":"","content":"Now, for one of the bigger changes, the function of the bloodline. It opens off the bat with the idea that the Dragons\u2019 blood doesn\u2019t refer to something literally genetic, but the metaphysical capacity of the Terrestrial Essence to propagate itself, rendering it beyond any magic lesser than the Exaltation itself. It takes time and energy to pass on effectively, and is never guaranteed. Okay, so how does that interact with the notion of a bloodline\u2019s strength?<br /> <br /> Ah, so it\u2019s not a matter of eugenics and ancestry, but on how long your parents waited for their progenitive Essence to replenish. There\u2019s a perception (that may be erroneous) that the so-called leftover children themselves have a lesser capacity to have Exalted children, so matchmaking in pursuit of stronger bloodlines isn\u2019t about things like how many mortals are in there, but whether or not one is the product of a union with maximized Essence, and how many generations back that trend held. I was already on board with progenitive Essence, but still had some reservations with the idea of and references to bloodlines, not least because my own background in genetics kept intruding on my attempt to conceptualise this whole part of their society. This <i>considerably</i> simplifies things, removes some of the skeezier elements entirely, but we still get the fun of those elements of tracking genealogies and intricate matchmaking (speaking of, <i>so</i> glad that term is in now, as an alternative to \u201cbreeding programme\u201d). Mortal children of the Exalted are still considered to inherit the progenitive Essence, which remains consistent regardless of their child-bearing patterns, although I imagine that it\u2019s considered to lessen across generations.<br /> <br /> \u2026unless\u2026 part of the idea of matchmaking mortals is that the potential <i>does</i> remain consistent across generations, so they\u2019ll be looking for mortals descended from a union of Exalted who maximized their Essence. I\u2019m going to put a pin in this.<br /> <br /> The Essence is passed on with conception (adding another dimension to needing proper contraception in one\u2019s affairs), and the mystical quality of it means that the same rules go even if the child is formed by magic. I wonder if that\u2019s something that can apply to another person generated whole cloth through the use of sorcery, or solely in cases where some of the parent\u2019s actual tissue is used as a basis.<br /> <br /> Okay, the subject of extramarital children\u2026 about what I would expect for men, a sense of greater stigma for them having numerous affairs because of the higher potential to keep expending their progenitive Essence. I must admit, though, that I can\u2019t <i>entirely</i> follow the logic for women\u2026 they\u2019re considered above reproach for extramarital pregnancy <i>because</i> everybody can tell that they\u2019ve done it? I\u2019m missing something here. On the other hand, extramarital relations with the same sex are held in higher regard because there\u2019s no potential for pregnancy and wasted Essence at all, although still the kind of thing where being really obvious about it invites hostility, and marrying the same sex is only an issue if one hasn\u2019t gotten children within a couple of decades via any of the proscribed methods.<br /> <br /> Hmm, another error\u2026 there probably wasn\u2019t intended to be something else in place of repeating the first paragraph. Instead there\u2019s a sidebar covering the subject of transgender\u2026 right, so they\u2019ve made Danaa\u2019d into a transwomen in the mythology, and that society holds one\u2019s gender to be what they say it is. I\u2019m guessing this is in stark contrast to being agendered, which would generally be taboo but for examples such as a Tepet making it an application of their irreproachable warrior oath. Marriage follows the same convention, but is expected to still be fruitful. It\u2019s an interesting place to also put details of the Dynastic attitude to employing sorcery in the endeavour; with the more mystical nature of the heredity, it\u2019s solely a matter of how squirrely the Dynasty is about sorcery in general, rather than such methods interfering with one\u2019s chances. Okay, that makes sense. Rawar of Arjuf has also been rewritten as a trans man (I\u2019m guessing that there was no occasion of him making statements that the throne would be a burden too heavy for the Empress, assuming that was ever about gender rather than pre-Contagion status), and Mnemon and Ragara are now the results of sorcery (while still having a father). Heh, if anything could have added to the dynamic between those two, it would be making them full blood siblings. And if I\u2019m reading correctly, it\u2019s saying that the example of Rawar lets them lift the sorcery taboo more for couples involving a transgender person, more than they would if it\u2019s same-sex.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got a section using the premise of the leftover children concept to detail how long the Essence takes to regenerate, and how that relates to the usual demographics of family size. It doesn\u2019t say directly, but I assume that it\u2019s working according to the principle I speculated; if one carefully husbands their Essence, then the majority of one\u2019s children can be expected to Exalt. In most cases of several children at once, if any Exalts it will generally only be the one because basically all of the Essence goes to them, while it\u2019s possible for more to Exalt as well.<br /> <br /> Whatever my confusions about the social attitudes to extramarital relations, the legitimacy is clear; women always have full claim to their children, men have no claim whatsoever on children outside marriage (so even if more of them could be expected to Exalt, there would be no advantage to it). Women can choose to acknowledge the biological fathers of their children, but that seems to only really give them a cultural avenue to a relationship with them. Men can publically acknowledge that they\u2019re in extramarital relationships with patricians and peasants, but is looked down upon and contributes to stereotypes. Aaaand while men don\u2019t get a unilateral legal claim on their natural children, there are conventions for bringing the pregnancy into the fold of the Dynasty (probably no sense in letting even a minor potential Exaltation go to waste, especially if the basis of bloodlines is different now), whether it\u2019s via a sister or cousin or whomever in the man\u2019s original House, while occasionally doing so with their wife\u2019s House, accompanied by some rough hazing. It seems pretty extreme, but I imagine that there\u2019s a desire to make it a hard time to ensure that the Dragon blood doesn\u2019t stray widely out of control.<br /> <br /> And the final part on the life of the Scarlet Dynast is the experience of parenthood, coming full circle\u2026 wait, no, obviously there are going to be sections on old age, retirement, and death\u2026 last part before going into details about outcastes. Anyway! We\u2019ve already seen this from the child\u2019s perspective, but here the parental one is that the manner in which they distantly manage the child\u2019s upbringing is itself a strong expression of love, since it prepares them for life and leaves them with strength. They have a whole literary tradition to emphasize the nobility of placing that concern over a personal relationship, and stigmatize those who opt not to do so. In any case, the most basic legal obligation is to provide for their essential needs and education.<br /> <br /> And a useful little sidebar clarifying how the Dynasty is very bottom heavy, with the lifestyle killing most before they can reach a hundred (presumably only having managed two to four children of their own), resulting in a vastly disproportionate number around the same age, clustered around a smaller number of venerable middle age, and a stark minority of elders. Lea commented elsewhere that it makes the Dynasty\u2019s demographics <b>less</b> fudgy, but still necessarily fudged a bit, but I\u2019m satisfied with the principles of it; it\u2019s credible enough, and removes some of the complication that would come from an extremely elaborate cross-section of ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T06:43:22-07:00","id":1202975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202956#post1202956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's a reminder of the red rule, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh I think it can be about more than just the sexual implications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd try to persuade the player to accept it because, well, unwanted marriages are a major point of the dragon-blooded socialite narrative, which can lead to fun stories. Whatever making the player uncomfortable is likely easy to dodge while still having the marriage there. (it compares neatly with L5R in this aspect)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOoohh, I, err... I wouldn't want to presume on that front. Certainly feel a bit squirrely over a line like &quot;we can take the one aspect of unwanted arranged marriage that they probably wouldn't like out, so it can be comfortably put upon them&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike, sure it can be fun, and there are things that can be fun because they're challenging and transgressive, but this is one where I would definitely argue against trying to pressure anybody.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's like I say in the part that you quoted; affecting the attitude of a fictional person who is against the marriage is all part of the diverse roleplaying experience, but actually putting that on the player is toeing a line at best. And the setting contains enough diversity that it hardly breaks verisimilitude to do otherwise, while the social nature of the Dynasty is such that arranged marriages can still have presence even if none of the players are part of one.<br /> <br /> Soo, yeah; I disagree with your statement, and do not endorse it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T06:53:09-07:00","id":1202981,"title":"","content":"&quot;pressure&quot; is quite far from &quot;try to persuade&quot;, don't know why you made that slip so fast.<br /> The whole point of such persuasion is so that the player doesn't feel pressured.<br /> Because the fundamental premise I always uphold when I'm talking about setting up a game with my friends is that no one is being a dick to anyone. A basic common ground friends tend to have and good starting point for any cooperative activity.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Barbs aside, rest comfortable that we agree that the book is giving solid advice. This is just a semantic disagreement on how people interact.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-04-2018, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:55:03-07:00","id":1203108,"title":"","content":"Well considering Tepet was also decimated recently there is also the possibility for PCs who don't want to deal with an arranged marriage to have just had their betrothed be a member of Tepet and have died in that incident. I mean can't hold not going through with the marriage against them when their spouse died before it happened, and with the current strain on relationships between the Great Houses, I'd imagine it could take an exceptionally long time for a new one to be arranged. <br /> <br /> Which if I recall didn't it say that more prestigious dynastic children can actually become harder to find matches for as the House is trying not to lose out too much on the marriage? Course now I'm just picturing a DB PC who's goal is get ever more famous and well regarded to just make it as impossible as they can for their family to get a match for them until the character decides they'd like to settle down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:33:16-07:00","id":1203116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203108#post1203108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which if I recall didn't it say that more prestigious dynastic children can actually become harder to find matches for as the House is trying not to lose out too much on the marriage?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOnly for men. It's part of the whole deal for how the wife's family starts needing to pay your stipend, plus the sense that they don't want their daughters to be overshadowed by their husbands.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:26:31-07:00","id":1203170,"title":"","content":"(I'm trying to move back away from simply summarising the book}<br /> <br /> Next up is the life progression of outcastes in the Realm. The lost egg term once again originated with the Scarlet Empress, a reference to an analogy concerning individuals who need to be returned to the nest. Never been entirely sure what the Dynast reference point for dragons having eggs is, though\u2026 So they\u2019re legally designated as distantly related to the Empress as the basis for the state asserting authority over them, which grants status above the Realm\u2019s mortals but below the true Dynasts.<br /> <br /> I suppose that patrician families can still reliably produce Exalted because they\u2019ll often be descended to greater or lesser extent from the Dynasty, and we\u2019ve got some specific codification for the whys and wherefores of their being incorporated into the higher society, including the benefits of the groundwork provided by the shared primary education.<br /> <br /> Sooo adoption seems like the option that yields greater benefits, becoming a full member of the House, but is harder to achieve because they\u2019ll only go through with it if one manages to excel in secondary school. Even with that, they\u2019re still only really considered half a Dynast. I wondered if they might cut loose somebody who can\u2019t hack it, but the book is right, that would be a waste of a valuable asset. I do wonder what the work of a client Dragon Blood entails; possibly not much different from another young member, just without the same pay and benefits, and under a system of working towards eventual adoption. Mind, if there\u2019s an associated stereotype of having no head for books, perhaps there\u2019s a tendency to give clients more of the muscle work.<br /> <br /> Oh jeez, needing to pay back what a House provided if the patrician is no good at all, that has to be <i>ruinous</i> I\u2019m picturing some patrician, all pride and gratitude that one of their own children was blessed by the Dragons, and a few decades later they look on from the end of their life as it turns out to have been a curse bringing about the downfall of their family. I wonder if there are a few outcastes wandering around with the memory of having compassed that.<br /> <br /> Fostering would be the system that gets the like of Bal Kerez through their education. If I\u2019m reading it right, the difference is\u2026 the client system entails a patrician family being paid by a Great House to secure the rights to their ultimate adoption, becoming a part of the House\u2019s businesses, while fostering has a patrician family go into debt with a House to secure their assistance in getting their Dragon Blood through schooling, at which point they take up a position with the patricians. The benefit of that is having an Exalt on their side, and the hope of eventually cultivating that into a bloodline strong enough to be incorporated wholesale into a House. It sounds like a system that entails a <i>lot</i> of risks, but if played effectively, can yield enormous rewards. Cadet houses can also take that option, and seem better suited to it, gaining the benefit of a member that will be viewed on more equal footing with members of the Dynasty.<br /> <br /> Outcastes from a commoner background don\u2019t have such lofty options, and they get the option of the razor or the coin. I have a vague recollection that before, the choice was something that was more immediate, and I think there being an extended grace period to give them at least an impression of what they\u2019re in for so that they can make an informed choice helps make it a bit less haphazard, a bit more effective at ensuring that one gets personnel that are suited for (or at least all in to) the role they take up with. I can also see making a lavish ceremony out of making the choice something that helps to instil a sense of awe and loyalty into prospective servants of the Empress.<br /> <br /> Errbepebrrr, taking the Razor gets you sent to the Cloister of Wisdom, dropping out or failing is not an option (although it least it\u2019s something as benign as needing to repeat years as necessary), and after you\u2019re directly initiated into the Order. I have no judgement about the Order developing a tendency to send outcastes directly for their training; it\u2019s not just that their motives are fairly altruistic, but it\u2019s got to be a bit of a cruel joke to have to endure Pasiap\u2019s Stair only to find oneself set aside at the end of all that training.<br /> <br /> Addressing the question of what happens to legion outcastes who finish their terms of service (extended or not) is good, that\u2019s another area where one used to have to fill in the blanks a bit. I\u2019m guessing that even ones who don\u2019t opt to marry into the Dynasty can find good opportunities, things like freelance work for Houses or using their own resources and connections built up in their career to build up an independent business. For those that <i>do</i> marry, there\u2019s something amusing in the idea of a degree of culture shock in taking on Dynastic expectations of marriage and gender roles. On the other hand, with the draws they can exert from marriage to patricians or the like, it might be that even an outcaste who retires with little to their name can very rapidly accrue what is needed to set themselves up alone. Hmm, between them and patrician families that go in for fostering, I\u2019ve got an image of the future of the Realm in which a coalition of patricians and outcastes try to independently set up a similar deal to House Nellens, cultivating their own stronger bloodlines.<br /> <br /> The Deliberative hasn\u2019t yet been mentioned very much, but the description of how it functions in the matter of contemporary adoption of lost eggs to the Houses has me thinking that it\u2019s being specified as an instrument of the struggle between the Houses, rather than having much potential to function as an independent body. For adoption itself, I suppose the benefit of going that route is that you get the outcaste under your umbrella, but don\u2019t need to tie up somebody\u2019s marriage in order to do so (that and when you\u2019re a small and new House, and could do with having your ranks filled out quite a bit).<br /> <br /> And a fun little extra note on how outcastes sometimes get snuck into a House by being given the identity of a dead scion. I\u2019m picturing something of the scenario in that really bad Simpsons episode; an outcaste serving in the legions alongside a Dynast comes home when the Dynast does not, and their family decides to tell everybody that it was the other way around. I\u2019m seeing montages in which the outcaste gets a crash course on the lost child\u2019s personality and mannerisms, and all motivated by some critical arranged marriage or the like.<br /> <br /> Oh, there actually is a description of what they do if they don\u2019t marry into the existing power structure. Not being Dynasts, their marriages could serve as the foundation of new patrician families, and I\u2019m picturing them as having a tendency to favour other outcaste patricians for further marriages; I\u2019m seeing a whole subculture of Dynastic marriage intrigue in miniature going on among the patricians. This is where the outcastes drummed out of the legions are widely ending up, and I think it\u2019s got some potential to transform the landscape of the Exalted of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s the foreign outcastes. Some prior references suggest to me that these occasionally intersect with the prior category (I suppose mostly in satrapies), but for the most part it\u2019s about the perception of Dragon Blooded who come up wholly independently of the Realm. I find this to be another effective area to elaborate on; there is, after all, a stronger emphasis on unique cultures of Dragon Blooded beyond the Realm (and Lookshy), and it makes for a richer and more plausible picture than previous Editions where it felt like there was an expectation that the Arbiters actually could be expected to pick up the majority of lost eggs. And even when the existence of foreign, independent Dragon Blooded was acknowledged, it was up in the air about how they would be received in the Blessed Isle; I recall at least one person being of the opinion that going around openly there would basically get you jumped by the Arbiters, and shanghaied immediately into the legions or the Order.<br /> <br /> No, this time there\u2019s a distinct element of classism crossed over with exoticism, with the idea that a foreign Exalt might be subject to lavish entertainments, but not really treated with as a serious actor unless they\u2019ve engaged in some service that suits the interests of the Realm or the Dynasty. Dragon Blooded from coherent societies like Lookshy occasionally defect, but will often be regarded as untrustworthy, and options to be tied into the Realm\u2019s upper classes are sharply limited and tightly guarded for the individual Exalt. The impression I get is that the foreign Dragon Blood faces a strong insinuation that they\u2019re not wanted; if they come to the Blessed Isle on their own business then they\u2019re allowed to undertake it, and even liable to be invited to an event as a curiosity, but they can\u2019t participate in the true life of the Exalted of the Realm, and are expected to leave fairly promptly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T19:00:19-07:00","id":1203235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203170#post1203170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that patrician families can still reliably produce Exalted because they\u2019ll often be descended to greater or lesser extent from the Dynasty, and we\u2019ve got some specific codification for the whys and wherefores of their being incorporated into the higher society, including the benefits of the groundwork provided by the shared primary education.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit in there about how sometimes, a family will actually pass up an for-real, touched-by-the-Dragons Exalted Dragon-Blooded in favor of an unExalted mortal with much more impeccable breeding, because it's felt that that will be more resource-efficient towards the end goal of producing more Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> This makes sense to me; it seems like if you're a leftover child who can trace back their descent on both sides to many, MANY well-bred Dragon-Blooded, you're possibly a better bet than some rando who more or less Exalted by accident. I bet the genealogists and match-making mavens of the Realm have very, very good records and statistics on this sort of thing, possibly combined with cultural shibboleths and superstitions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Outcastes from a commoner background don\u2019t have such lofty options, and they get the option of the razor or the coin. I have a vague recollection that before, the choice was something that was more immediate, </div> </div> </div>Not really; the 1e Outcastes book is very specific that there's an educational period in which the outcaste is given the tools they need in order to make at least a semi-informed decision.<br /> <br /> In MOEP: Dragon-Blooded, the description is much more... terse, and can be interpreted as being much more immediate, but doesn't HAVE to be interpreted that way.<br /> <br /> That said, there are some examples of fiction and lore that sort of... elide this ostensible &quot;choice.&quot; Kasif, for example, is literally shanghaied directly into the Immaculate Order in Aspect Book: Air. There is no choice between the Coin and the Razor for him, he just gets the shit kicked out of him and wakes up in the Palace Sublime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it\u2019s got to be a bit of a cruel joke to have to endure Pasiap\u2019s Stair only to find oneself set aside at the end of all that training. </div> </div> </div>Given the indoctrination that they cram into you at the Stair, I bet that's psychologically hurtful... but if you're a hard-headed sort, it might be to your advantage. After all... if the legions explicitly don't want you, and your training is over, that means your obligation to the Realm is fulfilled, right? You're free to make your own way in the world.<br /> <br /> Of course. You're a highly-trained Dragon-Blooded, possibly even a sorcerer, who has been schooled in the bending of your Essence towards the arts of war and conquest, and you have been socially isolated during your formative years such that you likely have no idea how to function outside the rigid role they prepared you for. I bet having guys like <i>that</i> at loose ends is a great idea, am I right?<br /> <br /> That section seems like it could do with some fleshing-out, because it doesn't make a ton of sense to me. I get that with the Imperial Legions no longer existing, the Great Houses are going to want their own scions and loyalists placed into their new House Legions at whatever level they can... but Pasiap's Stair graduates are highly-trained Exalted who have endured rigors that make the House of Bells look like a pleasant time, and they don't have ties to your political foes. You'd think that the Great Houses would be very, very eager to give them commissions as scalelords and fanglords and they'd be very, very eager to accep","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T19:28:56-07:00","id":1203246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203235#post1203235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a bit in there about how sometimes, a family will actually pass up an for-real, touched-by-the-Dragons Exalted Dragon-Blooded in favor of an unExalted mortal with much more impeccable breeding, because it's felt that that will be more resource-efficient towards the end goal of producing more Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> This makes sense to me; it seems like if you're a leftover child who can trace back their descent on both sides to many, MANY well-bred Dragon-Blooded, you're possibly a better bet than some rando who more or less Exalted by accident. I bet the genealogists and match-making mavens of the Realm have very, very good records and statistics on this sort of thing, possibly combined with cultural shibboleths and superstitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>A point of order: a leftover child is not an un-Exalted Dynast, but a child born too soon after an elder sibling, so called because they're said to receive the leftovers of their parents' procreative Essence. It's a nasty slur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","name":"Spider Queen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T19:39:24-07:00","id":1203252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203235#post1203235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a bit in there about how sometimes, a family will actually pass up an for-real, touched-by-the-Dragons Exalted Dragon-Blooded in favor of an unExalted mortal with much more impeccable breeding, because it's felt that that will be more resource-efficient towards the end goal of producing more Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that's in the House Nellens write-up, but I'm unsure how it connects to that quote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes sense to me; it seems like if you're a leftover child who can trace back their descent on both sides to many, MANY well-bred Dragon-Blooded, you're possibly a better bet than some rando who more or less Exalted by accident. I bet the genealogists and match-making mavens of the Realm have very, very good records and statistics on this sort of thing, possibly combined with cultural shibboleths and superstitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGiven the clarification on what strong bloodlines actually means, I think that's a system that still excludes leftover children, and favours the unExalted who still got a full share of the progenitive Essence at its most potent.<br /> <br /> The way it's described, the Dragon's blood of somebody who was conceived a year or two after another sibling is barely stronger than some random outcaste, because they inherited only a bare trickle of the Essence.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike I said before, I wonder if the progenitive Essence of the unExalted persists across generations, or if it gets progressively weaker, even if it remains consistent in the individual. I see benefits either way; on the one hand, there can be a strong base of useful mortal Dynasts being matched up throughout the system to continuously yield Exalted, a firm bedrock for the Houses, while on the other, a weakening bloodline being branched off into the patricians adds an extra dimension to genealogical records, and touches on the idea of nobility descending to humbler status over time which I like. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes, that's what comes of vague recollections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you have been socially isolated during your formative years</div> </div> </div> </div>The students of Pasiap's Stair are organised into units, aren't they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That section seems like it could do with some fleshing-out, because it doesn't make a ton of sense to me. I get that with the Imperial Legions no longer existing, the Great Houses are going to want their own scions and loyalists placed into their new House Legions at whatever level they can... but Pasiap's Stair graduates are highly-trained Exalted who have endured rigors that make the House of Bells look like a pleasant time, and they don't have ties to your political foes. You'd think that the Great Houses would be very, very eager to give them commissions as scalelords and fanglords and they'd be very, very eager to accep</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOn the one hand, as Eric or Robert clarified elsewhere, the problem with graduates of Pasiap's Stair is that they're indoctrinated to loyalty to the Realm as a whole, as embodied in the Scarlet Empress, so I'd say it makes sense that many of the Houses are squirrelly about filling out their legions with such people. I'd also say that goes along with many of the more ideologically inclined Houses, that would prefer people who have been raised their whole lives to believe in their respective causes, rather than being plucked from obscurity and raised to follow the dictates of the Empress. As an example, I could see a House such as Ledaal thinking that they'd much prefer their legions to be led by people who truly, deeply believe in the shadow crusade.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, the section does mention the idea that the number of outcaste households being formed by drifting Pasiap's Stair graduates are still resources in the intrigues between the Houses. Their skills aren't going completely to waste, they're just not part of the command structure for the big armies.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also read a subtext that more than a few Dynasts are preparing against the possibility of the Empress returning in terms of setting things up so that if she comes back, there'll be a few changes around the Realm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T20:28:09-07:00","id":1203267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203252#post1203252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that's in the House Nellens write-up, but I'm unsure how it connects to that quote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it seems like it relates to the patrician class and their ability to reliably produce Exalted; part of that reliability is going to relate to their careful match-making, and part of THAT is going to be sometimes paying more attention to the bloodline than to immediacy. An Exalted Dragon-Blooded clearly has SOMETHING going on for them... but there are many other considerations besides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bGiven the clarification on what strong bloodlines actually means, I think that's a system that still excludes leftover children, and favours the unExalted who still got a full share of the progenitive Essence at its most potent. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I absolutely and totally mis-used the term. You and Spider Queen are correct in pointing that out; that's my bad.<br /> <br /> (I spent eighteen years learning all the Exalted terminology inside and out and now there are all-new, all-different slurs for the ill-bred to learn! Vexing.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way it's described, the Dragon's blood of somebody who was conceived a year or two after another sibling is barely stronger than some random outcaste, because they inherited only a bare trickle of the Essence. </div> </div> </div>Or at least, that's the belief. Am I absolutely crazy, or does that section hint that there might be more to it than that? Because &quot;leftovers&quot; Exalt sometimes. Twins Exalt sometimes. Is that just a matter of their parents progenitive essence being so strong that it doesn't give a fuck, or is there something else going on?<br /> <br /> Although thinking about it, I sort of love the idea how if you have a leftover younger sibling who also Exalts, suddenly your own marriage prospects change radically for the better, because if your parents bloodline is so great that even their leftovers are Exalting, YOU, who are not a leftover, must be a real catch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bLike I said before, I wonder if the progenitive Essence of the unExalted persists across generations, or if it gets progressively weaker, even if it remains consistent in the individual. I see benefits either way; on the one hand, there can be a strong base of useful mortal Dynasts being matched up throughout the system to continuously yield Exalted, a firm bedrock for the Houses, while on the other, a weakening bloodline being branched off into the patricians adds an extra dimension to genealogical records, and touches on the idea of nobility descending to humbler status over time which I like. </div> </div> </div>This is very interesting to me. They don't really go into how it works for mortals, do they? Like, are unExalted Dynasts who are married to each other expected to control their child-making cycles in the same way? Because that's going to severely limit their number of kids; even with the advanced medical treatment available to those with money, it's going to put a hard cap on family size unless you get going VERY early. If the same &quot;ten years is a good number&quot; rule applies, an unExalted Dynasty or patrician couple, if they wed in their mid-twenties and have a kid right away, are going to produce, like, three kids max, and the third is likely to be kinda risky. (Pregnancy in your mid-forties is no joke.) How are patricians expected to manage their non-Exalted child rearing, if at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The students of Pasiap's Stair are organised into units, aren't they? </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry; I was unclear.<br /> <br /> By socially isolated I meant &quot;isolated from the society of the Realm and the people in it, especially the society of the Dragon-Blooded.&quot; They're mostly low-status outcastes, which means they had no idea how life as a Dragon-Blooded in the Realm worked from the inside to begin with, and they're spending a huge whack of their formative years being both isolated from that society and trained to fight and kill on its behalf.<br /> <br /> Now, I might be going out on a limb here, but that says to me that most of those guys are not going to have much of an idea of how to function as a Dragon-Blooded, the social rules and mores and limitations and expectations, what they can get away with and what they cannot, outside of the specific context of being part of a military unit of same, and they're ESPECIALLY not going to be well-prepared to make their own way in the world in a non-Legion context.<br /> <br /> It seems like guys like that being at loose ends, especially in a situation where law and order is breaking down, might cause... problems. Banditry and warlordism sorts of problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also read a subtext that more than a few Dynasts are preparing against the possibility of the Empress returning in terms of setting things up so that if she comes back, there'll be a few changes around the Realm. </div> </div> </div>I think you're absolutely correct here. You have some Dynasts who are prepping for &quot;she'll be back, and everyone who stepped out of line is gonna be in TROUBLE&quot; and you have others prepping for &quot;she MIGHT be back, and if she does come back there'll be changes that redound to our benefit.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T21:03:21-07:00","id":1203279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203267#post1203267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is very interesting to me. They don't really go into how it works for mortals, do they? Like, are unExalted Dynasts who are married to each other expected to control their child-making cycles in the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. As per the text, &quot;progenitive potential remains constant in mortals, neither waxing nor waning.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T21:09:08-07:00","id":1203281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203279#post1203279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. As per the text, &quot;progenitive potential remains constant in mortals, neither waxing nor waning.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's on me for not reading nearly close enough, then. Thanks for taking the time, Eric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T01:46:00-07:00","id":1203328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203252#post1203252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOn the other hand, the section does mention the idea that the number of outcaste households being formed by drifting Pasiap's Stair graduates are still resources in the intrigues between the Houses. Their skills aren't going completely to waste, they're just not part of the command structure for the big armies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Wait a moment...<br /> <br /> Graduates of Pasiap's Stair are highly trained paramilitary agents who are explicitly not part of the Realm's social structure, with no loyalty to the <s>megacorps</s> Great Houses, but who nevertheless do odd jobs for them here and there?<br /> <br /> ...They are basically shadowrunners. Now there's a Shard in the making, if I ever saw one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:20:48-07:00","id":1203386,"title":"","content":"Okay, chapter is almost finished.<br /> <br /> Sworn Kinships: I can\u2019t entirely remember the mechanics of Brotherhoods, but they weren\u2019t exactly a neglected part of the Dragon Blooded canon, so if there\u2019s any necessary expansion they had a solid base to build on. Given how it\u2019s now a natural capability rather than a function of sorcery, I like the spiritual perspective they have on it. Plus the idea that they become at least as close as family, given how much Dynast family has been set up to this point; it\u2019s interesting to imagine how, now matter far afield from the Dynasty a Dragon Blood is, if they\u2019ve formed a Hearth with the scion of a House, they\u2019re above reproach. Considering what I was saying before about other groups of Exalted who seem to kind of hate each other, I also appreciate the note on how Hearths will generally actually be loving.<br /> <br /> That and some guidelines on how they\u2019re named (particularly the Three Kingdoms influences), since coming up with a decent name for\u2026 anything is often a chore. Hmm, it\u2019s also interesting that the culture of the Scarlet Dynasty regards placing loyalty to Hearth above House is not the worst thing in the world. I\u2019m guessing that the benefit to the Empress was promulgating that attitude in general and letting it unfold organically, and only occasionally in the form of having the loyalty of a Hearth member and leveraging that to get Dynasts to act contrary to House.<br /> <br /> It was said in the opening fiction that the kinship oath varies based on cultural background, so I wonder what the most basic standard for what constitutes a functional oath is.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a repeated emphasis on Hearths arising from adventure and conflict, but I wonder if they\u2019ll confer benefits to more\u2026 peaceful life. Hmm, the idea seems to be that it necessitates being active, if not travelling, even if one\u2019s purpose is more cultural indulgence or journey of discovery than fighting. Yes, if settling down is the kind of thing that causes a Hearth to drift apart, it probably doesn\u2019t really provide much in the way of more administrative functions. Not to knock the emotional and psychological benefits of having a mystically bonded friend to seek repose with.<br /> Awww, the idea that they make their rededication public and that other Dynasts are moved by it is sweet.<br /> <br /> Ah, good, they actually do describe the necessities of the oath. Let\u2019s see, nothing so much as their names, the intent to form a Hearth and flaring the animas concurrently. Suddenly, I\u2019ve got an image of a Kinship sworn between Exalted who don\u2019t even speak the same language. I\u2019m guessing that the benefits of it will be most evident once we see the Charms; I had reservations about anything like Co-operative Charms still existing, but if it\u2019s been folded into the function of Kinships, that resolves a lot of my concerns. And yeesh, the process of ending that tie sounds brutal even when it doesn\u2019t entail active betrayal.<br /> <br /> And coming to the end of their lives\u2026<br /> <br /> There seems to be a balancing act there; needing to have worked long enough to acquire money to support one\u2019s lifestyle after having officially stopped working, while doing it early enough to be hale and strong. Suddenly I\u2019m seeing a factor that might contribute to so many dying relatively young; the desire to go on an adventure or get involved in an intrigue with a big payout, getting them in the path of something dangerous. Dragon Blooded are probably still strong enough that a decent number actually make it to that youthful retirement, while I suppose that a disproportionate number of the actually elderly just spent a century or two running a family business operation and living off of a lifetime of savings and investment.<br /> <br /> I do wonder what kinds of hobbies a Dynast might have when they\u2019re not traveling to strange, exotic locations and running the lives of the younger generation. Actually, no, that\u2019s probably the wrong attitude to take to it; more what the matriarch and any of her advisors do. It\u2019s more about being a teacher and advisor and enhancing one\u2019s image with their achievements.<br /> <br /> Heh, for all that I\u2019ve inferred motivations for assassination, I like that there\u2019s at least one spot that actually illustrates it directly, even if the idea of killing somebody rather than being obligated to fund their retirement is among the more grim.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see if there\u2019s any change to inheritance law\u2026 half goes to the spouse or eldest child, the rest to the other children, not generally relied upon, and contrary wills frequently overturned in court\u2026 nope, pretty much the same. Dynasts need to earn their own money.<br /> <br /> And last of all, funerals, something that I\u2019ve wanted to know about since we got descriptions of how the House founders are interred. Yyyyyeah, it looks as though having one\u2019s body preserved in such a manner is a privilege afforded only to somebody whose remains might be the centre of a House\u2019s rituals, and otherwise you get your lavish funeral followed by cremation. I am amused by the idea that they have a belief that the Immaculate Dragons can be swayed by endorsements and arguments made at the funeral.<br /> <br /> Aha, but there <i>are</i> a few more uncommon funeral methods based on devotion to particular Immaculate Dragons. Pasiap\u2019s emphasis on construction and monuments is expressed in mummification and interment in a mausoleum (I can imagine Mnemon arranging a particularly elaborate setup for her descendants to pay homage to in the event of her death, possibly based on being seated upon a throne), Danaa\u2019d goes in for burial at sea for obvious reasons, Sextes Jylis has one\u2019s body broken down and used to feed a lavish garden, and Mela gets you fed to the birds (I particularly like the detail of how their bones are ground for the bread of sparrows and the like). So yeah, the methods for founders are still unique, but it\u2019s all good that there\u2019s some colourful diversity to their funerals.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s some very good work in the society of the Scarlet Dynasty; a lot to give texture to the background of these characters and quite a bit for games set entirely on the Blessed Isle to work with. I admire how it\u2019s able to have such detail across a number of areas while still being very focused, not needing to describe the Realm as a whole (validating the separation of books) without anything feeling like a waste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:35:02-07:00","id":1203605,"title":"","content":"So, I\u2019ve tried to mostly avoid details about parts of the book that I haven\u2019t read yet, but I\u2019ve managed to pick up a few very mild and vague hints about the outcastes chapter, and I am pretty jazzed up for it.<br /> <br /> However, it\u2019s late, so for the moment I\u2019m just going to see how much of Lookshy that I can cover.<br /> <br /> After the fiction.<br /> <br /> Cutting in on our signature Hearth\u2019s son of Lookshy, sitting in a teahouse patronised by refugees. Heh, what\u2019s a good party of adventurers without a bawdy musician to round them out? Even Dune had somebody like that. Hell, the Owls of Ga\u2019Hoole movie had a character like that. Ah, but here we\u2019re seeing the more fraught side to a multicultural Kinship, when those cultures happen to be traditional enemies, particularly in the midst of a Time of Tumult. From the prior chapter, I suppose that the likes of Eshuvar providing info to Mathar would not be considered the worst kind of crime (even if it would be discouraged), but I like the way that the Lookshyan makes a point of not wanting to ask them, and that leveraging their bond in that manner would be a violation.<br /> And it\u2019s cute that they work in a reference to the old Sidereals in teacups meme.<br /> <br /> As an introduction to outcastes, it\u2019s a bit non-specific, but it does at least cover the basics of an outsider\u2019s perspective on the Time of Tumult, as well as a Dragon Blood that is a bit less used to privilege and command.<br /> <br /> So, Chapter Four: Beyond the Realm, starting off with Lookshy.<br /> <br /> I felt a bit of ambiguity before, but this is fairly clear cut on the order of contagion and invasion (to the extent that it matters). There is one very significant difference made to the backstory of Lookshy, though (really a combination of many small differences); the Seventh Legion is no longer a force that was assigned to protect Deheleshen to the last, and set up camp there in perpetual deference to those orders, but is now a legion that was far East (possibly in the midst of the fighting) and made its way west, collecting stragglers as it went.<br /> I won\u2019t say that being assigned as a garrison to a city on the edge of the Inland Sea in preparation for a Fair Folk breakthrough made no sense, but I do think that there\u2019s something beneficial to the Seventh Legion having been more battle scarred at the time, as well as the idea that they initially populated their city with a horde of displaced peoples. Ah, and their standing orders are quite different\u2026 yeah, acting as a provisional government of the fallen Shogunate makes a <i>bit</i> more sense as a basis for resisting the Realm than holding out on a final order to lock down a city.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think the structure of the city itself is very different, but\u2026 I don\u2019t know, somehow I\u2019m getting more of a Ba Sing Se vibe from them now than I used to. Maybe it\u2019s just because the description of the rings is short and sweet, and my mind can immediately go to a stark comparable image. Or I don\u2019t know, maybe some of the rings have actually had their functions and residents altered a bit. I <i>do</i> think the idea that they were at different elevations may not have been there, or have been less pronounced, but don\u2019t quote me on that. What\u2019s important there is that it\u2019s giving me a feeling of Lookshy being something more\u2026 Final Fantasy than I felt in the past, and I\u2019m liking it.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, Gentes. Before I get into what the book says, a personal perspective: I can\u2019t recall if, in the past, I expressed my reservation about Gentes as having been a thing only for the First Age, or extended that to the Shogunate itself. My reason for that emerged from a particular sidebar in the First Edition Dragon Blooded book that expressed the Great Houses as a relatively novel operation of the Empress, and I was drawn to the idea that in the First Age, the number of Terrestrials and security of their bloodlines made heavy emphasis on big family groups less of a thing. Obviously, that wasn\u2019t really a view that the writers shared, and I have no issue with that\u2026 but with my recent assessment of Great Houses as elaborate tribal groups organised in that manner, I wondered if I may be able to express <i>that</i> as the innovation of the Empress, in comparison to a prior era in which Dragon Blooded families actually were more fun-sized, cohesive groupings. So I\u2019ll be interested to see just how far the presentation of Lookshy\u2019s families strays from that reconciliation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Okay, from the outset, we\u2019ve got the return of that line contrasting Dragon Blooded numbers with quality of bloodlines, but in this context, I\u2019m suspecting that it refers to their openness to outcastes from around the Scavenger Lands; that they\u2019ll recruit you and marry you into their families without fretting too much on the quality of your progenitive Essence. Fair enough there.<br /> The way that it\u2019s talking about gentes suggests to me that there\u2019s more of them, which also lends itself to the idea that they\u2019re individually smaller than the expansive structures of Great Houses. I like the language incorporating the idea that there are a number of \u201cnew money\u201d gentes. If I\u2019m reading one line correctly, that includes cases in which a family does not strictly need to have Dragon Blooded actually come from it, although I suspect that a newly elevated gens of mortals is considered an ideal entry point for some immigrant Exalt looking to make their way in the city.<br /> <br /> The General Staff\u2026 I\u2019ve never been entirely clear on if the government of Lookshy was reserved for the Exalted. Nevertheless, I do appreciate having a concise breakdown of the structure of their governing body.<br /> <br /> Let me just peak ahead\u2026 oh damn, Lookshy covers about two-thirds of the chapter alone. Yeah, I\u2019m going to check out this section introducing the Gentes Major and the sidebar on the city\u2019s factions, and then call it a night.<br /> <br /> So, the Gentes Major have fluctuated over the centuries\u2026 I\u2019m guessing that it\u2019s not quite like the Great Houses, where when a House is gone, it\u2019s gone for good, and more a case where for a few families, there\u2019s been back and forth on whether one\u2019s gens is considered major or minor, with the latter a bit easier to recover from (or rise out of starting as), in comparison to the Realm\u2019s \u201cnot at all\u201d. Their system is patrilineal but otherwise egalitarian, aaaand\u2026 did Lookshy always have a position of authority called imperator? If not, is the intended reference to Ancient Rome, or to Mad Max? Either is good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Uh-hmm, major gentes get disproportionate representation in the upper ranks, allowing them to enact policy in accordance with their views, aaaand that leads to the affairs of the city being more tumultuous. I want to say that this has generally been expressed as uneven implementation of policy, rather than overt infighting and persistent violence.<br /> <br /> And to finish, Lookshy\u2019s five political factions: Mercenaries (not heavily described beyond their status in the city, but from context I can guess that their position is to fight only as circumstantial needs and being called upon by allies and clients warrants), the Interventionists (wants to use the army to elevate Lookshy\u2019s status in the Province to more overtly controlling, I\u2019m guessing by active military intervention to adjust the structures of their neighbours and decide regional conflicts in accordance with their own needs), the Isolationists (alternately want Lookshy to close ranks and adopt a kind of siege mentality, or de-emphasize the military culture altogether), the Imperialists (want to go further than the Interventionists and start actively conquering other territories and build an empire as a foundation for a new Shogunate, with a particular eye on abandoned satrapies), and the Purists (seem very similar to the Interventionists, but whereas the priority of that faction is on securing the city\u2019s hegemony and intervention for the sake of that goal, these ones want to actively crusade against elements of the region that are contrary to Immaculate values).<br /> <br /> I believe that all of these factions existed verbatim in prior Editions, and\u2026 yeah, I still find them all to be solid political divisions in views of the manner in which Lookshy\u2019s military power (the central purpose of the city) should be employed. Not much else to say about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:06:41-07:00","id":1203817,"title":"","content":"Have to agree on the layout. Lookshy was always sort of tiered but not it really does have more of a clearly Ba Sing Se feel. Which is awesome because Ba Sing Se is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:41:30-07:00","id":1203825,"title":"","content":"So, five major Gentes, conveniently allowing them to have one for each Aspect. \ud83d\ude09 I can barely remember anything about them, except a little bit about Karal, so I\u2019ll just assess them on their own merits for now.<br /> <br /> Hmm, if Gens Amilar was founded by a defecting Realm general, I would assume that it was some time around the original invasions, but if it was supposed to be recent then I would guess that they\u2019re only a generation or two away from Vondy Beulen (whom I would assume to have died fighting ahead of time). It doesn\u2019t say specifically, but I guess that their tendency to employ chemical and biological warfare goes against the tactical doctrine of Lookshy in general.<br /> <br /> Errrrr\u2026 I find them to be an intresting contrast to the similar House Ledaal, with an intellectual tradition that is at odds with the ideology of the state, at least insofar as they want to push Lookshy to interventionism. Still, it\u2019s good that they\u2019ve also got a priority of recovering and studying First Age knowledge, especially with the storyline of the city\u2019s diminishing resources.<br /> <br /> Okay, tell me about Karal\u2026 they stretch back to the city\u2019s beginning, they\u2019ve got that whole thing of charisma and embodying national ideals, standard so far\u2026 I think there\u2019s a good mix in the projected career paths for them. I like the idea that, on the whole, they care about the well-being of the people of Lookshy and the River Province, but their passions lead them to being internally conflicted about what serves that purpose. Aaaand I did always like that point that they make a priority on presenting a unified front to the rest of the city, whatever their internal disputes.<br /> <br /> (I feel it\u2019s a little bit odd to not at least be told about the family imperators)<br /> <br /> Maheka is good with its more even mix of crafting businesses than the likes of House Mnemon. Plus the contrast with the other gentes in being cautiously conservative to the point of inaction (although I\u2019d say that in play, that has to be approached carefully to ensure that they\u2019re not reduced to being an obstacle).<br /> <br /> Ah, here\u2019s at least one reference to an imperator, even if it\u2019s only in the form of being an authority that people who stray from the party line are concerned with.<br /> <br /> Teresu might be their navy, but it looks to me like it\u2019s more of the arbiter of their soft power, through the trade and projecting the city\u2019s image. I imagine that keeping up appearances in Lookshy\u2019s society is good practice for that. Not much else I can say about them.<br /> <br /> I guess I could characterise Yushoto as a kind of\u2026 altruistic spy? People taking to heart the idea that the best charity is the kind that isn\u2019t advertised? It stands out, at least, and is a good take on the Wood Aspect attitude.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say it\u2019s to be expected that you wouldn\u2019t really be a major gens if you widely held political views that deviated from the status quo. I do like some implications of that, though; that a lot of the agitation in the city is coming up from the roots.<br /> <br /> Yeeaahhh, I don\u2019t really have much to say about the gentes. There\u2019s nothing wrong with them, and I do understand the necessity of them being less detailed considering the small arena that they have to deal in, but it does keep them from being among the more interesting things in the game to me. I feel they work more as aspects of the overall fabric of Lookshy, rather than focused on in their own right (alternatively, <i>that</i> they\u2019re written mostly as aspects of Lookshy makes them less compelling to read). Even Gens Karal is one that I remember primarily because I like the story between Linwei and Fire-Orchid. I would say Amilar\u2019s unorthodoxy is the one with the biggest draw.<br /> <br /> Hmm, given the description of gentes earlier on in the chapter, I would have expected a few more than a bit better than twelve. That might just be me needing my sense of the city\u2019s scale adjusted.<br /> I do think the sense of history in Gens Kiriga is interesting, both for themselves and the image that can give for what Lookshy was like before; a more imperialist period that exhausted itself. Nefvarin stood out to me, but that was mostly because of that old subversion in the family of the city founder having a lower status, and I like the further idea that their fortunes were tied to the Legion\u2019s dwindling skyships, plus the little plot hook of (I assume) going for the Sword of Creation.<br /> <br /> Ahh yes, the Gunzota Incident was that time when a whole bunch were turned into crystal. I have a very mild sense that it used to be an accident, the result of tampering with a machine they had insufficient understanding of, rather than a deliberate attack. I\u2019d say that Lookshy has generally less room for intrigue than the Realm, so providing this one big secret underlying them has merit.<br /> <br /> Just a little check ahead\u2026<br /> <br /> Okay, when you say there are around a dozen minor gentes, seven of them is not a handful. &gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, gens involved in a lot of commerce and city inventory\u2026 ah, I like Sirel having roots in the Realm that it can use to make contacts with patricians and cadets, as well as a general follow-up to notes on Shogunate families being expelled. There\u2019s an interesting novelty to a family that is built around trying to capitalise upon the legacy of a legendary ancestor (I see a little deconstruction of any Shogunate sense of hero worship), plus a possible claim on another state\u2019s monarchy. I think there\u2019s a lot of potential in a family that holds itself as culturally separate from and preceding the Seventh Legion. And Yan Tu\u2026 is a little bit generic.<br /> <br /> Social classes in Lookshy are about the same, although I think some details of indentured servitude and slavery are different.<br /> <br /> And next is a section about the progression of their lives, so I\u2019ll leave it there for the moment. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:38:38-07:00","id":1203867,"title":"","content":"The Gunzota Incident was a covert assassination attempt on a leadership cadre that was drifting towards nepotism and corruption when it was first mentioned in <i>Outcastes</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:54:26-07:00","id":1203876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200398#post1200398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heyeyey, the detail of Nellens being father of Sesus was in previous Editions, so that's fine, but don't go trying to tell me things from later in the book than I have read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be precise, i think Nellens the consort was the father of Sesus <b>and</b> Ledaal, but would have to check the books to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T10:53:38-07:00","id":1203892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203876#post1203876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be precise, i think Nellens the consort was the father of Sesus <b>and</b> Ledaal, but would have to check the books to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was indeed the case, though in 3e Ledaal is apparently just a completely different person on the whole timlien of things, being the Empress' granddaughter instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T12:22:19-07:00","id":1203940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203825#post1203825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even Gens Karal is one that I remember primarily because I like the story between Linwei and Fire-Orchid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think if they want the Gentes to be more compelling, there should be more interpersonal stories. A big draw for a lot of the Realm Great Houses is the people in them and how they relate to each other. The reason people remember, and care about, Gens Karal is because of the political and social drama involving Karal Fire Orchid, her mother, and her brothers. We need some of that for the other Gentes as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nefvarin stood out to me, but that was mostly because of that old subversion in the family of the city founder having a lower status, and I like the further idea that their fortunes were tied to the Legion\u2019s dwindling skyships, </div> </div> </div>Whoever decided to narratively murder the Lookshy Sky Guard has <i>much</i> to answer for.<br /> <br /> Skywolf for life, mofos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have a very mild sense that it used to be an accident, the result of tampering with a machine they had insufficient understanding of, rather than a deliberate attack. </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of the cover story. The Gunzota Incident has always been a coup d'etat right from its inception.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T12:42:16-07:00","id":1203947,"title":"","content":"You know, from now on, I'm just going to qualify my vague recollections with &quot;but I was probably mistaken about that&quot; or some such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Whoever decided to narratively murder the Lookshy Sky Guard has </span></span></span></div><i>much</i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to answer for.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bCome on, we've (by which I mean the forum as a whole) literally had arguments about magitech for years. We've got a shiny new book now, why not dedicate all of that energy to fun new stuff like what kind of military forces Prasad might have.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:14:39-07:00","id":1203966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203947#post1203947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCome on, we've (by which I mean the forum as a whole) literally had arguments about magitech for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we will for many more!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We've got a shiny new book now, why not dedicate all of that energy to fun new stuff like what kind of military forces Prasad might have. </div> </div> </div>You know, that's a super interesting question I hadn't considered. Initial thought after not a ton of reflection: Prasad is engaged in building an empire, and they're Realm-descended, so they likely have an army that is, bare minimum, SEMI professional, and they almost certainly have <i>The Thousand Correct Actions of the Upright Soldier</i>, which if you can get your officer corps to read and internalize is going to give you a decent base to work from. They probably have a structure that is recognizably at least based off the Imperial Legion.<br /> <br /> However, their specific cultural milieu and Prasad's heavily caste and clan based society also leads me to expect they don't have full-on meritocratic we-serve-the-state-and-only-the-state-all-are-equal-in-service style Imperial legions. There are going to be some severe social fault lines running through their military, and probably more of what we'd recognize as corruption or inefficiency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:43:59-07:00","id":1203975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203892#post1203892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was indeed the case, though in 3e Ledaal is apparently just a completely different person on the whole timlien of things, being the Empress' granddaughter instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting as it breaks somewhat from a fanbase expectation that all house founders were the Empress' biological, adopted (or supposed in Nellens' case) children.<br /> It also creates a funny &quot;two Ledaals&quot; continuity bug between editions that i can certainly see Sidereal STs exploiting for drama, fun &amp; profit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:57:26-07:00","id":1203977,"title":"","content":"Exalted: The Outcaste actually encouraged making up more lesser gentes. It also listed wholly mortal gentes, though since this is the Dragon-Blooded book, they're probably omitted by virtue of not being Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:31:45-07:00","id":1204011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203975#post1203975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also creates a funny &quot;two Ledaals&quot; continuity bug between editions that i can certainly see Sidereal STs exploiting for drama, fun &amp; profit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are the Two Ledaals going to team up with the Four Rafaras?<br /> <br /> They solve crimes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T20:49:31-07:00","id":1204093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204011#post1204011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are the Two Ledaals going to team up with the Four Rafaras?<br /> <br /> They solve crimes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i had forgotten about the Rafaras....now i have to think of how would i explain/insert that scene in a game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:47:15-07:00","id":1204102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203975#post1203975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's interesting as it breaks somewhat from a fanbase expectation that all house founders were the Empress' biological, adopted (or supposed in Nellens' case) children.<br /> It also creates a funny &quot;two Ledaals&quot; continuity bug between editions that i can certainly see Sidereal STs exploiting for drama, fun &amp; profit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it depends on parts fo the fanbase I guess. Tepet never really felt &quot;adopted&quot; save in the legal sense to me even in 1e. Of the current 11 Houses, him, Nellens' descendents, and Ledaal are not direct children of her's. Apparently Iselsi wasn't either and I'm sure plenty of other forumer houses weren't either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:59:59-07:00","id":1204104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204102#post1204102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it depends on parts fo the fanbase I guess. Tepet never really felt &quot;adopted&quot; save in the legal sense to me even in 1e. Of the current 11 Houses, him, Nellens' descendents, and Ledaal are not direct children of her's. Apparently Iselsi wasn't either and I'm sure plenty of other forumer houses weren't either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, Tepet, at least in 2e, seemed to be a case of multiple children of the Empress grouping together under the name of their common father (might have been implied to be the case for Cathak too in 1e). No idea how this stands or not in 3e.<br /> <br /> Anyway, 3e is making a point of making this room for fluidity and dynamism, both in who might found a House and how not-monolithic and potentially ephemeral even they can be, clearer than it might have been on the previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T22:10:43-07:00","id":1204106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204104#post1204104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, Tepet, at least in 2e, seemed to be a case of multiple children of the Empress grouping together under the name of their common father (might have been implied to be the case for Cathak too in 1e). No idea how this stands or not in 3e.<br /> <br /> Anyway, 3e is making a point of making this room for fluidity and dynamism, both in who might found a House and how not-monolithic and potentially ephemeral even they can be, clearer than it might have been on the previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few things in the 3e take are outright retcons. A big thing to remember mostly is that the editions of Exalted are pretty explicltiy <i>not</i> just continuations of the same settings. <br /> <br /> I think Cathak was just the Empress son in 1e. In 3e Cathak was her daughter, and a lot of the other House founders were changed to be women (and have actual write-ups this time.) Tepet is an exception though. He was a Shogunate commander who went to war against hte Empress, failed, did some heroic stuff in his surrender and she liked him enough to give him a house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:27:14-07:00","id":1204131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204106#post1204106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few things in the 3e take are outright retcons. A big thing to remember mostly is that the editions of Exalted are pretty explicltiy <i>not</i> just continuations of the same settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. I have no problem with retcons of what was small background stuff from the start anyway. It's more of a matter that haven't really read What Fire Has Wrought, so can't really separate what's outright retcon or just change of emphasis on minor referential elements with my current knowledge.<br /> <br /> And my taste for occasional lampshade hanging on those through weird bits of plotline and such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204106#post1204106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Cathak was just the Empress son in 1e. In 3e Cathak was her daughter, and a lot of the other House founders were changed to be women (and have actual write-ups this time.) Tepet is an exception though. He was a Shogunate commander who went to war against hte Empress, failed, did some heroic stuff in his surrender and she liked him enough to give him a house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tepet being an actual consort from the get go is something that has been around since 1e, if memory tricks me not, in fact i remember that being referenced in PC family backstory or some bit of subplot in at least one or two old games with my group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:10:43-07:00","id":1204230,"title":"","content":"Okay, the general culture of the Dragon Blooded of Lookshy. I think I\u2019ll mostly comment on any interesting distinctions from the Scarlet Dynasty, and their implications.<br /> <br /> I take the line on the military focus to mean that while Lookshy\u2019s Exalted has the same belief in themselves as the top of the Perfected Hierarchy, but in practical terms they express that primarily in military missions for the sake of the city and River Province, rather than having quite the variation that the Dynasty does (even if there are a few gentes that shift in those directions, and would like it if society as a whole would do the same).<br /> <br /> Given how the city is apparently named for the standing order that the Seventh Legion is operating under, I wonder what the in-character basis for the name Lookshy might be. I also wonder exactly what their standards for the emergence of a new Shogun would be; are they waiting on somebody with a proven line of descent from the last Shogun, or a hero figure who proves themselves worthy of the rank, or has it ultimately just become a point of rhetoric?<br /> <br /> Yes, I could summarise the biggest difference between the cultures as being that Dynasts are raised to see themselves as rulers of the world, while\u2026 they really need a simple word of their own to be called by\u2026 Sevens are raised with military discipline to take up officer duties. It\u2019s interesting that they don\u2019t have a focus on individual glory, considering that House Tepet\u2019s emphasis on same is part of their Shogunate legacy.<br /> <br /> Their education also seems a bit less intense, possibly because Lookshy doesn\u2019t quite have the money to maintain the more elaborate infrastructure. It\u2019s not said, but if they\u2019re married at 18, I assume they graduate from their academies by then as well.<br /> <br /> Yeah, all of this stuff about the emphasis they place upon recruitment and encouraging adoption into the gens seems to validate that point on the difference between many Dragon Blooded, and well-bred ones. Considering the status of the Dragon Blooded, the General Staff wouldn\u2019t be the first head of state to have direct authority over a form of adoption, but the actual trappings of military administration gives it an amusing image.<br /> <br /> Sooo, even when the gentes have their own sidelines, all of their members will have engaged in at least some military service. I imagine that gives the Exalted as a whole a stronger sense of national identity and loyalty than the Scarlet Dynasty does. Personally, I\u2019d want to express things like training and practice drills as forms of regular festivity that Lookshy has; not necessarily that they\u2019re engaged in frivolously, just as the format in which such activity is engaged. As I recall, the weekly archery practice that was mandatory in periods of Medieval Europe was the kind of thing that they treated as a kind of regular picnic.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I wonder if Field Forces might be a bit smaller and more specialized than the legion-like bodies of prior Editions\u2026. Nnnot necessarily, not if they have those methods of ranking. They might still be broken up to distribute on multiple fronts.<br /> <br /> My read on Valkhawsen is that its method represents a single, unified form of sorcerous initiation, as opposed to the more freeform approach of the Heptagram. It\u2019s interesting that the martial focus of Lookshy would make them more comfortable with sorcery as a whole, even if they\u2019re still wary of the special branch for summoning spirits.<br /> <br /> Hmm, is chumyo another open position of the Seventh Legion?<br /> <br /> Ahh, so the academies may be more numerous and less intensive, but they\u2019re all nationalised as a means of maintaining an orthodoxy. It also seems like a good call for them to place such emphasis on the well-being of the troops; keep it from being something that might turn in on itself.<br /> <br /> Ah, I was wondering what the Shogunate Bureaucracy was, as I have no recollection of that whatsoever. Whether it\u2019s new or not, I am amused by the image of the local equivalent of a ceremonial Imperial Court being the last remnant of the civil service. Mind, if they\u2019re addressed directly in the Lookshy Directive\u2026 did the book already say where that order originated? <br /> Hmm, with the description of their First Age Armoury having more emphasis on being gradually diminishing, the changed nature of Artifacts in general, and some of the descriptions of the Realm, I wonder if Lookshy is now less strong then the Realm as a whole (possibly apart from the potential to bring all of its Exalted to bear), and while pivotal in the capacity of the River Province to resist, would be in significant trouble if they had to deal with the Realm alone.<br /> <br /> Money is also a very strong contrast with the Realm, both in the sense that it\u2019s not a natural entitlement of the Exalted and another method to keep them cohesive through state service. If a soldier\u2019s pay is expected to be reliable, I can see the Seventh Legion being very strenuous about keeping its revenue streams constantly flowing (although <i>possibly</i> not to the point that they deliberately sabotage peace to continuously secure contracts).<br /> <br /> The significance of the Immaculate Faith of Lookshy not being a state religion feels more apparent with the preview given of The Realm, if they\u2019re focused entirely on spiritual ministrations rather than having roles such as acting as a kind of morality police. The other stuff about not proselytizing and lacking a cohesive hierarchy, that would be different but could still fit in an officially recognised system, but lacking that kind of social remit really sets them apart. It also lends itself to the plot hook about there being a faction that does want the Seventh Legion to impose those values as far as it can reach.<br /> <br /> Ah, and their belief that being Exalted does not, on its own, constitute elevated spiritual authority would make sense as the basis for their only licensing somebody with Immaculate training to summon demons and elementals.<br /> <br /> Ha, I love the idea that when Realm Wyld Hunts come within Lookshy\u2019s sphere of influence, the Seventh Legion\u2019s response is to upgrade their troops. I\u2019ve suddenly got this image of more than a few leaders of the Hunt wanting to take deliberate detours through the Scavenger Lands for that very reason, even if they\u2019re going somewhere like the Caul.<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, apparently collaborations of that type against somebody very dangerous (probably like Sha\u2019a Oka and other Lunars of the Caul) would be a matter of course. Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Does anybody want to tell me if the Code of the Righteous Warrior is new? It at least sounds like something that would resonate with House Tepet\u2019s warrior codes. In any case, it\u2019s another interesting implication on the manner in which the Faith judges the Dragon Blooded. I can also see it as a particular sticking point between monks of Lookshy and the Realm (as well as something for a few of the latter to start preaching at home).<br /> <br /> Hmm, Lookshy may not be without its issues, but it might overall be a nicer place for its Exalted to grow up, without the extreme upbringing the violence and the mind games. I mean, sure, they have mind games of their own, just without needing to end in murder.<br /> <br /> Yeah, if Lookshy wants to generally avoid direct confrontation of the Realm, I\u2019m definitely feeling that they\u2019re not as strong against them as they used to be. With what I was saying before about the difference in Immaculates, this comment about them being restricted to a certain quarter puts me in mind of the popular Lookshyan image being somebody who goes around publically castigating folks for everyday activities. I\u2019m seeing something like a bawdy comedy in which a monk goes up to some popular Lookshy shop and starts ranting and raving about its sign (possibly getting into some pratfalls as they try to tear it down). Heh, I liked the parts about House Ledaal holding a grudge against the Mask of Winters, so I\u2019m moved by the idea of them having claimed the diplomatic rights to Lookshy in pursuit of that (although I can also see some of them having reservations about the possibility of Ledaal pulling them into their own crusade, domestic reservations about Thorns aside).<br /> <br /> Hmm, has the timing of the Battle of Mishaka been changed? Didn\u2019t it used to be something that was intimately tied to the downfall of House Iselsi?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019m glad that there\u2019s at least one place in which a strong relationship with the Guild is described.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand nothing new about the city\u2019s gods. They\u2019re fine.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Lookshy is solid. Still not quite as vivid as the Scarlet Dynasty to me, but it does its job. One thing that I do have a particular liking for is the sense that they\u2019re not quite the power in opposition to the Realm that they used to be, and whether there are other new details or not, I feel that makes their relationship a bit more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T12:07:19-07:00","id":1204248,"title":"","content":"The Code of the Righteous Warrior is more set and organized in this writeup. In 1e, it was presented as much more loose, without Virtues assigned to Immaculate Dragons or elements. It still serves the same basic idea, though.<br /> <br /> The Shogunate Bureaucracy was also all the way back to 1e. It also held only symbolic significance then.<br /> <br /> Mishaka's date hasn't changed. It also didn't seem to have anything to do with the ill fortune of the Iselsi house, since that was mentioned as happening way earlier by centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-07-2018, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T12:12:57-07:00","id":1204250,"title":"","content":"God, Exalted: the Outcastes made <i>no</i> impression on me.<br /> <br /> \u200bI definitely <i>tried</i> to read all of the other parts besides just the... Shogunate calendar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:52:12-07:00","id":1204338,"title":"","content":"Is it addressed whether the 7th Legion has a recruitment policy toward Lost Eggs of the Scavenger Lands (i.e. those not born into the support system of established territorial bloodlines)? I imagine stray bastards left around Legion redoubts are a thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:15:34-07:00","id":1204342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204338#post1204338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it addressed whether the 7th Legion has a recruitment policy toward Lost Eggs of the Scavenger Lands (i.e. those not born into the support system of established territorial bloodlines)? I imagine stray bastards left around Legion redoubts are a thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they eagerly accept them and recommend to them that they get themselves adopted into a gentes instead of trying to go it solo in Lookshy (and its not hard to get into a gentes, very very eager for more dragon blooded). There is no official punishment for not getting adopted but it does unofficially hamper their career since they have to compete with people that have gentes backing them with their influence on top of whatever merit they actually posses individually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-07-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:21:21-07:00","id":1204344,"title":"","content":"*posted in wrong thread - IGNORE ME!*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-07-2018, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:30:30-07:00","id":1204347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204338#post1204338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it addressed whether the 7th Legion has a recruitment policy toward Lost Eggs of the Scavenger Lands (i.e. those not born into the support system of established territorial bloodlines)? I imagine stray bastards left around Legion redoubts are a thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I feel as though you're asking two questions there. One is about the general policy that they have towards accepting foreign Dragon Blooded (lost egg being a specifically Realm piece of terminology), and the other is about the attitude towards children conceived out of wedlock.<br /> <br /> The general openness of Lookshy to recruiting other Dragon Blooded is described in detail, but natural children aren't really referred to.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose there are two things at work there. On the one hand, Lookshy being patrilineal might mean that men are indeed allowed to claim their children by any woman as members of their own family. On the other, if they're operating on a system of accepting and adopting Dragon Blooded anyway, I imagine that in the majority of cases, they don't bother <i>until</i> such children prove themselves Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat would be a bit like how it worked in prior Editions for the Realm, except that there, men who wanted to claim their children had to do it just about after they were born, and while such didn't immediately become members of their Houses, the men were expected to provide for their upbringing, meaning that they were taking a risk if their children did not prove to be Exalted. If they didn't make such a claim (and the financial obligation that came with it) early, then in the event that the child Exalted, they'd fall under the remit of the Arbiters.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut Lookshy doesn't seem to carry that same attitude of &quot;if there's a 1% chance that your child will Exalt, you need to treat it like an absolute certainty&quot;, nor have a direct system in which Exalted outside of the gentes are made wards of the state, so I can see Lookshy's men having a lot more flexibility.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen it comes to trying to get the government to approve an adoption, I imagine that being able to credibly claim that you're the child's biological father is a very strong basis. And if they never did Exalt, then you don't need to put anything into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:31:18-07:00","id":1204348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204344#post1204344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SORCERER OF THE WHITE REGISTER tier has appeared! Anyone who wanted a custom Charm but missed an available slot before, this is your chance!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think you've posted in the wrong thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:31:56-07:00","id":1204349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204348#post1204348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think you've posted in the wrong thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I did, sorry!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T19:21:56-07:00","id":1204388,"title":"","content":"And now to finish off the chapter with the rest of the outcastes.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit, I\u2019ve already gotten a vague sense of what some of these entail from surrounding discussion. It got me thinking about some of the premises of the Exalted when we were coming into this Edition. Between introducing the likes of Exigents, and the notion of as yet unrevealed types of Exalted, I recall people displaying a very distinct sense that the setting was going to start bursting at the seams with an eclectic variety of Exalted (some of whom did not respond positively to the idea). With time, I personally find that the ultimate realisation of the concepts was a lot more subdued (which I think was all to the good), and yet some of the principles seems to have found a home in the Dragon Blooded. I will say, in hindsight, it does seem like the Terrestrial Exalted, with their numbers and diversity and being spread far and wide across the setting, had a largely untapped potential for hosting a lot of weirdness deviating from the orthodoxy of the Realm and even Lookshy. Jenna Moran certainly recognised such; I\u2019ll be interested to see the specifics of the ideas that they came up with.<br /> <br /> For a start, though, I do think it\u2019s good to emphasize the notion that a lot of outcastes stand alone, and a bit of discussion of what that entails. I like the idea that many of them are driven by the example of the Scarlet Empress, even if it\u2019s possible that many far flung Exalted know the barest details about her, as well as the potential that the Dynasty represents for sworn kin. Mind, given the description of outcastes from the perspective of the Realm, I imagine that such an endeavour is most successful when one meets Dynasts engaged in business around the Threshold, rather than journeying to the Blessed Isle expecting a warm reception.<br /> <br /> So, a sidebar giving a brief description of some extra outcaste groups:<br /> <br /> I recall the Cult of the Violet Fang being mentioned earlier, but can\u2019t recall many of their details. I like the description of their home base, since structures carved directly from gemstones have always said \u201cFair Folk\u201d to me, and I like the idea of them having something like the treasure questing that the Raksha of Editions past engaged in with unshaped, particularly if the opponents are their own immortal ancestors.<br /> <br /> The Grass Spiders have been in the game for a while, although I\u2019m still not entirely sure what they\u2019re about; not what they do, that\u2019s clear enough, but why they do it. Maybe there\u2019s a hint in the idea of them going about assassination artistically? Perhaps their proximity to Lookshy and the Realm makes secrecy and criminal services a matter of preserving independence? They never quite had a lot going for them.<br /> <br /> A secret cadre of Terrestrials that have resided in Yu-Shan since time immemorial, on the other hand, seems like an intriguing premise (and a firm nail through the heart of Terrestrials being largely forbidden from the divine city). I particularly like the plot hook of them occasionally being cast out of Heaven, not just for the potential culture shock, but for the seed of friends and allies with dark backstories and hidden agendas.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a nomadic society of Dragon-Blooded, particularly with the isolationist bent that they have. In contrast there\u2019s the more recent desertion of Saloy Hin, and I like how their story has been changed from being on the hunt for a superweapon to leading a patchwork army around a more complicated strategic plan. I particularly enjoy the novelty of them, rather than being a mercenary force, or even trying to conquer their locality, are gathering and distributing munitions through the Realm\u2019s most lucrative satrapies as part of a long-term goal to return home for the big prize.<br /> <br /> And a bit of a more compelling mystery than the Grass Spiders in the form of Yatani\u2019s Children and their odd claims of an extraterrestrial (so to speak) origin.<br /> <br /> Now, what about some of the big ones\u2026<br /> <br /> I like the imagery of the Wanasaan, with their distinct appearance and how their schtick is reminiscent of a few good wandering exorcist/paranormal investigator stories. With all the talk of sorcery recently, I appreciate another vivid example of a form of initiation, and I appreciate a firm example of Terrestrials involved in some freaky magic not just because of the variety it lends them throughout Creation, but because it gives a sense of context for the kinds of powers that Dynastic Houses like Ledaal and Ragara might develop. I might have liked them to be a bit bigger, but I enjoy the manner in which their small size drives action.<br /> <br /> The Sisterhood of Pearls combines a couple of good things from the periphery of the Realm; Immaculate heresy, and Dynasts (or close enough) being far enough from home to break away and start their own game, sans blackjack and hookers. Plus the idea that their heterodoxy emphasizes pacifism and egalitarianism, of all things. Heh, the subversion of many common perceptions of the Exalted alone\u2026 I appreciate the motivations behind the growing division in their community, both for either side having a reasonable basis for what it wants to do and the manner in which its criticisms for the other are rooted in their ideology, and how they really <i>don\u2019t</i> want to be torn apart. It\u2019s a compelling dilemma surrounding a complicated situation without an easy answer.<br /> <br /> Hmm, the Temple of the Reverent Whisper\u2026 you know, for a moment there, I thought that what it was saying was that they were a group of Terrestrials dedicated to providing sex work for gods, which seemed both narrow, and a bit of an odd throwback to late-First/early-Second Edition ideas about the Dragon Blooded being the ultimate courtesans. But the novelty of their service instead taking the form of them offering specialised forms of worship to divinities with particular tastes, taking advantage of their greater hardiness and capability? On its own, that\u2019s genius, but I find it to also be another strong example of the kinds of stories that are unique to the Dragon Blooded. It\u2019s a kind of\u2026 this is the sort of story that you could <i>only</i> do with Exalted that function as a group like this, and it\u2019s in a kind of servile role, but it\u2019s still something that emphasizes their power and dignity as Exalted, which also helps to think of distinct ways that they might have served in the Old Realm (and might relate anew to the Solars) that makes them more than just lackeys or middle-management.<br /> <br /> And finishing off with the Seven Storms Brotherhood, which seems like a nice straightforward gang of bandits\u2026. with trained attack hyenas. Neat. They manage to stand out with some very vivid personalities at their head. If nothing else, I would appreciate the insight into the strongest possibility yet for realising the villains of Ninja Scroll in the game. It\u2019s curious that I never would have considered Dragon Blooded in that role before, but that\u2019s what this half of the chapter is about, eh?<br /> <br /> Kudos on the outcastes here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T13:05:01-07:00","id":1204950,"title":"","content":"Ohhh the day I'm having, the next section of the book cannot come quickly enough.<br /> <br /> \u200bHere's the plan: Character Creation and Traits shouldn't take very long to go through. They're generally short chapters as it is, and most of their content is fairly elementary. Plus the format of shorter sections on focused, technical subjects is easier to digest than prose detailing the fiction of the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bCharms are definitely going to be long, so even if I do intend to read all of them, in order (and it's not a full serving of them), I can only see it being worthwhile commenting on ones that have distinctly interesting effects, contrast notably against mechanics from prior Editions, and any general trends that I can discern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T14:13:36-07:00","id":1204974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204950#post1204950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCharms are definitely going to be long, so even if I do intend to read all of them, in order (and it's not a full serving of them), I can only see it being worthwhile commenting on ones that have distinctly interesting effects, contrast notably against mechanics from prior Editions, and any general trends that I can discern.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a good thing, because I'm planning to cover them in <i>excruciating detail</i> in my own WIR. I always wanted to do an analysis on what themes the Solar set conveys, and I think a comparative analysis with the DB charmset is going to be a fantastic place for this.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Honestly, at this point I'm tempted to temporarily put everything else on ice just so I can finally get to talking about the crunch.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:28:05-07:00","id":1205192,"title":"","content":"Ah good, our next part is relatively early.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve already seen the chapter fiction with Arada, since it was what came with the House Tepet preview. Suffice to say, it\u2019s a nice little account of the Exalted at war, between elements like the weird magics that they employ and the brutal battles. Plus the nice account of a higher Essence Dragon Blood, with the aid of a Hearth mate, putting down a Solar (who still hardly seems weak in the example).<br /> <br /> So, the character creation chapter; should be fairly boilerplate.<br /> <br /> Aspect Abilities are the same as they ever were, but I already knew that. What\u2019s <i>really</i> interesting is that they now get a full five Favoured Abilities. I was wondering if they would do that; in discussions about the Dragon Blooded in the past, it was noted that their Aspect Abilities were already diverse that even with the three they used to have, you could get a fairly diverse array of starting characters. But now, between the additional Abilities and the manner in which Charms are going to work, with every Ability having elements and its Signature, you have latitude to build any Aspect virtually any way that you want. I think that\u2019s a very good change, as I know people have had strong character concepts but struggled with which Aspect to give on the grounds of how to get the Abilities that they want.<br /> <br /> I also already knew about the additional specialities you can get based on the character\u2019s background. I find something perversely amusing in how education at Pasiap\u2019s Stair would give one specialties in Athletics and Resistance.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d also say that additional dots in certain key Merits is a good and balanced way to represent the additional power that comes from a privileged upbringing.<br /> <br /> Aaand that\u2019s the chapter done. I like how, even in something as simple as character creation, there was a standout detail. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Next!<br /> <br /> Now a chapter fiction from the perspective of lost egg Kingfisher Swift, and her adopted patrician family. I like the perspective on a family member growing old before your eyes.<br /> <br /> Oh no, her career is over?! Those goddamn Cathaks. {shakes fist}<br /> <br /> I like how so many of the chapter fictions are offering a different cultural perspective on the place of Dragon Blooded in generally, and the Realm specifically. In particular, Swift\u2019s sense of disillusionment in the Realm after having been brought in with the message of a lost egg\u2019s prospects, and the manner in which she and her niece/household matriarch are discussing their own opportunities in the face of coming war, with innuendo and implication. It also inspires a neat little plot hook, of Dynasts going to war and being shocked by an uprising of patricians backed by outcastes in key strategic locations. I\u2019ve often thought about how the Realm could resemble the Chinese Warring States, with many of the larger kingdoms often fighting over control of small but important states lying in between them, some of which had assets to maintain a measure of independence. I never considered the Imperial City itself in that role, somewhere between a haven of power for some strong patrician families and holdout of loyalism to the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> Now, let\u2019s see if I can quickly get through what new tricks the Dragon Blooded get.<br /> <br /> The distributions of existing Merits is all familiar and basic. I expected that Prasadi Dragon Blooded to be able to get Cult, what with being gods, and I quite appreciate a breakdown of what levels of Resources actually mean to the Dragon Blooded, especially how little to none can represent being severely indebted.<br /> <br /> Now, what\u2019s new\u2026<br /> <br /> Ohohoho God, a Merit to represent their fancy titles or nicknames, such as the Roseblack. That is priceless (and I mean that in the best manner possible). That\u2019s the kind of thing that I like specifically for my own fascination with names, and I think being able to occasionally upgrade stunts based off of it is a fine mechanical realisation.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m guessing that the Well-Bred Merit is at least partially covering the old Breeding Background, although if it\u2019s still exclusive to Dragon Blooded\u2026 So yeah, like they used to say, the slightly more abstract notion of improved odds for children to Exalt, and the firmer one of getting a tasty automatic success in bargaining rolls in which having a good pedigree is a farctor. Useful, but not with the sense of being mandatory that the old Background\u2019s extra motes was.<br /> <br /> Oh, is that the extent of them? Well, I must admit to being a little bit disappointed that there never was a Breeding Merit for mortals. Ah well, let\u2019s see about these flaws.<br /> <br /> Or rather, flaw singular. An inversion of the Merit for the likes of outcastes and leftover children makes sense, and can probably add a nice sense of texture to possible social interactions in the Realm, in return for the bonus xp.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if there would be a discussion on children Exalting in the absence of a Storytelling chapter, and a sidebar right next to the associated Merits is surely the best place. Good good; in place of a dice roll, providing a general ratio (something that I\u2019ve always wanted) as a guideline for Storytellers. I presume that this discussion of ratios to pedigrees is assuming that one is effectively husbanding their progenitive Essence; so if you\u2019re a pair of Dynasts with some mortals or leftover children in your family history, even if you maximize progenitive Essence in every child, odds of it taking are about fifty-fifty, whereas if your bloodline is consistently strong across generations, you can expect it of the majority of your children. But since even the best odds can fail, and with the manner in which statistics works, there are still some outlying cases of deviations from that standard; a high pedigree couple might improbably produce numerous mortals, while a lower one might have a few extra. It\u2019s a good, solid picture of the Dynasty.<br /> <br /> Next up are the Aspect write-ups; I\u2019ll be looking forward to these in the full book, as I expect the art pieces to really make them pop. For now, I\u2019ll mostly be interested in discussion of things such as Aspect markings and anima powers, since I expect the main body of the write-ups themselves to be fairly familiar.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the description of the Air Aspect is fairly standard. I\u2019ve actually got my pdf of the First Edition book to compare on a few notes, and I observe that one thing that\u2019s a bit different from them is a more detailed perspective on the place an Aspect within a Hearth, so that\u2019s nice; generate some of the dynamics they could have.<br /> <br /> Uh-huh, Aspect markings of pale skin, cool feels and smells and the occasional visual effect of wind or electricity. And the anima\u2026 wait, are they doing the same thing as the Solars, where the anima powers are described in detail a bit further on? Yeah, I suddenly remembered that was what they did before just before I got to this part, and I can see here they they\u2019re described, but without the mechanical breakdowns. I\u2019ll save comment on those until I see them in their full forms. For the moment, I like the touch of the light of which even a Dragon Blood\u2019s anima is composed resembling light with a particular association of the element, such as reflecting off of ice.<br /> <br /> With that, there isn\u2019t much to say about the other Aspects, beyond a general endorsement of some of the variety in their markings and character in their animas.<br /> <br /> Oh, I also like the revised take on exactly what the basis of their Aspect Abilities is, particularly the Fire one with the idea of excelling at things that draw attention and give them unrestrained access.<br /> <br /> Okay, <i>now</i> we\u2019re on to the anima banner. There\u2019s the breakdown of levels, something that I think they didn\u2019t often have before. Anima flux seems to not quite be the great danger that it used to be, at least unintentionally. It still has the notion of causing possible scenery damage (with the caveat of being dramatically appropriate), and the amusing element of creating a preference for hardier homes, but I think it\u2019s dropped the element in which it makes them widely averse to riding animals (although I\u2019ll reserve that until I see the Ride Charms, unless somebody in the know wishes to clarify).<br /> <br /> Now the anima powers, which have interactions with Elemental Aura of Charms. I like the detail of being able to spend a mote to have something like a minor, dramatic manifestation of your anima for purposes of convenience; it\u2019s actually the kind of thing I would have house-ruled before, given the opportunity. There\u2019s something a bit wrong if you can\u2019t, by default, snap a finger at your pipe to light it when you\u2019re a Fire Aspect (or Air, with a spark of electricity).<br /> <br /> So, the powers; I\u2019m particularly interested to see the part about drawing upon one\u2019s passions and the like. Air gets to make high leaps vertically and horizontally and be resistant to falling damage, generate a slight environmental penalty on ranged attacks, and occasionally add extra dice to mental and social actions in upholding a Principle. Earth gets to boost soak and Hardness and Defence against certain Earth-themed attacks, a slight resistance to pain and physical debility, and a knockback effect to their Anima flux. Fire gets immunity to natural fire and improved soak against fire attacks, improved damage to their anima flux, and can occasionally get dice from emotional Intimacies to boost actions upholding them. Water lets you walk across the surface of water and improves mobility in difficult terrain (nice sense of their adaptability there), breath and and act within water without difficulty, and boost effects to get away from enemies and keep from being grappled. And Wood gets immunity to mundane poison from plants and improved resistance to all other poison and disease, can reduce penalties to Evasion and movement actions, and their Anima flux can inflict poison of their own.<br /> <br /> I think these additions to the anima powers are reasonably solid; they\u2019re low key as is appropriate to Dragon Blooded, but still useful and convey some nice character. The ones that give some dice bonuses also have interesting implications; between their non-Charm dice and Dragon Blooded being able to add their specialties to their dice cap, I can see some circumstances in which one can gain a rather decent bonus to a dice roll. Not with the consistency of a Solar, but if applied in the right moment\u2026<br /> <br /> And the character advancement. As I recall, there was going to be something in that for their expression of the Great Curse\u2026<br /> <br /> The Expression Bonus is about what it was with Solars, building off of one\u2019s Intimacies and Flaws, whereas the Role/Aspect Bonus\u2026 Ah, right, the Great Curse is an additional criteria for earning the experience, along with ceding the spotlight and expressing one\u2019s Aspect. I take it that their Curse will be described in a bit. The Aspect roles that can be rewarded are all what one could derive from the Aspect write-ups.<br /> <br /> Hmm, a reiteration of training times is a curious thing, since it seems about the same as in the core rules to me. The principle of raising Essence is the same, although I understand that the numbers are a bit different, and I\u2019ll be interested to compare them a bit later on.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Dragon Blooded Great Curse. The much weaker effect than on the Celestials manifests through lacking a Limit Track, instead being a more subtle influence on behaviour that is incentivized through awarding experience points if it enhances the game. I find that to be a stronger expression of the principle than before, where it was about acting in a deleterious manner if you ran out of Willpower.<br /> <br /> Air Aspects are Cursed with a potential for bad reactions to the world falling short of their ideals, become so caught up <i>in</i> ideals that they ignore the well-being of others, or become self-aggrandizing to the point of being touchy or arrogant. Earth can have a bad attitude with regards to how they defend their traditions, become intractable in upholding them, or violent or morose in response to insult or challenge of their validity. Fire can become dangerously excessive or overwhelmingly driven by extreme emotions with regards to how they relate to others or perceive themselves. Water can make perseverance into something that loses perspective or becomes extreme in its methods, as well as loosening moral standards or becoming caught up in unnecessarily circuitous planning. And Wood might make one hedonistic or thrill-seeking followed by significant emotional lows, or overbearing in relationships with others.<br /> It\u2019s an interesting take on the Curse, where the emotions and impulses are all the kinds of thing that a Dragon Blood may already have, but the benefits create an incentive to play them up at dramatic or inopportune moments that emphasize them as something that can undermine the Exalted.<br /> <br /> I think the Traits chapter is nice and lean now; it trimmed away a <i>lot</i> of unnecessary benefits to the Dragon Blooded, while seasoning a bit with some nice anima powers and incentives to play into the characterisation of Aspects.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll get a start on Charms later, although for today I\u2019ll probably just stick to the introductory parts and actually look at the Abilities over the next few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T08:57:53-07:00","id":1205237,"title":"","content":"I dug that Heart Eating Palm made it into a chapter fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:58:17-07:00","id":1205322,"title":"","content":"All right, a start on the Charms chapter. Beginning with a chapter fiction featuring Mnemon! Don\u2019t let me down now.<br /> <br /> Ah, and she\u2019s in Jiara. I\u2019m not usually a fan of that idea of immortals becoming bored with the world, but it\u2019s fitting to her particular traits; plus, it reaches my soft spot for recognition of behavioural patterns in the aggregate. In keeping with Mnemon\u2019s stronger Immaculate leanings now, I like the manner in which she expresses contempt for grandiose mortal architecture\u2026 oh, that covers her other element as well, delightful! I also appreciate this idea that she\u2019s here to personally direct operations.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaand she\u2019s thinking about how having her personal guard keep a respectful distance leaves her \u201calone as she ever was\u201d, and my heart\u2019s breaking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I like the description of her mystically taking in the city, an-oh yes, kung fu fight with Novia Claro!<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got to say, I like the idea of Mnemon being a bit light-hearted in battle, even when she\u2019s slashed to ribbons. That and the demon-summoning; she wouldn\u2019t be her without it.<br /> <br /> As a chapter fiction, it doesn\u2019t necessarily present the powers of the Dragon Blooded much more than several of the others. But it features Mnemon being haughty and kicking ass, and it\u2019s hard for me to not like such a thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, on to the actual powers\u2026 well, the outline.<br /> <br /> A fairly concise reiteration of the basic point of what Charms are, with a reference to their perception in the context of a big society of Exalted.<br /> <br /> Something that I had caught a passing glimpse of elsewhere; Dragon Blooded ultimately did <i>not</i> get free Excellencies, instead having to buy them as separate Charms. I saw Holden begin to say something about playtesting, so I presume it was found that access to such power for the Dragon Blooded was too unbalancing. Mind, I imagine that the non-Charm dice that they can occasionally get from their anima can mitigate that a bit.<br /> <br /> Elemental Aura was introduced months back, but if there\u2019s anything more mechanically detailed here\u2026 Ah, the manner in which Aura manifested in Anima wasn\u2019t described before. The Fire Aspect\u2026 heh, speaking of Avatar influences. Overall, I like the notion of their animas being able to transform a bit like that, as I feel it ties into the organic and cyclical elemental themes.<br /> Right, so Aura is activated by spending a short period using elementally pure powers, lasting either for a scene, or until another element is wielded. A bonfire anima prevents any alternate element\u2019s Aura, to the point where it automatically shifts an extant Aura. So that would mean that if you enter an Aura other than your native element, using enough Essence will cut it off. That answers a question I had before about whether there would be anything giving one\u2019s native element prominence.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an even mix of effects there, Charms that can only be used in Aura, Charms made stronger, ones using it as fuel and others being tied to its duration. Ah, and there\u2019s a helpful keyword to give some Charms that don\u2019t mess up the Aura, as well as elementally neutral Charms. And finally, non-Dragon Blooded powers have no interaction, regardless of their own elemental nature, with the exception of the Immaculate Dragon Styles.<br /> <br /> Signature Charms were also introduced, but now there\u2019s the interesting detail of Essence 5 letting a Dragon Blood to learn their Aspect element\u2019s Charm in their Aspect and Favoured Abilities. So there\u2019s another thing to give that element centrality, albeit in a nicely soft manner that doesn\u2019t undermine the potential elemental diversity of the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Keywords\u2026 most have already been introduced, one for each element, Aura for the ones that require that, Balanced for what doesn\u2019t mess it up\u2026 oh, the detail of a mix of Balanced Charms letting you enter any of the Auras is neat. There\u2019s a keyword to denote Excellency Charms, and the Signatures.<br /> <br /> Ah yes, of course there would be Charms with multiple elements, Elemental Bolt and the like.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the end of the introduction. Good foundations here, and I\u2019m looking forward to seeing how they play out in the actual Charms tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:32:15-07:00","id":1205354,"title":"","content":"So I looked into what Holden said specifically; apparently when people got Excellencies automatically, playtesters too frequently relied on that alone, and it made the Dragon Blooded feel more like cut rate Solars. There was an adjustment with the intention of Dragon Blooded wheeling and dealing to bring their powers to bear with maximized strength.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm excited to see how that was realised.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn fact... screw it, I don't have anything else to do. I'm going to get a start on the Archery Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:45:01-07:00","id":1205368,"title":"","content":"Follow up quote from Holden says where the charmset ended up was not what he was referring to - Neall\u2019s commented on subsequent playtesting and why they moved back toward more traditional Excellencies, though still not automatic ones like Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:57:12-07:00","id":1205405,"title":"","content":"First observation: I think that Unobstructed Hunter\u2019s Aim may have more keywords than any previous Charm that wasn\u2019t in Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Second observation: it\u2019s interesting for Charms in the same cascade to have different elements. I suppose that\u2019s the only way that they could be managed without making each Ability massively bloated. Besides, the whole thing already has a sense of elemental integration.<br /> <br /> Oh, Unobstructed Hunter\u2019s Bow is the Excellency; I wouldn\u2019t have expected those to be elemental. But it\u2019s also Balanced, so you don\u2019t need to mess up your non-Wood Auras in order to add dice to Archery attacks. And it\u2019s spruced up a bit with being able to ignore a sensory penalty.<br /> <br /> I like how Harvest of the Hunter interacts with the mechanics for ammunition checks; it makes the basic ammo producing Charm a bit more interesting, on top of the image of drawing them from surrounding plant life.<br /> <br /> I like the way the Charms can be elemental, while the actual effects don\u2019t carry elemental manifestations for two reasons: one is that it emphasizes that for the Dragon Blooded, the elements can be things more metaphorical as well as inherent to the basic way of doing things, and the other is that it overlays a significant tactical element to their use of Charms. Being able to reflexively reload a flame weapon is simple enough, but what if it\u2019s going to break your Aura?<br /> <br /> Still, it\u2019s nice that they do get more overt manifestations, and I like the expression of Wood themes in the entangling vines that eat undead.<br /> <br /> Oh, they got Arbor Sentinel Technique into the book after all. I wonder what changed for Vance to be satisfied by it.<br /> <br /> Drawing Lightning Style has a nice little effect, and I like the visuals of drawing lightning into an arrow.<br /> <br /> Ahh, the signature Charms. Horizon-Spanning Arc is interesting to me because it seems to play off that theme of long-ranged support that was stated as part of why Archery is a Wood Aspect Ability. Plus it\u2019s another nice example of something understated, but pretty powerful.<br /> <br /> I like the way that Earth\u2019s Judgement Awakened realises the idea that the counterattack is powered by one\u2019s personality by how the counterattack rolls Presence.<br /> <br /> Blazing Phoenix Pinion\u2026 fairly straightforward. Exploding arrow. It\u2019s a bit odd to have a description of people being set on fire here rather than in the core, but I guess that while there are still effects there, it\u2019s not as prominent as it is with the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Fang-of-the-Depths Draw adds a nice element over the natural Water Aspect capacity to move in water (even if it\u2019s not limited to them). I also like the dynamic in the concealment effects, with the image of a Terrestrial switching back and forth between attacking from the water and popping out to stab somebody, before just falling back into the water.<br /> <br /> And Heartbeats before Death is a nice, straightforward Charm for rapid and precise loosing.<br /> <br /> Hmm, clashing attacks <i>really</i> work well with Dragonfly Finds Mate.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really get why Salamander Swallows Flame doesn\u2019t have the Wood Keyword, but I am loving the image of a Dragon Blood catching a Solar\u2019s Blazing Bolt, an Abyssals Crypt Bolt, or an Infernal\u2019s Green Nimbus, and shooting it back at them.<br /> <br /> Now, I don\u2019t remember if Sparrow Dives Hawk was ever a thing before, and I am definitely not going to trawl through old Charm chapters, but from apart from the additional power it provides, that name is inspired.<br /> <br /> Huh; not very many Essence 4 Charms, and we go very quickly to Essence 5. What have they got there\u2026<br /> <br /> Seven-Year Swarm Volley seems like a good example of the kind of Charm that has a good, strong teamwork element, and definitely the kind of thing that should be limited by needing the Aura and only getting one shot per scene. And Arrow Rain Tempest\u2026 heh, I love how that name is not metaphorical, as a way of realising a powerful Water based Archery attack. Plus how it\u2019s pretty powerful, even in comparison to some Solar effects, but for the limits in use and Aura.<br /> <br /> The Archery Charms are a good showcase. There\u2019s a nice mix of effects being metaphorically and literally elemental, how even the metaphorical ones have their obvious strengths, and a good sense of what Aura does for the ebb and flow of how Dragon Blooded powers are employed. It also makes good use of the limited charge thing that the core introduced; how they can get stronger powers than they used to, but they have to be used <i>very</i> carefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:58:27-07:00","id":1205406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205368#post1205368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow up quote from Holden says where the charmset ended up was not what he was referring to - Neall\u2019s commented on subsequent playtesting and why they moved back toward more traditional Excellencies, though still not automatic ones like Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis sentence feels like it's missing several words.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Okay, nevermind; having found the context elsewhere allows me to make sense of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-10-2018, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T19:31:39-07:00","id":1205440,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s <i>technically</i> the day after\u2026<br /> <br /> I remember when I read one of the quick character Dragon Blooded Melee Charms (I can\u2019t remember the name), with its effects of continuous attacks until one failed, I got an impression of elemental fire having a certain relentless potential to it, and I see a tinge of that in Effortlessly Rising Flame with the potential to get additional dice. If nothing else, I like the realisation it gives to the Charm\u2019s name.<br /> <br /> Bellows Pumping Stride seems like a bit of a gamble, but I suppose that\u2019s the price you pay for a potentially strong effect like that when you\u2019re Dragon Blooded. It at least helps to get the upgrade to make the flaming trail.<br /> <br /> Heh, until I recognised that Verdant Dragon\u2019s Footsteps was Wood, I was thinking it was going to be a matter of being unimpeded because you burn everything in your path.<br /> <br /> Soaring Leap Technique looks like another gamble one. I wonder if that will be a bit of a thing with non-combat dice tricks, or if it\u2019s just an Athletics thing. I can get a certain sense of the elemental take on the movement Ability having a kind of mercurial sense to it.<br /> <br /> Grandmother Oak Exertion has a neat synergy with Strength of Stone Technique; that notion of them being alternately complementary and contradictory, the playoff between letting it boost your effective strength and having the bonus not count towards dice caps.<br /> <br /> Perfect Climbing Attitude is giving me this image of newly Exalted children revelling in the ability to scale any building that they want.<br /> <br /> And the Signature Charms:<br /> <br /> Soaring Zephyr Flight: Dragon Blooded are straight up able to fly. Words cannot express my jealousy of them. Given that it\u2019s Aura dependent, I like how it being prematurely ended doesn\u2019t create a danger of falling to your death.<br /> <br /> Unshakeable Mountain Spine sounds like it could enable some tremendous feats of strength, so it makes sense that it has a rather limited access.<br /> <br /> Huh, I would have thought that Inescapable Blazing Advance was the kind of thing that was strong enough to have limited use, but I guess that given its major attack effect requires crashing an enemy, it makes sense as the kind of thing that might need to be used repeatedly over subsequent rounds.<br /> <br /> Dragon Surmounts the Water is similarly available, which is probably down to it mostly being something that adds an additional axis to your movement options (plus a nice assistance to accomplishing things within it).<br /> <br /> And Graceful Dryad Dance is similar, but for forest and other heavily grown areas. I\u2019m guessing that the wording is specific enough to not apply to buildings thickly covered in ivy.<br /> I need to review the rush rules to understand a few of these.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4 already again. I understand the impulse to not make a massively bloated Charm set, but I wonder if some of these entries might be a bit thinner. On the other hand, it may reflect a greater inaccessibility at the top for Dragon Blooded, considering the expense of high Essence and the lack of Supernal Ability. Besides, there are only a few at Essence 4 and 5 (which is still more than the ever got before). As for Seething Dragon Footprint itself, it\u2019s a nice upgrade and a striking image of footsteps turning into huge flames.<br /> <br /> And at the top there\u2019s Falling Star Maneuver, for when you want to go all Negasonic Teenage Warhead on folks.<br /> <br /> Considering the hour, I appreciate the relative shortness of the chapter. There are still some fun effects in there.<br /> <br /> (In future, shorter Ability entries will be doubled up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T19:38:12-07:00","id":1205443,"title":"","content":"Thing that I'm calling as being a Charm, based on season 3 of Legend of Korra:<br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Killing a person by sucking the breath directly from their lungs.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T22:02:46-07:00","id":1205463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205354#post1205354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I looked into what Holden said specifically; apparently when people got Excellencies automatically, playtesters too frequently relied on that alone, and it made the Dragon Blooded feel more like cut rate Solars. There was an adjustment with the intention of Dragon Blooded wheeling and dealing to bring their powers to bear with maximized strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how it'll work in play or not, but the Charms thus far released are DEFINITELY in this vein, and it's very very interesting to me.<br /> <br /> Like... previously, the Dragon-Blooded were sort of &quot;worse Solars&quot; when it came to the charmset. The things they had going for them were hyper-efficient Excellencies, a smattering of synergy Charms, and at the meta level the fact that they had access to all sorts of resources via chargen that Solars usually did not. But mechanically speaking they operated a LOT like Solars, just with the top end removed; no or highly limited perfects, a smaller mote pool, Charms that did basically the same stuff but were strictly not as good, etc.<br /> <br /> (My personal table experience was that starting DBs were a LOT like starting Solars, and then the Solars would gain access to their top end and the Dragon-Blooded were like &quot;... oh. Right. I can't... I can't do that.&quot; Others mileage may vary.)<br /> <br /> Well, one look at this Charmset says that this has changed radically. They are still, strictly speaking &quot;worse than&quot; Solars, for a given value of &quot;worse,&quot; but they are emphatically <i>not</i> &quot;worse Solars.&quot;<br /> <br /> What's been done, and someone correct me if I'm wrong here, is that they've been given a very powerful but also very limited toolkit, with internal synergies AND internal anti-synergies. The hyper-efficient Excellencies have gone away and been replaced with what looks like either &quot;flexible&quot; Excellencies (dice-adder OR more expensive success adder) or &quot;bonus&quot; Excellencies (dice adder AND special sauce.) The Charms do very very potent things but require setup, forethought, and the proper circumstances to be fully exploited; where a Solar would just brute force their way through by being so fucking amazing that they can't be stopped, a Dragon-Blood needs the right tool for the job and the right circumstances to use that tool... but if that applies, their raw heroism and elemental power often carries the day. There's definitely wheeling and dealing involved.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a big re-emphasis on their elemental nature and their ties to Creation. I'm seeing a LOT of Charms here in this first set that are essentially &quot;You're trying to use the environment against me? Yeah, that, uh. That won't work. And the reason it won't work is because I <i>am</i> the land, the sea, and the air; 'Prince of the Earth' isn't just a cool-sounding title.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't speak to how effective or ineffective, how balanced against other Exalt types this will be. But on eyeballing it, it would appear they've succeeded at differentiating the Dragon-Blooded. They've SUPER succeeded at it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:27:06-07:00","id":1205565,"title":"","content":"Awareness, go!<br /> <br /> In Precision Observation Method, it\u2019s nice to know that they do still occasionally get a more normal Excellency. It also suddenly occurs to me that the Aura mechanic and Elemental keywords is that it gives substance to things that used to be only flavour text. Before the \u201cserenity of earth\u201d didn\u2019t exactly change that you were using a Charm largely indistinct from a Solar one, but <i>now</i> that association is setting you up with an Aura of Earth Essence that you can build other Charms off of. That\u2019s neat.<br /> <br /> Now, if I\u2019m understanding Cloud-Piercing Focus, one purchase of the Charm allows you to access all of the effects, it\u2019s just that what you use it to see through determines what Aura it will contribute to. But it\u2019s also Balanced, so you have no restriction on seeing through something else if you need to.<br /> <br /> I like how the elemental variations of All-Encompassing Earth Sense are more than just the same thing in different environments, and still kind of gives a pre-eminence to earth, like in the idea that sensing air requires one to be in an enclosed room.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Awareness seems to be the kind of thing that gets afforded a lot of Balanced Charms, I\u2019m guessing on a principle that they don\u2019t want to discourage analysis of one\u2019s surroundings. For Dragon\u2019s Crushing Gaze, I think it\u2019s good for Terrestrials to get their own kind of Awareness Charm to directly impose upon an opponent, and I particularly like the image of a disguise being washed away.<br /> <br /> Heh, Hesiesh\u2019s Discerning Tongue gives me the sense of a fun twist on cartoons in which somebody eats something harmful and it sets their tongue on fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> While Feeling the Dragon\u2019s Bones feels like another thing that is strong (with a nice synergy with another Charm) while being a bit situational; you might get a lot of Awareness Charms that can be used in combination with your ability to sense surrounding vibrations, but other Charms will mess up the Aura that you need to keep that thing up.<br /> <br /> Signature Charms:<br /> <br /> Horizon-Spanning Echoes: the first image I get from a Charm that lets you listen for specific people from miles away is that it can be a very useful thing for a Wyld Hunt. Lunars might be the best equipped to get away by turning into birds or whatever, but this seems like a good power to help them keep up the chase. Plus the benefits to governing a territory.<br /> <br /> The impression I get from One-With-Earth Embodiment is that one is able to kind of chase after the senses that they extend through other Earth based Awareness Charms\u2026 or more specifically, you can close the distance with something that you sensed by virtue of your earth sense. Its cost definitely means that it isn\u2019t the kind of thing you can use for long distance travel, which keeps it focused as an Awareness Charm.<br /> <br /> And as something extending the assault capabilities of Dragon\u2019s Crushing Gaze (even if the Charms are unrelated) is Eye of Blazing Truth, to let you search out a person even in darkness and then shoot fiery eye beams at them! I like how it has a mystical element in the form of burning away disguises.<br /> <br /> While Serpent-of-the-Depths Discernment\u2026 feels a bit weaker than some other Awareness Charms, with the shorter range. I can\u2019t quite tell if you can listen to people who are <i>on</i> the water, like in a boat or something. I do suppose some of that is made up for by how it is cheap, and lasts a scene.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Dragon\u2019s Flaring Nostrils provides a range of scent-based benefits that can be applied across a variety of situations, and is <i>also</i> scene long.<br /> <br /> The Dragon Blooded have always had a sense of a combative element through several of their non-combat Abilities, which was supposed to convey their image of having been soldiers in the army of the gods. That\u2019s been seen in a few places already with unconventional attack Charms, but I think it\u2019s always conveyed effectively by Dragon\u2019s Twitching Whisker providing senses finely tuned to enemies or people whom a character hates or fears.<br /> <br /> And Sense the Hidden Ember is another one useful for Wyld Hunting with its capacity to sense places where an Exalt strongly used their anima. It\u2019s a curious distinction to have varying effects based on numbers of successes rolled; with it specifically as something that varies the amount of information you get, it reminds me of some stuff in Chronicles of Darkness books.<br /> Hmm, I feel as though Sense-Riding Technique would make more sense as a Wood Charm, for the manner in which it directly interacts with another being.<br /> <br /> No Essence 4 Charms, but their pinnacle of Essence Disruption Attack is another interesting kind of assault Charm with its forcing enemies to pay what can be a rather hefty surcharge on their powers. For something like that, even having to expend your Earth Aura seems like a small price to pay (which I mean in the good way). <br /> <br /> \u200bI had mixed up my alphabet and thought that Bureaucracy would be next and I could follow up immediately, but Brawl is sure to be a more complex Ability, so that comes later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T07:03:40-07:00","id":1205577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205565#post1205565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if I\u2019m understanding Cloud-Piercing Focus, one purchase of the Charm allows you to access all of the effects, it\u2019s just that what you use it to see through determines what Aura it will contribute to. But it\u2019s also Balanced, so you have no restriction on seeing through something else if you need to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The &quot;Multiple Aspects&quot; box at the end of the keywords section (right before the Archery charms) explains it. It also means you can see through only one type of obscurant at a time, which could be an issue with, say being underwater with smoke from burning ships above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T07:20:23-07:00","id":1205582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205577#post1205577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. The &quot;Multiple Aspects&quot; box at the end of the keywords section (right before the Archery charms) explains it. It also means you can see through only one type of obscurant at a time, which could be an issue with, say being underwater with smoke from burning ships above.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very specific example that makes me think you've played some Exalts who have made poor life choices with regards to boats and/or ships. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T08:11:14-07:00","id":1205600,"title":"","content":"There <i>may</i> have been a few ships that have been sunk ... sometimes on purpose even ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T08:18:46-07:00","id":1205603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205577#post1205577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">xplains it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes, it's one of those things that is more apparent once you have a solid example of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:30:32-07:00","id":1205655,"title":"","content":"I think you can activate multiple versions of it simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T11:25:56-07:00","id":1205689,"title":"","content":"Yes, for when you need to see through those underwater sand storms that are on fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T12:44:27-07:00","id":1205716,"title":"","content":"Okay, Brawl. When I had heard the name \u201cBecome the Hammer\u201d, I actually assumed that it would be a Craft Charm. It\u2019s an interesting combination of Excellency and uncommon dice trick on a damage roll.<br /> <br /> Inescapable Whirlpool Hold refunding Initiative costs for grapples gives me a sense that Water Aspect Brawl is very grappling oriented.<br /> <br /> Heh, I\u2019m expecting a somewhat dense tree, but if these initial Charms are an indication, they\u2019ll mostly be your meat and potatoes types that will not elicit much comment from me.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Blade-Deflecting Palm being based on an enemy\u2019s dice pool reminds me of my old speculation that things such as this create a risk to excessively high dice pools. So apart from its expression of a water theme, it gives me the sense of the Dragon Blooded having their own take on fighting things that are bigger than them. That and how Onslaught eases the burden of having to use the Charm multiple times in a round, even if that comes at the cost of the reduced Defence.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m guessing that Crushing Avalanche Grasp will have some nice synergy with Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> Ah, I remember the preview of Currents Sweep to Sea. It\u2019s still a neat elemental and tactical effect.<br /> <br /> For the first of the Signatures, there\u2019s Flying Whirlwind Razor, a name that sounds oddly familiar. Its effect of being able to shoot a blade of wind that you have the option to be carried along with sounds enjoyable for the possibilities that it carries. Plus it\u2019s nice to see the occasional elemental blast outside of Elemental Bolt Technique.<br /> <br /> Firmament-Shattering Impact is something like the Dragon Blooded answer to Heaven Thunder Hammer. Possibly not as strong, but apart from the general benefits of flinging people around, it also creates an impact crater that makes it hard for the knocked down opponent to move around when they get up.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Erupting Fury Barrage looks a bit complicated\u2026 so you roll a normal decisive attack and get a number of attacks against a single foe equal to your rolled 10s plus 1. The attacks don\u2019t need to be rolled each time, all having the successes of the initial roll. Each time you successfully inflict damage (or just hit? I need to look back at the attack rules), your Initiative is lowered by how many successes you rolled, down to your Essence. When you\u2019ve laid out all attacks, you reset to base as normal, even if you kept missing. Furthermore, successful attacks create a vulnerability in the target meaning decisive attacks cause them to suffer minor explosions. It\u2019s unusual, but I imagine that if applied correctly, it can be unusually powerful.<br /> <br /> Embracing the Violent Flow\u2026 ah, of course, one of those cool instances in which a Waterbender would drape water around their shoulders to have tentacles extending from their arms, crossed over with the Octopus Technique, in something reminiscent of that Red Lotus Waterbender from Legend of Korra. Even has the unique benefit of being used with Martial Arts, which I can picture making for some very pretty White Crescent Style.<br /> <br /> (God I\u2019ve got to dig out my Avatar DVDs and rewatch it)<br /> <br /> And Body of Deadly Thorns, to allow Terrestrials their own variation on the dreaded spiky hug.<br /> <br /> Become the Wave is another one that shows a good emphasis on teamwork, and a nice sense that a group of Dragon Blooded can be a bit difficult to pin down.<br /> <br /> Wait\u2026 did I misunderstand the mechanics of the Sworn Kinship? When a Dragon Blooded Charm refers to something that keys off of \u201callies\u201d, is it only referring to Hearth mates? They don\u2019t have a keyword referencing the Hearth, so\u2026 I\u2019ll need to check back over some things.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Swift-Striking Tide builds nicely off of the prior Charm by giving one a free attack against somebody that an ally distracted. Yesss, of course I was mistaken in boxing Water Brawl into one niche. There\u2019s a nice combination of grappling, defence and mobility in there.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Waves Swallow the Mountain has to render some opponents awfully vulnerable. I guess that the manner in which Hardness being set to 0 manifests is fairly subtle and metaphysical, unless it\u2019s a simple case of holding somebody so effectively that it becomes easy to hit the vulnerable spots.<br /> <br /> Fist-Spinning Maelstrom offers the alternative take on multiple attacks, ones that hit separate enemies. I believe that multi-attacks for withering are uncommon, and it\u2019s got a clever little elemental manifestation there at the end.<br /> <br /> Drowning Embrace is pretty self-explanatory, although it does remind me that I ought to consider Initiative Crash more often in terms of effects that might capitalise on a vulnerable opponent or end a fight more quickly.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I guess that Hanging Tree Technique does not need to have the Exalt\u2019s limbs actually extend, it just adds some quality of wood to each of them so that they have the strength and firmness to handle one or two targets each. Still, it\u2019s an interesting way to handle the unorthodox idea of grappling multiple enemies at a time, and damaging them therein. It also has to deal with multiple withering attacks.<br /> <br /> And at the top is Smashing Tidal Wave Technique, an enhancement to Currents Sweep to Sea that lets them enhance the water limb they create with their own anima, extending its range, enhancing its power and letting it target opponents that are bigger than usual but distinctly <i>not</i> Legendary Size. That\u2019s an interesting distinction from Solars, even if the overall set has its strengths; it makes me think that Dragon Blooded are a bit more dependent on things like warstriders in the event that a gigantic monster comes rampaging through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T12:59:12-07:00","id":1205723,"title":"","content":"*Edited so as not to derail the thread*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","user":"Equitable Remedy","date":". 04-11-2018, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T13:10:19-07:00","id":1205726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205723#post1205723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that this will be a very popular take on the forums, but I don't think that it's supported by what's in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For what it's worth, I don't think so either. But I think they nevertheless look viable and fun to play (and the more I look at the Aura mechanic and how it manifests in actual Charms, the less limiting it seems compared to my initial impression).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T13:12:15-07:00","id":1205727,"title":"","content":"There is a general discussion thread for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:12:47-07:00","id":1205804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205689#post1205689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, for when you need to see through those underwater sand storms that are on fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Happens all the time when we try to beach Cecelyne from Kimberry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T18:31:54-07:00","id":1205857,"title":"","content":"Well, since I can\u2019t find a way to enjoy anything at the moment because my brother deeply insulted me, I might as well take this moment to see what they\u2019ve gotten out of Bureaucracy. My big query going in is how Aura will interact with it, considering that it tends to be one of the more passive Abilities.<br /> <br /> Confluence of Savant Thought bestows the capability of introducing facts using Bureaucracy. That aspect of Lore was a good addition to the game, but it\u2019s a bit unfortunate that Bureaucracy might feel a need to crib it. Finding the Water\u2019s Depths provides a custom read intentions roll to get a sense of what would entice somebody in a bargain action. Testing the Waters is an old Charm, with some new twists; it uses read intentions as the foundation of its effect of determining how somebody will vote in a system now, as well as adding parts such as revealing Intimacies that motivate the intention, and an upgrade that allows one to determine factional lines within a general body.<br /> <br /> Some other familiar things with delegating authority and speeding along projects; I do like how Dashing Brook Method ties its multiplier to an Attribute reflecting the character\u2019s leadership style, in how it characterizes the Charm as engaging in activity rather than just casting an efficiency spell.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Unshakeable Mountain Management, an Earth Charm. Boosts the Resolve of members of an organisation against influence to sabotage it or abuse a position. But it only works momentarily, and the Exalt has to be personally present for such attempted influence. I\u2019m on board with the idea that Bureaucracy entails a certain degree of buy-in, that you have to be into those kinds of scenarios playing out as a character that respects their basic principles, but I must admit that I find it a bit of a stretch to think that a Dragon Blood would see somebody acting improperly in one of their organisations, and respond by bolstering people against being taken in by it, rather than intervening directly.<br /> <br /> Shells-for-Silver Ruse is an interesting crossover with the Water capacity for deceit with the aspect of Bureaucracy focused on perceived economic status or capability.<br /> <br /> Okay, let\u2019s see if the Signatures have anything a bit more dazzling.<br /> <br /> Humble Exemplar Attitude lets you provide sizable non-Charm bonus dice to Bureaucracy rolls in service to a project or administrative task that upholds a Defining Principle. It also makes the Principle obvious to everybody participating, and a successful project restores Willpower and automatically instils the Principle (one level lower) into those who could see it. I\u2019d say it\u2019s not half bad; the Terrestrial Exalted\u2019s own take on shaping an organisation to reflect their belief systems, less absolute than that of Solars, but with some benefits in place of that.<br /> <br /> Graven Stone Edict is a bit closer to being absolute, even if it has the limit that people can follow Defining Intimacies to go against one\u2019s edicts, and the rule created by the Charm needs to be very specific. It\u2019s a nice interplay between institutional order and the Wyld for the rule to help defend people against powers of the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Ah, now Seething Firebreak Technique has an interesting concept to it: galvanizing dissatisfaction within an organisation in order to expose existing opponents (with the added benefit of improving job satisfaction to those who are already on your team).<br /> <br /> And what can the Water Signature do for its associated Ability? Ah of course, one of those powers for making highly obscure and compelling legal agreements. Mechanically it prevents the character from being aware of certain Intimacies that would oppose a bargain, while it is offset by penalties depending on how severe the results of the clauses would be. If they don\u2019t become aware of the hidden clauses on their own terms, then it twists their mind into assuming that they must have consented, and feeling honour-bound to it. It\u2019s effectively devious.<br /> <br /> While One Forest, Many Trees\u2026 is the first Mute Charm that I\u2019ve seen them have, for one. I was wondering if they would get or need Mute, but if nothing else it would be necessary for Stealth\u2026 anyway, it\u2019s a Charm to let a character grant themselves ad hoc Merits representing social contacts. I do like a bit of chicanery with Merit dots such as that, both for the mechanical element (not very obtrusive, and allows one to modify certain factors of a build circumstantially) and for the kind of characterisation that it represents.<br /> <br /> Jeez, there is a surprising number of Charms past the Signatures\u2026<br /> <br /> Bestow the Saffron Mantle is another old Charm, but I think in the past it may have just allowed one to grant a character their Bureaucracy dots. For the effects here, while they all look useful as a whole, I\u2019d say the biggest ones are bestowing one\u2019s proxy with an intuitive sense of one\u2019s intentions in the right context, and greatly extending the range to ride senses.<br /> Nice to see another Fire Charm in Blazing Hoard of Hesiesh, allowing one to use their relative wealth to enhance social rolls.<br /> <br /> I imagine that Following the River\u2019s Course plays a major role in the Realm\u2019s financial sector, and the regulation therein. Thrashing Carp Serenade is also returning; I recall that Charm being a form of sabotage, and now it\u2026 multiplies the time taken for an organisation to accomplish something, depending on the results of a roll made against the target\u2019s leader.<br /> <br /> Sea-Changed Secrets enhances attempts at blackmail. Man, a lot of Dragon Blooded Bureaucracy is nasty; no wonder they have such harsh intrigues. It\u2019s an interesting contrast with Solars, with things like striding over an organisation as an exemplar and calling upon old loyalties. <br /> <br /> A Wood Charm now, with Sprouting Bamboo Cultivation to provide a straightforward but reasonably strong boost to actions that would aid in building an organisation up. The charmingly named Drowning in Negotiation Style returns to allow one to bind people to agreements with the threat of mystically imposed injury.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s Flowing Authority Insinuation, another Psyche Charm to let one forge credentials or permits to engage in activities, carrying the weight of a Major Intimacy, and the Wood Charm Sowing the Dragon\u2019s Teeth, providing a strong bonus to Strategic Maneuvers that would benefit from some previously established undertaking of logistics. Of all the additional elements, I particularly like how Wood has that theme of drawing people together and collating assets, in contrast to Water slipping through the cracks and seams and tangling people up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T19:40:37-07:00","id":1205876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205716#post1205716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait\u2026 did I misunderstand the mechanics of the Sworn Kinship? When a Dragon Blooded Charm refers to something that keys off of \u201callies\u201d, is it only referring to Hearth mates? They don\u2019t have a keyword referencing the Hearth, so\u2026 I\u2019ll need to check back over some things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, this is not resticted to Sworn Kin. Allies are <i>anyone</i> on the same side of the combat.<br /> <br /> There are charms later that interact specifically with Hearthmates. You'll know the difference when you get to them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:00:45-07:00","id":1205879,"title":"","content":"Define a rhetorical question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T01:58:30-07:00","id":1205968,"title":"","content":"Introducing facts with abilities other than Lore seems to be A Thing in the dragonblooded charmset. There was a survival charm that did something similar previewed a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T02:49:44-07:00","id":1205974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1205968#post1205968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Introducing facts with abilities other than Lore seems to be A Thing in the dragonblooded charmset. There was a survival charm that did something similar previewed a while back.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dragon-blooded-charms-preview-exalted/\u200b\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Wandering Forester's Charm</a>. I recall that it was a well received concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:59:45-07:00","id":1206225,"title":"","content":"So yesterday was kind of odd in a manner that meant I was kind of insufficiently motivated to read the book at all. And I\u2019ll admit that at least part of that was a sense of trepidation about reading the Craft Charms.<br /> <br /> But I would feel remiss if I went to sleep without giving the text another look, so I\u2019m ready to get stuck back in.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m curious about any of the limitations that Dragon Blooded will have in comparison to Solars, so it\u2019s interesting that their Excellency is even something that can yield silver craft points for them.<br /> I\u2019m always going to want the Exalted to have an incentive to use tools, so I appreciate how Stone-Carving Fingers supplements the capacity to work without them with a halfway decent multiplier for using them, even if it\u2019s only for smaller scale and non-magical work with specific materials.<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s good for Flaw-Finding Examination to build off of the rules for repair and demolition, although I\u2019d need to look back at how the Charm used to work to pin down my exact preference.<br /> Ah, Shaping Hand Style is an elegant way to extend the materials that Dragon Blooded can work with. It\u2019s also a fun little call back to the elemental Crafts of Second Edition.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been wondering about Charms that might provide additional sources of crafting points (it appears to me that referring to them as XP has been quietly dropped, unless that shorthand was also in the Solar Charms). With Flawless Facet Realization, it\u2019s more mechanical than I would have expected here (even if Solars also had Charms that provided additional points in methods other than extra objectives to crafting). I wonder if that\u2019s a case for the Ability focus and lower key of Terrestrials, or just that such Charm technology isn\u2019t as viable as I would think.<br /> <br /> Strike the Dragon-Anvil gives an interesting look at a way for a Terrstrial to get at some stronger Craft enhancement, at the cost of the limited craft points.<br /> <br /> And for a pure Fire Charm there\u2019s Passion-Inflaming Artistry. Now, this is interesting; in the past, I\u2019ve expressed a sentiment that I was averse to crafting Charms to lend an inherent emotional quality to what one made, at least for Solars. I saw it as a kind of enchantment, that undermined the relevance of both non-magical crafting and Artifacts. However, the idea of that coming through, not as a Psyche effect, but an inspire action, that implicitly ties the desired emotional tenor to the nature of the actual crafted thing, it feels a bit stronger to me. It\u2019s got me wondering about a few other ways to apply the concept.<br /> <br /> I find Talents-to-Obols Refinement to lend a certain implication to Dragon Blooded crafting; that they might end up with white or gold points that they\u2019re not really in a position to use, and can ensure that they don\u2019t go to waste. Conversely, past Essence 4, they can get a utility out of their Charms to generate silver points as a means of shoring up their gold.<br /> <br /> Ah, I see, Ephemeral Form Composition, which I\u2019ve been seeing repeated glimpses of, is actually their Air aspected Signature. Well, I suppose the idea of projecting images through a sense of worldly patterns still holds true, although I\u2019ve also got another notion of its manifestation\u2026 anyway, it seems like a decently powerful crafting effect, at least insofar as it eases some of the burdens of higher level projects, even if they need to find their own ways of getting the numbers. If nothing else, it\u2019s a nice realisation of being able to revise a planning stage.<br /> <br /> Hmm, for that cost in gold points, what might Eternal Omphalos Forge do\u2026 provides them with extra terminus to one of the higher crafting projects, a not insignificant benefit (as well as a handy bonus of Willpower if they turn out to have not needed it).<br /> <br /> Conversely, Blazing Dragon-Smith Arete lets them trade in terminus for extra non-Charm dice (plus, strictly speaking, lowering their mote pool by 15 for the duration of the project), and providing an extra source of white points. I wonder if both the lowered terminus and mote pool together might be too hefty a cost even for those non-Charm dice.<br /> <br /> Fortune-from-Flotsam Ingenuity is your standard MacGyver Charm, nicely prevented from overwhelming the system by its craft points cost and limited use, and is finally an instant of bringing a Sworn Kinship into the operation of a Charm (even if it\u2019s not so much combining effects or providing special benefits to a mate as it is their well-being and achievement providing a restoration). I do like the general sense of it being something specially reserved for emergencies, and it kind of enhances my appreciation of Craftsman Needs No Tools. It\u2019s actually an interesting comparison to that, being more limited, but in a manner with some character to it.<br /> <br /> Imago-Hatching Realization is a curious kind of Charm, and possibly among the more flavourful of them, at least insofar as it affects result rather than process. The idea of Craft Charms oriented to particular kinds of products has always come up in regards to redressing deficiencies in the Ability, or speculating on its future, and I\u2019ve often thought it was a bit limited. What\u2019s interesting here is that it\u2019s not about enhancing the crafting of a particular kind of thing, but lends a unique quality to the thing that you make. I especially like the idea that it can make something unique in Artifacts; that\u2019s an area that I have often wondered about ways that different Exalted might have different results, and I like the idea that somebody could pick up a daiklave or the like and find that it has certain tangents in its power, and conclude that it was very likely that a Terrestrial made that.<br /> <br /> Back to the normals, and\u2026 does Forge-Hand Prana render Shaping Hand Style a bit of a speed bump? Let me try and compare them\u2026 Shaping Hand Style lets you spend 6 motes in order to perform a Fire craft for a basic or major project without tools or workshop, and multiplies the rate of activity by your Essence plus one if you do use tools. Forge-Hand Prana lets you spend 5 mote, 1 Willpower perform a Fire craft basic or major project, <i>or</i> a superior project crafting jade, where you need no tools\u2026 ah, but the multiplication is lower. So it frees them up for crafting things that include Artifacts, but the multiplication is lower than the prior Charm. Mind, it\u2019s a case of benefiting the crafting of Artifacts without the need for tools, and I don\u2019t quite like that, least of all for Dragon Blooded. It also partakes of the Dragon Blooded inclination for fighting, by the flaming hands being viable to enhance unarmed fighting (if not the best tools for it).<br /> <br /> And finally Stoking Inspiration\u2019s Forge allows them to gamble the silver points they get from projects on another source of gold points. There are not yet any Charms above Essence 3.<br /> <br /> Now, I\u2019m somebody who\u2019s on board with the crafting system, so I\u2019ll have no discussion on the merits of its basic existence. What\u2019s important to me here is that, in the past, I always found Dragon Blooded to really illustrate the weaknesses of the Craft system. As Ability Exalts, they needed to do something with it, in contrast to Lunars for whom it didn\u2019t need to be as big a priority, Sidereals who were going weird anyway, and Abyssals playing about the same game as Solars were, just limited to killing. Alchemicals had a basis to be kind of as good at it as Solars, and Infernals could more or less get away with never having to address the subject at all (one could kind of assume that they might have Charms to help with it, but the Yozi Charm setup let it not feel like an outright deficiency if they never did). And it didn\u2019t afford much variation and Solars got to soak up the basic good stuff, so the best that Terrestrials really got amounted to\u2026 certain specific forms of direct material manipulation and this one strange (and kind of broken, when applied to Artifacts) Charm to break things down into their raw materials, to be placed on top of inferior multipliers.<br /> <br /> Here, I think the Dragon Blooded get something with a bit more punch to it, and remarkably without needing to fall back on things like pulling up earthworks and the like. I think the methods of enhancing crafts interact meaningfully with the system, maintaining their place in the hierarchy while providing a few costly avenues for shooting at the heights of it, and that its got some good ways of letting them go elemental metaphorically. I appreciate how the primary focus remains on the crafting, and I think it\u2019s got some good methods of realising that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:39:54-07:00","id":1206437,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve gotten a few interesting hints about Dodge, so I\u2019ll like to see what it has. Heh, with all of the contentious discussion around it, I would almost forget that the Ability is Fire Aspected. On that note, it\u2019s a nice bit for Threshold Warding Stance to convey that image of moving like flame by removing environmental penalties.<br /> <br /> I enjoy Heat-of-Battle Advance running on a logic of \u201cI\u2019m not running away, I\u2019m advancing towards somebody else\u201d. Plus Hopping Firecracker Evasion being about lighting a little explosion to burst you away from an enemy.<br /> <br /> Virtuous Negation Defense, now there\u2019s one that I do remember, because I referenced it once in a scenario of Exalted working together. With defend other rules being a thing, it obviously works a bit differently now. Wood certainly seems fitting to the concept, and the idea of a discount if used to defend Hearth mates.<br /> <br /> Hmm, did Solars have any or many Charms to inflict withering damage by dodging? Either way, I like the metaphor behind it of smoke making one more vulnerable to flame.<br /> <br /> Or wait, is Safety Among Enemies the Charm I recalled from before? Have any Charms from prior Editions been upgraded to Signatures? For the moment, yes, nice idea of creating air buffets to redirect attacks into other targets.<br /> <br /> With my talk before about Earth having the spiritual quality of being unmoving and stolid enough to turn attacks aside, I like how that comes out in Dodge with something that actively pushes nearby enemies away from them.<br /> <br /> Ah, the description of Unassailable Body of Fire letting a Dragon Blood explode as a means of dodging was a bit of an exaggeration from something that enhances Hopping Fire to create a damaging burst of flame. I\u2019m almost certain that the name of this one, at least, is carried over from prior Editions, even if I recall that back then it could utilise any element, and literally made the Exalt\u2019s body into it.<br /> <br /> Huh; the mechanics of Flow With Strife are very close to Heavenly Guardian Defense, making it a kind of power I\u2019m surprised to see Dragon Blooded get. I suppose it all evens out with things like the cost in Water Aura, the difficulty of <i>building</i> Water Aura while using other Dodge Charms, and not working against aggravated damage. It\u2019s a nice little touch for the cost to be slightly reduced by being in the presence of water.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, the kind of Evasion bonus provided by Swaying Grass Elusion looks like it could cast a few enemies with a nasty surprise, with the nice benefit of a means of recouping some of the cost in it.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ve got Elusive Crosswind Defense to give them extra Evasion without encroaching on their dice cap. That seems to be a thing across much of the Dragon Blooded Charms, making up for their lower dice cap in several key spots but with distinct costs and limitations.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s Bonfire Shadow Evasion to give them a distinct tactical advantage of using their anima to blind attackers, and Coiling Dragon Dance to allow their Aura to provide a nice little general enhancement in the for of getting a bit of Initiative for successful dodges and enhanced soak against failed ones (which count as successful if there\u2019s no damage)\u2026 but they only get the benefits of failed dodges to withering attacks. Fine.<br /> <br /> And finally there\u2019s Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion, and <i>here\u2019s</i> the part where Unassailable Body of Fire gets to bring in the other elements (with the benefit of it being based on Aura, so one doesn\u2019t even need repeated repurchases). For Air they get to push enemies away, Earth adds a bit of extra damage and either knocks an enemy down or blinds them, Fire\u2019s blast is enhanced a bit, Water makes it bashing damage but imposes a dice penalty for a few rounds, and Wood exchanges a damaging blast for creating a clump of grappling brambles.<br /> <br /> Yeah I\u2019d say there\u2019s some neat stuff here. Nice couple of improved defences, and some quirky elemental side effects.<br /> <br /> \u200bAh good, coming up on the end of the preview. Only Integrity and Investigation left now, I think. Might have that finished off by the end of the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:10:40-07:00","id":1206952,"title":"","content":"Okay, two Abilities left. The Dragon Blooded have had some decent defence from the physical, and the Solar Charms went in some interesting directions with Integrity, so I\u2019d like to see how they deal with the social and mystical.<br /> <br /> Granite Curtain of Serenity is another nice example of the elemental take on an Excellency extending it to offsetting some penalties, particularly the Earth quality of mitigating pain or weakness. Follow up with a couple of basic Charms to let them lend a different emotional tone to their Resolve through the elements, in the form of calculating the stat with different Attributes.<br /> <br /> Oath of Ten Thousand Dragons looks a lot more straightforward this time around, but an ongoing bonus to Resolve in defence of a sworn loyalty or duty sounds like a good benefit all on its own. Certainly the kind of thing that will help a Wyld Hunt resist the honeyed words of an Anathema. Heart-Hardening Meditation looks similarly useful.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I wonder how one might play the experience of Inviolate Dragon Spirit. It\u2019s like\u2026 overcoming Resolve bolstered by an Intimacy represents an argument that gets around it, but then they\u2019ve got a Charm to\u2026 I suppose bolster their commitment to the Tie or Principle, and use it as a basis for resisting a convincing argument. Mind, I sounds like the sort of thing that would make any sufficiently invested Terrestrial difficult to persuade indeed.<br /> <br /> Heh, Unquenchable Battle-Passion, unmoved by pleas for mercy. It\u2019s a nice image, enflaming your own passion to contain the battle against any attempts to dissuade you.<br /> <br /> I need to look back at the relevant Solar Charms to assess Chaos-Warding Prana\u2019s effect on the Wyld, beyond the benefit it can provide to a Sworn Kinship.<br /> <br /> Ohhhh, Ten Thousand Dragons Fight as One, what might this do with an impressive name like that? Errrr forming an ad hoc Charm-bolstered oath of loyalty towards another Terrestrial that one sees in distress. Not bad, not bad.<br /> <br /> And to go along with Integrity steeling one against pain is Wound-Denying Dragon Faith, letting one bolster dedication Charms with being able to ignore wound penalties.<br /> <br /> Now, the Signature Air is one Ascendant Ideal Inspiration, allowing one to bolster dedication to a powerful ideal with a novel method of interfering with attempts to weaken it or make one act against it <i>and</i> make it easier to win other people over to that ideal. The cost of that, apart from the basic Charm cost, is that one needs to actually stand by the ideal, lest breaking with it cause the severe psychic shock of losing all Willpower. I think it\u2019s another nice little example of Dragon Blooded Integrity going in some unique directions, particularly with the element of improved instil actions.<br /> <br /> Aw jeez, if some of the other Integrity Charms made it harder to influence a Terrestrial, Flawless Diamond Heart really takes the cake. Reducing the Willpower costs to as low as zero for maintaining one\u2019s Major and Defining Intimacies, and even being able to reset it by acting in accordance with that Intimacy. I\u2019m just picturing the cocksure Solar who is so sure that they can convince anybody of anything, getting a rude awakening with the shikari who is having none of it.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Immolating Phoenix-Soul Fury has a name with a concerning implication. Ah, good thing that it\u2019s not as literal as its protesting monk name suggests. It\u2019s just a simple matter of being able to respond to somebody trying to mind control you by losing your shit. Mind, from what I\u2019ve heard in the past, many players responded like that regardless of the character they were playing, and without need for special magic; this just has some clearer mechanical process, and a special reward for winning. Plus the image of somebody trying to use a Psyche effect in a relaxed, social situation and running off to fight somebody\u2026 or possibly starting an actual war.<br /> <br /> Waves-Swallow-Mountains Persistance allows the Exalt to subtract 1s from an opponent\u2019s influence rolls, with the curious distinctions of the Charm actually getting stronger the more that it\u2019s used, but it can only be used against the same person during a scene. Man, Water can have some weird stuff sometimes.<br /> <br /> And Roots-of-the-World Meditation lets one go into a physically or even mentally heal oneself from a variety of ailments. I appreciate using that as the basis for a sidebar that clarifies precisely what meditation is in mechanical terms.<br /> <br /> Heh, I like the wordplay underlying the Charm name Thicker Than Stone, and the associated boost to Resolve against influence against positive feelings towards other Terrestrials, the family, and subordinates, interestingly enough.<br /> <br /> With all of the Charms based around dedication to an oath, it would be incomplete if one didn\u2019t have something to swear eternal vengeance against somebody who has wronged one. Unflagging Vengeance Meditation sounds rather strong even before I can see the Resistance Charms that it bolsters, particularly with the added soak and Hardness that it provides. Mind, the power in one\u2019s blood is not messing around with holding you to it, if it eats away at your Willpower and then your body.<br /> <br /> And while The Mountain Still Stands is quite short and simple, being able to reap Willpower back from successfully defending one\u2019s Defining Intimacies synergizes nicely with several other Charms to improve Resolve, Intimacies and change social Willpower costs.<br /> <br /> So Dragon Blooded Integrity is a good deal more low key than what the Solars can get\u2026 oh damn, that\u2019s also where they had a Charm or two to get spirit Charms that aligned with powerful Intimacies as well, isn\u2019t it? Anyway, it can definitely be seen as weaker on fronts such as that, not quite having the same defence against malefic powers and transformations, and even several of the actual things that manage Intimacies, but it\u2019s not boring, or irrelevant, and it has its own distinct lines of strength running through it. As a possible comparison to Solars, I actually find it to be one of the more interesting ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T05:17:23-07:00","id":1207222,"title":"","content":"All right, last Ability before the remaining seventeen come out on Tuesday. Investigation starts off with another straightforward success adder that also rerolls 6s, and advances into Tampering-Detection Technique; it makes nice use of the newly added case scene action by enhancing it to allow determination of concealed evidence, as well as having a unique action of observing an object and knowing whether or not it has been interfered with in some criminal manner recently.<br /> <br /> Permeating Insight also has a nice little combination of effects; it\u2019s another that grants a non-Charm dice bonus in order to profile characters, and then grants an Investigation specialty on the person that you profiled that can last forever without needing a mote commitment. I\u2019m getting this image of being able to develop a criminal nemesis on the fly.<br /> <br /> So Scent-of-Crime Method allows one to make an enhanced roll to realise that somebody in their presence has recently committed a crime, while actually figuring out who it was requires them to be profiled. I like how that\u2019s useful, but still limited, and prompts further action. While further assisting those profile actions is Heart-Maze Navigation, allowing one to penalize a target\u2019s Guile with Intimacies (and rapidly increase the speed of the action, if in Water Aura), which I find to be another nice instance of Water slipping between seams and cracks.<br /> <br /> Revelation-of-Associates Hunch is now a Fire Charm, and thus uses fire-based imagery not only as the basis of its concept of determining how many people were involved in a crime, but as the basis for how the Dragon Blood intuits it. There\u2019s actually a nice form of connection there, that the number of criminals is metaphorically a fire casting off numerous embers that the Exalt can literally, physically feel.<br /> <br /> Bloodhound\u2019s Nose Technique runs on the curious image of a Dragon Blood being able to actually pick up a criminal\u2019s scent from a crime scene, and pursuing them through that. I\u2019m going to go with the idea that such isn\u2019t just a matter of Water or Wood power, but a bit of actual draconic imagery touching off of one of their Charms.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s one more straightforward Charm to remove penalties, and then it\u2019s into the Signatures. Warrant of Divine Safety actually looks remarkably powerful; you can bind somebody to their word (under the right circumstances, such as hospitality offered by somebody who is legally within a house) such that violations incur actually elemental phenomena manifesting to halt or punish the offenders. It only lasts a few hours, is confined to a certain space, and for entities of higher Essence than the user can \u201conly\u201d extend to giving heavy penalties or creating environmental hazards, but even within those confines it\u2019s got clear benefits as to how it safeguards and what kinds of avenue it can open up. It\u2019s a very interesting Charm, mystical, <i>very</i> overtly elemental, and with some grand story potential.<br /> <br /> Echoes Caught in Stone has a tough act to follow, but\u2026 it does all right. Its capacity to hear words that were spoken around a suspect object is limited, but I suspect that\u2019s necessary to prevent it from being overpowered or bent towards purposes a bit too far afield from Investigation.<br /> <br /> Heh, Shadow-Immolating Talon has a neat effect in the form of enhancing an actual, physical attack with an armour-piercing question, that can compel the one struck by it to answer honestly and unequivocally (even if the attack means that they\u2019re dying). The only recourse of the victim is if they have an opposing Defining Intimacy, and even then they only get to give an obscure or incomplete answer. It even has the benefit of not wasting the motes if the attack is made on somebody who couldn\u2019t actually answer, although the attack is not enhanced either. As somebody whose world view is strongly influenced by the idea of incompleteness of information, this is a Charm that speaks to me; if an investigation should end in violence, the pursuer has recourse to ensuring that they actually do finally get an answer, rather than needing to kill the last person that could clarify what was even going on.<br /> <br /> Clear Water Prana is more straightforward compared to the other three, providing some strong benefits to casing a scene, being able to detect deliberately hidden items in that scene, and empowering them to contest magically enhanced concealment. Not much more to say about it than that.<br /> <br /> While Death-Unravelling Eye allows one to examine a corpse, even a heavily decayed one, without penalties related to the damage to the body, and being able to form a mental picture of it when fresh for the purposes of identification and further medical examination. Plus being able to tell the body\u2019s process of decay, which can be used as a basis for its own deductions. I find it to be a good Investigation Charm for the manner in which it improves such queries with additional diagnostic tools and can provide additional direction to a story. It\u2019s not an absolute thing, rather empowering the Exalt to ask questions and find answers that they might otherwise be incapable of.<br /> <br /> A Face in the Fog is another Mute Charm, allowing one to form a kind of visual silhouette of a criminal if one successfully cases a scene that somebody attempted to conceal. This is another one that feels as though it\u2019s very good at driving stories, both for providing additional information to pursue and creating a capacity for a good \u201caha\u201d moment when the quarry is actually discovered. I\u2019ve got this mental picture of a Dragon Blood having investigated a case that went cold years ago, still having the mental imprint of the perpetrator\u2019s image, and then at some point they happen to meet somebody and profile them as a matter of course, and are shocked to feel the murky image in their head suddenly come into focus to reveal the person in front of them.<br /> <br /> Falsehood-Unearthing Attitude is an Earth Charm, with the rather distinct effect of being able to determine Intimacies that a person would be willing to lie for the benefit of. Even apart from investigations, that\u2019s an interesting possible avenue of information for an Exalt to have, whether it be informing their picture of that person\u2019s character or having an idea of what kinds of things they would say that might be lies even before they say them (and thus, what to give particular scrutiny to).<br /> <br /> Foul Stench of Lies Discernment is finally the Dragon Blooded having their own version of the Charm to detect lies. It\u2019s a bit less absolute than Judge\u2019s Ear Technique and is another one tied into the profiling character action, which endears me a bit more to it.<br /> <br /> Scent of the Stranger\u2019s Threshold is a nicely flavoured Wood Charm to determine whether or not a given individual is from round these parts. I like the way it always registers Fair Folk as non-natives, which seems like it would be lent to another nice moment of realisation as the Exalt looks more into them and finds a contradiction in the apparent fact that they\u2019ve lived in the area for as long as anybody can remember. It also has an interesting synergy with Bloodhound\u2019s Nose Technique, considering that telling whether or not a specific, known person is from a given area is a kind of inversion of the Charm\u2019s normal effect.<br /> <br /> Heh, there are a few non-Water Charms concentrated more at the top. Homeward Trail Discovery Method is Air, and lets one build upon the prior Charm\u2019s power to tell whether a target is from somewhere to be able to intuit when one sees their own actual home, as well as boosting actions to enter it through things like breaking down the door or picking its lock.<br /> <br /> Back to Water, and River-of-Memory Meditation acts like a kind of mental database, letting a character measure the details of a crime against people that have been recently profiled, allowing one to determine that somebody would have had motive (even if it doesn\u2019t on its own reveal what that motive could have been), as well as whether or not the crime scene contains a particular identifying characteristic or calling card (including telling it apart from somebody copying it). This is an interesting one for the manner in which it can start investigation stories, or maybe kind of come in the middle of them. I\u2019m seeing the Agatha Christie-esque story in which the first session of a story consists of introducing a cast of characters, many of whom the investigator is liable to profile, and then the second begins with an actual crime committed and the Exalt being able to narrow their list of suspects from the outset.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s an Essence 5 Charm in the form of Inescapable Wave Insight. This one provides a number of benefits if a character should have already uncovered a variable number of clues, to allow one to pursue the case to its conclusion: bonus dice are given to rolls to find and fight the one that they\u2019re looking for, Charms to enhance the investigation have lower Willpower costs and\u2026 I presume they get the Mute keyword, but actually think the wording is a little bit unclear, and they can treat influence to get them to drop the investigation as unacceptable (as is anything to override their own judgement on what to do with their quarry, if they should be caught).<br /> <br /> I actually think that the Investigation Charms of Terrestrials are better than those of Solars in a few respects. Not stronger, but I feel as though these more effectively play into and enhance narratives of investigating a crime or pursuing a truth, with Charms more frequently based on improving one\u2019s diagnostic arsenal and compelling one onto the next stage of pursuit, or into the next question, as well as some very distinct and attractive methods for the story to end.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s it for now. Come Tuesday, I look forward to starting off with the Larceny Charms that Dragon Blooded criminals might pit against these powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T06:16:55-07:00","id":1207958,"title":"","content":"All right, with seventeen Abilities to go through, I\u2019m going to want to pick up the pace a bit to keep ahead of the next update.<br /> <br /> First off, for a reason I find hard to define, I like Underground River\u2019s Flow as the name for the initial Larceny Charm; I guess it\u2019s just because it\u2019s a cute idea for crossing water imagery over with this Ability. Then there\u2019s Flowing Body Disguise, the first appearance modifying Charm, with not only eliminating penalties for disguises to impersonate specific people or make significant alterations to appearance, but actually provides a non-Charm bonus success to impersonating a blood relative.<br /> <br /> There are a few straightforward Charms to enhance criminal or underhanded activity before Observer Awareness Method, allowing one to roll to determine that they\u2019re being watched. Then there\u2019s the first of the non-water Charms, Rose-Among-Thorns Distinction, which allows one to acquire a specialty in interaction with a specific criminal organisation and convince others that they belong to it. Following that is the Air Charm Whispering Thief Technique, allowing one to perform supernatural feats of ventriloquism to make their own voice sound from elsewhere, or allow them to speak without breaking their stealth.<br /> <br /> Back to Water with the Charm Artful Flowing Theft, which improves both attempts to steal and making it more difficult for the target to notice, limited to only being used once per scene. The Earth Charm Dragon\u2019s Hidden Treasure was, I believe, among the previewed ones, allowing an Exalt to hide an object inside of structures of earth or stone. Face-Stealing Reflection is an interesting take on a familiar concept; it touches on a usual \u201cread somebody\u2019s mind to disguise as one they know\u201d effect, but ties it to the lower power of the Dragon Blooded by making it dependent on a modified read intentions action, and bases it on revealing a Tie (and its nature) to somebody that the Dragon Blooded already knows well enough to try disguising as. I find this to be another good example of making the Dragon Blooded less powerful, but using a more interesting mechanical approach than just the weaker version of a Charm a Solar or Lunar might have.<br /> Bramble Purse Technique allows one to penalise attempts to pickpocket them, and inflicts injury upon those who fail to do so. Instant Disguise Prana allows one to more rapidly disguise themselves and do so without the need for any tools (although granting double 9s if they do, coming back to my preference for powers that encourage such). And Waters-of-Honesty Method allows one to make a read intentions roll to identify somebody engaged in cheating or criminal activity and what they\u2019re doing (with even failure allowing one to intuit that something underhanded has taken place).<br /> <br /> The Signature Air Charm is Vault-Emptying Whirlwind Heist, which is their version of the \u201cmake retroactive changes as a representation of planning for contingencies\u201d effect. Specifically, one needs to perform the Charm prior to the actual crime, making a roll and banking the successes to be spent on Charm bonuses to a number of helpful Abilities and various retroactive effects, ranging from being able to leave some kind of calling card to retroactively using the evidence concealing Charm.<br /> <br /> Dragon Snatches Jewel is their version of an enhanced disarm gambit (doubling 9s on the roll and refunding the Initiative cost if they succeed) that allows one to automatically attune a snatched Artifact weapon, or its hearthstone. It\u2019s straightforward, but distinctly powerful for Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Burning Sins Seduction allows one to make a specialised inspire roll to turn one against the law or stoke an attraction to criminality, although the player of the target is the one that decides what the provoked emotion is and the specific Intimacy that they\u2019d be willing to break the law for (instantly forming a Minor one to fulfil that purpose if none of the others fit the bill).<br /> <br /> Flowing God-Dragon Stance is the first Larceny Charm with the Aura keyword, and is the uncommon Signature Charm with <i>multiple</i> prerequisites, allowing one to actually convert their body into liquid. In that form, they can naturally flow through any gaps that aren\u2019t watertight, impossible to grapple without magic, makes one more difficult to damage, and improves stealth (especially in water). It has a failsafe against the Charm ending in a space too tight for the Exalt. It\u2019s another fairly straightforward effect, but a rather dramatic and iconic one.<br /> <br /> And Terrifying Forest-Devil Mask was another previewed one, allowing one to don a mask that creates an iconic persona, acquiring additional specialties, an unchangeable Defining Intimacy appropriate to the persona, and can induce a Minor Tie to the persona in people who don\u2019t see past the disguise. My thoughts on this are the same as when I first saw it; how it\u2019s an interesting extension of a basic concept of the Ability, and a nice synthesis of Wood in its literal and metaphorical details.<br /> <br /> For a fun little countermeasure if somebody manages to see past a character\u2019s disguise, there\u2019s Vaporous Visage Evasion, allowing one to reflexively obscure their features with supernaturally generated mist. It breaks down the disguise for general onlookers, but allows one to conceal their identity against somebody that the disguise has already failed against.<br /> Incendiary Accusation Approach is a fun little comeuppance effect, building on the Charm to uncover cheating and the like by causing the unveiled person to mildly light on fire in a manner that reveals their wrongdoing to any onlookers.<br /> <br /> Investigation-Deflecting Current was already hinted at in the Signature Air Charm, and is elaborated as a Charm that specifically conceals evidence in a manner that implicates a particular person known to the Exalt. Characters who fail in their investigations find the false leads, while even the successes find both, and can\u2019t tell the difference (with mechanics provided for how one can figure out which clues are false).<br /> <br /> Mischievous Wind Grasp provides one with the power to generate subtle wind currents for purposes of knocking around small objects in a manner that readies them to be picked up by the Charm\u2019s user. That subtle Charm is appropriately followed up by Exploding Evidence Technique, which\u2026 is pretty self-explanatory (the only necessary elaboration being that it rigs the evidence to explode only if somebody tries, and fails, to case a scene imbued with the Essence).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s another returning Charm with Window-In-The-Door Technique, allowing one to see through solid obstacles, and even use Mischievous Wind Grasp through them. I think it may be slightly more mechanically intricate than it used to be, but it\u2019s a basically solid Charm.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s a couple of Essence 5 Charms. Expectation-Mirroring Stance allows one to build off of Face-Stealing Reflection, allowing one to instantaneously assume the appearance of somebody revealed by the prior Charm, even reaping additional motes for threshold successes on the initial read intentions roll. And Infallible Alibi Approach allows an Exalt to intuit evidence of their wrongdoing that they\u2019ve put effort into concealing is being discovered, giving them an opportunity to remotely destroy the evidence, carrying the rather interesting cost (in addition to the motes) of placing an incriminating mark upon the user.<br /> <br /> The Larceny Charms look good overall, although they don\u2019t quite have the wow factor for me that a few other Abilities have had. That might just be appropriate to the nature of this one, though, with all of the subtlety and misdirection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T08:46:19-07:00","id":1207998,"title":"","content":"What did you think about the current power level of the charms? In general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T08:57:57-07:00","id":1208004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgrimas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1207998#post1207998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you think about the current power level of the charms? In general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean what I think the power actually is, or what my opinion on them being less powerful is, or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:48:53-07:00","id":1208190,"title":"","content":"Next up, Linguistics.<br /> <br /> Heh, only one Charm in, and we\u2019re at an out-of-Aspect element. Still, going by the name Cryptic Essence Cipher, it certainly sounds like one fitted to Water. It\u2019s fairly straightforward mechanically, creating a code and designating who can read it. I do like the kinds of stories implied by having the option to make it decipherable to somebody sharing a Principle; the notion of writing an innocuous message that will convey a special meaning to somebody of a particular bent.<br /> <br /> Water Charm Signature-Stealing Calligraphy improves one\u2019s capacity to imitate others in writing, Fire Charm Fervor-Inciting Brushstrokes enhances a written inspire action, and Earth\u2019s Tenacious Dragon Scholar improves Resolve against writing, so they\u2019re fairly basic.<br /> <br /> Back to Air is the return of the classic Wind-Carried Words Technique. It\u2019s about the same as it ever was, being able to send your words a few miles away, although I believe that enhancements from improved Linguistics alone is new. Plus it\u2019s got a rather decent difficulty calculation for what needs to be overcome to magically intercept a message.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve often felt a bit iffy about Language-Learning Ritual, and\u2026 it\u2019s all right. It\u2019s limited enough to not completely overcome the language barrier at convenience, while still be useful enough to be worth using.<br /> <br /> Enigma-Reading Eye is their straightforward code-breaking Charm, and then Thousand Tongues Meditation to offset some of the limits of Language-Learning.<br /> Voices on the Wind reminds me of the Solar Charms to enhance hearing and touch, in a manner that let you listen in with things like a length of string or wire. It\u2019s interesting to consider some ways in which the different power structure leads to some mildly similar effects being put under different umbrellas.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I vaguely recall Speech Without Words as having had more general utility in the past\u2026 oh wait, it can still apply to people in general, just that one gets Sworn Kin added to the limit. I suspect that the detail of it relying on visual signals that can be noticed by others is also new. I need to look back and see if the Charm used to function outright as something like telepathy.<br /> Back to some nasty Water in the form of Caustic Wit Invective to write messages that erode a target\u2019s Intimacies, and then into the Signatures.<br /> <br /> The effect of greatly speeding up writing provided by Flashing Saga Flourish is another example of something fairly basic but strong, with the per story limit giving an interesting sense of how discerning one has to be in what they choose to write.<br /> <br /> Unshattered Diamond Parables has the very distinctive and unusual effect of being able to harness the theme or moral of a work that one has written as the equivalent of an Intimacy in a Decision point. That one seems to particularly have a strength in the form of incentivizing characters to continuously write, as well as the implications from their body of work; is it diverse in order to give them a base of pseudo-Intimacies that they would not naturally possess, or things that continuously reference and reinforce the character\u2019s own beliefs, such that they can still call upon them even if the Intimacy in question has been used to bolster Resolve.<br /> <br /> Fire is realised in Wildfire Words Technique, in the form of a Charm to empower attempts to spread one\u2019s ideas through literature. I feel something for this Charm distinctly, as it reminds me of something that the previous developers once suggested as an idea of what it would be like to live somewhere ruled by the Dragon Blooded, that would still be fairly covert.<br /> <br /> Heh, does it represent a bias on my part if I keep seeing Water as sneaky and underhanded? Anyway, Rewriting the Truth Technique is another Psyche Charm, allowing one to make a powerful written instil action to make somebody believe in something that is untrue. I take it that the Principle doesn\u2019t need anything supporting or justifying it besides the writing itself, so it looks like it can be fairly strong, appropriately offset by being focused on an individual and only being usable once per story (with the very fitting reset condition of getting somebody to act on belief in something that is untrue in an extreme manner).<br /> <br /> Oh, but Enthralling Lotus Calligraphy is another Psyche Charm, imbuing their writing with a draw to bring people to read the letter. I feel as though\u2026 oh, wait, it only works on the person who was intended to receive it. I\u2019ve got to admit, I feel a bit underwhelmed by this one. It\u2019s like, there are a lot of other Linguistics Charms that are operating on the assumption that people can be relied upon to read their letters, and here\u2019s a power that only has an effect that is relevant on the assumption that somebody won\u2019t do so? I don\u2019t know, maybe it can be targeted at somebody that you know will be very adamant about not reading their letter, but otherwise?<br /> <br /> Err, Incendiary Argument Approach for your supernaturally provocative writing. Poisoned Tongue Technique lets one disrupt the attempts of another to make social influence. And Reading the Unspoken Word gives one an intuition for what a given listener expects to hear, which can have benefits to impersonation or general conduct, either of which can provide non-Charm dice.<br /> Dragon\u2019s Voice Mastery is just a kind of general improvement to speaking actions that align with higher Principles. While Tantalizing Dragon\u2019s Tongue is provocative in a rather different manner than Incendiary Argument.<br /> <br /> Building off of Enthralling Lotus Calligraphy is Intoxicating Lotus Manuscript, which looks like a much more readily applied power; creating written works that are outright addictive to read. It\u2019s certainly an interesting effect, although I can\u2019t find much more to say about it.<br /> <br /> Last of all is With One Mind. It\u2019s possible that I conflated Speech Without Words with this, considering how it actually does create a telepathic bond. I\u2019d say that before it was rather nebulous, so it benefits a lot from additions such as defend other and distract gambits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T18:02:33-07:00","id":1208264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208190#post1208190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, but Enthralling Lotus Calligraphy is another Psyche Charm, imbuing their writing with a draw to bring people to read the letter. I feel as though\u2026 oh, wait, it only works on the person who was intended to receive it. I\u2019ve got to admit, I feel a bit underwhelmed by this one. It\u2019s like, there are a lot of other Linguistics Charms that are operating on the assumption that people can be relied upon to read their letters, and here\u2019s a power that only has an effect that is relevant on the assumption that somebody won\u2019t do so? I don\u2019t know, maybe it can be targeted at somebody that you know will be very adamant about not reading their letter, but otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have access to the preview, so I may be off-base here, but maybe you could use it not to get the attention of someone that wouldn't read your letter, but of someone who would take a long time to do so when you want it read as soon as possible? That merchant prince who is super-busy and has a backlog of 300 things to read and respond to? Well, I guess <i>your </i>business proposal just happens to have <i>something </i>intriguing about it that will make the merchant put it ahead of the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T19:06:02-07:00","id":1208278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208264#post1208264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That merchant prince who is super-busy and has a backlog of 300 things to read and respond to? Well, I guess <i>your </i>business proposal just happens to have <i>something </i>intriguing about it that will make the merchant put it ahead of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPossibly? It does actually say that the compulsion won't force somebody to endanger themselves or abandon pressing tasks, so it might depend a bit on the circumstances of why the letter has fallen to the bottom of their in tray.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe main thing that strikes me is a sense that it's underwhelming specifically as a Signature Charm, particularly compared to the other Linguistics ones that, even when they're straightforward, are fairly solid. I'm honestly grappling with whether or not to dismiss the Charm as an air-breathing mermaid.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's particularly annoying because the flavour text refers to it as a &quot;trap from beautiful words&quot;, which might suggest that there's something dangerous or sinister or seductive in the Charm, but the result comes across as relatively benign, especially when it says that it can't endanger somebody.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not saying that it's useless, but it does feel a bit like it's in that &quot;fan perception of Sidereal Charms&quot; space in which you'd really need to bend it to some convoluted applications to get some of the best use out of it. <i>Unless</i> one places it into a context of Written-only Charms having a logical weakness in which they can go completely to waste if they're not actually read by anybody (or, since a lot of the relevant Dragon Blooded Charms are target specific, aren't read by the correct person), but that introduces its own issues. I feel that if that weakness is leaned too heavily on, then it unduly messes up a large number of Charms, but to not lean on it at all renders this one rather prominent Charm kind of redundant. I can't help but feel that it exists in the state of Nightboat encountering a canal; it's a thing whose most prominent use would arise only to counter obstacles that only exist in the first place to make it useful.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd say if it was the kind of thing that worked on people in general, or maybe had some effect that allowed it to compel people who aren't its intended recipient to do their best to see it delivered (whether carrying it themselves or passing it along to somebody who can reasonably carry it along, creating a chain of connections) until it reached the person that will actually be forced to read it, that would be something more compelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T20:26:49-07:00","id":1208304,"title":"","content":"All right, checking out Lore before calling it a night. This should be interesting, considering how in the past, it was home to some of the more overt elemental interactions.<br /> <br /> The Excellency, Careful Insight-Gathering Study, obviously adds a benefit to Lore\u2019s new hotness of introducing and challenging facts. Hmm, I was expecting that to be followed immediately by a tree expanding on improvements to fact actions, but instead we get an interesting effect of being able to use Lore to perform instil actions to make a person highly receptive to being taught by the Exalt. Conversely, Flawless Study Focus allows the character to engage in study that allows them to gain a temporary additional Lore specialty.<br /> <br /> Now we get to the ones to connect with elements. Elemental Concentration Trance to allow one to briefly meditate upon a physical expression of an element, and the introduce facts related to subjects thematically connected to that element (such as masonry to Earth) using any of a variety of Abilities. I can\u2019t quite recall how the Charm worked in prior Editions, but this is both an intriguing method of tying it to the Lore mechanic, and conveying the idea of drawing enlightenment and knowledge directly from the elements. Whereas Dragon-Kin Empowerment not only allows one to transfer some motes, but their own Elemental Aura (and, at a higher level, some of the anima) to other Dragon Blooded. It\u2019s another nice example of the benefits to the Terrestrial Exalted working as teams.<br /> <br /> That leads to that old favourite, Elemental Bolt Attack. The first thing that I notice is how its cost can now include a level of anima, which apart from any other mechanical considerations, just conveys a nice visual effect (especially if combining with a non-Aspect element). I\u2019d say it has some decent damage, and some nice tactical variations between the elements.<br /> <br /> Elemental Empowerment Meditation returns to allow characters to draw motes from the elements, necessarily offset by factors such as a potential cost in health, the motes being limited to Charms of the element that they were drawn from, and only being available once per day (with no reset condition).<br /> <br /> That leads back into the Charms more directly associated with the Ability, starting with Sagacious Elder\u2019s Instruction, allowing one to empower people that one has advised with an idea supported by a fact that the user introduced, by giving those persons an appropriate temporary specialty that can be applied to <i>any</i> Ability. It\u2019s a handy little tool for characters in an instructing or supervisory role. Following that is Stern Tutor Discipline, a more straightforward Charm to help teach people things such as Attributes and Abilities, and ultimately magical powers.<br /> <br /> Lightning Flash Inspiration allows the user to reroll non-1 failures on Lore rolls, and then it\u2019s the Signatures. Fulminating Thunderhead Brilliance allows one to modify rolls to introduce facts, instead stating a goal that one seeks and rolling to have the Storyteller introduce or provide a fact that would assist in achieving that goal. I\u2019ll have to see, but I think this might be a good Dragon Blooded variation on the Solar capacity to predict (or create) the future, both in its realisation of being less powerful while still driving stories forward, and the description of the mindset used when following lines of intuition to arrive at those conclusions.<br /> <br /> Hoo boy, Truth-In-Stone Binding is wordy. Let me see\u2026 ah, it allows one to use Lore in a special gambit against Wyld creatures to instantly and indefinitely calcify them, with the only possibility for escape being if words on the resulting stony body being removed in some fashion. It can also be employed against Wyld landscape features, rendering them safe to people of Creation. It\u2019s suggested that very powerful beings or phenomena can only be contained temporarily, but otherwise it\u2019s a rather powerful Charm. Obviously a number of steps below what Solars can do with the Wyld, but far from insignificant, and a nice realisation of this power level and element covering this aspect of Lore. Possibly a bit <i>too</i> good, although I\u2019ll need to check back on the gambit rules to fully figure it out. Mind, as a Signature Charm, it\u2019s still offset by how choosing this means not choosing the others.<br /> <br /> Ten Thousand Minds Ablaze enables the wielder to create a combined introduce fact and instil Intimacy (of fascination regarding the revealed fact) into a single action, which can target a large number at the same time without penalty.<br /> <br /> Ink-Black Ocean Depths lets one very rapidly absorb information, as well as vandalizing the media containing the absorbed info to disrupt others being able to learn it, further adding to Water's disreputable nature.<br /> <br /> And Root-and-Branch Wisdom gives the user the power to cultivate an exchange of positive emotional connections between the use and a student; it doesn\u2019t even require motes or a dice roll. It can also grant the user additional specialties, if the teacher\u2019s Tie should remain intact by the end of the story.<br /> <br /> Aaaand I\u2019m too tired to continue with this right now. I\u2019d say the last of the Signature Charms is a decent place to let off, and I\u2019ll resume first thing tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T04:52:27-07:00","id":1208395,"title":"","content":"All right, I\u2019m back.<br /> <br /> Now, there\u2019s Elemental Succor Method, an upgrade on top of Elemental Empowerment that allows the user to convert the motes gained by elemental meditation into healing some damage. Then Thunderstruck Charlatan Imprecation, an empowered form of challenging facts; if expressed as a spoken rebuke to the one who made the statement, and beating the Resolve, then it humbles the challenger and forms or strengthens an appropriate Tie to the Exalt, as well as striking them temporarily dumb. It\u2019s nice to see that the Dragon Blooded get their own version of being the highly impressive teacher or debater.<br /> <br /> Back to elemental manipulation with Elemental Burst Technique, allowing one to use Aura to improve their Elemental Bolt and make it explode. While it has the standard multi-attack quality of dividing Initiative between targets, it\u2019s interesting how several elements provide their own methods of adding on to that damage, and the ones that don\u2019t carry their own complications. The reset condition of using Elemental Bolt Attack to lower an enemy\u2019s Initiative below the Exalt\u2019s also seems fairly reasonable.<br /> <br /> Now at Essence 4, and there\u2019s the expensive looking Eternal Mind Meditation. Ahh, something to allow one to introduce facts without regard to their educational backgrounds. I initially thought that it functioned off of a kind of consultation of the Akashic record, but now I see it\u2019s supposed to be based in a complete immersion in one\u2019s own life experiences, which is a nicely distinctive basis for one finding important information. Oh, and I like how that basis also allows it to function as a means of overcoming memory altering effects. While I find that the Charm\u2019s basis is a bit more abstract and nebulous than a person being able to literally have a total recall of their life, I\u2019m liking an image that I\u2019m forming in which older Dragon Blooded who might use the Charm frequently are less likely to be nostalgic, or form idealised narratives of their own past; they may not precisely remember their whole life, but they can effectively detach themselves from filling in the gaps with sentiment. I\u2019m not saying that would be a good thing or bad thing, just a thing.<br /> <br /> Glorious Birthright Font is another meditation upgrade, this time with the simple (but potentially quite useful) addition of getting some Willpower on top of whatever else they were drawing from the element.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s gotten into Essence 5, which looks like it has more Charms than usual. Endless Coils Enlightenment improves Eternal Mind Meditation, by allowing the user to apply that Charm as a kind of communal experience, being able to draw upon the lives of additional Dragon Blooded in establishing one\u2019s facts, also providing the benefit of some non-Charm dice. I take it that the last line has a bit of a typo, and is meant to read as the Charm bestowing a Major Tie towards the world\u2019s Dragon Blooded as a collective, upon those who take part in that communal experience. It\u2019s a nice enhancement of the prior Charm\u2019s potential, and an interesting idea for an experience of the participating Exalted.<br /> <br /> The Wind Turns is a final extension of being able to draw Essence from the world, letting one instantaneously draw in a bunch of motes for oneself and one\u2019s Sworn Kin, at the cost of some Willpower, their Air Aura, and almost definitely being limited to use in combat.<br /> <br /> And the much-vaunted Dragon Vortex Attack has been brought home from its brief stay in War. It makes sense that this would be dependent on and expend Aura, and I find that and the requirement for minimum Initiative to help root such an otherwise powerful effect into the standing of the Terrestrial Exalted; they still get the awesome power, but a bit less immediately than they used to. Mind, that power is probably still a bit less extreme than it used to be, even if it\u2019s still something to worry about. Although on the other hand, the element that one goes for might further improve the damage to a significant degree; if nothing else, the descriptions of them help make it feel a bit more like a local natural disaster than a generic energy vortex. Ah, but as one last benefit, there\u2019s a return of that old idea of Dragon Blooded being able to combine their power, in the form of Hearthmates being able to expend their own Auras into the vortex to add their Initiative, increase the difficulty of the environmental hazard made by the power, and put in another elemental effect. I actually like that being reserved here quite a bit, both for how it keeps other Charms from being too finickity, while also giving the image of one of the most iconic destructive effects of the Terrestrial Exalted being maximized when many Dragons are fighting as one.<br /> <br /> So I think Lore is quite good. It effectively distinguishes itself from the Solar form with things such as its elemental meditation and attacking, while still making generous and frequently intriguing use of the new mechanics for introducing information into the chronicle. It\u2019s another one in which it\u2019s evident in multiple spots where it is less powerful, while still being interesting and evocative in its own right.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's all of the Ls, so I'm looking forward to seeing what they do with Medicine (another one where I think it got short shrift and had to rely on adding a few gimmicks to make it interesting) and Melee (because swords are cool).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T05:19:11-07:00","id":1208401,"title":"","content":"On the rider damages of Dragon Vortex Attack:<br /> Double 9 is a good 50% more damage - though the chance to do any damage is unchanged.<br /> A Short Fall is 5B dice + 3B levels of damage.<br /> That hazard, right there? It's the reason Flight of the Brilliant Raptor is almost as good an opener as it is a finisher, and this one is a bit better.<br /> On average, that tsunami's adding 3B for every 8L the vortex does, a veritable 40% extra damage with some pigeon chess quality on top. It more or less should toss people to the edges of the vortex.<br /> That poison will have at least 6 rounds to resist, and it's probably closer to 8-10, with a heavy penalty to accompany, being all but guaranteed against a target that isn't a supernal/high essence resistance master.<br /> <br /> It's very nasty all around. Earth is particularly nastier on the minimum vortexes (being analog to some 13 initiative in damage dice), along with Wood making them great &quot;openers&quot; for damage and still good for their added control if used later.<br /> Fire wants to be an opener to enjoy that hazard, but doesn't do anything else and thus is wasted on a nuke DVA. It's particularly valuable against large numbers of individuals hit, since its damage is not divided.<br /> Air/water absolutely destroy when you go into 30+ initiatives, thus being prime candidates for vortexes with multiple dragon-blooded and those moments where you manage to build up ludicrous initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-18-2018, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T07:28:57-07:00","id":1208432,"title":"","content":"So the Medicine Excellency provides an interesting suggestion of what a running theme might be, with its note on refining to perfection and how that lets filling your dice cap give you an extra success. Disease-Banishing Technique is another example of a Charm that grants somebody a specialty, Venom Expulsion Method lets you perform a rush job on treating poison, and Wound-Closing Technique is back as one to let you downgrade the severity of a patient\u2019s injuries. That\u2019s the basic trifecta, so let\u2019s see where it goes from there.<br /> <br /> Ailment-Sensing Meditation is basic, but then there\u2019s Nature\u2019s Healing Bounty to serve as the Dragon Blooded version of the Charm to be divested of equipment by allowing one to improvise with credible and available sources of plants, or else use them to supplement one\u2019s medical equipment.<br /> <br /> Constitution-Tempering Discipline lets one play with the new disease rules by converting the automatic botches they apply into straightforward dice penalties for patients that have already been treated with Infection-Banishing, albeit not indefinitely. Poisoner\u2019s Deft Hand goes in on the other side of Wood, and I can alternately read that as the Exalt\u2019s Essence enhancing the poison itself, or their enhanced medical knowledge allowing it to be applied with particular precision or potency.<br /> <br /> Death-Defying Endeavor is a rather striking name, although the actual effect is a straightforward dice trick. Grievous Wound Alteration Energy upgrades the previous healing Charm to allow it to treat aggravated damage. Aaand it\u2019s at the Signatures already.<br /> <br /> Purity-of-Mind Method allows one to treat Flaws representing mental illness in a rather intricate manner. I appreciate how it can\u2019t remove the illness completely, instead going for being able to reduce it to its least intense state as well as helping one cope with episodes. Magically removing mental illness has always been something that I found a bit iffy, both for it being too much of an easy way out and for the statement it made about what qualified as an ideal state of mind. I prefer the subject to be approached like this; a method of providing assistance, without trivialising the issue or invalidating the identity of a person for whom such matters <i>are</i> the default and the natural.<br /> <br /> Marmoreal Body Fortification is much simpler in comparison, with its power to reinforce the body of a patient to provide temporary extra health levels and occasional soak.<br /> <br /> Unbinding the Inner Flame looks like a neat method of briefly overclocking a person\u2019s body, with a number of small, but key, bonuses to apply in combat, followed by a bit of a nasty crash.<br /> <br /> Body-Cleansing Ablution is a more subtle kind of enhancement than the previous, alleviating pain in the form of wound penalties (I presume it applies even to wounds that are inflicted after receiving the treatment) and providing a bit of assistance to treating disease and poison.<br /> <br /> While Rebirth of Flesh and Ivy allows one to fix a wounded person up with plant material sprouted from the anima, represented by being able to instantly heal damage levels, as well as being able to fix up forms of crippling damage that the patient could recover from (so splinting a broken arm is fine, but you can\u2019t give them a prosthetic tree limb). The one who was healed in that manner can elect to incorporate memorials of it into their eventually healed body, and it has the nice reset condition of saving somebody that had been reduced to their Incapacitated health level.<br /> <br /> The Signature Charms are good overall, although the middle three are fairly basic as different forms of providing an enhancement. The last has striking visual effects, while the first has very nice implications for characterisation.<br /> <br /> Moving on, there\u2019s Dread Infection Strike. This one is quite explicit in being based in Essence, and allows one to perform a special gambit in combat to infect somebody with a disease that the Terrestrial has already successfully treated. I like the image that I get from that, of their Wood Essence partaking of the quality of diseases that they\u2019ve managed to dominate, to eventually learn to inflict it upon others. At higher Essence, they can learn to extend that power to supernatural ailments (people had best be wary of veterans of war against the Bull of the North or Mask of Winters, lest they be given the dreaded bonus eruptus), although it can\u2019t handle malady of the likes of the Great Contagion.<br /> <br /> Huh, interesting that it\u2019s taken this long to get a non-Wood Charm outside of the Signatures. I suppose that this particular Ability would be one that would not accommodate quite as many deviations from its element. Anyway, Flesh-as-Stone Inurement is another type of Charm to alleviate wound penalties; possibly less potent than the Signature that did it, but with the additional application of being able to weaponise its\u2026 darn, I\u2019m sure there\u2019s an adjective related to morphine that I want to use, but it\u2019s slipped from my mind\u2026 anyway, use that on an enemy in order to numb their limbs in a manner that penalises their use until one gets some bed rest. It almost looks like an example of pre-empting a manner in which some players might want to apply a power to numb the body, and so goes ahead and systemizes it directly.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4, Jade Crucible Method allows one to take an aggravated health level of damage in exchange for being able to reap additional motes and Willpower to be applied to Medicine effects. I can see this one applying most heavily to a field medic situation, in which one has a number of patients to treat and it pushes them to the limit. As a possible alternative, it might entail a case of wanting some extra motes to put into enhancing an ally, so that they can head into battle with a fuller tank (even if they have to deal with a persistent injury).<br /> <br /> Last of all, there\u2019s the Essence 5 Charm, Most Beneficent Seed of the Five Dragons. Heh, for a moment I was worried that this was going to be a return of one messing around with Aspects, but no, it just lets a physician sacrifice their own blood to give some of its vitality to the patient, providing a rare double 7s effect to a roll for treatment.<br /> <br /> With that, I\u2019d say that the Medicine Charms have done a good job, filling out some of the space of providing treatments, exploring a few spaces unfamiliar to Solars, not needing to add a gimmick with Aspects, and having a very measured and sophisticated approach to the subject of mental health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T16:49:02-07:00","id":1208623,"title":"","content":"Now, to look for some enjoyable bits around Melee.<br /> <br /> Stoking Bonfire Style looks rather wordy for an Excellency Charm. It allows one to add bonuses to Melee rolls and increase their Parry, but has the additional benefit of having its cost lowered every time it is used against the same opponent after having been successful against them. I speculate that this is setting up how the Fire quality of Melee will work, with effects that can build up as they\u2019re applied against opponents, evoking the image of a flame that is stoked to ever greater intensity.<br /> <br /> Next is Burning Fury Wreath to let one ignore points of Hardness in an enemy\u2019s armour and Flame-Borne Interception, which allows one to increase their Parry by 1 each time they successfully block an attack for the duration of a round. Since it\u2019s not referred to as a non-Charm bonus, that would still be limited to one\u2019s dice cap, but considering how it costs 3 motes compared to the 2 motes per point that the Excellency costs, it can certainly be more efficient, if a bit of a gamble.<br /> <br /> Ah good, there\u2019s Blinding Spark Distraction again to let one make blinding sparks from their weapon, this time working in clashes as well as parrying. Then a Water Charm, Graceful Flowing Defense (which sounds like a familiar name, which I wonder if it used to belong to another Ability) that allows the user to reduce penalties to their Parry, especially if they\u2019re in Water Aura, a rather nice example of a stronger Dragon Blooded power that can be brought down a bit by using the Charms that surround it.<br /> <br /> Crimson Fang Bite provides a fairly straightforward bonus to damage rolls, and then the Wood Charm with the great name of Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite that allows one to increase the Overwhelming value of attacks and, in Aura, the raw damage as well.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s Elemental Sheath, the rather curious Dragon Blooded variation on a Charm to banish a weapon Elsewhere; it only works on jade weapons, and is based on sending the weapon on through a local instance of an element (or a level of their anima), to be pulled later out of the same kind of substance. It\u2019s an interesting kind of variation; it doesn\u2019t necessarily change anything in the basic function of an Elsewhere storage Charm, but it plays into the nature of the Dragon Blooded and how they relate to the world.<br /> <br /> And considering that it\u2019s followed by Dragon-Graced Weapon\u2026 yeah, I suspected it would work like this when I saw them alongside each other, and it\u2019s actually a pretty damn cool image; that one enhances their weapon with elemental power not just by will, but by drawing the element along as the weapon is unsheathed from Elsewhere through it (although there\u2019s also the option to simply form a regular weapon out of the element). As for the advantages provided by each element, they\u2019re not massive or anything, but I imagine that some of them can synergize nicely with some weapons.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s Crossfire Flash to enhance the Blinding Sparks into scorching flames that allows one to weaken an enemy\u2019s roll in a clash, and Flame Warden Stance to allow one to apply a defend other action across a scene, with the added benefit of parrying effectively granting one a bonus die to attack rolls. I like how, thus far, so much of Fire Aspected Melee is defensive, if only for the subversion of what one might expect of those things crossed over.<br /> <br /> In that spirit is Blazing Interception, allowing one to apply a counterattack when they successfully defend another, with the added benefit if they\u2019re in Fire Aura of letting the defended person make a distract gambit to benefit the counterattack. It actually gives an interesting image of what can make a Dragon Blooded weapon fighter dangerous; being in the middle of a group of allies to defend them, and building off of that as a whirring engine of deadly reprisal.<br /> <br /> Now, for the Signature Air Charm, Steel Tempest Strike. It\u2019s not quite the kind of thing that the old developers suggested of an Air Melee Charm in that preview so many years ago; rather than shooting a blade of wind, it\u2019s another example of using Air to carry the warrior into range of their target for a decisive attack, while still being allowed to attack again. Mind, I like that; it\u2019s not as if Dragon Blooded lack for powers to shoot the elements, and the name gives me an image of somebody clean and quick in a manner that feels very much like becoming the wind yourself.<br /> <br /> Next along is Falling Mountain Fang, a rather different Charm for allowing one to use one of three unique gambits, all extending from a premise of increasing the weight of what is struck; one to make it necessary to use a feat of strength just to not drop your weapon (and levelling penalties even if successful to represent straining to carry and move with it), one that increases the mobility penalty of armour and makes one cost Initiative just to move (with a subsequent use intensifying the effect to the point where the armour\u2019s wearer can\u2019t even stand), and one to make less durable structures implode. It\u2019s actually pretty damn cool; I often like the idea of Elemental Earth extending to gravitational effects, and the idea of knocking them into an enemy through one\u2019s weapon seems\u2026 what am I looking for\u2026 a nicely blunt way of doing it. I don\u2019t know, maybe its just because I find it reminiscent of Octavian\u2019s attacks to cripple enemies by striking them to apply his oil, which I just like all on its own.<br /> <br /> And know there\u2019s the Signature of Melee\u2019s native element, Harnessed Firestorm Assault. While the name might imply an actual fire blast, this happens to be another metaphorical one, but in the form of another of those rare multi-attack Charms that does not evenly divide Initiative\u2026 at least on the surface. Hmm, the fact is that if one is limited to their Dexterity divided by two (rounded down) attacks, then the most that you\u2019ll ever be able to use <i>is</i> two, so even though each attack has a standard of Initiative divided by two\u2026 it\u2019s the same difference; you make two attacks, and they each get half of your Initiative, the same as just about any other multi-attack. Hell, if you don\u2019t have a minimum of Dexterity 4, then it means that you\u2019re spending 10 motes, 1 Willpower and expending your Fire Aura to make a single attack, which will use half of your Initiative. I mean, okay, if you have the right kind of specialty then you can add one more attack in there, but that still seems as though it only really has much value at Dexterity 5. I\u2019ve\u2026 got to be honest here, I don\u2019t think this is a very good Charm. It\u2019s especially a pity, since it\u2019s Fire and Melee, and they ought to go together like gangbusters.<br /> <br /> Well, moving on from that is Roaring River Slash, which uses the image of one\u2019s blade being followed by a ribbon of cutting water to allow one to roll their decisive attack damage twice and <i>combine</i> the results, and this is more like it. I even like the image of how the water\u2019s existence means that magically lit fire will be extinguished.<br /> <br /> Last is Aura of Grasping Branches, letting one adopt a defensive stance reminiscent of dense foliage, allowing them to ignore Onslaught penalties, albeit in an unusual manner; the Exalt is basically given a pool of penalty counters, that is distributed as one chooses across a round. Still, it\u2019s a scene long Charm, the application is flexible, and Wood Aura allows one to not take onslaught penalties if an attack is successfully parried, so I\u2019d say it\u2019s a nice way of rounding out one\u2019s defence.<br /> <br /> Moving on to Dragon Soul Burst, and there finally is something to channel fire into one\u2019s attacks, specifically in the form of a special decisive attack that, while it does require aiming beforehand, has its own damage without needing to use Initiative (although it has that option in Fire Aura), ignores Hardness (meaning that it can be used against an armoured opponent even if the base damage is low), and has a chance of setting the target aflame. Unlike a lot of other Charms like this, it doesn\u2019t even have a limited use. It\u2019s not half bad as a proper fiery sword attack.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s Smoldering Essence Attack, letting one not only increase the amount of Initiative lost on a withering attack, but setting them on a kind of spiritual fire that continues to burn away at their Initiative until a number of turns pass, or the ones so afflicted hits the Dragon Blood who did it to them with a withering attack. It\u2019s another take on an element that I like; along with the physical and metaphorical, being able to apply the logic of the physical <i>to</i> the metaphorical.<br /> <br /> Burning Pinnacle Strike is used to reflexively launch an extra attack (withering or decisive) when an attack raises one\u2019s Initiative to the top of the order, and the Balanced Wood Charm Root-and-Hand Merging lets one connect their hand to their weapon in a manner that improves one\u2019s parry and makes it harder to disarm them.<br /> <br /> Leading up to the often contentious Portentous Comet Deflection. It\u2019s fairly streamlined compared to prior Editions; rather than being a kind of semi-perfect defence, it lets the user reflexively clash an attack with a decisive attack, which may or may not count as one\u2019s attack for the round if they have a Fire Aura to expend. I need to look back at the clash rules to have a good sense of how useful this is, but if nothing else, it fits in with the defensive aspect of Dragon Blooded Melee being more focused on responding offensively than something to simply provide an absolute defence would.<br /> <br /> From there we get Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds, letting one combine power over fire and water to make a clash attack that, if successful, creates a cloud of steam that conveys some Initiative to the Exalt\u2019s allies, and I presume creates a form of obscuring cover, although that isn\u2019t systemically described here.<br /> <br /> And for the last two Charms, we get\u2026 ones that aren\u2019t actually Fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mela\u2019s Flashing Tongue is an Air Charm, that lets the user make repeated withering attacks on an opponent, the number equal to the user\u2019s onslaught penalty, with Air Aura allowing one to make the last strike decisive (based on the image that the previous attacks built a static charge, that can be unleashed with the last).<br /> <br /> Last of all is Mirror-on-Water Focus, a Water Charm of all things at the pinnacle of Fire Aspected Melee. It can only be used if one\u2019s anima is at the dim level (helped by the Charm itself being Mute), and provides a special kind of decisive counterattack that is rolled prior to the opponent making their own attack, only using half the Initiative for damage, but that applies the successes not only to health levels, but also to stripping successes from the ensuing attack. It can be reset, but if I\u2019m reading it correctly, in a rather costly manner, needing to deal at least <i>twenty</i> withering damage in a clash attack generated by Fire Incites Water.<br /> <br /> Melee is an interesting mix of effects; rather than the straightforward attack options that one might expect from it and the element of Fire, it\u2019s oriented around a lot of tricky tactical ideas, such as inflicting certain kinds of penalties on enemies or turning successful defence with it back around on opponents. Hell, it didn\u2019t even have the multi-attack Charm from prior Editions that one of the Terrestrial quick characters from the core did (not a complaint, just an observation). It definitely feels very unique as an attack Ability, and considering how Archery and Brawl have already been seen as having more direct offensive power (and Dodge more direct defence, come to think of it), seems to have its own niche well guarded. Hell, I actually like the sense of its take on offensive fire that I come to in the end; it feels a bit less like wielding flame to blast and incinerate opponents, and more like <i>being</i> flame, something flickering, hard to grasp and often painful for those who do so, and harming more by sparking off embers or swaying a tongue into kindling then being a raging inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T17:19:04-07:00","id":1208633,"title":"","content":"Regarding the fire signature, I think they've given up pretending that people make exalted characters with dexterity less than 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T17:52:35-07:00","id":1208642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208633#post1208633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the fire signature, I think they've given up pretending that people make exalted characters with dexterity less than 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's not really a satisfying answer even if true, and if it <i>was</i> true, then it seems to me that it would be better to just write it as something that lets you make two decisive attacks in a round and splits your Initiative between them (which would still seem a bit weak compared to similar Charms).<br /> <br /> \u200bYou put it like that, and it makes the Charm feel disingenuous to me; as though it's trying to obscure what it actually does behind algebra that doesn't actually amount to much or provide much variation, in an effort to make it look more impressive than it is. I'm not saying that was the intent, it's just how I feel in response to the Charm.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, I've managed to reconcile Enthralling Lotus after somebody else pointed out that you could apply it in scenarios of actively placing the letters in innocuous places that your target will cross paths with, ensuring that they'll be drawn to pick it up and read it without needing to rely on couriers, and that made it feel more worthwhile and in the player's hands. I can't really see Harnessed Firestorm Assault getting the same benefit while it has these mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T18:37:57-07:00","id":1208657,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that seems weird. Making 2 attacks at half-initiative seems worse than making a simple Decisive. You are paying 10m, 1wp and your aura...to possibly have to pay twice for the excellencies to guarantee you hit for the same total damage, and each attack must be able to overcome Hardness. If it worked like the Solar charm Iron Whirlwind Attack in which you only pay for extra charms supplementing it once it would potentially be different*, but with it as you explained it does seem weak.<br /> <br /> *Even so, at that cost you would need a lot of enhancing charms for it to be really worth it, assuming that, like on IWA, excellencies would still have to be paid for each attack.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:17:54-07:00","id":1208667,"title":"","content":"I fully agree with Isator and Danelsan. I just did a quick check through the rest of the melee tree to make sure I'm not missing some devastating combo here and I can't really find one. Honestly with what Danelsan points out even at dex 5 with a specialty it's kind of bad. You can either attack once with another simple charm, or attack 3 times and pay for all the enhancements each time for dealing 1.5 times as much damage if you hit with all three. On top of all that it's a signature charm too, which are supposed to be solid and defining.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I wonder if it might be too uncouth to ask a developer what they think? Maybe we're interpreting it wrong somehow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:39:44-07:00","id":1208675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208667#post1208667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it might be too uncouth to ask a developer what they think?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat thread is filled to the brim with mechanical questions and answers. I'm only not doing it myself because I don't want to say any that will give away Charms that I haven't read yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:42:00-07:00","id":1208676,"title":"","content":"The one thing I can think of in relation to HFA is that it can be either multi-target or single target, allowing flexibility that many multi-attack charms sometimes lack, this flexibility lets you direct fire (say target one has taken some HL damage, and targe 2 is full health, it could theoretically allow you to apply 2 attacks to target 2, and one to target 1, potentially eliminating 2 separate threats for the price of one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:52:47-07:00","id":1208683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208676#post1208676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I can think of in relation to HFA is that it can be either multi-target or single target, allowing flexibility that many multi-attack charms sometimes lack, this flexibility lets you direct fire (say target one has taken some HL damage, and targe 2 is full health, it could theoretically allow you to apply 2 attacks to target 2, and one to target 1, potentially eliminating 2 separate threats for the price of one</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI considered that, and then I thought that Dragon Blooded Melee seems to have a number of far better options for dealing with multiple attackers, in the form of things like its various Charms to improve defence and provide counterattacks. I mean, right before the Signature Charms there were those ones that allow you to provide defend other to everybody in a certain radius, and then to perform a counterattack after defending somebody, while also letting the one you guarded get in a free distraction gambit. My cursory assessment is that options such as those are a lot more worthwhile than this Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:55:52-07:00","id":1208686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208676#post1208676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I can think of in relation to HFA is that it can be either multi-target or single target, allowing flexibility that many multi-attack charms sometimes lack, this flexibility lets you direct fire (say target one has taken some HL damage, and targe 2 is full health, it could theoretically allow you to apply 2 attacks to target 2, and one to target 1, potentially eliminating 2 separate threats for the price of one</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible! But extremely expensive. If you're popping Crimson Fang Bite and lets say just 4 motes into Stoking Bonfire for each of those attacks you just spent 31 motes, 4 willpower and your fire anima. That's just a lot of resources for a fairly niche situation, and only if you're dex 5 with a specialty.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind that signature charms are supposed to have a little &quot;Wow!&quot; to them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T20:00:26-07:00","id":1208688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208683#post1208683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI considered that, and then I thought that Dragon Blooded Melee seems to have a number of far better options for dealing with multiple attackers, in the form of things like its various Charms to improve defence and provide counterattacks. I mean, right before the Signature Charms there were those ones that allow you to provide defend other to everybody in a certain radius, and then to perform a counterattack after defending somebody, while also letting the one you guarded get in a free distraction gambit. My cursory assessment is that options such as those are a lot more worthwhile than this Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but those tactics require you to risk being hit, letting the enemy attack and hope the attack misses. This by contrast is an offensive answer, which is important since from what I remember reading there are no onslaught negators for fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T20:06:37-07:00","id":1208689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208686#post1208686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's possible! But extremely expensive. If you're popping Crimson Fang Bite and lets say just 4 motes into Stoking Bonfire for each of those attacks you just spent 31 motes, 4 willpower and your fire anima. That's just a lot of resources for a fairly niche situation, and only if you're dex 5 with a specialty.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind that signature charms are supposed to have a little &quot;Wow!&quot; to them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>But would you need CFB the entire chain? Yes I get having double 10s is nice, but if you say are throwing 10 dice per attack, with an average of what 4.5 damage per hit, unless the opponent is rocking roughly 10+ Health levels that should be sufficient to put one down without spending more for the the extra HL that double 10s get you<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:32:15-07:00","id":1208713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208675#post1208675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat thread is filled to the brim with mechanical questions and answers. I'm only not doing it myself because I don't want to say any that will give away Charms that I haven't read yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Isator, just to let you know since you're avoiding the thread Vance flagged it for another pass to reevaluate it. Nice catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:40:00-07:00","id":1208716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208689#post1208689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But would you need CFB the entire chain? Yes I get having double 10s is nice, but if you say are throwing 10 dice per attack, with an average of what 4.5 damage per hit, unless the opponent is rocking roughly 10+ Health levels that should be sufficient to put one down without spending more for the the extra HL that double 10s get you<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not? But if you drop it off one of the attacks it doesn't become much cheaper. If you're doing the split 1 one wounded guy and 2 on non wounded guy, and have 16 initiative, here are the two options you have with that charm.<br /> <br /> Spend 7m 1wp to get a 16 damage attack against non-wounded guy.<br /> <br /> Or spend 14m 2wp to get that same attack, and then 14m 1wp 1 Aura, without-CFB, to smack the wounded guy for 8.<br /> <br /> The difference there being you're paying 21 motes and 2 willpower to get one additional half damage attack. That's a lot, especially since that feat can only be accomplished by a dex5 character with applicable specialty. If you're not both of those things that totally goes out the window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:44:56-07:00","id":1208719,"title":"","content":"Okay, going to see if I can\u2019t hash out Occult before turning in.<br /> <br /> Hidden Secrets Whisper is the Excellency, and can use 10s on the dice roll to reroll non-1s. But the cascade goes very quickly into an interesting (and non-Air) effect with Soul-Fire Cremation Technique. It\u2019s basically a slightly weaker version of one of the Zenith anima powers, allowing one to perform a funerary rite to rapidly make a corpse combust, and ensure that its lower soul won\u2019t turn into a hungry ghost, although it doesn\u2019t work on the bodies of Exalted. It also provides some relief to the deceased\u2019s higher ghost, either encouraging them to accept reincarnation, or creating a magically empowered positive Minor Tie for the Exalt who used the Charm. Proper respect for the remains of the dead is something that matters a fair bit to me, so I would appreciate a Charm such as this on those grounds alone.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s Seed and Salt Warding, a Charm that can be either Earth or Wood, whose effect can be pretty readily guessed after the prior one and with the name. Sure enough, it\u2019s a line to produce a slightly more powerful ward of germinated grain or salt lines, meaning that ghosts who could normally cross such lines by spending Willpower can only do so if their Resolve is higher than what the Exalt produced from an Occult roll, as well as being able to repel things like hungry ghosts and zombies outright. I\u2019d say that it\u2019s good to get Charms like these, some basic ways of dealing with some of the nuisances of the spiritual world, out there first, before proceeding into the main path of the cascade.<br /> <br /> Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique is back as the Terrestrials\u2019 unique take on seeing the dematerialized via reflective surfaces, followed by Spirit-Grounding Shout to enhance normal attacks to strike them. There seems to be a slight error, as the text of the latter refers to the former as a prerequisite, while the actual prerequisites section lists it as having none.<br /> <br /> Secret Wind Revelation is an interesting take on responding to hidden spirits as though they\u2019re in stealth, providing an early warning for when the dematerialized come within a certain range, and treating the being that manages to win the opposed roll to establish concealment, meaning that even magic to observe the dematerialized will have a hard time finding them.<br /> <br /> Dragon\u2019s Sacred Talon is another Earth or Wood Charm, this time calibrated to dealing with certain kinds of extraterrestrial threat; Earth allows one to strike Wyld creatures with the stabilising power, while Wood\u2019s cleansing improves attacks on the undead. I\u2019m reminded of old comments about the issue with Dragon Blooded having Charms with the Holy keyword, and how it had them aping the Solar capacity to inflict aggravated damage rather than having their own. Here I see a nice response to that; basing such power in the Dragon Blooded connection to the substance of the world, and empowering them specifically against beings from outside of it. It\u2019s a small touch, but I like what it adds to the mystical side of them.<br /> <br /> Fivefold Resonance Sense looks like it has been expanded quite a bit from prior Editions. It has a basic capacity to sense the presence and nature of the local geographic layout in terms of each element, and provides a slight non-Charm bonus to sense and follow not only jade, but elementals, Terrestrial demesnes and manses, and similar forms of magic.<br /> <br /> Spirit-Chaining Strike now takes the form of a gambit, but is otherwise still a matter of rendering a spirit visible and vulnerable to physical harm, albeit very temporarily.<br /> <br /> Occult\u2019s Signature Charm is Hundred Devils Whirlwind, a nice little Charm to roll Occult (with double 9s) to create a magical whirlwind that applies the results of the roll against the Resolve of any spirits that come into range; if it wins, it either blows them away or sucks them close (keeping them held tight, both with preventing use of Hurry Home and acting as difficult terrain to actions to escape) as chosen by the Exalt. I must say, so far Air has gotten some rather nice instances of creating manifestations of itself to be applied to the purposes of a Dragon Blood.<br /> <br /> Sage of Iron Meditation allows one to enter a state of meditation within the Wyld that can be maintained for several days, allowing them to create a small zone of stability around themselves. It particularly has a nice interactions with the actual creatures out there, granting one a significant Hardness against their attacks, sapping their Initiative if they get close, and inflicting a bit of aggravated damage on those who crash. Considering how the meditation probably requires one to stay still and the range of the stability is fairly short, I feel as though this one primarily functions to bait the Fair Folk and similar creatures, going out into the Wyld carrying a sign looking for trouble and luring them in to break against the stable zone and hardened Exalt, probably best with some friends who\u2019ll help cut down the entities that are offended by stability, while themselves protected from the deleterious Wyld.<br /> <br /> Smoke Ascends to Heaven acts as a means of empowering burnt offerings to spirits, and actually acts as a form of prayer Charm that people have often asked for. It specifically takes the form of either giving powerful double 7s to a persuade action made to the spirit in person, or ensuring that they\u2019ll hear the entreaty from afar. It also treats supporting Intimacies as though they\u2019re one step higher (meaning that somebody can undertake life-threatening tasks just on the strength of a Major Intimacy). It can only be used once per story, but is reset if major goals are accomplished through interaction with spirits (which are probably often facilitated by the Charm in the first place). So what do I think of it as a prayer Charm? It\u2019s all right. I\u2019m seeing it primarily as a power to communicate with spirits in a manner improved by their natural capacity to receive prayers and offerings, rather than something that empowers prayer in its own right, if that makes sense. I also think it\u2019s helped by the limited use. I\u2019m not sure how such a thing could be handled by Solars.<br /> <br /> Moving on to Crashing Wave-Dragons Warding, for a Charm that lets one convert running water into a kind of spiritual barrier. Ah, right, I heard somebody allude to this going all Lord of the Rings Imladris river, rather than my initial expectation that it would be a simple hard barrier. So yeah, deleterious creatures that enter the body of water are hit by an environmental hazard in the form of dragon-shaped waves, beating on them, making it harder to cross the water, and enhances withering attacks on them. It also includes a nice note of how beings with higher Essence than the Charm\u2019s user aren\u2019t just spending Willpower to be able to ignore the effect, but how doing so is accompanied by a display that makes them look good; it\u2019s a nice encouragement to make the effect more dramatically interesting, rather than my own first impulse for it to just stop, or the being to no longer be impeded.<br /> <br /> And with Wood, there\u2019s Eternal Death-Banishing Blossom. When the Exalt is at bonfire anima, a big ethereal tree grows out of it that provides improved Defense and soak (even more so against undead or necromantic stuff), and on the following turn the trees flowers bloom, aaaaand\u2026 expel a cloud of ethereal petals that, when they make contact with undead entities that fail to make a rather difficult Resistance roll, inflict a rather significant load of aggravated damage. Even the Abyssal Exalted and Deathlords can take some nasty damage. So yeah, this is another one that includes some rather striking visuals, and constitutes a uniquely Dragon Blooded take on inflicting aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, next is Blazing Purification Chant is a method for dealing with entities that have possessed somebody; putting a prayer strip on the victim\u2019s head that bursts into flame and burns the possessor for aggravated damage. It can force an entity out even short of killing them, although if they survive and hang on, then they get a relief period of a day. It\u2019s also another example of a Charm that the Exalted can use cooperatively, although unlike Dragon Vortex, everybody needs to know the Charm, and the participants only provide extra dice to the damage roll.<br /> <br /> Spirit-Shredding Attack is back in modified form, enhancing a decisive attack against a crashed spirit by letting threshold hit successes improve the damage roll, and while it doesn\u2019t permanently destroy a spirit killed by it, it does ensure that they\u2019ll come back sans a dot of Essence, possibly with fewer Charms. I\u2019ll be interested in if the Terrestrials do get a Charm to permanently destroy them (at least outside of martial arts); if not, the modification that this represents in who can and cannot permanently destroy a spirit carries interesting connotations for the setting\u2019s history, and the social dynamics between various beings.<br /> <br /> Seal of Heavenly Binding is straightforward as a Charm to create a binding circle around a spirit (that they have a potential to break through), while Chaos-Banishing Revelation Gesture (Earth) allows one to free others from Psyche and Derangement effects imposed by powers of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Purifying Dragon Suspiration is the Essence 4 Charm here, an Air/Water one to harness Creation\u2019s purifying Essence to free somebody from the power of curses (such as the spell Corrupted Words) or baleful transformations, as well as weakening magically created Derangements, although it\u2019s still not capable of ending the effects of sorcerous workings. It can take a lot of time and energy to accomplish, but the Exalt is given a fairly lengthy amount of time in which to accomplish it. This here is the one return that I\u2019ve seen of a power that does simply place some enemies beyond its reach; however, it reserves that for the very top of the scale, your Solar Circle Sorcery and your cosmic entities, so I\u2019d say that, considering everything else that they have to deal with, that\u2019s a fair cop on the part of Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Last is the ominously named Anathema-Sealing Tomb provided by Earth and Essence 5. Despite the name, this is not actually targeted at other Exalted, but spirits; when they\u2019re incapacitated, one has the option of sealing them within significant local instance of Earth, such as caverns, noteworthy stone monuments, or beneath mountains, preventing them from reforming for centuries or at all (but still short of properly killing them) if they\u2019re weak enough (although all such spirits can be freed if their prisons are broken). So while Dragon Blooded don\u2019t <i>quite</i> have power to permanently kill spirits, the more powerful ones have something that is close enough for most purposes, while still retaining plot hooks of pissed off spirits being able to wait around practically forever, as well as referencing cool mythological or folkloric imagery of beings sealed in sacred places. It even includes a hanging question of what might happen if it was used on the likes of Deathlords and Yozis.<br /> <br /> As a special bonus, there are also some sorcery Charms off in their own space. Obviously there\u2019s the basic Charm to initiate into sorcery, the only one that these Exalted can learn, but there are also a few to supplement them. Five Winds Raiment acts as something like a milder version of the Twilight anima, shielding user a bit while they\u2019re engaged in shaping of a spell, and Dragon-Sorcerer Puissance provides some additional sorcerous motes when one is shaping a spell with a distinct elemental character (with even more if they\u2019re in a matching Aura while doing so). They\u2019re not too much, and seem like some decent rounding Charms; one to prevent people smashing up an Exalt busy casting, one to lend at least a little something to the idea of casting elemental spells.<br /> <br /> So Occult came out well, some very vivid effects in there and a nice sense of how the Terrestrial Exalted relate to entities that are from outside of the Terrestrial plane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:50:34-07:00","id":1208721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208688#post1208688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but those tactics require you to risk being hit, letting the enemy attack and hope the attack misses. This by contrast is an offensive answer, which is important since from what I remember reading there are no onslaught negators for fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy biggest objection is really just... if it's going to just hit two people and split the Initiative between them, then fine, just say that. Don't couch it in algebra that has such a minor gradient that it's basically meaningless. That was what disappointed me the most; that it was written so indirectly that it seemed as though it was a more impressive effect until I actually looked closely at it and realised that the resulting numbers were minor and with basically no variation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T22:04:37-07:00","id":1208723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208716#post1208716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe not? But if you drop it off one of the attacks it doesn't become much cheaper. If you're doing the split 1 one wounded guy and 2 on non wounded guy, and have 16 initiative, here are the two options you have with that charm.<br /> <br /> Spend 7m 1wp to get a 16 damage attack against non-wounded guy.<br /> <br /> Or spend 14m 2wp to get that same attack, and then 14m 1wp 1 Aura, without-CFB, to smack the wounded guy for 8.<br /> <br /> The difference there being you're paying 21 motes and 2 willpower to get one additional half damage attack. That's a lot, especially since that feat can only be accomplished by a dex5 character with applicable specialty. If you're not both of those things that totally goes out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally get ya, and Vance\u2019s flagged it for reattack, so it\u2019s all good. I think the idea of it allowing variable attacks is really neat, what I would like is to see it dropped in cost maybe by like 5-6m. I get their not wanting to give DBs a super powerful multi-attack charm though.<br /> <br /> One other edgecase I thought of deals with Legendary size opponents, as each separate attack let\u2019s you skirt around the damage threshold that is normally applied to attacks (ie each hit might net you 4-5 dmg, but with three that nets you 15 against a LS opponent)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T22:19:49-07:00","id":1208728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208723#post1208723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally get ya, and Vance\u2019s flagged it for reattack, so it\u2019s all good. I think the idea of it allowing variable attacks is really neat, what I would like is to see it dropped in cost maybe by like 5-6m. I get their not wanting to give DBs a super powerful multi-attack charm though.<br /> <br /> One other edgecase I thought of deals with Legendary size opponents, as each separate attack let\u2019s you skirt around the damage threshold that is normally applied to attacks (ie each hit might net you 4-5 dmg, but with three that nets you 15 against a LS opponent)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, totally, there's cases where I'd use it for sure. Even just getting out that full max damage 3 attacks on one target I'd use it there. For a signature charm in its own elements aspect though it should probably be swapped for something more widely usable or powerful, just to make it more appealing for your signature slot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T22:33:21-07:00","id":1208733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208728#post1208728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, totally, there's cases where I'd use it for sure. Even just getting out that full max damage 3 attacks on one target I'd use it there. For a signature charm in its own elements aspect though it should probably be swapped for something more widely usable or powerful, just to make it more appealing for your signature slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, like I can see what they were trying to go for, but just not enough oomph for the cost. It does remind me of Hammer on Iron Technique but without Five Fold fury go give it some real bite, nor cheap synergizers like solar brawl has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T07:04:34-07:00","id":1208843,"title":"","content":"<br /> Now, to see what they can do with Performance. Like with the Solars, it\u2019s divided into paths of application.<br /> <br /> The Universal Charms start with the Excellency, Audience-Enthusing Display, letting one add successes and eliminating the penalty for targeting several people with social influence. That\u2019s followed by Hidden Petal Aria, which allows one to hide a short, but potentially influential, message within a performance, that is conveyed to a select individual and presents a difficulty of the user\u2019s Manipulation or Performance to magical attempts to pick up on it.<br /> <br /> Invisible Street Performer Technique is back as a curious method of going unnoticed, allowing one to shift the attention of onlookers away from themselves and onto their performance, to the extent that they can engage in other, non-violent actions clandestinely by flurrying them with the performance. Dance of Flashing Swords covers the violent side, allowing one to incorporate their actions into a performance and convince onlookers that it\u2019s all just part of the show.<br /> <br /> Talented Improvisation feels like an interesting take on Wood\u2019s capacity to connect to others, in the form of being able to intuit the whole of a song from a brief snippet, as well as growing a misstep into an elaborate dance, which are mechanically represented by being able to reroll some failed dice on a roll, as well as lowering the Charm\u2019s cost if they make a stunt of their fumble.<br /> Using Soul-Stirring Performance, an Exalt can make inspire rolls with non-Charm bonus dice, with the result requiring a Decision Point to not be moved by. Then there\u2019s Heart-Strengthening Defense, allowing one to make a performance that will strengthen the Resolve of those who witness it, especially against Psyche effects, being able to flurry that performance with other actions since the boost evidently only lasts while the performance does. Similar is Harmonious Life-Affirming Song, providing a performance that both improves resistance to poison and disease, and increasing the rate at which they can recover from injury; I like to imagine how this can synergize with Medicine, using Charms to downgrade somebody\u2019s wounds to bashing damage, and then putting on a show for them to speed them along to health.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s a Water Charm, Irresistible Whirlpool Diversion, allowing one to forcefully draw people\u2019s attention to their performance. It\u2019s less absolute than a similar Solar effect, taking the form of exerting a penalty on Awareness actions to look at anything besides the performing Dragon Blood. Like several others, it lets one flurry the distracting performance with other actions.<br /> Next is the Signature Charm Thundering Dragon Proclamation, magnifying one\u2019s voice to a boom that can be clearly heard from a great distance. It only functions for inspire or threaten actions, but ignores penalties based on distance and environment, doubles 9s on voice-based Performance and military command, and while it\u2019s scene-long, the user can selectively return their voice to normal volume, which is necessary to engage in other forms of social influence at all.<br /> <br /> Tears-From-Stone Eloquence allows one to make inspire rolls that help align people to traditional values, although it\u2019s the player of the one who is hit by the inspire action who decides what those values are and how they\u2019ll act in favour to them. I like that touch, both for making it something more nuanced than just imposing values on people, and for the image of Earth Aspects who might place a greater priority on people believing in and living up to <i>something</i>, rather than what the Exalt specifically would have of them.<br /> <br /> Immolating Passion Alleluia (interesting spelling) instead makes an inspire actions that can roll some non-Charm dice, creating very intense emotions that prompt characters to engage in actions equivalent to what could come from a Major Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Mesmerizing Siren Call looks much more elaborate than the preceding ones, being a Psyche Charm and another with variable effects depending on rolled successes. The character gets to make a Performance roll, with rerolled failed dice, hypnotizing onlookers whose Resolve is overcome, and spending threshold successes on conjuring particular illusions, even being able to impose different illusions on different people in the same group. The base effect shows people phantasmal sensory stimuli that they\u2019ll know are unreal, one success creates a single illusory being of about human size that can\u2019t imitate a real person, two successes overcome that limitation for a character known to the Charm\u2019s user, and three lets one weave an image the size of a house, including objects and structures, which can also imitate specific people. Because the illusions are dependant on maintaining the performance, it can also be flurried with other actions, and the user can will the illusions to act however they want; while they can\u2019t interact physically, they can engage in social influence (although unable to benefit from any of the Exalt\u2019s other magic). The targets get the option to spend Willpower to break the illusion if they see something that shows it up as unreal, or if the illusion might lead to violating a Major or Defining Intimacy. It can only be used once per story, but is reset by accomplishing major goals through deception. So yeah, chalk another one up to the evils of Water. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Last is Life-Spirit Symphony, allowing one to cause local vegetation to align with the Dragon Blood\u2019s performance, providing the benefit of allowing oneself and one\u2019s allies to ignore difficult terrain as a result of such flora as it parts to let them through, as well as providing a benefit to resisting threats from plants such as poison or environmental hazards. On top of that, it can give the option to direct the plants at enemies in the form of a gambit to entangle them, which can remain to impede their movement even if they\u2019re hacked through.<br /> <br /> Last of the universal Charms is Blossom Hides Thorns, allowing one to hide an unexpected attack or ambush within a performance, either for the Exalt or an ally.<br /> <br /> Aaaand oh Jesus Performance is long. There\u2019s another five pages of this? I\u2019m going to try my best to bomb through.<br /> <br /> Okay, oratory. Air Charm Lightning Declamation Style lets one reroll certain failures on oratory, Earth Charm Legend-Hewn Wisdom is used to inspire emotion and instil Intimacy based on the moral of a spoken story (with an upgrade to let them give Willpower to those who don\u2019t resist the influence, that can be spent towards staying the course), and Storm-Gathering Fervor grants non-Charm dice when trying to influence somebody with a shared Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Epoch Saga Memory gives one a perfect recall of stories that can benefit their recitation or the mental and social use of an Ability that might benefit from knowing a story, plus strengthening Resolve with its moral or Guile with its distraction. Puissant Precursor\u2019s Monologue lets one make a persuade roll with double 7s for actions going along with the user\u2019s Defining Principles, making it harder to resist for those who share the Intimacy.<br /> <br /> For music and singing Charms, there\u2019s Sanxian-Charming Fingers to give double 9s for playing an instrument, while Voice-Uplifting Aspect lets one reroll singing failures for every rolled 10. Blossoming Instrument Evocation lets one draw instruments out of the local flora. Vibrating Strings Defense is still a defensive Charm harnessing music, but now it\u2019s a clash using a gambit that, if it wins, knocks the attacker down and makes them highly vulnerable to Performance influence if they crash. Then there\u2019s Three-String Sword Prana to let one wield their music as an attack, with double 10s on the damage roll. Last is Battle Anthem of Ten Thousand to provide fighting bonuses to people that hear the Exalt\u2019s music.<br /> <br /> Okay, almost done. Dancing Charms. Swaying Boughs Arabesque lets one dance to lower the Resolve of targets, which can increase the Appearance benefit. Petal-Strewn Pavane lets one add Performance to combat movement rolls and flurry movement with Performance actions, with Wood Aura providing a non-Charm success and removing difficult terrain penalties. Falling Leaves Sway lets one use Appearance to provide non-Charm dice to dance-based inspire actions, which grants an auto success to an influence based on the inspired emotion. Last of all is Waltz of Honeyed Wine, to convert Appearance based non-Charm dice into non-Charm successes and makes it harder for people with Resolve lower than Appearance to resist influence.<br /> <br /> Huh, no sexual Charms? Well, maybe later.<br /> <br /> Performance looks good, although I\u2019ll probably want to give it a bigger look later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T08:48:46-07:00","id":1208899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> allowing one to perform a funerary rite to rapidly make a corpse combust, and ensure that its lower soul won\u2019t turn into a hungry ghost, although it doesn\u2019t work on the bodies of Exalted </div> </div> </div>I imagine this would cause some surprises occasionally ^_^<br /> <br /> *Tries to burn person that appears to be made of bodyparts from multiple bodies, and who only finally died after their head was cut off, despite seemingly fatal injuries suffered in earlier battles*<br /> <br /> &quot;Hesiesh's Flaring Nostrils! This...undead...stitched together...<b>thing </b>is an Exalt?!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T13:34:50-07:00","id":1208998,"title":"","content":"Okay, hopefully Presence will be less dense than Performance was.<br /> <br /> Excellency Glowing Coal Radiance lets one buy automatic successes and roll extra dice for every 10 on their roll. Then there\u2019s Eternally Argumentative Flame to reduce or eliminate penalties for flurrying Presence or Socialize influence rolls. And Unbearable Taunt Technique is another power to effectively provoke somebody to hostility, which can also be deployed in combat to make somebody focus on attacking the user specifically, and penalizes their Initiative if they resist.<br /> <br /> Burning Dragon Mien provides a threaten roll with double 9s, and in combat this causes the target to lose a bit of Initiative. Warm-Faced Seduction Style lets one make a persuade roll to seduce that also instils a Minor Tie of lust or desire, and with the benefit of Fire Aura, allows one to convert bonus dice added by Appearance into non-Charm successes. I wonder if they might get any more Charms to seduce, but for the moment, this is one that has a marked contrast with Solar power of the same type, in terms of the mechanical path it takes and how the result is thus less extreme.<br /> <br /> Debate-Sparking Bonfire is another Charm to provoke, but works a bit differently than the prior; it can target more than one person at once, and the hostility it creates needs to have a social component, even if it\u2019s physical violence. I\u2019m imagining the scenarios in which this might occur; the social situation that one might wish to sabotage by prompting a wave of acrimony, or trying to rib a rival into undermining their own image by rising to bait or acting uncouthly.<br /> <br /> Hot-Blooded Ardor allows one to briefly treat their Appearance as one dot higher, or even greater by expending their Fire Aura. Then there\u2019s a Water Charm, Passion-Transmuting Nuance, and I dread to imagine what that underhanded element could do in Presence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh, it\u2019s actually relatively benign, allowing the user to change one inspired or otherwise significant emotion to another, and give it the force of a Major Intimacy. Hell, that can even lend itself to some beneficial applications. Fair enough there.<br /> <br /> Fearsome Dragon Presence allows a Terrestrial to briefly impose a penalty on people who would oppose them, as a result of their intimidating aura. Moth to the Candle is a somewhat more powerful form of Charm to draw enemies to focus on attacking them specifically. The Earth Charm Grinding Millstone Argument lets the Dragon Blood immediately reset an attempt to persuade somebody after failing a roll, and lowers the benefit of an Intimacy already used to bolster Resolve.<br /> <br /> Haunting Words Infliction is the Signature Air Charm. With it, one can make a boosted Instil roll to give another an Intimacy that the Exalt possesses, and keeps the argument echoing with them even if they don\u2019t get the Intimacy, meaning that any time within the next few weeks they encounter evidence that could be used to try the Instil roll again, the affected character makes it against themselves, with the Exalt\u2019s Essence in non-Charm dice added. It\u2019s a nice thing to bring out some of the Air Aspected qualities; passionate belief in one\u2019s ideals, and a concise and logical tone that can be hard to ignore.<br /> <br /> Virtuous Mountain\u2019s Shadow is used in response to a witnessed social influence that one wishes to disrupt, allowing one to make a counterargument from one of their Major or higher Intimacies that allows witnesses to treat the Intimacy as their own for the purposes of resolving the social influence, with those who do so gaining it for themselves as a Minor Intimacy. It\u2019s another interesting one to represent the Earth place in society.<br /> <br /> Now, to see if Fire can do better for its next Signature in an Aspect Ability\u2026 Terrifying Fire-Dragon Roar\u2026 ah, I think I remember this one: Presence as a means of actually breathing fire. That\u2019ll do the trick. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It\u2019s got a rather decent range, adds Essence to Initiative to determine the damage that is divided between targets, and also functions as a threatening action to make people try and flee, even if the flame didn\u2019t hit them. It works nicely.<br /> <br /> Fluid Recollection Insinuation is back to that good evil Water stuff, with a Charm to convince somebody that a false prior encounter occurred, applying a Psyche effect to create a false memory reinforcing the claim. Implausible claims can be made, removing successes rather than inflicting a penalty. It can create a Minor Tie to the user if the target never actually met them at all, which can only be eroded by the influence of others, at which point Willpower can be spent to realise that the memory was fake. People who already knew the Exalt also form a Minor Tie, but don\u2019t need to remove it before they have the option to realise that the memory is false.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s then Spirit-Cultivating Leadership, a Charm that can only be used on people with a Defining Tie of loyalty to the Dragon Blood. It\u2019s extremely cheap and persists over days to give the person so empowered improved Resolve to protect their loyalty, three specialties in a variety of Abilities, and extra Willpower each day to resist social influence. Not a bad mix of effects there.<br /> Back to Fire with Blazing Heart Ascendency, allowing one to limit the Intimacies that a person can use in a Decision Point against influence to persuade or threaten made with Presence or Socialize. The character so affected can only use Intimacies based on passion to resist, rather than things such as abstract Principles. However, it only works on people that have such passions in the first place; somebody who doesn\u2019t has nothing to inflame, and is thus immune.<br /> <br /> Heartstring-Pulling Approach is another more straightforward Charm; it adds a single non-Charm success to a Presence or Socialize influence roll, and if the target\u2019s Resolve is lowered by a Major or Defining Intimacy based on a passion, then it increases the Willpower they need to spend to resist. Nice and simple.<br /> <br /> Back to combative effects with Aura of Invulnerability, which makes a kind of transition from the emotional to the physical; the user can roll their Willpower to gain extra health levels, and adds their Charisma to their soak. This is offset by how the damage inflicted on temporary health levels transitions to their actual body when the Charm ends (which can happen prematurely, since it has the Aura keyword), although they\u2019re specifically protected against being killed by this.<br /> <br /> Vivacious Dragon Beauty is another seduction Charm, this time with Wood, and grants a bonus dot of Appearance. I\u2026 will need to look back at the other Charm that granted Appearance to see how they square up, because on the face of it, that seems a little bit minor. Unless\u2026 the significance is that somebody using a lot of Performance will have an option to raise Appearance as well? Need to look back over the others later\u2026<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an Earth Psyche Charm now in the form of Mind Like Fertile Fields. With that one, an Exalt can use a common aphorism as a Presence roll to place somebody briefly into a kind of placid, hypnotic state, during which Influence rolls can be made against them that their Intimacies don\u2019t get any relevance to\u2026 at least for Resolve. It doesn\u2019t say so, so I presume that Decision Points still function. It\u2019s another one that compares directly to a Solar Charm, definitely less powerful, but good in the added capability it can give for the Dragon Blooded. Although, I <i>would</i> like if it was written a bit more; not because it requires any clarity, it\u2019s obvious enough, I\u2019d just like to know a bit more about the perspective of the recipient. Are they aware in their passive state, for instance?<br /> <br /> Following is yet <i>another</i> Earth and Psyche power (as well as needing the Aura), Entombed Mind Technique. This is used for a more extreme kind of hypnotism; it drives a person targeted with the prior Charm into an oblivious sleep that they can\u2019t be roused from without magic for several hours, and won\u2019t waken from on their own for at least a day. In that time, the same kind of influence roll as the prior Charm can be made against them once. But it can also be repurchased at Essence 4 to be able to place somebody with a Willpower lower than the user\u2019s Essence into an <i>indefinite</i> sleep, with a kind of stasis effect to keep them alive and preserved, and can only be broken with magic (and to which only the Exalted are immune). Repurchasing again at Essence 5 extends this to outright petrifying a person, an effect that the user can revoke with physical contact and spending motes, and otherwise requires magic such as Order-Affirming Blow. Sooo, yeah, that\u2019s definitely taking the concept of suggestive hypnotism and the Exalt making it their own.<br /> <br /> The cascade stops at Essence 4, back with a Fire Charm: Dragon Warlord\u2019s Convocation. Targeted at a single character, it lets a Dragon Blood make a Presence roll with double 9s to create a Tie of loyalty that <i>starts</i> at Major, and can strengthen and existing one directly to Defining. Unlike other instil actions, it requires a Decision Point, as well as spending two Willpower. Furthermore, for the rest of the story in which it was used, it can\u2019t be voluntarily eroded, unless the Dragon Blood harms them personally or something else to which they have a strong Intimacy. Its power is offset by only being possible to use once per story, unless reset with achieving a legendary social goal.<br /> <br /> \u200bPresence is good there, nice mix of social and combat effects, and the former are vivid in a manner that gives an interesting picture of what Dragon Blooded societies might be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T20:21:11-07:00","id":1209108,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve actually been a bit interested to see what Resistance might get, since it\u2019s an Ability where one might expected to find forms of bodily transformation, or at least wreathing oneself in elemental substance.<br /> <br /> Of course to start is Ox-Body Technique, which doesn\u2019t actually have an element, since it\u2019s never even really supposed to be a Charm even by the standards of \u201cCharms aren\u2019t things\u201d; it\u2019s a representation of the hardiness of the bodies of the Exalted. It functions on the same principle as the Solar one, where the exact benefit depends on Stamina, improving as the Attribute goes up, and able to be purchased repeatedly, the main difference being that it can only provide two health levels, and the best it can do is give a -1 level. The actual excellency is Purifying Blood Ascendancy, adding successes and letting one reroll 6s.<br /> <br /> Following that is Body-Cleansing Prana, a Charm that can be Air, Fire or Water, enabling one to resist poison or disease; Air for inhaled toxins, Water for ingested or blood-transmitted ones, and Fire for disease, doubling 9s on the resistance roll. A repurchase at Essence 3 allows one to dramatically expel poisons specifically in an unblockable, short ranged attack, so long as the resistance roll is high enough. Already the Ability is going for some neat, and even a bit nasty, application.<br /> <br /> For a proper Earth Charm there\u2019s Uneating Earth Meditation, assisting the Exalt in being hardened against deprivation of food and drink by eliminating the penalties for them, and increasing the time that can be gone without consumption, followed by Untiring Earth Meditation, to alleviate penalties for like of sleep while in contact with ground or stone.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s Impervious Skin of Stone, letting one double their Stamina for soak calculations against a single withering attack, with Earth Aura allowing one to reserve use of the Charm until an attack actually hits them (but before rolling damage).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a Water Charm called Eternal Tide Endurance, allowing the Dragon Blood to convert 1s on an incoming withering attack roll into additional soak to apply against it, with the Aura letting one apply this to decisive attacks to create Hardness. That\u2019s followed by a Wood Charm, Supple Viridian Scales, allowing one to momentarily reduce their armour\u2019s mobility penalty by a little bit, or else grant a non-Charm die to movement and disengagement in light armour, with Aura being able to extend the Charm so long as the Aura is maintained.<br /> <br /> Ah, here\u2019s the good stuff, (Element) Protection Technique\u2026 unless this is about being protected <i>from</i> the element. Let me see\u2026 yeah, the latter, gain improved soak and a bit of natural Hardness against attacks in the form of the element, and subtract Stamina or Resistance from the damage of an environmental hazard. But hey, at least it\u2019s not something dependent on repurchases for the element that you want anymore. It also notes that it won\u2019t work on more indirect forms of the element, such as Earth against metal or Fire against magically generated pseudo fire such as a Solar Bolt.<br /> <br /> Elemental Aegis functions in the same manner as Melee\u2019s Elemental Sheath, although one thing it has going for it is a slightly more interesting visual element, with the suggestions for how the element might remove the armour directly off of the Exalt\u2019s body.<br /> <br /> Continuing with the theme of meditating into being like the earth\u2019s lack of need for things is Unsleeping Earth Meditation, to acquire the effects of a full night\u2019s rest with just an hour of meditation (although after a number of days of continuous use, it can\u2019t keep substituting for actual sleep), Unbreathing Earth Meditation to greatly extend the time that one can hold their breath, and Unfeeling Earth Meditation to let one briefly ignore wound penalties (with the extension from Aura requiring a repurchase at Essence 4).<br /> <br /> The Signature Air Charm provides us with Body-Like-Clouds Meditation, which allows one to take on the quality of air such that withering damage is lowered by the character\u2019s Essence (which can even take it below its minimum damage), and steals Initiative from an attacker who hits but fails to damage.<br /> <br /> Perfected Scales of the Dragon lets the Terrestrial harden into an impervious crystal form, granting a rather significant Hardness for a round, which can stack with Hardness provided by other Resistance Charms. Decisive attacks that are thwarted by the improved Hardness don\u2019t reset the attacker to base Initiative, but cause them to lose it as though they\u2019d missed, with it granted to the Dragon Blood. It also comes with a cost of preventing the user from attacking or moving on the turn following its use.<br /> <br /> Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit allows one to take on a quality of fire, becoming faster and stronger at risk of burning out; they get a bonus Strength dot, can ignore a bit of wound penalty, and add some bonus dice to rolls for attacking, rushing or feats of strength. Apart from costs such as an aggravated health level and having a Duration of Aura, using it means that Stamina stops being added to soak, and a point of Initiative is lost at the end of each round. This one I like for being an instance of that transformation thing I was talking about at the start.<br /> <br /> With Fathomless Depths Replenishment, one can meditate for an hour in order to make a roll of Essence + Stamina, with successes providing temporary -1 health levels. This one has a strange and interesting cost in terms of how those health levels stick around; when the Charm\u2019s Duration elapses, undamaged ones fade, but damaged ones stick around, counting against successes on future uses of the Charm; that is to say, it can\u2019t be repeatedly stacked on top of itself, so if, say, you have three damaged temporary levels and roll four successes, it will count the three you still have against the total allotted. The temporary health levels need to be healed first by any recuperation or magic, and the longer they stick around, the more painful they become i.e. the higher their wound penalties; when they do heal, they vanish. It\u2019s funny that the flavour text for this Charm describes it as contemplation revealing oneself as eternal, when the result becomes something that is capable of lingering and festering; eternity has its disadvantages. I suppose that Dragon Blooded Water is capable of even screwing up itself; truly the spirit of the Second Edition Ebon Dragon lives on in its inky depths.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well-Tended Garden of the Soul instead lets one create a reinforcing loop of life energy; Wood Essence is focused out through physical contact into surrounding plant life (rejuvenating any that is sickly or dead), and then, should it not be interrupted by the Exalt crashing, taking decisive damage or being forced out of range of any plants, it flows back into them, allowing for Essence + Stamina to be rolled with successes healing non-aggravated health levels. It\u2019s an especially pretty and flavourful use of Resistance as a means of healing damage.<br /> <br /> Moving on, there\u2019s Earth Bears Witness, by means of which one can shunt decisive damage to themselves into surrounding earth, or structures made from it (which can create minor dramatic effects such as difficult terrain, as appropriate). Particularly large and impressive forms of stone or earth even allow one to increase how much damage can be negated. With higher Resistance, one can purchase variations of the Charm in Water and Wood, functioning the same but with appropriate variations (and now I wonder, does subtracting the highest possible damage by sending it into something like a lake cause it to churn up in a manner that might cast waves over the battle?).<br /> <br /> Immovable Mountain Technique lives up to its name, rooting one to their spot and making mundane attempts to shift them, such as being knocked back or thrown from a grapple, fail outright, and even magic that would do so is mitigated, although the precise manner of how is necessarily a Storyteller call (a suggestion is given for Heaven Thunder Hammer). It has the Perilous keyword, so it would fail in crash anyway, but it also ends prematurely if the Dragon Blood should actually move or be moved.<br /> <br /> Ripples-on-Water Defense is obviously another Water Charm, used to either make a withering attack subtract successes for 1s that appear on the dice roll, while decisive attacks apply that number to rerolling successes, starting with any that show 7.<br /> <br /> For those who max out their purchases of Ox-Body Technique, Dragon\u2019s Unfailing Vigor provides one more benefit to the Terrestrial Exalted constitution, granting a single -0 and -4 health level each.<br /> <br /> Essence 4 lets one use the Water Charm Flowing Dragon-Body Endurance, which, for the duration of their Aura, allows an Exalt to apply the value of their <i>Initiative</i> as Hardness against decisive attacks. The Charm can\u2019t be used in armour, but it means that while it\u2019s active, being hit by somebody with a lower Initiative is basically impossible (barring appropriate counter magic), while it\u2019s also something that is variable in a manner nicely evocative of water.<br /> <br /> And up at Essence 5 is an Air Charm, of all things: Revolving-Hurricane-Force Defense. The character is able to roll Stamina + Resistance, with non-Charm bonus dice equal to their Essence (so, basically, five), and gains a bonus to soak equal to the successes rolled against withering attacks by enemies with lower Initiative. Its duration is tied to Aura, and the bonus drops by one every time an attack actually manages to hit the Exalt.<br /> <br /> So in the end, Resistance didn\u2019t have much in the way of personal transformation after all, nor very much interacting with armour, come to think of it. Still, what it does have looks robust and functional, and there are a few rather pretty effects dotted around in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T20:28:56-07:00","id":1209109,"title":"","content":"Heh, speculation on what the Sail Charms will consist of:<br /> <br /> \u200bMostly stuff to sink other people's ships, and sabotage floatation devices for the survivors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T00:06:39-07:00","id":1209132,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-blooded Ox-body Technique does provide three health levels at Stamina 5. One -1 and two -2's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:40:21-07:00","id":1209148,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you actually compare it with the solar version they get the same at stamina 3-4 as a solar gets at stamina 1-2, and the same at stamina 5 as a solar gets at 3-4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T06:47:23-07:00","id":1209220,"title":"","content":"The last few cascades have been rather dense, owing to being related to combat or social influence, so I\u2019m hoping that Ride will be comparatively relaxed.<br /> <br /> The Excellency lets one add successes and lets the user\u2019s mount ignore a point of mobility penalty from their barding. Then there\u2019s immediately an Air Charm in Heaven-Racing Leap, allowing one\u2019s mount to make a gravity-defying bound to automatically jump one range band forward, or use 10s to reroll failures on a movement roll including jumps, with Air Aura allowing one to leap vertically so long as they have something to land on.<br /> <br /> Tread Rooted in Life allows the Exalt\u2019s mount to ignore penalties to movement actions resulting from plants, probably including things such as roots and heavy vines and the like. Or\u2026 I\u2019m actually a little bit unclear on if it ignores penalties altogether, or just removes two points, or is absolute for one action and just two for any other ones. I need to look back at the Ride rules. In any case, one can pay experience points to get variations for Air, Earth and Water (the last applying to partial immersion or wet and slippery surfaces).<br /> <br /> Great Heart Companion lets one either give their mount improved Resolve against threaten rolls or increases their own Defence against unhorsing gambits, with Wood Aura extending the duration from Instant to Aura and providing both benefits. Cloud Harnessing Technique is then an Air one to let a mount spend the turn walking or standing on surfaces that would otherwise be unable to bear their weight, as well as ignoring difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> Dance of the Jade Bridle allows an Exalt to very rapidly tame a wild animal for a mount with a stunt appropriate to the animal in question, with a variety of possible Attributes. The animal that is beaten will submit to being saddled and mounted and forms a Minor Tie of loyalty. It can\u2019t fully tame a wild animal on its own, but it serves as an effective starting point, with guidelines provided for how to continue the process.<br /> <br /> Reins-Like-Roots Unity is another Charm to assist against unhorsing gambits, making 1s detract from successes and increasing the difficulty of the gambit, with Wood Aura able to maintain the duration.<br /> <br /> Earth gets a Charm with Creation-Turning Hoof, which is used to impose a penalty equal to the Speed bonus of one\u2019s mount onto an enemy\u2019s roll to oppose their rush.<br /> (Hmm, when did I get to describing every individual Charm? Eh, I guess at a certain point their more basic function Charm became a bit more interesting)<br /> <br /> Anyway, Ebony Spur Technique, that\u2019s a fun name. If an ally that is also mounted lands an attack of their own within short range, the Dragon Blood can reflexively ride up to the enemy and make a decisive attack that gets the mount\u2019s Speed bonus added on. That counts as one\u2019s combat action, but not their movement, and it can be reset within a scene by crashing an enemy while mounted.<br /> <br /> Hmm, a Charm for coordinated cavalry attacks, not a Charm to protect one\u2019s mount from Anima flux in sight, a prior reference to the House of Bells teaching mounted warfare\u2026 I think I can definitively conclude that the idea of Dragon Blooded having a distinct aversion to riding animals has been consigned to the ash heap.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, there\u2019s Ass-to-Elephant Method to let one use the power of Earth to let a mount add their Speed bonus to their Strength for purposes of feats of strength, both in terms of rolling dice and the minimum feats they can try. That\u2019s got to make for some very effective draught animals for the purpose of things like dragging large treasures to be shipped back to the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> Now, Signature Air, Untethered Pegasus Spirit. Hmmm, what could this do? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But yeah, the Terrestrial is able to make their mount\u2026 not fly as such, rather not fall if they should gallop out onto an empty space, like over a cliff or pit. The closest to true flight it gets is being able to spend Willpower when using Heaven-Gracing Leap to rush enemies in the air to do\u2026 something. I\u2019m finding it a little bit difficult to figure it out exactly through all of the range band terminology, but that\u2019s just me. I get the basic gist that it helps one ride their mount up to an enemy that is flying. Finally, it\u2019s another one that insures one against falling to death or severe injury if any conditions that would disrupt the Charm are fulfilled.<br /> <br /> Mountain-Trampling Hoof lets an Exalt strengthen their mount to serve as a damn battering ram, adding non-Charm successes to a feat of demolition against large structures. The Strength requirement to attempt the feat is lowered by building up momentum across multiple range bands, and the resulting feat can be instantaneous even if it would normally take time. The mount is also not fully protected against the force of the impact, with any 1s on the feat\u2019s roll being used to roll bashing damage against the animal. The Charm can\u2019t be used for an animal that is on the verge of unconsciousness or death.<br /> <br /> Fire gives Charge of One Hundred Generals to make a rush attack against a battle group or a noteworthy enemy that needs to be further than medium range, but no farther than four bands away, immediately rolling to Join Battle if it hasn\u2019t already been started. If the rush is successful, then both the Dragon Blood and mounted allies and battle groups will become locked on to the target, allowing for continuous movement towards that target without using up the movement action for the next four turns, until within close range. Each range band crossed in the charge provides one extra Initiative point. It seems like a bit of a circumstantial Charm, but seems pretty powerful if it can be used. Plus, it has a rather striking image to it; whether it\u2019s the Scots Greys at Waterloo or the Rohirrim at the Pelennor Fields, nothing beats a good cavalry charge.<br /> <br /> Ride Beneath the Waves is a more basic enhancement for a mount to go through water; they become amphibious, is capable of swimming effectively, and can run at the bottom of bodies of water without penalty. Plus the rolls to control the mount underwater will get double 9s.The only complication is that the benefits don\u2019t actually extend to the rider; if they want to go underwater as well (which I\u2019ll note that they don\u2019t necessarily need to), they\u2019ll need to use other powers to breath.<br /> <br /> Heh, I\u2019ve sometimes wondered if there would ever be a Charm that would use the term \u201cexaltation\u201d more colloquially. Anyway, Dragon-Among-Horses Exaltation is used to anoint a steed with one\u2019s own blood, imbuing it with some of the Exalt\u2019s own power (maybe not so colloquial); the anima banner builds up out of them, and it gets the benefits of either improving Strength rolls and withering damage, Dexterity rolls, or Stamina ones with soak, as well as getting increased Hardness (which <i>does</i> immunise it to anima flux, so\u2026 I guess it\u2019s a matter of how flux takes a higher anima to even start inflicting damage) and some extra -4 health levels. Ah, I missed how the Charm\u2019s effect is permanent and costs experience points, but there\u2019s a very neat note on how the Scarlet Dynasty has access to rare, highly bred horses descended from stock crossed with elementals that waive the experience cost of the Charm being used on them. Even if it\u2019s not the most powerful Signature Charm of all, it\u2019s among the more impressive alignments of element and Aspect Ability, if only for how it has a cultural expression.<br /> <br /> Now, Indomitable Warhorse Endurance functions as a special defence for one\u2019s mount, being able to spend Initiative to reduce a decisive damage pool against the mount. It\u2019s not as good as the kinds of similar powers that the Exalted can apply to themselves, only reducing the damage by up to Essence. It can also be used outside of combat against an environmental hazard, for a flat reduction of (Essence) dice to the damage roll.<br /> <br /> Oh jeez, I spoke too soon about being less dense, there are <i>so many more</i> of these. Damn necessary expansion to neglected Abilities! I\u2019m gonna speed through most of them.<br /> <br /> Seizing-the-Reins Approach. Fire Charm. Lets you take control of the mount of somebody that you\u2019ve unhorsed as a custom gambit, have it reflexively make a withering attack. Fire Aura lets it function reflexively. Next!<br /> <br /> Unbreakable Stallion Spirit. Provides a few general bonuses to riding an animal and keeping one\u2019s seat on it. Next!<br /> <br /> Seven-League Gallop. Charm to greatly increase a mount\u2019s speed, as well as an improvement to movement actions in combat timing.<br /> <br /> Trail-Blazing Dragon Steed. Lets one leave a trail of fire in the wake of a steed charging at full tilt. Creates a brief environmental hazard, that might be longer in a sufficiently dry environment.<br /> <br /> Vanishing Cloud-Rider Ways enhances disengage rolls, and with Air Aura also refunding the Initiative cost of success.<br /> <br /> Essence 4 now. Blazing Charger Attack is a Charm to create a rush with double 9s, being able to reflexively move across more range bands at the end, and reflexively making a decisive close-quarters attack at the end. It also lets one use a lance to make an impaling attack without needing the usual requirements that I cannot remember. While Elusive Skirmisher Tactic empowers attacks made in the opposite direction, being able to reflexively make the classic Parthian shot, or get a bonus to the raw damage if they do aim.<br /> <br /> Last is the Essence 5 Charm, Horses-Like-Dragons Stampede. The Charm allows one to make a dramatic action to round up a herd of wild, ridable animals (using the framework of a group of Ride-based rally for numbers actions) to build up the size of a battle group up to a maximum of 3, making a herd whose approach cannot be concealed without appropriate magic. But its function in combat is not as a battle group, but as a disruption while stampeding across the battlefield, imposing the Size as a penalty to Join Battle rolls, with anybody whose roll is beaten by the Dragon Blood taking damage from being trampled, with damage based on dividing a combination of Initiative and herd\u2019s Size among targets, and not resetting Initiative to base if it succeeds. Finally, it can be learned in different elemental variations to marshall things other than wild animals, in the appropriate terrain: Air gets avalanches (that can knock damaged people back and down and hits them with extreme cold to penalise movement until they receive medical treatment), Earth has rockslides to also knock people around and then bury them (requiring a feat of strength to pull loose and stand back up), Fire ignites a blaze in dry grass to create a bonfire to continue damaging anybody who was hit in the initial attack (as well as possibly creating a sustained burn on its own), and Water lets one drag a river or similar body behind oneself into battle, which then becomes directed to create a beneficial environmental barrier.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say that Ride has done well in filling out the tactical dimension of the Ability here, making the choice to use a steed more significant for the Terrestrial Exalted, and the last one has what might be some of the most dramatic and impressive elemental effects that they\u2019ve had thus far.<br /> <br /> Okay, next is Sail. Sail is going to be simper, right? Yeah, nothing but drowing people and brainwashing sailors, and maybe the occasional thing to pilot a boat. Yeah, it should take, like, ten minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:32:00-07:00","id":1209238,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m kind of interested in the whole anima-mount thing. If the first charm to protect your mount from your anima, and indeed the animas of all your sworn kin in close range, is essence 3, that\u2019s a long journey of being extremely delicate with your horse. <br /> <br /> Or maybe it\u2019s more of a statement about the dynasty? In general horses are an expendable resource that you use up as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-20-2018, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:38:48-07:00","id":1209239,"title":"","content":"Vance's response to what to do about a mount that shares your initiative was basically &quot;don't worry about it&quot;. Stronger stuff probably has a few ways around it. Elephants have natural hardness, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:00:33-07:00","id":1209250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1209239#post1209239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance's response to what to do about a mount that shares your initiative was basically &amp;quot;don't worry about it&amp;quot;. Stronger stuff probably has a few ways around it. Elephants have natural hardness, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! That\u2019s helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:59:32-07:00","id":1209433,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I am left with a dilemma; shall I look over one more Ability today, or give myself a bit of a break and do an even three a day over the weekend, leaving me done a day ahead of the last preview?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:09:52-07:00","id":1209444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1209238#post1209238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m kind of interested in the whole anima-mount thing. If the first charm to protect your mount from your anima, and indeed the animas of all your sworn kin in close range, is essence 3, that\u2019s a long journey of being extremely delicate with your horse. <br /> <br /> Or maybe it\u2019s more of a statement about the dynasty? In general horses are an expendable resource that you use up as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are noted to specifically breed horses descended from the usage of the signature Wood Charm, so maybe the assumption is most horses used by Dynast Dragon-Blooded in the legions already have the Hardness necessary to be immune to Anima Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:16:38-07:00","id":1209485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1209433#post1209433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I am left with a dilemma; shall I look over one more Ability today, or give myself a bit of a break and do an even three a day over the weekend, leaving me done a day ahead of the last preview?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three a day sounds doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T21:04:58-07:00","id":1209501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1209485#post1209485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three a day sounds doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, from my perspective, it's what I've <i>been</i> doing, so long as I count a day as meaning between the time I wake up and go to sleep. If one mentally adjusts their own time displays to GMP, it will be evident that I've written a number of these at around four or five in the morning.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's just that, because there's sixteen, it would mean either getting it done in five days with one of them covering four, or what I've ultimately decided on, where it's a day longer and one gets one Ability.<br /> <br /> \u200bBah, Performance and Ride were denser than I might have expected, I think that was enough to warrant having let Friday be a bit easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T05:48:04-07:00","id":1209590,"title":"","content":"Okay, Dragon Blooded Sail. Gonna try and go back to that attitude of skipping over many that provide basic enhancements, and focus on the ones with distinct effects and implications. That being said, just noting how the Excellency, Fine Passage-Negotiating Style, adds successes and rerolls 6s.<br /> <br /> The first couple, Storm-Outrunning Technique and Ocean-Darting Manuever, are in that mould of providing some enhancements to certain kinds of Sail roll. Where it starts to get interesting is with Dragon Mariner Attitude, their own version of a power to represent general experience and style as a sailor. In particular, with some of the qualities provided by Water, they can exert a kind of control over their own reputation, alternately acting as a magnet for people who would provide services to a sailor on shore leave, those who would be looking for a seafaring hero to solve their problems, draws the respect of sailors under their command (and sailors in general if they\u2019re trivial characters), or else able to exert a general aura of being menacing and disreputable (including getting the Hideous Merit). Come to think of it, this one doesn\u2019t precisely represent being a sailor, so much as being able to control the kind of sailor that people perceive you as.<br /> <br /> Skipping over one to the Air Charm Hurricane-Predicting Glance, which allows the user to make a Sail roll against a difficulty determined by how familiar they are with the local waters, which if successful allows for flawless prediction of the weather long their charted course for the next day, including the highly unlikely and unexpected, but not things produced by magic. It also bestows a specialty in dealing with that weather phenomenon, until they\u2019ve gotten through it.<br /> <br /> With Old Salt Spirit, I get a sense that capabilities that Solars get all at once with Salty Dog Attitude are distributed among a few Dragon Blooded Charms. Before, there was Deck-Striding Prana to improve rolls to move around or stay balanced on a ship, and now this one to boost Resolve both against general influence for fear, as well as things that would draw them to bring their ship into danger <i>and</i> prevent them from going out to sea. I find it interesting that their minds can conflate these things. As another special benefit, the bonus to Resolve can increase to half their Sail (rounded up) if they should use a stunt to reference memories of their past adventures at sea. I particularly like that as an idea for resisting fear in general; some giant rock monster tries to threaten them, and they bolster themselves with memories of the time that they escaped the grasp of the dreaded spindly killer fish.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Seven Seas Wind-Luring Chanty seems familiar, but I wonder\u2026 did it used to be an Occult Charm? I have a distinct recollection that there was an impulse towards keeping Abilities elementally pure for things that wouldn\u2019t partake of <i>all</i> the elements, so where a need was seen for something to call upon wind, it was placed in Air\u2019s Occult rather than Water\u2019s Sail. Well, whether it was anything and whatever it was before, now it\u2019s a Charm to make a Sail roll (using Charisma, since it\u2019s supposed to be about calming the ring with a rousing song), which lets them use successes to lower penalties from ill-favoured wind, or else boost their ship\u2019s speed a bit in fair weather.<br /> <br /> Given the material of most ships, it makes sense that there would be a Wood Charm, Sturdy Bulkhead Concentration. An Exalt can spend a level of their own anima to spread it out over the ship, reinforcing its structure against perils and enemy weapons, allowing the player to roll some extra non-Charm dice on an already failed roll to get through a hazard or deal with an enemy\u2019s stratagem. Raising success enough to beat the initial difficulty reduces the damage suffered, without necessarily eliminating it completely or changing how the result of the roll registers as failure.<br /> <br /> The Signature Air Charm builds upon Seven Seas Wind-Luring Chanty. When faced with threats from the air such as hurricanes or electrical storms, the Charisma + Sail roll can be made with double 9s against the hazard\u2019s difficulty, with success dispersing it entirely, and failure still affording the option of dealing with it mundanely. It\u2019s limited to once per story, but is reset by either dispersing or navigating through a hazard for the purposes of achieving significant goals.<br /> <br /> Water\u2019s counterpart in Earth gets Hull-Shattering Avalanche Impact, another to let one reinforce the ship with a level of anima, for the purpose of giving the ram stratagem double 8s, and lowering the number of threshold successes needed to increase the resulting damage. It can also be used outside of combat to wield one\u2019s ship for feats of demolition, rolling Wits + Sail with the ship\u2019s Speed in non-Charm dice, and being able to engage in Strength 10 feats. It\u2019s a curious image, of dealing with something like a sea wall or fortress by ramming a trireme into it, and being able to expect to succeed.<br /> <br /> Dragon Sets the Seas Ablaze has the rather dramatic effect of letting one discharge their anima through their ship\u2019s ranged weapons, letting one make a broadside stratagem with double 9s, and a capacity to set the targeted ship on fire. The fire will continuously roll a little bit to damage the ship\u2019s Hull, and the burning ship can make a special stratagem to put themselves out, although even failure keeps them from rolling for damage in that round. Mostly, it\u2019s an interesting image, of an Exalt pouring their Essence into a ship\u2019s weapons to add some energy to the attack, although it\u2019s counterbalanced by being only once per scene with no reset condition; it has to wait for the opportune moment, rather than laying a barrage.<br /> <br /> Shipwreck-Strewn Tempest Wake is the first of these to depend on Aura. With it, a ship that has succeeded in getting ahead of a pursuer or breaking away from naval combat can stir up a naval hazard in their wake to create an obstacle for those pursuers if they want to keep up the chase. The hazard has its own rules, with failure to navigate it not only inflicting damage, but throwing them off course in a manner that prevents effective pursuit for days. It\u2019s a power that can apply to multiple ships, and its once per story use can be reset by achieving a major goal through seafaring prowess or managing to reach a key place through sailing.<br /> <br /> And Benediction of the Living Ship allows the Dragon Blooded sailor to put a bit of vitality back in the wood of the ship, giving it a capacity to pull itself back together, as the Exalt rolls their Essence plus an applicable specialty to repair Hull damage. The scented aura or sprouting fruit of the ship in that time also heals the user and allies aboard of one non-aggravated damage level, which can also be used to harvest enough food to keep the crew going for the rest of the story, if it\u2019s needed. It finally provides an extra success to resist poison or disease while aboard. I like the way that this one synthesizes exerting a kind of manipulation of the ship\u2019s wooden structure to deal with specifically naval issues; turn your shell of dead wood into a little floating garden where you won\u2019t starve or get scurvy.<br /> <br /> Now, with Vanishing Fog-Bank Escape, you can expend a level of anima (a lot of these Charms are functioning on the need to put your anima into your ship or its weapons or the sea), to create a cloud of mist to aid one\u2019s escape. An escape stratagem is made with a reduced Momentum cost, and the number of Momentum the user has over a pursuing ship adds bonus dice on the roll to escape. For rolls to pursue at sea, it can also be used to impose a penalty on the roll to keep following. And outside of actual combat, it can be used to create a fogbank that will generally obscure the ship, and persists for a scene unless something strong manages to disperse it. This is a Charm that does <i>not</i> have a limited use, so one can repeatedly build up their anima and pour it into creating fog, if it\u2019s needed.<br /> <br /> Pirate-Masquerading Method builds on the mist generation to create an illusion over the Exalt\u2019s ship, to cause others who see it to regard it as one flying their own colours, proverbially speaking. A roll is made to determine how hard it will be for other people to see through the illusion, which can be attempted by any nontrivial character that is close enough, although doing so with their mundane senses suffers a penalty. It can also be seen through automatically by somebody who actually makes it on board the ship. It can instead be used to obscure the Dragon Blood themselves, adding Sail to dice rolls to disguise oneself as a member of a noteworthy society of sailors, such as a Tya or Lintha, and giving a bonus to Guile against actions that would expose them as an outsider. I\u2019m just imagining some of the uses that House Peleps could put this Charm to; making raids on neutral nations or possibly even the shipping and ports of other satrapies, and leaving behind witnesses who can only say that the attacker was disguised as one of their own.<br /> <br /> Bellowing Thunder Admiral is another Air Charm, this time to shout one\u2019s orders over any obscuring din and fill the hearts of one\u2019s shipmates to courage and valour, adding a success bonus equal to half of one\u2019s Essence to command actions for the benefit of battle groups of sailors. They also get that same bonus to their own rolls against rout, and get the same bonus to Resolve as the Exalt gets from Old Salt Spirit, so long as they remain within medium range (and honestly why should they ever not be they\u2019re on a ship where the fuck else are they going t-). I feel as though there have been other Charms that could modify their type under the right circumstances, but this one calls attention in the style of Martial Arts to special activation rules in the form of being able to use the otherwise Simple Charm reflexively after winning Join Battle for a boarding action.<br /> <br /> Coming up to the end is the Essence 4 Charm Ship-Seizing Dragon Talon, through which a Terrestrial can provide their boarding actions with double 9s, for a rather reasonable price of 1 mote and 1 willpower point. Success allows them (and any allies) to then roll Join Battle with bonus dice equal to threshold successes on the stratagem roll, and waives the Willpower cost in Bellowing Thunder Admiral.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s the Essence 5 Mute Charm, Fog Shroud Ambush. The Dragon Blooded captain is able to shroud their ship in mist again (without needing to spend their anima), this time to waive the Momentum cost for concealment in naval combat altogether, and allowing the next round\u2019s attack or escape stratagems to succeed automatically, without regards for an opposing roll. Even if the opponent has supernatural senses that could see through the fog, the Dragon Blood is able to impose their Manipulation as a penalty to the opposing naval roll. It can only be used once per scene, but is reset by incapacitating an enemy ship with a naval stratagem.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s it for Sail, comparatively short and sweet. For all of my snarking before, I am actually a little bit surprised that it didn\u2019t have things for recruitment or sabotage in the end, but otherwise think it\u2019s very effectively focused on providing benefits and added capabilities to actual sailing, and effectively conveys the formidable challenge of dealing with sailors that have some actual power over the water.<br /> <br /> Speaking of water, that\u2019s it for the Water Aspect then. My final assessment is that their element crossed with their Abilities does manage to make them very distinctly evocative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T14:07:01-07:00","id":1209774,"title":"","content":"Now, finishing off the Fire Aspect with Socialize, something that I always thought was one of the more interesting ones to give to that element.<br /> <br /> The Excellency is Loquacious Courtier Technique, a name that really speaks to me. It adds successes and raises Guile. Then there\u2019s Wary Yellow Dog Attitude (a name that I still need to figure out the meaning of), which allows the character to roll Socialize in Join Battle rolls when a fight breaks out from a social scene, with the possibility of getting non-Charm dice if they\u2019d influenced or read anybody who starts attacking them.<br /> <br /> Friend-to-All-Nations Attitude is a Wood Charm, and permanent. From just spending an hour in the presence of a new culture or social group, the Dragon Blood can gain a temporary specialty in that group, and can carry as many of those as their Essence, and can pick up new ones by dropping the old. I understand that all of their Charms are elemental, and that this one could be a simple case of the right element for the right effect, but I do wonder if the moment when the speciality is formed it either breaks a different Aura or creates a Wood one, as appropriate. I\u2019ll need to ask about that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, next there\u2019s Loyalty-Reading Meditation, to let one read intentions for an emotional Intimacy in a manner that makes it penalize Guile, and Smoke-Wreathed Mien to force others trying to read the Exalt\u2019s intentions to reroll their successes if they get 1s.<br /> <br /> Auspicious First Meeting Attitude is Water, soooo\u2026 ahh, it\u2019s not so sinister, just combine a read intentions and instil action in one, as a representation of figuring a new person out and tailoring one\u2019s demeanour to them.<br /> <br /> And another old favourite, Brother-Against-Brother Insinuation. Enhances instill attempts to weaken a positive Tie to somebody from your target\u2019s culture or group, or to create a negative one. Also prevents boosting Resolve against that action by drawing on an Intimacy to the culture that the targeted people share. I can\u2019t recall exactly how the Charm used to work, but if the element of being specific to people from the same culture is new, I like the way it allows one to target a cohesive group for dissolution.<br /> <br /> Air Charm Seizing-the-Tongue Technique allows a Terrestrial to recover from their spoken fumbles, rerolling failed dice in Presence or Socialize rolls, with the Aura allowing it to be used reflexively after having made the roll, rather than Supplemental to reinforce a roll that might have done fine anyway.<br /> <br /> I was expecting Sweeten-the-Tap Method to be Wood now. Rather, it is Wood and Fire in combination. I recall that in Second Edition, they gave this a bit of expansion to include a variety of indulgences, owing to a certain lack of hard mechanical effect. That\u2019s rolled back now to return to its roots; enhancing the potency of alcoholic beverages supplied by the Dragon Blood. The mechanics of it now are that everybody who drinks the stuff can be treated as though they have a positive Minor Tie to one another, and their Guile is slightly reduced. At the same time, the instability of the magically enhanced inebriation means that anybody who botches socially will have everybody else under the effect turn nasty towards them.<br /> <br /> Nooooww\u2026 Shadow-Dispersing Radiance used to add the difference between Appearance and a target\u2019s Guile as non-Charm dice to a read intentions roll. Eye-for-Passions Scrutiny lets you get told an extra Intimacy when your read intentions action succeeds. And Watching the Salon\u2019s Shadows allows one to apply a bonus to Guile against somebody that the user is unaware of reading intentions, and automatically rolling Awareness with double 9s to detect ones that fail. Last before the Signatures is Smoke Without Flame, both enhancing Guile, and giving those whose read intentions actions fail a false impression of success, revealing an exaggerated or caricatured version of the Exalt\u2019s current emotional state (so if you\u2019re a bit miffed, they\u2019ll think you\u2019re venomously hateful) or an emotion-based Intimacy, with Fire Aura making the Guile bonus non-Charm, and a repurchase at Essence 4 giving the option to expend Fire Aura to make the same effect work on somebody who successfully beat the Guile.<br /> <br /> Now, to start with Clear-Eyed Courtier\u2019s Scrutiny. It can basically be used to read the intentions of an entire group, with the added benefits of double 9s. It can either be used to determine their individual motives within the context of the scene or how all of the individuals feel about a certain topic. If it fails against any given person, a regular read intentions act can be performed on them in the same scene without needing to be reset.<br /> <br /> Unfaltering Pillar of Unity lets a Dragon Blood have an improved instil roll to grant members of a group a Tie of loyalty towards their group, reinforcing traditional social order. Characters can only resist forming the Tie using a Decision Point, and need to wait several weeks to be able to voluntarily weaken it, unless the Tie contradicts a Defining Intimacy. Other characters instil actions to weaken the Intimacy need to deal with rules to overturn a successful persuasion.<br /> <br /> The Aspect\u2019s Signature is Wildfire Scandal Revelation, a Charm with a prerequisite condition of having uncovered somebody\u2019s embarrassing or incriminating secret. The secret can the be used in conjunction with the Charm to double 8s on a Socialize roll to instil negative or weaken positive Ties to the person who keeps the secret, as well as a group or culture that they belong to. From therein, the person with the altered Intimacy gains a temporary specialty in spreading the information, and resisting it costs extra Willpower.<br /> <br /> Water gets a Psyche Charm, Ego-Dissolving Deception. Ah, but it\u2019s one that the user applies to <i>themselves</i>; they can spend an hour meditating, at the end of which they can rewrite their own memories of an event or relationship, an event lasting for up to a story. A Major Principle reflecting the altered memory is gained, and influence that would contradict the memory by weakening it is unacceptable. The motes maintaining the Charm can be reflexively released at any time, but doing so retains the created Principle until naturally eroded, which can create a confusing double memory. When the Exalt reaches Essence 5, the Charm upgrades to allow one to expend a Water Aura to use the Charm reflexively in response to somebody seeing through their Guile, to depict falsified memories to the scrutiniser.<br /> <br /> Last is Poisonous Sneer Reproach, allowing a Terrestrial to counter somebody else\u2019s attempted social influence by making a Socialize roll representing a counterargument or general derision, with every success penalising the targeted speaker\u2019s roll, with a dice pool reduced to zero or a botch resulting in the desired influence being inverted for every listener whose Resolve was lower than the Terrestrial\u2019s successes.<br /> <br /> With the Charm Ember-Fanning Provocation, persuade rolls based on negative Ties to the Other or ones created with Brother-Against-Brother Insinuation get double 9s, and if higher than Minor, the Willpower cost to resist is raised to two.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s another Psyche Water Charm, Smoothing-Over-the-Past Technique. It\u2019s a rather lengthy one, and I\u2019ve kind of been on Socialize for a while now, so I\u2019ll summarize: it let\u2019s an Exalt suppress somebody\u2019s memory of some way that the user has acted that would negatively dispose the target to them, and interact with them for a scene on that basis (although the Charm itself is Instant). There are a few caveats and conditions, and the memory suppression can be resisted if it would cause action inconsistent with a Major or Defining Intimacy. At Essence 5 it can be repurchased to allow one to expend Water Aura to erase a memory permanently, and it takes repeated Willpower expenditure to restore the memory for more than a scene.<br /> <br /> There are three more before getting to Essence 4. Enticing Flame Feint lets one draw attention away from allies, in the form of penalising attempts to read their intentions (while doing so penalises the user\u2019s Guile). Rumor-Dredging Gaze is another for Water, allowing an Exalt an enhanced read intentions to discover an Intimacy that the target would most want to hide from the scrutiniser, with rolls to blackmail from this information also being enhanced. Implacable Dragon Mien is Earth and grants bonus Guile except against reading intentions that would reveal a Major or Defining Intimacy based on emotion, or an intent arising from those, with Earth Aura increasing the general Guile bonus, and adding a bit against reading emotions.<br /> <br /> At the end is Rippling Mirror Face, ironically a Water Charm for the last Fire Aspected Ability. Its effect is actually comparatively simple; when someone fails to read the user\u2019s intentions, they think they succeed, and instead see the Intimacy of another character in the scene that the Charm\u2019s user has already read, with being in Water Aura allowing one to use the Charm after a roll has already failed.<br /> <br /> So Socialize has some interesting effects, a lot of nice enhancements for reading intentions, and a distinct throughline of sabotaging groups and societies by being able to mess up how others see them, or how they see themselves.<br /> <br /> The Fire Aspect themselves\u2026 I was initially thinking that they contrasted with what one might expect of the element, but then I considered how the Abilities that they have are rather focused; three with strong benefits to combat, two to engaging in major social scenarios. So I\u2019d say they kind of get both; the intent of those five Abilities is rather focused, but the steps and applications are unusually varied and intricate. All in all, I\u2019d say it\u2019s a unique but easily recognisable representation of Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T15:45:31-07:00","id":1209796,"title":"","content":"Hey Isator, do you think Swallows Defend the Nest from archery also deserves a mention to the developers for the same problem as the melee multiattack charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T17:06:13-07:00","id":1209824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1209796#post1209796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Isator, do you think Swallows Defend the Nest from archery also deserves a mention to the developers for the same problem as the melee multiattack charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI mean, I'm no game mechanics expert. I called the Melee Charm as I saw it, I'm hardly somebody who needs to give the go-ahead for you to make a query of your own finding.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, assuming that I'm reading it correctly, that Charm looks a bit better because it gives each of your attacks a bit of extra damage to roll, that increases as your Essence goes up. So even if you're somebody with either Dexterity or Perception of 2 or less, and can only make one attack (which is not referred to as being halved by default), then you can make a ranged decisive attack with a bit of extra damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T20:56:34-07:00","id":1209883,"title":"","content":"Rrrrr...<br /> <br /> \u200bMy day came out unexpectedly, so I don't have time to do Stealth. I'll get the remaining four covered starting in the morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T22:28:38-07:00","id":1209906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1209824#post1209824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI mean, I'm no game mechanics expert. I called the Melee Charm as I saw it, I'm hardly somebody who needs to give the go-ahead for you to make a query of your own finding.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, assuming that I'm reading it correctly, that Charm looks a bit better because it gives each of your attacks a bit of extra damage to roll, that increases as your Essence goes up. So even if you're somebody with either Dexterity or Perception of 2 or less, and can only make one attack (which is not referred to as being halved by default), then you can make a ranged decisive attack with a bit of extra damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's sort of what I was thinking, it's also cheaper and isn't a signature which I feel is a big deal. Signature charms need some wow factor to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T09:31:52-07:00","id":1210054,"title":"","content":"Okay, I ended up leaving this later than I intended to, and I\u2019ve got too much shit to do today, so I\u2019m going to try and bomb through Stealth.<br /> <br /> Distracting Breeze Meditation is uncommon as an Excellency with no effect besides adding to the Stealth roll. Not sure at the moment what the implications or purpose of that might be.<br /> Vanishing Wind-Body Technique combines reduction of penalties with general immunity to effects that detect somebody through air vibrations.<br /> <br /> Flowing Shadow Stance is a Water Charm to reroll 6s and grant Initiative for beating enemy rolls to detect you.<br /> <br /> Soundless Action Prana extends the idea of being soundless a bit mechanically by being able to reroll dice, as well as penalising superhuman or magical hearing.<br /> <br /> Shimmering Heat-Mirage Tactic is a Fire Charm, making one\u2019s body hazier and trail afterimages to boost Evasion, with the interesting detail of being able to end prematurely if somebody makes an attack roll with no 1s against them.<br /> <br /> Huh, Signature Charms already? Okay. Air has the Permanent Charm Whispering Dragon Soul, allowing one to apply the Mute Keyword to any Air or Balanced Charms with a two mote surcharge. Extra purchases can give that effect to other elements. Considering how anima affects Aura, this can probably have some significant benefits.<br /> <br /> Sleeping Dragon\u2019s Lair\u2026 I think I saw this in the previews as well, Charm to hide oneself in the earth. It makes one almost undetectable, while needing additional magic of one\u2019s own to be aware of anything else. It also literally buries the user rather than mystically merging with it, so one still has a limited air supply. Sudden emergence allows one to bring up an obscuring cloud of dust. Repurchasing at Essence 5 allows one to do this to solid rock, and emerge with a spray of shrapnel.<br /> <br /> Fire-Becomes-Shadow Technique lets one roll Stealth against the Resolve of characters with Intimacies that might support deference or submission, which renders the Exalt basically invisible to them until they initiate hostilities or chooses to unveil themselves. Hmm, it\u2019s referred to as unnatural influence, so shouldn\u2019t it have the Psyche keyword? Unless I\u2019m reading the term too systemically, and it should be considered to function primarily through the character\u2019s stealth.<br /> <br /> Depth-Stalking Discipline lets one give regular Stealth rolls double 9s, and when surrounded by water such as being submerged or in heavy rain, they get double 8s and can\u2019t be followed by smell at all.<br /> <br /> Shadow-Stalking Predator Spirit bends flora and foliage to help obscure the Exalt, allowing them to make rolls opposing Stealth subtract rolled 1s from successes when hiding in areas of moderate to heavy growth, as well as being able to spend Wood Aura to boost unexpected attacks made from their cover.<br /> <br /> Burning Shadow Double uses Fire to leave behind a heat mirage double while hiding in concealment and can move around (with limited actions) within medium range of the user as they wish, using the character\u2019s Manipulation as Evasion (only against attacks from further than short range) and vanishing if hit. There are mechanics for figuring out which images are fake, and being in Fire Aura allows one to leave multiple images.<br /> <br /> Zone of Silence Stance renders the user completely silent, even to supernatural senses, and radiate that effect out to close range, making everything within unable to hear one another or be heard from outside, with Air Aura able to expand the cone.<br /> <br /> Deadly Riptide Executioner is Water, and lets one gain Initiative from stalking a chosen target while in concealment. Water Aura can be expended when the Charm is ended with an unexpected attack to transform into water for lunging forward, letting one ignore points of soak or Hardness and doubling 10s on decisive damage rolls.<br /> <br /> Essence 4 has Dragon Shroud Technique to let an Exalt impose a penalty on all rolls to oppose Stealth, and they don\u2019t need to pay motes for muting Air Charms with Whispering Dragon Soul.<br /> <br /> Essence 5 gives Mela\u2019s Hungry Jaws. Ah, of course; I called this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Steal the breath from the lungs of people, the Stealth element being given by restricting its use to characters that are in concealment. It imposes the basic rules for asphyxiation, with trivial opponents getting no opportunity to survive. The Dragon Blood has to stay still, and the victim needs to successfully disengage to move, and can only escape the Charm if they manage to see the Exalt or get far enough away. Somebody else attacking the user can also end it, possibly even if they miss.<br /> <br /> Obviously that last one is a real stand out, and the rest is nice and functional, including against supernatural opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T09:44:38-07:00","id":1210060,"title":"","content":"If you compare the stealth excellency with the larceny and socialize ones you'll notice that all 3 simply add successes with no caveat. They're also all mute.<br /> <br /> So the mute keyword seems to count as a bonus feature for excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T09:45:00-07:00","id":1210061,"title":"","content":"EDIT: What Elfive said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T11:52:12-07:00","id":1210106,"title":"","content":"I didn't notice those were Mute, that's a pretty substantial benefit (for those abilities, anyway). Thanks for pointing that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:34:38-07:00","id":1210150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1210060#post1210060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you compare the stealth excellency with the larceny and socialize ones you'll notice that all 3 simply add successes with no caveat. They're also all mute.<br /> <br /> So the mute keyword seems to count as a bonus feature for excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=os3IqzajS9I\" data-code=\"os3IqzajS9I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/os3IqzajS9I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:36:48-07:00","id":1210151,"title":"","content":"Right, finish off the Wood Aspect with Survival.<br /> <br /> Ration-Enhancing Method, a combination of Excellency and Charm to improve foraging for basic food.<br /> <br /> Quarry Revelation Technique lets one reroll 6s on tracking rolls, and allows one to roll against otherwise perfect magic concealment. That is a pretty huge change over prior Editions, since I would often look over the tracking Charms and note how the Dragon Blooded were patently incapable of chasing after anybody with decent Charms to cover themselves. It stood out as a particular obstacle to a good Wyld Hunt, so it\u2019s good for them to have something to redress this.<br /> <br /> Conversely there\u2019s Trail-Concealing Measure letting one double 9s on Survival rolls to cover tracks or Stealth rolls to establish concealment in areas with heavy flora. They can learn elemental varients for environments such as heavy snow and ice, underground or mountainous terrain, deserts, active volcanoes and fire and smoke, and in or near watery areas or rainfall.<br /> <br /> Beast-Taming Aspect lets one make rolls to train animals or influence them with Performance and Presence with double 9s, gets the respect of animals that have been scared off, and turn an animal into a familiar over the course of weeks. Animal Empathy Technique lets one add non-Charm bonus dice to influence rolls made against animals, and eliminates any Resolve bonuses based on language.<br /> <br /> Wild-Wandering Forester\u2019s Charm\u2026 I think this was previewed. Lets you roll Survival to introduce facts about a wild area that the character is familiar with.<br /> <br /> Mother-of-Beasts Mastery lets one reduce the internal for training animals and ignore the specialty requirements, and can be repurchased at Essence 3 to train their magical abilities.<br /> <br /> Invoking Nature\u2019s Forgiveness, interesting Charm name\u2026 use it to briefly train oneself, Sworn Kin or others to give them a temporary Resistance specialty in the local environment, and ignore part of the penalties produced by harsh climates. This is another instance of a Charm that can be used co-operatively, letting several characters that know the Charm using it together to determine how many people can be brought under the effect and how much the penalties are reduced by.<br /> <br /> Stalking Wolf Pursuit ignores penalties to tracking rolls based on environmental factors such as visual obstruction or the age of tracks, as well as successful rolls letting one tell how long it\u2019s been since the target was present.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s finally a different element with Air giving Vanishing Tracks Technique. They can reroll 6s on rolls to cover tracks, and apply some of that result to allied characters whose covering rolls aren\u2019t as good.<br /> <br /> Signature Charms, with Cunning Beast-Mind Inspiration to improve the minds of your familiar, making a Survival roll and adding half the successes to a familiar\u2019s action, while also letting the familiar reflexively defend other to protect the master, and gives them double 7s to distract gambits.<br /> <br /> Earth-Moving Kata lets one create a minor seismic burst to knock aside earth-based environmental obstacles that are natural, as well as briefly creating useful features such as bridges or stairs to cross other obstacles.<br /> <br /> Wildfire-Taming Technique was previewed, and lets one control the direction of a wildfire, and possibly set it to track and chase a specific enemy.<br /> <br /> Roaring Dragon Font is used to locate and summon underground sources of water in otherwise arid environs. The water is also mystically imbued, and can provide a slight bonus to rolls for Athletics, Resistance and Survival if they\u2019re well disposed towards the Exalt.<br /> <br /> Stalking Apex Predator Technique lets one ignore penalties to moving in forested terrain or entering concealment in combat there, attempt rushes in stealth, and add non-Charm bonus dice to concealing tracks. They can also expend Wood Aura to make an enhanced unexpected decisive attack.<br /> <br /> Past the Signatures there\u2019s Tireless Caravan Prana, a permanent Charm to add a 7 mote surcharge to Invoking Nature\u2019s Forgiveness to give it the additional effect of greatly improved speed passing through the environment, although the worst obstacles can half how far they get, and being another thing helped by the Charm being used cooperatively.<br /> <br /> Dragon\u2019s Nest Shelter creates a shelter against the elements from the local environmental substances, with the particular conditions that it is best suited to protecting one from being based on the elemental Essence infused into it. At Essence 5, it also protects against the effects of the less severe portions of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Uncanny Fugitive\u2019s Intuition is an Air Charm, allowing one to gain a sense of when somebody is trying to track you (although it requires them to have failed a roll to get the opportunity to activate the Charm), including their general distance and direction.<br /> <br /> Fire gives Burning Fang Strike, through which an Exalt can expend Fire Aura into an attacking familiar to enhance their offensive power for a decisive attack, although it also means that the user shares in the familiar\u2019s Initiative resetting to base if successful.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Survival has a curious number of Charms without specific elemental keywords. Eternal Elemental Harmony is used when a roll against an environmental hazard is failed, making a Stamina roll whose successes reduce the hazard\u2019s damage. If reduced to zero, the Exalt gets a point of Willpower. If one is in an Aura matching the hazard\u2019s elemental quality, the duration of the Charm is matched to the Aura, repeatedly using the initial dice result to weaken the hazard, although only able to recover Willpower once.<br /> <br /> Last is the Essence 4, Air/Water Charm Labyrinth of Mist Technique. Rolls to conceal tracks benefit from double 8s, and others who fail on tracking rolls will follow false trails that lead to becoming lost in the wilderness, with getting out being dependent on managing a difficulty 5 Survival roll (which delays one for a day if the roll is failed).<br /> <br /> Survival is a lot like Stealth, mostly functional effects rather than highly impressive ones. It\u2019s an interesting comparison to Solars that this Ability focuses a bit more on navigating environments than enhancing familiars. On that note, I\u2019ll reiterate how good it is that their capacity to track and conceal having its relationship with perfect effects has been revised.<br /> <br /> Wood came out rather nicely. Survival kind of leaves it ending on a less flashy note, but Archery, Medicine, Performance and even Ride all do a lot to balance that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T20:50:28-07:00","id":1210261,"title":"","content":"My day wound up being too overstuffed to fulfil my goal. If so much house work had not been piled in, I could have done the last two. They'll have to go tomorrow/later today.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm annoyed at having filled the entire week with this, but I suppose I can console myself with the idea that 16 Abilities is rather a lot to look over.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd hey, my reward shall be seeing Immaculate Dragon Styles using the Elemental Aura and Vance's polish (which are also likely to be mercifully shorter), Artifacts passed down through generations of Exalted, and stat write-ups for some of the notable personages. It's not all bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T06:46:09-07:00","id":1210388,"title":"","content":"All right, time to end this. Both Abilities in quick succession.<br /> <br /> Thrown starts off with Seeking Throw Technique, which presents itself not just as throwing very well, but being able to bend projectiles through the air, represented as both adding dice and being able to ignore light cover, with Air Aura even allowing one to slightly ignore heavy cover if they aim.<br /> <br /> The immediate follow-up is an Earth Charm, Armor-Rupturing Fang. Ah, another kind of gravitational effect, lodging a weapon or projectile from a decisive attack in an enemy\u2019s armour (and sometimes body, if their outer layer is durable) to mess it up by lowering soak and increasing mobility penalty, which requires a feat of strength to pull loose. Earth Aura lets one do so repeatedly to the same target, and I like the image of pelting an enemy with objects to increasingly weigh them down.<br /> <br /> Fire then gets one with Blinding Spark Throw, which looks like it throws only the sparks rather than the weapon they\u2019re ground off of. It lets one make a gambit to blind somebody for a few rounds, unless they pay Initiative and succeed on a Resistance roll to regain their sight, with the option to expend Fire Aura when an enemy is crashed to use the Charm on them reflexively.<br /> And Wood gets in with Venomous Thorn Attack, letting the Dragon Blood secrete their own poison to coat their weapon as they make a decisive attack. Hmm, I feel as though this should have a specification somewhere about the property of the poison it creates, even if it was just to say that one had their choice of venom to apply.<br /> <br /> Back to Air is Arcing Levinbolt Precision. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve commented on it much, but I\u2019ve enjoyed the references to Air based lightning attacks having improved effects on people wearing metal armour, so I like this one using that as the basis of an improved Thrown attack. An arc of electricity probing armour for a weak spot, represented by applying mobility penalty against soak or Hardness. It seems like a good effect (even if I presume it only counts natural mobility penalty, rather than stuff that has been stacked onto it), and considering how Lore gets the actual Charm to shoot lightning, I think it\u2019s a good way to add at least the visual effect to Thrown.<br /> <br /> Earth-Shattering Strike is simpler, using an Earth Aura to add weighty force to a thrown weapon such that a decisive attack can be made at a target\u2019s feet to create a zone of difficult terrain from the impact crater. I\u2019m a little bit unclear on if the attack is purely for that effect, or if it\u2019s added to a normally damaging attack.<br /> <br /> Invisibly Hidden Chakram Method\u2026just sends a throwing weapon Elsewhere? I mean, fair enough that it isn\u2019t limited to jade weapons like Elemental Sheath is but\u2026 actually, thinking about it, I guess I can see the advantage, being able to carry one\u2019s ammunition undetectably, keeping up with a typical clandestine image for Thrown, but needing to commit motes for the privilege. Okay, that\u2019s fine.<br /> <br /> Mela\u2019s Twin Fangs obviously can\u2019t be as impressive as the last Charm to bear her name, but it\u2019s not half bad, playing off of the prior Charm to allow one to rapidly pull a weapon out of Elsewhere in the wake of making another attack to make two withering attacks against somebody in the same turn. While Elusive Zephyr Strike lets one make a wind-guided distract gambit to benefit from double 9s, and Air Aura to add threshold successes from the attack roll to the Initiative one.<br /> <br /> Before the Signatures is the Fire Charm Smoke Burst Eruption to cause a weapon to emit a shockwave upon striking an enemy that stirs up a cloud of dust in which one can establish concealment, from which one can gain a slight bonus to unexpected attacks. Repurchasing it at Essence 5 allows one using the Charm in Fire Aura to spend Willpower on the Charm to reflexively roll themselves into hiding in the smoke.<br /> <br /> Air\u2019s Signature is Persistent Hornet Attack, with which one can give a thrown weapon a kind of life of its own, taking the Initiative gained from an initial withering attack and using that for itself, while it moves, aims and attacks those at close range. It can\u2019t benefit from other Charms, but can build Initiative toward inflicting its own decisive attacks, which end the Charm should one succeed, and conversely loses Initiative if it should go a round without managing to hit somebody. The weapon also has a Defense value and can have its Initiative taken with withering attacks, or else a disarm gambit can knock it from the air to end the Charm. A thrown weapon being able to move of its own accord is something that I\u2019ve wondered about sometimes, and I think the realisation here works well.<br /> <br /> Devastating Avalanche Barrage starts off well with describing another particularly striking elemental image, drawing a cloud of earthen projectiles to concentrate around a weapon to be thrown. They hurl their weapon in a withering attack against one person, and the added debris and shrapnel follows after to make an unblockable withering attack against the same person and anybody within short range of them, with the anima being a viable substitute in an environment with no appropriate features. The damage rolled by the follow up is also unsoakable, but not permitted to exceed damage rolled by the normal attack. The rocks render those hit by them prone, and if they are crashed then they\u2019re sufficiently buried to be unable to move without clearing the debris with a feat of strength.<br /> <br /> Exploding Weapon Technique provides a Decisive-only Charm, to concentrate one\u2019s anima (if their Initiative is at least 12) into their weapon as an explosive force, that is discharged on making an attack. Unlike other explosive effects, the force seems to be concentrated solely on the targeted person, taking the form of adding the Exalt\u2019s Essence to the damage roll, as well as being able to roll another die for every 9 and 10 that is rolled. It happens to destroy most mundane weapons that might be used for it. The Charm can be repurchased at Essence 5 to add a couple of extra effects: my liking for Armor-Piercing Fang is compounded by the idea that the embedded weapons can also be set off for additional motes, adding three dice of damage each (and which has to leave behind a rather messy body), and also adding to a Charm I haven\u2019t seen yet, letting Exploding Weapon be activated reflexively, as a Balanced Charm without needing Fire Aura, and modifying an effect for repeated explosions (I\u2019ll need to see the other Charm to fully know what is going on). Finally, this has the interesting distinction of <i>not</i> being limited in how much it can be used.<br /> <br /> Fatal Riptide Strike gets to use both avenues, being Uniform (and also Mute), letting a Dragon Blood add aqueous Essence to their weapon so that it can be thrown without impediment through water, also enhancing surprise attacks that are made from within the water. It also gives the option of, once per scene, being used when the Dragon Blood makes an unexpected attack on somebody with lower Initiative with the addition of one Willpower and their Water Aura to make the attack an ambush.<br /> <br /> Last is Hundred Thorns Blossom, with which an Exalt can make confusing, distracting motions to open an enemy up to attacks with a barrage of hidden weapons (there\u2019s a reference to them being produced from hair, fingertips and the throat, but I\u2019m unclear if this means that the Charm manufactures them, or they need to have been already there). In any case, it can be used on an enemy with lower Initiative to force them to roll Awareness against the user\u2019s Guile, with failure meaning that a reflexive unexpected decisive attack can be made on them with damage equal to Manipulation, plus dice based on how far below the difficulty the target failed, which ignores Hardness, and doesn\u2019t reset the user to base. It even has a rather generous reset condition, of successfully establishing concealment against all nearby enemies.<br /> <br /> The regular Charms start again with Earth in Stone Needle Strike. It\u2019s a short Charm; hitting somebody with a decisive attack literally pins them to the floor, requiring a feat of strength to be used before they can move again. Nice, simple and brutal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then it\u2019s Winter Fang Attack, adding a numbing chill to a weapon such that successful gambits or decisive attacks cause the enemy to also lose Initiative for 10s that turn up in the damage roll. Following that is Thousand Razor Wind (the one that the Exploding Weapon Technique repurchase could enhance), aaaand ah, here is something that I was thinking Invisibly Hidden Chakram could use; the option to send all of the weapons hidden elsewhere flying at once in decisive attacks (something else that helps validate the Charm as separate from Elemental Sheath and justifies the mote commitment). While Initiative needs to be divided evenly between each weapon, they get to ignore Hardness, the Exalt\u2019s Initiative\u2026 oh, wait, they still reset to base Initiative, just only when all attacks have been made. Still, it\u2019s fairly cheap, and can probably be a bit devastating under the right circumstances\u2026 and I see what Exploding Weapon does now, adding three dice to each attack made with the recalled weapon.<br /> <br /> Aww, we\u2019re reaching the end already? Thrown has had such intriguing effects that I was actually starting to want it to keep going on for longer, in contrast to most other Abilities. Anyway, there are three Essence 4 Charms.<br /> <br /> Whirlwind Shield Technique lets an Exalt surround themselves with a vortex of air in which local debris and any weapons tossed in swirl. It\u2019s an unusual kind of defensive barrier; it rolls to Join Battle with Wits + Thrown, having a Parry rating equal to half the rolled successes (rounded up) and can provide a defend other action with that, moving to follow the Exalt for the scene, gaining Initiative whenever successful. It also has a soak of its own, which can probably be rather strong for being based on a combination of Essence, Dexterity and Stamina. It needs it, since withering attacks can take Initiative as normal and decisive attacks take two for each point of damage, with the Charm being prematurely ended if the shield is crashed. This is another where I\u2019ll want to look back at what it used to be, but I can say that what it is now looks like both a strong defensive benefit and another intriguing instance of mastering an element to one\u2019s will.<br /> <br /> Vengeful Gust Counterstrike is a Charm with the Clash keyword, and another spin on the concept of generating a burst of wind to deflect attacks. Oh wait, it\u2019s an actual enhancement of Whirlwind Shield, letting one reflexively clash attacks from out to short range with a decisive attack rolling damage equal to the whirlwind\u2019s Initiative, not taking up the user\u2019s combat action or resetting their own Initiative. It does, however, reset the whirlwind to just three Initiative if it succeeds, while if it fails the whirlwind is what absorbs the attack.<br /> <br /> And last is Wind Armor Technique, a permanent enhancement to the whirlwind, meaning that while it is active it confers its Initiative as Hardness for the Exalt who used it (which doesn\u2019t work while armoured), and inflicts a die of Hardness ignoring lethal damage on close range attackers that are parried by it. Right now, I\u2019m picturing the dramatic circumstance of two Terrestrial Exalted who both know this Charms engaging in a duel that involves clashing whirlwinds; that would probably be a sight to behold.<br /> <br /> Thrown is quite engaging, combining that niche of varied, tactical effects with some very impressive powers, and a nice even mix of elements.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll need to review Charms at some point, because at the moment I don\u2019t quite get the same sense from Air Aspected Abilities as a whole that I did from Water\u2019s duplicity, Fire\u2019s eclecticness and Wood\u2019s interconnectivity (even if the Abilities individually are rather striking).<br /> <br /> Just a little while before finishing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T08:49:38-07:00","id":1210438,"title":"","content":"Just to let you know, so you can amend (or not) Venomous Thorn Attack, Vance has clarified that you must have the poison on you, the Charm only lets you apply it reflexively, it does not create a poison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:02:17-07:00","id":1210443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1210438#post1210438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to let you know, so you can amend (or not) Venomous Thorn Attack, Vance has clarified that you must have the poison on you, the Charm only lets you apply it reflexively, it does not create a poison.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAhh yes, I remember seeing that. I suppose the image of it being secreted from the hands would be a matter of not needing to take the poison out of its container.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot just being reflexive, mind; usually, poison can't be applied to a weapon without the correct tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:36:56-07:00","id":1210460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1208004#post1208004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean what I think the power actually is, or what my opinion on them being less powerful is, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess both in general. Having read the recent dev update on the charms I have a better idea where they're coming from with the charm ideas though.<br /> <br /> Do you feel they're less powerful then? And do you feel that they give the DBs enough punch versus a solar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T10:21:58-07:00","id":1210477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1210443#post1210443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAhh yes, I remember seeing that. I suppose the image of it being secreted from the hands would be a matter of not needing to take the poison out of its container.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot just being reflexive, mind; usually, poison can't be applied to a weapon without the correct tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, it allows any weapon to be poisoned (not only those with the Poisonable tag) and for it to be done reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T10:45:03-07:00","id":1210487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgrimas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1210460#post1210460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess both in general. Having read the recent dev update on the charms I have a better idea where they're coming from with the charm ideas though.<br /> <br /> Do you feel they're less powerful then? And do you feel that they give the DBs enough punch versus a solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve got a long of stuff to say on this and I don\u2019t want to hijack Isator\u2019s thread so I\u2019ll make my own tonight, but what are you looking for specifically? Like how dangerous a Wyld Hunt can be, can a DB go one vs one? Anything in particular?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T10:58:22-07:00","id":1210491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgrimas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1210460#post1210460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you feel they're less powerful then?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat, then Solars? Oh absolutely; their best effects require significant setup to use or have constraints on their frequency, and Solars can achieve a number of powers that they cannot.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, technically Dragon Blooded have powers that Solars don't as well, it's just that a Solar isn't really limited by the inability to enforce hospitality with displays of elemental power in the way that a Terrestrial might be by an inability to shape land, people and Artifacts from the Wyld.<br /> <br /> What the Dragon Blooded are definitely not, is boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgrimas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And do you feel that they give the DBs enough punch versus a solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bProbably. It depends on their Essence and how clever they are about it, as well as precisely how their enemy fights, but they've got some powers and means of enhancing their dice pools and defences that should help it be more even. Probably less a case of Solars reaching a point at which Dragon Blooded attacks are going to ping off of them so much as Dragon Blooded often needing to put in greater costs and risks to bring to bear the kind of power that can mess up a decent Solar who is contesting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T13:16:16-07:00","id":1210564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1210487#post1210487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve got a long of stuff to say on this and I don\u2019t want to hijack Isator\u2019s thread so I\u2019ll make my own tonight, but what are you looking for specifically? Like how dangerous a Wyld Hunt can be, can a DB go one vs one? Anything in particular?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll look forward to reading your thread on it XD. I'm not a big mechanic monkey as I don't have a game right now, so was looking for what isator just said.<br /> <br /> I think I did read that in another thread Solars are a little less &quot;invincible&quot; this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T15:57:53-07:00","id":1210659,"title":"","content":"Now, for the last Ability, we have War.<br /> <br /> I certainly like the name of Tactics Mean Everything. It adds bonus dice and rerolls 6s.<br /> <br /> Excellence of the Dutiful General lets situational bonus dice on Strategic Maneuver rolls into successes that don\u2019t count towards the dice cap. Tireless Footfalls Cadence enhances one\u2019s army by letting the user ignore penalties for their fatigue or movement through difficult environments in Strategic Maneuver rolls, as well as fatigue-based penalties for the duration of the fight if their Maneuver beats that of an opposing general. That, on its own gives a nice picture of a basic advantage of the army led by Dragon Blooded, being able fast through marching longer and going via routes that other armies would need to go around.<br /> <br /> Roaring Dragon Officer appears to have some incomplete editing. If I\u2019m reading it correctly, it was <i>originally</i> written to reduce penalties for placing a command action in a flurry, and not penalizing Defense, with Earth Aura ignoring the penalties entirely. Given how the non-crossed out text states that the basic effect lets a command action be placed in a flurry (though not with an attack), I\u2019m guessing that somewhere along the way it was recognised that command actions can\u2019t be put in a flurry; Earth Aura now gives the capability that the basic Charm previously had.<br /> Fire has a Charm with Blazing Courageous Swordsman Inspiration. I remember, ages ago, when there were descriptions of the problems with the mass combat system, how it emphasized being the general who led from the front, and how that worked well for Dragon Blooded but not for half of Solar concepts and basically none of Sidereals. Mind, considering how War was an Earth Aspect Ability, it arguably didn\u2019t really fit for them either. Anyway, here\u2019s a Fire Charm to adopt that quality, getting non-Charm exploding 10s on command rolls to give orders that use Charisma or Appearance. The Aura allows one to apply their bonus dice to the commanded battle group\u2019s Willpower roll to prevent being routed.<br /> <br /> Army-To-Mob Assault is a Water Charm that allows one to enhance a battle group under the Exalt\u2019s command attacks another battle group, so that they can convert up to their Manipulation in bonus dice granted by commands into automatic successes, and adds to the difficulty to resist rout if the enhanced attack empties the enemy\u2019s Magnitude (pop pop).<br /> <br /> Through Wood they can use the Choking Weeds Tactic, the idea being that it controls special raids on the enemy\u2019s logistics to weaken them and shore up your own side, mechanically conveyed in increasing the threshold of an opposing general when they\u2019re contesting Strategic Manuevers, while allowing the winning Dragon Blood to benefit from a penalty to the enemy battle group\u2019s Join Battle roll.<br /> <br /> And Air gets Changing Winds Cunning, letting non-1 failed dice on Strategic Manuevers get rerolled, with an Essence 5 repurchase to let them spend Willpower after rolling a maneuver (and before rerolling the failures) to change the stratagem is they want it.<br /> <br /> So, even before the Signatures, War gets a full spread of elements. That\u2019s nice and all, but I do kind of hope that Earth is more prominent on the other side.<br /> <br /> Well, to get there. First is Storm-Calling Strategos: create a magical stratagem to control weather to make enemies deal with storms and\u2026 this feels familiar, was this previewed? Well anyway, impose an environmental penalty on an enemy army\u2019s physical actions, with a lesser penalty on singular enemies, and nothing to the Dragon Blood and their allies. Ah yes, I definitely remember this part; when the user\u2019s Initiative is high enough, they can pay a bit to hit the other battle group with something like lightning or an avalanche as an environmental hazard.<br /> <br /> Ah, here\u2019s another return of an old classic as a Signature Charm: Ramparts of Obedient Earth. It\u2019s been made a good deal more mechanically intricate and specific compared to how it used to be; for one thing, it specifically tied to commanding an army, since it can only be used while leading them through a stratagem. Join Battle can be rolled with Intelligence + War, with successes creating a pool of points to spend on shaping the battlefield. Sinkholes can be created to make difficult terrain adjacent to a battle group and force them to act last in the turn order for the first round of battle, with a point cost equal to the target\u2019s Size. 4 points can be spent for creating barricades as an instantly successful Fortifications stratagem. 7 points can be used for sapping an enemy\u2019s Fortificiations to negate their benefits, not need to treat the terrain as difficult, and reflexively advance one range band forward (as well as circumstantial benefits defined by the Storyteller). And a hefty 10 points can be used to reshape the entire battlefield; if the commander successfully enacts a Strategic Placement stratagem, they have freedom to add basically any earthen features to the field that they want, with the Storyteller adjudicating the particular effects of any given added feature, and the only limit being unable to directly harm enemies. This one I think is particularly good to systemize and focus (while still being able to do a lot); I think in the past it was a bit too broad, and could be use too easily to overwhelm singular opponents.<br /> <br /> Deadly Wildfire Legion lets an Exalt expend their Fire Aura across their commanded battle group to add flame to the edge and tips of their weapons as they charge, adding non-Charm dice equal to Essence to the command action for orders, with the successes not only adding to their attack roll, but their damage as well. The group can finally take the action to fulfil the command immediately, rather than waiting for its place in the Initiative order. It can only be used once per scene, but gets reset by an allied battle group incapacitating a major enemy or routing a battle group.<br /> <br /> Fog-of-War Misdirection is Mute, creating an eerie fogbank to lure and trap an enemy within, a magical stratagem to create that imposes a -2 penalty on vision-based rolls and attacks made from medium range or further, and a -1 penalty on checks for rout for battle groups caught within the fog itself (although also slightly penalising actions to target the ensnared group\u2026 wait, no, that\u2019s a penalty on somebody trying to give them orders, that makes more sense). If the battle group does rout, the Exalt who made the forgets half its Size (but no more than their Essence) in Initiative. The fog can\u2019t be dispersed through natural weather, but magical means are effective. While it can only be used once per story, it can be reset when one roleplays a scene to gain an advantage that adds dice to Strategic Maneuver actions through deception, subterfuge or treachery. For Water\u2019s final Signature Charm of the game, it\u2019s quite appropriately dickish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Wood gets Hidden Thorn Treachery, letting them spread out spies to become deeply embedded in enemy ranks. It creates a magical stratagem to have a traitor infiltrate enemy ranks, although only possible when the Dragon Blood already has a Strategic Manuever bonus from spies or traitors. If successful, they can reflexively reveal the agent\u2019s presence at any valid point in combat (although the Storyteller can adjudicate impossible betrayals, barring an appropriate stunt). It also can\u2019t be used on groups with Might 2 or higher or perfect morale. When the betrayal is declared, the battle group immediately falls apart from the reveal of a notable and high-ranking member as loyal to the enemy (unless that would be somebody narratively important and difficult to believe). If a commander manages to rally them, they can do\u2026 something, I need to reread the battle group rules to understand what this does. Something to do with only getting part of the force, while the rest goes to the Dragon Blood who used the Charm, while the group not being rallied means that they <i>all</i> go over.<br /> <br /> Just a couple of pages left. Enfolded in the Dragon\u2019s Wings is Earth, and allows one to fortify their group\u2019s ranks and lines, rolling a special command actions reflexively for an allied battle group within short range that has been attacked, with every two successes adding to their Defense and soak. It can only be used once per scene, but reset by successfully rallying, and at Essence 5 its range can be extended to medium.<br /> <br /> Fire gets a couple now, with Phantom Fire-Warrior Horde to expend a level of anima to create ranks of illusionary warriors to fill in gaps in a force, adding half their Essence to the Magnitude (pop pop) of a group when it\u2019s rallied for numbers. The result of the rally roll can also be applied as a threaten action against all groups that see the illusory warriors come into existence, with those whose Resolve is beaten retreating until successfully ordered to do otherwise. Then it\u2019s Indomitable Flame of Valor to ignite their courage, doubling 9s on rolls to rally or rally for numbers, and grants perfect morale for a round to a group with elite Drill; at Essence 5, 4 Initiative can be payed to extend the duration of the perfect moral to the full scene.<br /> <br /> And the very last Charm is the Essence 4 sample, Earth Charm Blessed Dragon Champion. It\u2019s another that requires a group led under a successful stratagem to use, after which 9s are doubled on <i>all</i> War rolls (the Charm lasts for a scene), and the user has increased Defense against battle groups. Non-Charm dice equal to the size of the largest battle group that the user commands to all attacks against enemy battle groups. So here, at the end, is one to let one basically wear their army.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I\u2019m surprised at the lack of Charms to enhance artillery here, but I\u2019d say if word count was limited, those would be among the lower priority. As a whole, War does very well despite the removal of Dragon Vortex Attack, having very effectively shifted the focus back to being an exceptional commander of troops.<br /> <br /> Not much to say about the Earth Aspect as a whole. They\u2019re ultimately\u2026 I\u2019m not using a pun. The Abilities align well with the concept.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t really say any more about the Charms as a whole that isn\u2019t already evenly distributed. It\u2019s a grand piece of work.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m ready for the final preview!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T18:37:45-07:00","id":1210733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgrimas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1210564#post1210564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll look forward to reading your thread on it XD. I'm not a big mechanic monkey as I don't have a game right now, so was looking for what isator just said.<br /> <br /> I think I did read that in another thread Solars are a little less &quot;invincible&quot; this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so it ended up...long, but here's a link.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded\"> A Closer Look: Solars vs Dragonblooded - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So I've seen this kind of thing crop up in a few threads, there's even another thread about it but that's kind of drifted. I've got a lot to say anyway. Plus it's exam time and all my exams are over, so time to turn that hard analysis to Exalted! That means it's time for a closer look. I'd like to point out here that I love the DB charmset as previewed and I have very very few criticisms of it. I'm head over heels for most of it and this is not meant to bring it down. Most of what I've seen has concerned the idea of Dragonblooded being able to fight Solars, let's take a look at that shall we? Here </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:01:48-07:00","id":1210939,"title":"","content":"And now, the final preview has come out. It\u2019s almost as long as the prior one, but should come in an easier to digest form.<br /> <br /> First a chapter fiction, taking us back to the year of\u2026 the setting\u2019s default year. Hmm, my initial impulse would be that it would depict the familiar scene of an adherent travelling to an Immaculate dojo in search of training, but the end of the first paragraph makes it more apparent that it\u2019s somebody going off to deal with illicit worship.<br /> <br /> It seems a bit on the nose to have a fertility god trying to compel an Immaculate monk (one born to House Cynis, no less). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do like the idea of the god being non-binary gendered. Plus, when the fighting starts, the little idea of a god who doesn\u2019t need to breathe not really appreciating that until they begin suffocating.<br /> <br /> Also a bit of affirmation about why one might oppose a corrupt god, both practical and rooted in Immaculate doctrine. I like some of the mystical elements of what the god employs to fight.<br /> And there\u2019s an interesting mix of ominousness and kindly instruction in the final line having the monk respond to \u201cI yield\u201d with \u201cGood, but will you obey?\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m surprised that this didn\u2019t feature Righteous River, although on the other hand she <i>was</i> rather prominent in the opening fiction. In any case, it\u2019s a nice introduction for the Immaculate Dragon Styles.<br /> <br /> On that note, into the chapter proper, and the introduction to those styles.<br /> <br /> So it\u2019s the same note on how the basic function of the styles was to afford a better means of beating the gods into line, with a bit of emphasis on how they arose from collaboration between Terrestrial martial artists and Sidereal instructors, a bit less one-sided. Now, what are some of the distinctions in how they work\u2026<br /> <br /> The styles have their aspects and benefit from Aura (with a note on how non-Terrestrials don\u2019t get one), knew that already. Hmm, the demands of the styles mean that, besides Dragon Blooded, anybody who would be restricted by the Terrestrial keyword can\u2019t learn the Charms. It gives Solars and Sidereals as examples, but that would surely also include Lunars and Abyssals and the like, only really leaving out Liminals, most small gods and probably more than a few Exigents.<br /> <br /> They have no Terrestrial or Mastery keywords of their own, also known. Ohh, here\u2019s something interesting; there were always references before to a benefit of getting deep into an Immaculate Style, but I could never fully parse them, and they seemed a bit dull. Whereas now, learning up to the Form Charm confers the benefit of being able to expend an Aura whose element corresponds with an advanced style while in the Form of <i>any</i> style, to ignore the Terrestrial keyword on all Martial Arts Charms for one tick. That\u2019s a very interesting way to represent the unique benefits of learning these styles and how they align with the Dragon Blooded Essence, plus it plays nicely into the picture I had of Terrestrial limits depicting one straining their hardest and coming just short; that with the right boost, they can stretch a bit past that limit. Neat idea.<br /> <br /> Given the strong ties between the styles and the Order, it\u2019s good to have a sidebar elaborating on where and how they\u2019re learned. I\u2019m suddenly imagining a Dynast who went off to the Threshold to be taught in the dojo of a renegade, and how that might affect their reputation back home.<br /> <br /> And then it\u2019s into the styles\u2026 eh, they\u2019re surely shorter and more accommodating than a full Ability cascade, and the introduction was short enough. I can squeeze Air Dragon Style in.<br /> Teaches one to take on the qualities of the wind, utilises a lot of acrobatics (apparently more for the awareness it gives one of their own body, rather than manoeuvring in its own right), and mastery of breath control, with an emphasis on distant attacks. Fights with chops, spinning kicks and the chakram, compatible with light armour, and benefits from complementary Occult, Dodge and Stealth.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon\u2019s Sight improves spatial awareness through air sensitivity, ignoring half of one\u2019s Perception in onslaught penalties or environmental penalties to Evasion, while surprise attacks inflict no penalty (ambushes still work). Being in Air Aura confers the first bonus that nobody else, even the Solars, can enjoy; being able to ignore one\u2019s full Perception in those penalties.<br /> Cloud-Treading Method lets the user ignore penalties for moving through difficult terrain, in concealment, and other environmental issues, as well as going across surfaces that would otherwise be unable to bear them (although not to stand still on them). Air Aura extends that to liquids, or even vapours besides the air; I\u2019m suddenly picturing one being complemented by somebody shooting a lot of fire into a body of water to create a cloud of steam that can be ran across.<br /> <br /> Wind Dragon Speed lets one make special hit-and-run strikes by flurrying a disengage action with an attack, without the usual penalties, with a disengage that effectively carries them out of range of all enemies (besides the crashed and the trivial) not causing Initiative loss. Air Aura allows a disengage to instead be flurried with an aim, but only for the benefit of Air Dragon attacks.<br /> <br /> Breath-Seizing Technique is a much lengthier Charm than the rest. Let\u2019s see\u2026 needs to have Initiative 12 and up, makes a decisive attack, and before rolling for damage they get to roll the attack roll\u2019s successes against the target\u2019s soak (with minimum damage) for withering damage. There are some caveats based on Overwhelming damage that I don\u2019t quite understand on the face of it. The user doesn\u2019t acquire any Initiative lost by the target, but does benefit from Initiative break for the decisive damage if the enemy is crashed. It also has some interaction with Lightning Strike Style that I would need to review. As a couple of final notes, it can lower the amount of time that somebody can effectively hold their breath, and has a compounded effect against spirits, causing them to lose motes as well as Initiative on the withering attack (although not working on things that categorically do no breathe, such as zombies and machines).<br /> <br /> So it turns out that not every Dragon Style Charm benefits from Aura, meaning that there will be effects in which Solar and Terrestrial users will be equal.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the Air Dragon Form. While in the form, withering chakram attacks treat their range as close for the Accuracy benefits, regardless of their range, and the user benefits from a bonus to Evasion, disengagement and Stealth. It can be activated reflexively when the fighter deals enough withering damage to place an opponent\u2019s Initiative below their own.<br /> <br /> Shroud of Unseen Winds allows one to benefit from a bonus to Stealth rolls, either in dice or successes depending on how high the user\u2019s Initiative is. It also lets one stunt to be able to roll Stealth without a usual hiding place, with Air Aura letting one add successes without need for minimum Initiative (save not being crashed) and waves the need to stunt for concealment in the open.<br /> <br /> Avenging Wind Strike is used to double 10s on a decisive damage roll, and with success can knock an enemy prone and back, with sufficient damage increasing the knockback distance from one range band to two. Air Aura lets them knock an opponent back two bands regardless of how little damage is done, but lets sufficient damage increase them to three bands.<br /> <br /> Lightning Strike Style is used to extend the range of decisive attacks (to a maximum of long) and adds\u2026 I\u2019m a bit unclear, I believe that it\u2019s saying that Essence + Strength gets rolled, and the successes of that roll are\u2026 no, wait, it\u2019s saying that extra successes on the attack roll up to a maximum of Essence + Strength get added as extra dice to the damage roll. The electrical discharge of the attack also allows it to ignore the Hardness of metal armour. Air Aura also lets it ignore the cover of metallic objects and structures, as the lightning is simply conducted straight through them, although full cover can give a benefit to their Defense.<br /> <br /> Thunderclap Kata allows one to clap their hands to create a shockwave that forces everybody within medium range to make a Resistance roll against it as an environmental hazard to inflict bashing damage, which can also target dematerialized characters (and does worse damage to them), and has the cosmetic effect of being audible for miles. It can be used reflexively if one enters Air Dragon Form with at least 20 Initiative.<br /> <br /> Tornado Offense Technique is a promising name. Ah, but it lets one (figuratively) become a tornado, rather then creating one. The fighter selects a range band within their weapon\u2019s range, and delivers a decisive attack to everybody within it. It still requires aiming at a certain range, but it rolls a flat one-third of your Initiative in damage against every enemy that gets hit (which will be everybody with a Defense lower than the single decisive attack that you need to roll, so one should probably feel free to\u2026 do the Dragon Blooded have no Charm to add dice or successes to their general Martial Arts rolls?), in addition to extra dice equal to Perception for those who get the attack unexpectedly (and trivial characters just getting the full Initiative). Furthermore, Air Aura lets one add the number of enemies that were struck to their base Initiative after resetting, to a maximum of their Essence.<br /> <br /> This one is pretty damn strong, arguably among the best multi-attack Charms in the game. It probably benefits best from a bit of manoeuvring and maybe some allies to herd as many opponents as possible into the same range band, but so long as there are more than three of them, it pays for itself, and even if there are three or fewer, having to only roll to hit once might make up for the reduced rolled damage. I mean... unless you\u2019ve used one of Air Dragon\u2019s other Charms to enhance stealth to conceal yourself before making the attack, meaning that you can add dice to every damage roll made against those opponents.<br /> <br /> You know, I was gearing up to reserve judgement on the styles until I had seen all of them, and kind of leaning towards \u201cthey\u2019re basically functional\u201d, but this Charm here, and the manner in which it can synergize with others means I\u2019m calling it early; Air Dragon Style alone has become truly impressive now, compared to how the Immaculate Styles were written in prior Editions that failed to capture my imagination.<br /> <br /> And there are still a few to go. Wrathful Winds Kiai makes a gale-force shout, rolling Stamina + Martial Arts as an unblockable withering attack against everybody in a certain arc out to medium range, with no Accuracy bonus but a raw damage of Strength + the user\u2019s Initiative, plus threshold successes on the roll, with a minimum of their Strength. Everybody that gets hit is knocked back and prone, and crashed enemies can\u2019t make a movement action on their next turn. The user doesn\u2019t gain any of the Initiative that enemies lost, and their own 10s on the damage roll lead to\u2026 sorry, thought of something, lead to them needing to roll a die of decisive bashing damage against themselves\u2026 or against the one that was hit? The latter would make more sense, but I think the wording could be cleared up. Spirits take decisive damage as a matter of course, and can be hit even when dematerialized. The Charm gets reset by incapacitating a threatening enemy.<br /> <br /> Yeah, another synergy I realised in the Charm; the number of effects to knock people back, and render them prone. Jump about pushing people into position, pinning them down, and then throw your chakram to hit all of them with a devastating attack. Beautiful.<br /> <br /> And last is Hurricane Combat Method, an actual Essence 5 Martial Arts Charm. It functions as a permanent enhancement to Air Dragon Form, letting one add a surcharge of 6 motes and one Willpower to enhance it, increasing the Evasion bonus and doubling 9s on Stealth and movement rolls. Once per round, they can pay five Initiative to reflexively make a withering or decisive attack that doesn\u2019t count as their attack for the round, and can be used to clash. It\u2019s a nice final benefit for the Style\u2019s tactical approach.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Air Dragon Style gets the ball rolling well and sets a very high bar. Good work there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T08:43:17-07:00","id":1210969,"title":"","content":"The brawl excellency pulls double duty as martial arts as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1363-brett-alexander","name":"Brett Alexander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:27:29-07:00","id":1211074,"title":"","content":"Okay, I am surprisingly psyched to see the rest of the styles. Two more now, Earth and Fire.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon is described as being about overwhelming force with meticulous deliberation, moving slowly and surely. Training involves hardening the body with things like beating up barrels of gravel and sleeping on beds of nails (incidentally, one thing that I <i>did</i> always like about the Immaculate styles were the descriptions for their training regimens). The result creates warriors who can withstand deadly blow and answer them back with tetsubos. The style\u2019s unarmed strikes are said to be solid and powerful, often delivered with elbows and knees, as well as two-handed blows. It\u2019s compatible with all armour, and is complementary not only with Occult (which can probably be safely assumed to be comprehensive to the styles) but Athletics for feats of strength.<br /> <br /> It starts with Stone Dragon\u2019s Skin, letting one ignore half their Stamina in wound penalties to Parry, as well as adding to natural soak against withering attacks, and a bit of Hardness against decisive ones. It has reduced costs depending on how low the grade of one\u2019s armour is, down to being completely unarmoured.<br /> <br /> Force of the Mountain lets one add dice to raw withering damage, or double 10s on decisive damage rolls, with Earth Aura increasing the amount that can be done for withering attacks. Stillness-of-Stone Atemi is used to increase the Overwhelming value of withering attacks, and gives the option to pay Initiative for each 10 that shows up on the damage roll to level a mobility penalty on the one who was hit until their next turn ends, or, if the attack crashed them, until they recover from crash. Earth Aura lets them also spend Initiative for rolled 9s.<br /> <br /> Unmoving Mountain Stance is used when the fighter is hit by an attack, but before it rolls damage, letting them reduce the Initiative that enemies gets from hitting them with withering attacks and\u2026 I think there\u2019s an error there, since it says that it both does and doesn\u2019t affect the Initiative that attackers gain (unless withering attacks gave default Initiative just for successfully landing the hit that I\u2019ve forgotten about). It also makes Smash attacks or similar to shift them fail automatically unless it deals a minimum of withering or decisive damage (different values for each). Earth Aura adds to the Initiative denied to opponents, as well as how much damage needs to be done to knock them back.<br /> <br /> It comes to Earth Dragon Form, with which one becomes able to add half their Strength to attack rolls for Smash attacks or ones made on prone enemies, and adds full Strength to natural soak. The form can be reflexively entered when an enemy with lower Initiative manages to hit them.<br /> <br /> Ghost-Grounding Blow is a main attack for hitting spirits, used after crashing one with a withering attack to instantly force them to materialize and becomes incapable of dematerializing or using Hurry Home until a number of rounds equal to the user\u2019s Strength have passed following the spirit recovering from crash.<br /> <br /> Following that is a lengthier one with Earthshaker Attack. When they have Initiative of 15 or higher, they can make a single decisive attack against all characters in short range, which is unblockable, undodgeable, and can\u2019t be clashed, and requires those hit by it to roll Athletics to maintain their balance. Those who fail are knocked prone and suffer dice of Hardness ignoring bashing damage equal to the attacker\u2019s Strength, and doesn\u2019t reset the user to base Initiative. Battle groups that lack Might fail the roll automatically, and enemies that take at least 3 levels of damage are knocked back a range band, suffering damage equivalent to a short-range fall. Earth Aura allows one to divide their Initiative between opponents and add it to the Charm\u2019s base damage, which <i>will</i> reset them to base. The Charm can only be used once per scene, and is reset by crashing an opponent while they\u2019re prone.<br /> <br /> Earthshaker Attack isn\u2019t quite the revelation that Tornado Offense Technique was, but it looks like an impressive Charm to strike multiple people in its own right.<br /> <br /> Shattering Fist Strike is used to enhance disarm gambits to actually break weapons with strikes, completely destroying mundane weapons and expending Earth Aura to make a gambit with the difficulty increased by the targeted Artifact\u2019s rating to render it inoperable until repaired. I\u2019m always going to be a fan of dramatically breaking magical weapons, so I like this Charm being here. It also lets one perform feats of demolition with double 9s and in the span of a miscellaneous action rather than necessarily longer.<br /> <br /> Following that is Weapon-Breaking Defense Technique, which allows a reflexive clash attack on a close range assault that applies the effect of the prior Charm, without counting as the combat action. Winning the clash adds the attack roll\u2019s threshold successes to the Initiative roll. The Charm doesn\u2019t function to clash unarmed or other Natural attacks. Being in Earth Aura allows one to clash Artifact weapons without needing to expend Aura, and the Defense can only be used once per scene unless reset with dealing 7 or more levels of decisive damage to an enemy.<br /> <br /> For their Essence 4 Charms, we first get Avalanche Method, which is rather costly, an Instant Charm that requires a whopping <i>twenty</i> motes and one Willpower. The Charm\u2019s user needs at least 12 Initiative to use it, and the target must have a mobility penalty of at least -1 (I\u2019m unsure if that includes penalties inflicted by Charms). The user gets to continuously make decisive attacks against an enemy until they\u2019ve made a number equal to their mobility penalty, or miss, and each attack loses Initiative equal to the damage inflicted, only resetting to base when all attacks are made. If it\u2019s used to land a smash attack, the enemy won\u2019t be knocked back until the barrage is finished, with repeated smashes compounding how far back the character is flung, and being able to suffer falling damage if sent back to medium range or further. It also won\u2019t free an enemy trapped by Hungry Earth Strike, while still being able to suffer falling damage from how far they might have been flung. Finally, being in Earth Aura allows one to use the Charm to its fullest even if an attack misses.<br /> <br /> I feel as though the Charm might as well be limited to hitting an enemy with a mobility penalty of at least -2, since it\u2019s not really worth it to use the Charm to hit somebody once, but apart from that it looks like a solid Charm.<br /> <br /> Hungry Earth Strike was another good looking classic, standing out from the others for its evocative and readily comprehended effect. A withering attack (that must be either smashing or directed at somebody who is prone) can be made with double 8s on the damage roll, and if it succeeds in crashing the target (and they\u2019re standing on rock or soil, or sent there by knockback), then the target gets sucked into the ground. While trapped, the character can\u2019t take movement actions, suffers the penalties of being prone (which would include being vulnerable to several other Charms in this style), and each turn inflicts a die of Hardness-ignoring bashing damage. Spirits will suffer the effects of Ghost-Grounding Blow while they\u2019re trapped, and anybody who is incapacitated in that state will die, being drawn into the earth. Buried characters can attempt to break free using an extended Strength + Athletics action, with the attacker\u2019s Strength as the difficulty and their Essence + Strength as the goal number, with allies able to make their own rolls and adding their successes to the total towards the goal. Being in Earth Aura allows the user to bury an enemy without crashing them, so long as the attack reduces their Initiative below that of the user. It also needs to be reset, by incapacitating an enemy from a decisive attack made with 20+ Initiative.<br /> <br /> Last is Perfection of Earth Body, another enhancement to the Form Charm. Paying the same surcharge as Air Dragon Style had, the character becomes capable of adding their Stamina to withering or decisive damage for attacks to smash or against prone enemies, becomes immune to wound penalties, and the effects of crippling attacks. If the character is unarmoured, the soak bonus from the Form Charm is increased, and they gain Hardness.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon Style doesn\u2019t quite have the same apparent tactical hook that Air Dragon did, but it does have some noticeable synergies, and it comes together well.<br /> <br /> The styles are actually long enough on their own, so I\u2019m going to post thoughts on them individually, but won\u2019t be as long between them as I was with the Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:46:39-07:00","id":1211083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200127-isator-levi-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1211074#post1211074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unmoving Mountain Stance is used when the fighter is hit by an attack, but before it rolls damage, letting them reduce the Initiative that enemies gets from hitting them with withering attacks and\u2026 I think there\u2019s an error there, since it says that it both does and doesn\u2019t affect the Initiative that attackers gain (unless withering attacks gave default Initiative just for successfully landing the hit that I\u2019ve forgotten about).</div> </div> </div> </div>You gain 1 iniative for landing an attack, regardless of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:10:55-07:00","id":1211114,"title":"","content":"Fire Dragon Style, go!<br /> <br /> In that spirit, it\u2019s description is shorter. A combination of unpredictable violence and self-discipline, trained by\u2026 huh, performing drills and practices in time to music, I think that\u2019s new, they used to be repeatedly set on fire. They style is based on alternately reserving and unleashing force, unarmed attacks being rapid barrages of punches and chops and powerful kicks, also using short swords (traditionally paired), and compatible with light and medium armour. It has no other complementary Abilities.<br /> <br /> Flash-Fire Technique represents a finely honed combat instinct by being able to roll Join Battle twice (paying enhancement Charms separately for each), taking the higher result and letting them make a decisive attack on the first turn with extra successes on the attack roll (up to a limit of Dexterity) to the damage dice roll.<br /> <br /> Searing Edge Attack focuses killing intent through the strike in the form of painful heat, letting withering attacks cause those struck with them to lose additional Initiative, that the Exalt doesn\u2019t gain.<br /> Flame-Flicker Stance is used to convert up to Essence 1s on an enemy\u2019s attack roll into extra points on their Parry, with successfully blocked attacks from enemies with lower Initiative not inflicting onslaught penalties. Fire Aura removes the limits of how many 1s the Charm\u2019s user can benefit from.<br /> <br /> Perfect Blazing Blow can double 9s on decisive attack rolls against enemies with lower Initiative, upgraded to double 8s against crashed opponents, and with Fire Aura letting each doubled success add a die to the damage roll.<br /> <br /> Now, what of Fire Dragon Form? Against enemies with lower Initiative, their attacks inflict onslaught before they\u2019re rolled, and when the fighter successfully parries a decisive attack, it doubles the Initiative that the enemy loses. The Form can be reflexively adopted when the Exalt wins Join Battle.<br /> <br /> Yes, I\u2019m seeing Fire Dragon\u2019s distinct methodology here; certain benefits to Defense and withering attacks, building towards greater power on enemies with lower Initiative. It\u2019s nuanced, but still very direct and straightforward.<br /> <br /> God-Immolating Strike is their spirit attacking Charm, letting a decisive attack deal aggravated damage to spirits and treating their Initiative as though it\u2019s a number of points higher equal to Essence for the sake of the aforementioned Charm that function off of lower Initiative foes. When a spirit is damaged, its next turn has it roll\u2026 I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s the user\u2019s or targets Essence, but whichever one rolls that number for Hardness-ignoring aggravated damage (a number that dematerialized spirits add 2 to).<br /> <br /> With Essence-Igniting Nerve Strike, the fighter can light their foe\u2019s Essence to burn them from within. A withering attack against a lower Initiative target; the Initiative reaped from the target is halved, but every 9 and 10 that show up on the damage rolls remove one or two motes, respectively (with the Charm\u2019s user deciding if they\u2019re personal or peripheral). If the enemy is crashed, the burning motes burst out of them, rolling one lethal die for every two motes, up to a maximum of the attacker\u2019s Essence, and ignoring Hardness. If the user expends their Fire Aura, they get to reap the full Initiative from the successful attack.<br /> <br /> Overwhelming Fire Majesty Stance lets the Exalt really start to reap their patience, become wreathed in flame that imposes a penalty on enemy attacks on them, and causing those that do manage to succeed at close range to suffer a Hardness-ignoring die of lethal damage, although foes can pay Willpower to become immune to the attack penalty for the scene. Fire Aura allows the Exalt to waive the Charm\u2019s Initiative cost and make it lose the Perilous keyword.<br /> <br /> Fiery Blade Attack is fairly self-explanatory; successful decisive attacks ignite a bonfire that burns the victim without fuel so long as they remain within it, where escape requires a disengage action (with a set difficulty of 2 if they\u2019re not disengaging an actual enemy).<br /> <br /> Breath of the Fire Dragon makes an unblockable decisive attack based on Stamina + Martial Arts against everybody in a cone out to close range, plus an extra range band for each 10 Initiative (another example of reserving energy to be unleashed dramatically), to a maximum of medium range. It can also strike the dematerialized, and rolls a third of Initiative against everybody, that ignores Hardness. If anybody is hit, the attacker resets to base. Enemies that take sufficient damage ignite, suffering the user\u2019s Essence in dice of lethal damage that ignore Hardness each turn until they put out; dematerialized spirits take aggravated damage and are made visible, unable to extinguish themselves unless they materialize. It can also light flammable scenery. It\u2019s reset by gaining at least 15 Initiative on one tick.<br /> <br /> Smoldering Wound Attack is used when a decisive attack hits, but before its damage is rolled. Every 10 on the damage roll lets the attacker roll a die of unsoakable withering damage, adding to the fighter\u2019s Initiative when they reset to base (unable to gain more than their Essence). If used on a crashed enemy, the additional rolled damage is also decisive, but still adds to the user\u2019s Initiative. Being in Fire Aura allows one to use the Charm <i>after</i> the damage has been rolled (i.e. when the player knows how good of an effect it will have).<br /> <br /> Last is Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon, with which a martial artist can enhance Fire Dragon Form to let them treat their Initiative as though it is increased by a value equal to Wits for deciding turn order, as well as for the purpose of Charms based on having lower Initiative. The fighter\u2019s withering attacks gain half their Strength as an Overwhelming value, and decisive attacks add one to their damage rolls. Enemies that hit them at close range take a die of lethal damage. As enemies are incapacitated, the Initiative, Overwhelming and decisive bonus, as well as the damage taken by attackers, is increased by one.<br /> <br /> Initiative has really done a lot for Fire Dragon, creating a metric by which the reserved and unleashed energy can really be measured, and thus giving the concept a lot more texture and verisimilitude. Its goals and synergies are even more readily grasped than Air Dragon, even if I think I still like that one a bit better. All in all, this is another nicely done one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:35:48-07:00","id":1211130,"title":"","content":"Ah, darn it, I had forgotten that these Martial Arts were going to include things like White Veil and Golden Janissary. It's going to take longer to get through the front of this chapter than I thought.<br /> <br /> I'm growing impatient to see some of the other neat stuff, but I shall emphatically not read out of order. That isn't our way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T16:00:22-07:00","id":1211196,"title":"","content":"Now, to see what was done with Water Dragon Style. It\u2019s used by monks, there can\u2019t possibly be any duplicity, deception and manipulation here, right?! Just\u2026 making people drown in their own blood\u2026 well played Water, you magnificent bastard.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the principle of the style is described as being in tune with the flow of things, rhythm, blood and Essence, so that they can redirect or impede those flows, with fluid defence and repeated and exploitative offence. Its unarmed attacks are based on swift sequences of punch, kick and claw strike, and uses tiger claws for weapons. It\u2019s compatible with light and medium armour, and like Fire Dragon has no other complementary Abilities.<br /> <br /> For a start they have Flowing Water Defense, letting a full defence be flurried with an attack without penalty, and Water Aura allowing successful attacks to refund the Initiative cost of full defence. Rippling Water Strike is conversely used to increase the Overwhelming value of a withering attack, and can use Dexterity in place of Strength for determining raw damage (which should have a nice reception <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />); if a foe is crashed with the attack, all the rest within close range take an onslaught penalty. Water Aura allows one to <i>add</i> their Dexterity to the usual raw damage calculation, rather than switch out Strength for it.<br /> <br /> Speak of the devil, Drowning-in-Blood Technique; redirect somebody\u2019s blood flow into their lungs. Of course Water would govern one of the more horrifying effects in the game (at least in concept and character). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Decisive attacks double 10 on their damage rolls, and if they deal at least three levels, the choking on blood results in an increase wound penalty until the end of the scene or they crash the one that did it to them. Spirits are also susceptible to the technique through the flow of their Essence, and can have the wound penalty increasing effect stacked up to the user\u2019s Essence. In their Water Aura, the martial artist adds half the foe\u2019s wound penalty as bonus dice to the damage roll.<br /> <br /> Shrugging Water-Dragon Escape gives double 9s on a Martial Arts based roll to resist grapples, disengage rolls, opposing enemy rushes, or rolling to escape constraints, with Aura providing a point of Initiative from success on the roll. Then it\u2019s Water Dragon Form: bonus dice equal to a target\u2019s wound penalty are given to attack rolls, and Stamina is regarded as double for soak calculations, with the capacity to enter the Form reflexively when enough decisive damage is inflicted on an enemy to increase their wound penalty.<br /> <br /> Ah yes, an aspect of Water\u2019s bastardry that I forgot to consider; theft. Theft-of-Essence Method can be used when an opponent is crashed to steal some of their motes (based partially on the wound penalty of the crashed enemy), adding them to the type of pool that they were taken from.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Bottomless Depths Defense, previously one of the strongest defensive options available to Dragon Blooded. Now, they use it to roll their Essence + Stamina after being hit by an attack, and subtracting the result from damage successes, with a minimum of one removed even if no successes are rolled. Alternatively, Water Aura can be expended to negate all damage, so yeah, still one of the stronger defences. That\u2019s offset by it only having a per-day use, unless reset by being hit with three decisive attacks without taking any damage. The only thing I regret is that it doesn\u2019t have the flavour text of shunting that damage to the Elemental Dragon of Water anymore, but that\u2019s a very minor quality.<br /> <br /> Essence-Dousing Wave Attack is described as attacking with a dark, smothering Essence, that quenches the flame of an opponent\u2019s battle prowess. Used when a decisive attack on a crashed enemy inflicts at least the target\u2019s Essence in damage, then one of their ongoing Charms can be deactivated, so long as it belongs to a combat Ability or combat-based physical Attribute (I\u2019m guessing the same basic parameter applies against the rare opponent with only Essence-based Charms). For an especially strong boost, Water Aura can be expended to use on an opponent that is not crashed.<br /> <br /> Flow Reversal Strike is another one to interfere with somebody\u2019s bodily fluids, reversing their course in the form of making an opponent roll Stamina + Resistance in response to being hit with a decisive attack, with a difficulty of the attack\u2019s threshold successes, and where failure results in rolling extra decisive damage equal to the shortfall, and after the damage is inflicted, also inflicting withering damage equal to the current wound penalty (which the attacker <i>does</i> get). When used on spirits, their wound penalties will subtract successes, rather than dice, from the initial Resistance roll. It gets reset by crashing an enemy whose Initiative was higher than the Exalt\u2019s before being attacked.<br /> <br /> Hmm, we\u2019ll be getting into some big ones now. Crashing Wave Style is this art\u2019s access to multiple attacks; withering attacks can be made in sequence against a single enemy until an attack misses, the enemy is crashed, or they\u2019ve inflicted enough of them equal to the target\u2019s wound penalty plus one (when used against battle groups, it can keep going until it misses or depletes Magnitude (pop pop)). When in Water Aura an enemy being crashed is dealt dice of lethal damage equal to their onslaught penalty, ignoring Hardness. It can be reset by landing a decisive attack on a crashed enemy, and then building Initiative back up to 12 Initiative.<br /> <br /> While Ghost-Restraining Whirlpool allows one to generate a maelstrom that draws in spirits; those within medium range cannot move away unless they disengage, nor can they use Hurry Home. Initiative lost by disengaging is transferred to the Exalt, as well as being able to steal two Initiative from each spirit that did not spend a turn moving towards the Exalt or being in close range of them. If the spirits are dematerialized, they\u2019re even more susceptible, with the whole range of the Charm being difficult terrain, and suffering dice of Hardness-ignoring bashing damage if their Initiative is stolen. Water Aura extends the range to long, and the Charm can be activated reflexively when entering Water Dragon Form. <br /> <br /> Finally there is Tsunami-Force Shout, which is <i>not</i> an enhancement to the Form Charm. Instead, it\u2019s a special form of decisive attack; it requires at least 20 Initiative to use, and rolls an unblockable attack using Stamina + Martial Arts against all enemies in a cone out to medium range (although if the prior Charm is being used, the Shout extends through the entire whirlpool). The attack deals bashing damage to each enemy that is hit equal to the attack roll\u2019s threshold successes <i>multiplied</i> by the struck person\u2019s wound penalty, plus one, ignoring Hardness. Battle groups are considered to have a -4 wound penalty, and the attack doesn\u2019t reset the Exalt\u2019s Initiative to base (although as well as the cost in motes and Willpower, it has a rather hefty cost of 10 points anyway). An enemy damaged by the Shout will be knocked back and prone, although spirits that would be forced beyond the range of the Ghost-Restraining Whirlpool (which they cannot go beyond) will take damage as though they experienced a short fall. Enemies that take three or more damage will go back two bands and suffer short falling damage, unless it\u2019s a spirit knocked into the boundary of the whirlpool, who takes it as a medium range fall. It can be reset by landing a decisive attack that resets Initiative, and then building back towards 20.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say that Water Dragon is similar to Earth; less built around a specific internal tactical setup than Air and Fire, and more about applying conditions and exploiting circumstances, which I would say is very fitting to the concept. I\u2019d also say that the quality of messing targets up painfully is applied more consistently throughout than the prior Editions.<br /> <br /> On a final note before going off into Wood, I want to say that I especially like the many and varied ways that the styles can be particularly brutal towards spirits, while still short of having effects to permanently kill them. In general, it\u2019s very effectively plays up the idea that an intended function of these styles was in dealing with unruly spirits, while it doesn\u2019t interfere with my prior observation of generally lacking such power, and the dynamics that would present in the setting\u2019s history; the plausibility that there are more than a few spirits that have been subjected to pain, humiliation and death from the Immaculate Dragon Styles, and can still be around in the Time of Tumult to be salty about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:28:24-07:00","id":1211253,"title":"","content":"To finish off for the time being is Wood Dragon Style, the most mysterious of them. It can oversee cycles of life and death, as instructed through gruelling regimens of being brought to the brink of death, fasting to the body\u2019s limit and consuming copious quantities of hallucinogenic and entheogenic drugs, bringing strange insights when they recover. They utilise pressure points and Essence flows to harm foes and heal friends, and we\u2019re given a hint of their dread final power. The unarmed attack are described as precise finger jabs, as well as staves. The bow is still here, but with a twist; the martial artist is trained to wield it in close quarters like a staff, and while the style\u2019s attacks don\u2019t work through shots, the fighter doesn\u2019t require a ready weapon action to switch between methods of using it. The style is only compatible with light armour, and is complemented by\u2026 Performance for distraction and misdirection. I would have sworn Medicine was in there, but have to remind myself that these Abilities aren\u2019t often directly about what is used for the Style, but what helps them.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon Vitaliy strengthens the martial artist\u2019s body, adding Martial Arts to their natural soak, and subtracting a die from decisive attacks, with the former bonus increased by Essence and the latter subtracting half the Essence in dice when in Aura. The Eyes of the Wood Dragon can instead see Essence paths through the body for precise strikes, adding Perception in raw damage to withering attacks, and letting a piercing attack by made, with Aura allowing the latter to ignore the usual Defense penalty.<br /> <br /> Mind-Over-Body Meditation allows the Exalt to fix themselves up, rolling the lower of Essence or Stamina and applying the successes to heal non-aggravated damage, with a minimum of one, although it can only be used once per scene (no reset condition) and can\u2019t be used when not fighting.<br /> <br /> Soul-Marking Style is the start of messing with people\u2019s souls, driving a thorn of Essence into them. If a decisive attack managed to deal damage with the Charm, then the fighter benefits from aiming for the remainder of the scene, so long as Wood Dragon attacks are used. Spirits hit with the thorn suffer a slight crippling penalty for the scene.<br /> <br /> The Wood Dragon Form is activated by the Dragon Blood striking their own pressure points and chakras to align their Essence, gaining the lower of Essence or Stamina in temporary -1 health levels, that are kept for the scene even if the form is left, although when they fade at scene\u2019s end the damage is transferred to the normal health track. It also allows for Mind-Over-Body Meditation to be reset by landing a decisive attack from at least 12 Initiative. Reflexive activation comes from using that Charm or similar effects to heal enough damage to reduce one\u2019s wound penalty.<br /> <br /> With Spirit-Wracking Method, withering attacks against spirits double 8s on the damage roll, but don\u2019t grant the attacker the Initiative. They instead get to roll a die of Hardness-ignoring lethal damage for every 10 on the withering damage roll. A spirit crashed by the attack is wracked with agony, doubling wound penalties and the crippling penalty of Soul-Marking Style until they leave crash.<br /> <br /> Death-Pattern-Sensing Attitude allows one to apply full defence against enemies hit with Soul-Marking, and ignores a penalty to Defence from their surprise attacks. If the fighter is ambushed by a marked person, a point of Willpower can be included in the Charm\u2019s cost to be able to block the attack, although only with a Parry of half their Essence, which no effect can raise.<br /> Spirit-Rending Technique allows one to tear apart unruly gods; a spirit that is Marked can be hit with a decisive attack with the value of Willpower added to the damage roll, dealing aggravated damage, with the attacker gaining motes equal to the spirit\u2019s Essence if the attack incapacitates it.<br /> <br /> Oh, Unbreakable Fascination Kata constitutes an instance in which Performance actually is helpful to the Charm. It is used to make a roll against enemies that can see the user, and any whose Resolve is beaten can neither attack on their next turn, nor move away from the object of fascination without successfully disengaging. The effect can be resisted by spending Willpower (if I\u2019m reading correctly, it\u2019s a little bit unclear), they\u2019re immune to losing their attack for the scene, but still need to disengage to move away. Fascinated enemies that are Marked need to spend Willpower twice in resistance to gain that immunity.<br /> <br /> Into the top level ones with Enthralling Blow Attack, which can be reflexively used upon activating the prior Charm to roll a single withering attack against all enemies in close range that were beguiled, even if they resisted with Willpower. Each hit enemy has a separate damage roll made, while only the highest yields points to the attacker, and damaged enemies can\u2019t move on their next turn. If the enemy is crashed by the attack, then they experience the full effect of Unbreakable Fascination until they recover from crash, regardless of Willpower spent. Wood Aura enhances the Initiative reaped, allowing points equal to half of the user\u2019s Essence to be taken from each person after the highest.<br /> <br /> With Wood Dragon Succor (usable only with at least 12 Initiative), the mystic is able to lay hands on another character and rolls their Initiative, applying the successes (up to a maximum of the beneficiary\u2019s Stamina + Resistance) to heal levels of non-aggravated damage, although the Exalt suffers one level of bashing damage for every two levels that they heal, which cannot be prevented. It resets the user to base Initiative, unless they can expend a Wood Aura to only need to lose Initiative equal to the healed health levels, down to a minimum of base. The Charm can only be used on the same person once per day.<br /> <br /> And that brings us down to the infamous Soul Mastery. The Charm can only be used against opponents hit with Soul-Marking Style, allowing one to roll a gambit against a difficulty of the target\u2019s Essence + Willpower, minus their wound penalty, down to a minimum of 6. If successful, the target is destroyed utterly; spirits are permanently destroyed, undead crumble to dust, and the living immediately die while their souls (mercifully) survive, immediately sent to Lethe. It cannot affect things that neither qualify as living nor dead, and can only be used once per scene. I\u2019d say that this is about the best possible way that such an instant death effect could be utilised in this system, while still staying true to the essential concept of the Charm.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon came out well, managing to consolidate many of the themes and ideas from prior Editions while being less of a grab-bag of effects, and it sorted out the pinnacle Charm. Indeed, it should be evident that I think highly of what was achieved with all of the Immaculate Dragon Styles, and find their place in the lore and metagame to be secured.<br /> <br /> Ahhh, it\u2019s so late, but all I want to do is keep reading Charms, in contrast to the prior chapter. See, this is the problem with Third Edition Martial Arts; while they\u2019re not necessarily short (if often a bit shorter than a given Ability), they\u2019re immensely compelling to read due to the manner in which they internally synergize with one another, and build up towards dramatic effects. So I just want to keep consuming them.<br /> <br /> Still, it\u2019s probably for the best that I call it for the time-being, and the last of the Immaculate Styles seems like the best place to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T03:04:26-07:00","id":1211339,"title":"","content":"I haven't had a chance to go through the previews yet - does a master of Wood Dragon Style still need to carry a mouse in his pocket for the occasions where he can't hit someone with Soul Mastery in time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":